. Exactly. How many of these multi-billion dollar metrics would actually survive? It really makes you wonder how much of the personal data we obsess over every day is actually a clean failure, quietly strapped to our wrists.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 9.84, "text": " You know, if you pay attention to your industry's news, or honestly, just sit through like a single corporate strategy meeting, you probably noticed a very specific pattern.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 458, 11, 498, 291, 1689, 3202, 281, 428, 3518, 311, 2583, 11, 420, 6095, 11, 445, 1394, 807, 411, 257, 2167, 10896, 5206, 3440, 11, 291, 1391, 5694, 257, 588, 2685, 5102, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08887080488533809, "compression_ratio": 1.5433070866141732, "no_speech_prob": 9.072127272503894e-13}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 10.0, "end": 11.86, "text": " Oh, definitely. It happens all the time.", "tokens": [50865, 876, 11, 2138, 13, 467, 2314, 439, 264, 565, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08887080488533809, "compression_ratio": 1.5433070866141732, "no_speech_prob": 9.072127272503894e-13}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 12.0, "end": 22.84, "text": " Right. Someone stands up, they invent this highly technical sounding buzzword for a completely old concept, and then they act like they've just cracked the code to the universe.", "tokens": [50965, 1779, 13, 8734, 7382, 493, 11, 436, 7962, 341, 5405, 6191, 24931, 13036, 7462, 337, 257, 2584, 1331, 3410, 11, 293, 550, 436, 605, 411, 436, 600, 445, 25140, 264, 3089, 281, 264, 6445, 13, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08887080488533809, "compression_ratio": 1.5433070866141732, "no_speech_prob": 9.072127272503894e-13}, {"id": 3, "seek": 2284, "start": 22.84, "end": 35.88, "text": " Yeah, it's a remarkably common tactic. I mean, they slap a shiny new label on something, maybe dress it up in some complex sounding math or slick diagrams, and suddenly we're all supposed to believe a massive breakthrough has occurred.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 309, 311, 257, 37381, 2689, 31012, 13, 286, 914, 11, 436, 21075, 257, 16997, 777, 7645, 322, 746, 11, 1310, 5231, 309, 493, 294, 512, 3997, 24931, 5221, 420, 37406, 36709, 11, 293, 5800, 321, 434, 439, 3442, 281, 1697, 257, 5994, 22397, 575, 11068, 13, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07879691395333142, "compression_ratio": 1.5953757225433527, "no_speech_prob": 6.333600094041159e-13}, {"id": 4, "seek": 2284, "start": 36.16, "end": 39.56, "text": " Exactly. It creates this illusion of measurement and discovery.", "tokens": [51031, 7587, 13, 467, 7829, 341, 18854, 295, 13160, 293, 12114, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07879691395333142, "compression_ratio": 1.5953757225433527, "no_speech_prob": 6.333600094041159e-13}, {"id": 5, "seek": 2284, "start": 39.9, "end": 42.68, "text": " But it's really just rhetorical sleight of hand.", "tokens": [51218, 583, 309, 311, 534, 445, 24182, 284, 804, 2426, 397, 295, 1011, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07879691395333142, "compression_ratio": 1.5953757225433527, "no_speech_prob": 6.333600094041159e-13}, {"id": 6, "seek": 2284, "start": 42.68, "end": 52.379999999999995, "text": " Which brings us to the real question for you, listening to this deep dive right now. How do you actually prove that they haven't discovered anything new? Like, how do you systematically call their bluff?", "tokens": [51357, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 957, 1168, 337, 291, 11, 4764, 281, 341, 2452, 9192, 558, 586, 13, 1012, 360, 291, 767, 7081, 300, 436, 2378, 380, 6941, 1340, 777, 30, 1743, 11, 577, 360, 291, 39531, 818, 641, 44191, 30, 51842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07879691395333142, "compression_ratio": 1.5953757225433527, "no_speech_prob": 6.333600094041159e-13}, {"id": 7, "seek": 5238, "start": 52.38, "end": 54.42, "text": " That is the million dollar question.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 264, 2459, 7241, 1168, 13, 50467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0966514732878087, "compression_ratio": 1.396551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751709611476095e-12}, {"id": 8, "seek": 5238, "start": 54.56, "end": 64.32000000000001, "text": " Well, that's exactly what our mission is today. We are pulling from two truly fascinating papers published in 2026 by an independent researcher named Flixian.", "tokens": [50474, 1042, 11, 300, 311, 2293, 437, 527, 4447, 307, 965, 13, 492, 366, 8407, 490, 732, 4908, 10343, 10577, 6572, 294, 945, 10880, 538, 364, 6695, 21751, 4926, 3235, 970, 952, 13, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0966514732878087, "compression_ratio": 1.396551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751709611476095e-12}, {"id": 9, "seek": 5238, "start": 64.62, "end": 67.84, "text": " And they are quite a pair to read side by side.", "tokens": [50977, 400, 436, 366, 1596, 257, 6119, 281, 1401, 1252, 538, 1252, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0966514732878087, "compression_ratio": 1.396551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751709611476095e-12}, {"id": 10, "seek": 6784, "start": 67.84, "end": 83.32000000000001, "text": " They really are. The first is this dense philosophical essay titled Prediction Before Interpretation. And the second is a hardcore physics paper titled Capacity, Dissipation, and the Onset of Motility-Induced Phase Separation.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 534, 366, 13, 440, 700, 307, 341, 18011, 25066, 16238, 19841, 32969, 4105, 4546, 5751, 6629, 399, 13, 400, 264, 1150, 307, 257, 28196, 10649, 3035, 19841, 8363, 19008, 11, 413, 891, 647, 399, 11, 293, 264, 1282, 3854, 295, 8956, 1140, 12, 21790, 41209, 24432, 43480, 399, 13, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11021936507452101, "compression_ratio": 1.3944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722224090865654e-12}, {"id": 11, "seek": 6784, "start": 83.4, "end": 84.24000000000001, "text": " That's quite a mouthful.", "tokens": [51143, 663, 311, 1596, 257, 4525, 906, 13, 51185], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11021936507452101, "compression_ratio": 1.3944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722224090865654e-12}, {"id": 12, "seek": 8424, "start": 84.24, "end": 95.32, "text": " Yeah, it is. But the goal today is to equip you with the ultimate toolkit for spotting when new terminology is actually new knowledge and when it's just, you know, hot air.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 309, 307, 13, 583, 264, 3387, 965, 307, 281, 5037, 291, 365, 264, 9705, 40167, 337, 4008, 783, 562, 777, 27575, 307, 767, 777, 3601, 293, 562, 309, 311, 445, 11, 291, 458, 11, 2368, 1988, 13, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06654944053063026, "compression_ratio": 1.4666666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860291595684584e-12}, {"id": 13, "seek": 8424, "start": 95.44, "end": 95.66, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50925, 865, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06654944053063026, "compression_ratio": 1.4666666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860291595684584e-12}, {"id": 14, "seek": 8424, "start": 95.75999999999999, "end": 100.25999999999999, "text": " And we're going to use this highly rigorous physics simulation as our testing ground.", "tokens": [50941, 400, 321, 434, 516, 281, 764, 341, 5405, 29882, 10649, 16575, 382, 527, 4997, 2727, 13, 51166], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06654944053063026, "compression_ratio": 1.4666666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860291595684584e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 10026, "start": 100.26, "end": 110.12, "text": " It's a brilliant exercise, honestly. Primarily because Flixian doesn't just complain about bad science or vague terminology. They built an incredibly strict philosophical standard to prevent it.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 10248, 5380, 11, 6095, 13, 19671, 3289, 570, 3235, 970, 952, 1177, 380, 445, 11024, 466, 1578, 3497, 420, 24247, 27575, 13, 814, 3094, 364, 6252, 10910, 25066, 3832, 281, 4871, 309, 13, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07595712063359279, "compression_ratio": 1.6547231270358307, "no_speech_prob": 1.1970954826370783e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 10026, "start": 110.34, "end": 110.5, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50869, 865, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07595712063359279, "compression_ratio": 1.6547231270358307, "no_speech_prob": 1.1970954826370783e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 10026, "start": 110.58000000000001, "end": 115.38000000000001, "text": " And then they actually subjected their own physical research to that exact standard just to see if it would survive.", "tokens": [50881, 400, 550, 436, 767, 32153, 641, 1065, 4001, 2132, 281, 300, 1900, 3832, 445, 281, 536, 498, 309, 576, 7867, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07595712063359279, "compression_ratio": 1.6547231270358307, "no_speech_prob": 1.1970954826370783e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 10026, "start": 115.68, "end": 124.76, "text": " So before we get into the physical experiment itself, the colliding particles and the simulations, we really need to establish the philosophical standard the author is holding themselves to.", "tokens": [51136, 407, 949, 321, 483, 666, 264, 4001, 5120, 2564, 11, 264, 1263, 2819, 10007, 293, 264, 35138, 11, 321, 534, 643, 281, 8327, 264, 25066, 3832, 264, 3793, 307, 5061, 2969, 281, 13, 51590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07595712063359279, "compression_ratio": 1.6547231270358307, "no_speech_prob": 1.1970954826370783e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 12476, "start": 124.76, "end": 128.18, "text": " Yeah. We have to start with that first paper, Prediction Before Interpretation.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 492, 362, 281, 722, 365, 300, 700, 3035, 11, 32969, 4105, 4546, 5751, 6629, 399, 13, 50536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10087237486968169, "compression_ratio": 1.5902777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132579434321003e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 12476, "start": 128.36, "end": 130.28, "text": " Right. So break that down for us.", "tokens": [50545, 1779, 13, 407, 1821, 300, 760, 337, 505, 13, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10087237486968169, "compression_ratio": 1.5902777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132579434321003e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 12476, "start": 130.28, "end": 142.04000000000002, "text": " Well, the core argument revolves around what Flixian calls field-like constructs. And we see these everywhere, right? In complex systems theory, ecology, economics.", "tokens": [50641, 1042, 11, 264, 4965, 6770, 47934, 926, 437, 3235, 970, 952, 5498, 2519, 12, 4092, 7690, 82, 13, 400, 321, 536, 613, 5315, 11, 558, 30, 682, 3997, 3652, 5261, 11, 39683, 11, 14564, 13, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10087237486968169, "compression_ratio": 1.5902777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132579434321003e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 12476, "start": 142.38, "end": 143.62, "text": " What kind of words are we talking about here?", "tokens": [51246, 708, 733, 295, 2283, 366, 321, 1417, 466, 510, 30, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10087237486968169, "compression_ratio": 1.5902777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132579434321003e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 12476, "start": 143.96, "end": 147.94, "text": " We're talking about words like capacity, resilience, agency, or alignment.", "tokens": [51325, 492, 434, 1417, 466, 2283, 411, 6042, 11, 19980, 11, 7934, 11, 420, 18515, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10087237486968169, "compression_ratio": 1.5902777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132579434321003e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 12476, "start": 148.38, "end": 151.38, "text": " Okay. Words that sound incredibly scientific and rigorous.", "tokens": [51546, 1033, 13, 32857, 300, 1626, 6252, 8134, 293, 29882, 13, 51696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10087237486968169, "compression_ratio": 1.5902777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132579434321003e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 15138, "start": 151.38, "end": 163.32, "text": " Exactly. They do the grammatical work of a measurable quantity. Like when you hear the word resilience, it sounds like something that could be larger in one place or smaller in another or, you know, changing over time.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 814, 360, 264, 17570, 267, 804, 589, 295, 257, 43615, 11275, 13, 1743, 562, 291, 1568, 264, 1349, 19980, 11, 309, 3263, 411, 746, 300, 727, 312, 4833, 294, 472, 1081, 420, 4356, 294, 1071, 420, 11, 291, 458, 11, 4473, 670, 565, 13, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05776600734047268, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920850792230934e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 15138, "start": 163.4, "end": 164.51999999999998, "text": " Right. It implies a metric.", "tokens": [50966, 1779, 13, 467, 18779, 257, 20678, 13, 51022], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05776600734047268, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920850792230934e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 15138, "start": 164.68, "end": 172.38, "text": " But the text points out a major flaw here. These terms are often introduced without any actual measurement procedure attached to them.", "tokens": [51030, 583, 264, 2487, 2793, 484, 257, 2563, 13717, 510, 13, 1981, 2115, 366, 2049, 7268, 1553, 604, 3539, 13160, 10747, 8570, 281, 552, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05776600734047268, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920850792230934e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 15138, "start": 172.54, "end": 172.94, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [51423, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 51443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05776600734047268, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920850792230934e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 17294, "start": 172.94, "end": 187.5, "text": " You can define a quantity with full mathematical formality pages of integrals and coupling terms, but if two competent observers looking at the exact same system cannot independently arrive at the same number, well, that word is just doing rhetorical work.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 6964, 257, 11275, 365, 1577, 18894, 1254, 1860, 7183, 295, 3572, 1124, 293, 37447, 2115, 11, 457, 498, 732, 29998, 48090, 1237, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 1185, 2644, 21761, 8881, 412, 264, 912, 1230, 11, 731, 11, 300, 1349, 307, 445, 884, 24182, 284, 804, 589, 13, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11262348370674329, "compression_ratio": 1.5023041474654377, "no_speech_prob": 1.2491985527593452e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 17294, "start": 187.57999999999998, "end": 188.92, "text": " It's not doing empirical work.", "tokens": [51097, 467, 311, 406, 884, 31886, 589, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11262348370674329, "compression_ratio": 1.5023041474654377, "no_speech_prob": 1.2491985527593452e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 17294, "start": 189.0, "end": 189.44, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51168, 7587, 13, 51190], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11262348370674329, "compression_ratio": 1.5023041474654377, "no_speech_prob": 1.2491985527593452e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 17294, "start": 189.64, "end": 190.56, "text": " Okay. That makes sense.", "tokens": [51200, 1033, 13, 663, 1669, 2020, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11262348370674329, "compression_ratio": 1.5023041474654377, "no_speech_prob": 1.2491985527593452e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 17294, "start": 190.66, "end": 190.76, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51251, 865, 13, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11262348370674329, "compression_ratio": 1.5023041474654377, "no_speech_prob": 1.2491985527593452e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 19076, "start": 190.76, "end": 198.34, "text": " It's like a struggling company rebranding with a sleek new logo and calling their new internal strategy synergy.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 411, 257, 9314, 2237, 12970, 3699, 278, 365, 257, 43464, 777, 9699, 293, 5141, 641, 777, 6920, 5206, 50163, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1504551539911288, "compression_ratio": 1.6233333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6678831709845965e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 19076, "start": 198.72, "end": 200.16, "text": " Oh, that's a perfect parallel.", "tokens": [50763, 876, 11, 300, 311, 257, 2176, 8952, 13, 50835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1504551539911288, "compression_ratio": 1.6233333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6678831709845965e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 19076, "start": 200.16, "end": 207.92, "text": " Right. Because they haven't actually changed their product or their manufacturing pipeline at all. They just rename their meetings and they expect the stock price to go up.", "tokens": [50835, 1779, 13, 1436, 436, 2378, 380, 767, 3105, 641, 1674, 420, 641, 11096, 15517, 412, 439, 13, 814, 445, 36741, 641, 8410, 293, 436, 2066, 264, 4127, 3218, 281, 352, 493, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1504551539911288, "compression_ratio": 1.6233333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6678831709845965e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 19076, "start": 208.04, "end": 210.66, "text": " Yeah. It's vocabulary dressing up as discovery.", "tokens": [51229, 865, 13, 467, 311, 19864, 17211, 493, 382, 12114, 13, 51360], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1504551539911288, "compression_ratio": 1.6233333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6678831709845965e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 19076, "start": 211.44, "end": 220.04, "text": " Flexion actually states this as a very clear foundational slogan. They say, new terminology is not new predictive content.", "tokens": [51399, 29208, 313, 767, 4368, 341, 382, 257, 588, 1850, 32195, 33052, 13, 814, 584, 11, 777, 27575, 307, 406, 777, 35521, 2701, 13, 51829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1504551539911288, "compression_ratio": 1.6233333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6678831709845965e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 22004, "start": 220.04, "end": 221.06, "text": " I love that.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 959, 300, 13, 50416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1287828469887758, "compression_ratio": 1.5114155251141552, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404742810543824e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 22004, "start": 221.06, "end": 231.42, "text": " Right. A theoretical framework can rename existing variables using much more evocative language without actually adding a single thing that a skeptic should care about.", "tokens": [50416, 1779, 13, 316, 20864, 8388, 393, 36741, 6741, 9102, 1228, 709, 544, 1073, 905, 1166, 2856, 1553, 767, 5127, 257, 2167, 551, 300, 257, 19128, 299, 820, 1127, 466, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1287828469887758, "compression_ratio": 1.5114155251141552, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404742810543824e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 22004, "start": 231.64, "end": 236.94, "text": " But wait, I have to push back a little here because there is an aesthetic side to science, right?", "tokens": [50945, 583, 1699, 11, 286, 362, 281, 2944, 646, 257, 707, 510, 570, 456, 307, 364, 20092, 1252, 281, 3497, 11, 558, 30, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1287828469887758, "compression_ratio": 1.5114155251141552, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404742810543824e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 22004, "start": 237.0, "end": 237.22, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [51213, 4894, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1287828469887758, "compression_ratio": 1.5114155251141552, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404742810543824e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 22004, "start": 237.34, "end": 240.22, "text": " Isn't mathematical elegance enough sometimes?", "tokens": [51230, 6998, 380, 18894, 14459, 719, 1547, 2171, 30, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1287828469887758, "compression_ratio": 1.5114155251141552, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404742810543824e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 24022, "start": 240.22, "end": 249.88, "text": " Like, if a new theory or a new construct is beautifully written and it clarifies how we visually think about a problem, doesn't that have value on its own?", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 11, 498, 257, 777, 5261, 420, 257, 777, 7690, 307, 16525, 3720, 293, 309, 6093, 11221, 577, 321, 19622, 519, 466, 257, 1154, 11, 1177, 380, 300, 362, 2158, 322, 1080, 1065, 30, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09988377012055495, "compression_ratio": 1.396341463414634, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689021905228919e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 24022, "start": 250.07999999999998, "end": 253.22, "text": " You know, the author actually anticipates that exact defense.", "tokens": [50858, 509, 458, 11, 264, 3793, 767, 10416, 1024, 300, 1900, 7654, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09988377012055495, "compression_ratio": 1.396341463414634, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689021905228919e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 24022, "start": 253.26, "end": 253.68, "text": " Oh, really?", "tokens": [51017, 876, 11, 534, 30, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09988377012055495, "compression_ratio": 1.396341463414634, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689021905228919e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 25368, "start": 253.68, "end": 262.8, "text": " Yeah. They say explanatory unification, conceptual clarification, and mathematical elegance are perfectly legitimate reasons to develop a theoretical framework.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 814, 584, 9045, 4745, 517, 3774, 11, 24106, 34449, 11, 293, 18894, 14459, 719, 366, 6239, 17956, 4112, 281, 1499, 257, 20864, 8388, 13, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12383181639391967, "compression_ratio": 1.6936170212765957, "no_speech_prob": 1.5365308851655879e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 25368, "start": 262.98, "end": 264.16, "text": " Okay. So it has a place.", "tokens": [50830, 1033, 13, 407, 309, 575, 257, 1081, 13, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12383181639391967, "compression_ratio": 1.6936170212765957, "no_speech_prob": 1.5365308851655879e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 25368, "start": 264.48, "end": 267.68, "text": " It does. But, and this is the crucial distinction we have to make.", "tokens": [50905, 467, 775, 13, 583, 11, 293, 341, 307, 264, 11462, 16844, 321, 362, 281, 652, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12383181639391967, "compression_ratio": 1.6936170212765957, "no_speech_prob": 1.5365308851655879e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 25368, "start": 268.22, "end": 273.54, "text": " Elegance is not a reason to think the idea has found something empirically real in the world.", "tokens": [51092, 462, 6363, 719, 307, 406, 257, 1778, 281, 519, 264, 1558, 575, 1352, 746, 25790, 984, 957, 294, 264, 1002, 13, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12383181639391967, "compression_ratio": 1.6936170212765957, "no_speech_prob": 1.5365308851655879e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 25368, "start": 274.5, "end": 275.98, "text": " Elegance is not evidence.", "tokens": [51406, 462, 6363, 719, 307, 406, 4467, 13, 51480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12383181639391967, "compression_ratio": 1.6936170212765957, "no_speech_prob": 1.5365308851655879e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 25368, "start": 276.14, "end": 277.62, "text": " Elegance is not evidence.", "tokens": [51488, 462, 6363, 719, 307, 406, 4467, 13, 51562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12383181639391967, "compression_ratio": 1.6936170212765957, "no_speech_prob": 1.5365308851655879e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 27762, "start": 277.62, "end": 286.12, "text": " Wow. So you can have a beautiful theory, but you cannot claim it predicts physical reality until it earns that right.", "tokens": [50365, 3153, 13, 407, 291, 393, 362, 257, 2238, 5261, 11, 457, 291, 2644, 3932, 309, 6069, 82, 4001, 4103, 1826, 309, 46936, 300, 558, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15909168409264607, "compression_ratio": 1.576271186440678, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279237494645995e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 27762, "start": 286.48, "end": 294.98, "text": " Precisely. And to earn what Flixing calls predictive standing, a proposed construct has to pass a strict four-part empirical test.", "tokens": [50808, 48746, 736, 13, 400, 281, 6012, 437, 3235, 970, 278, 5498, 35521, 4877, 11, 257, 10348, 7690, 575, 281, 1320, 257, 10910, 1451, 12, 6971, 31886, 1500, 13, 51233], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15909168409264607, "compression_ratio": 1.576271186440678, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279237494645995e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 27762, "start": 295.1, "end": 296.08, "text": " Okay. Lay it on us.", "tokens": [51239, 1033, 13, 20084, 309, 322, 505, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15909168409264607, "compression_ratio": 1.576271186440678, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279237494645995e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 27762, "start": 296.42, "end": 300.46, "text": " It's essentially a gauntlet designed to strip away the poetry and leave only the math.", "tokens": [51305, 467, 311, 4476, 257, 5959, 2760, 2631, 4761, 281, 12828, 1314, 264, 15155, 293, 1856, 787, 264, 5221, 13, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15909168409264607, "compression_ratio": 1.576271186440678, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279237494645995e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 27762, "start": 300.88, "end": 305.36, "text": " So the first step is that the concept must be reconstructable from observational data.", "tokens": [51528, 407, 264, 700, 1823, 307, 300, 264, 3410, 1633, 312, 31499, 712, 490, 9951, 1478, 1412, 13, 51752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15909168409264607, "compression_ratio": 1.576271186440678, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279237494645995e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 27762, "start": 305.78000000000003, "end": 306.72, "text": " Meaning what, exactly?", "tokens": [51773, 19948, 437, 11, 2293, 30, 51820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15909168409264607, "compression_ratio": 1.576271186440678, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279237494645995e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 30672, "start": 306.72, "end": 317.32000000000005, "text": " Meaning there has to be a precise, mechanical procedure that recovers the quantity from raw data, so that anyone else can run the procedure and get the exact same values, no magic black boxes.", "tokens": [50365, 19948, 456, 575, 281, 312, 257, 13600, 11, 12070, 10747, 300, 7759, 840, 264, 11275, 490, 8936, 1412, 11, 370, 300, 2878, 1646, 393, 1190, 264, 10747, 293, 483, 264, 1900, 912, 4190, 11, 572, 5585, 2211, 9002, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07563319753427974, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359668611118372e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 30672, "start": 317.42, "end": 322.24, "text": " Okay. That feels like a solid baseline. But I imagine having just one formula isn't enough, right?", "tokens": [50900, 1033, 13, 663, 3417, 411, 257, 5100, 20518, 13, 583, 286, 3811, 1419, 445, 472, 8513, 1943, 380, 1547, 11, 558, 30, 51141], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07563319753427974, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359668611118372e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 30672, "start": 322.28000000000003, "end": 323.08000000000004, "text": " No. Not at all.", "tokens": [51143, 883, 13, 1726, 412, 439, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07563319753427974, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359668611118372e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 30672, "start": 323.28000000000003, "end": 329.46000000000004, "text": " Because if I invent a formula for, say, capacity, there are probably three other ways I could have mathematically defined it.", "tokens": [51193, 1436, 498, 286, 7962, 257, 8513, 337, 11, 584, 11, 6042, 11, 456, 366, 1391, 1045, 661, 2098, 286, 727, 362, 44003, 7642, 309, 13, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07563319753427974, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359668611118372e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 30672, "start": 329.78000000000003, "end": 332.72, "text": " It seems like you shouldn't just get to pick your favorite one and ignore the rest.", "tokens": [51518, 467, 2544, 411, 291, 4659, 380, 445, 483, 281, 1888, 428, 2954, 472, 293, 11200, 264, 1472, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07563319753427974, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359668611118372e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 33272, "start": 332.72, "end": 338.46000000000004, "text": " You've hit directly on step two. The construct must be compared against alternative definitions.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 600, 2045, 3838, 322, 1823, 732, 13, 440, 7690, 1633, 312, 5347, 1970, 8535, 21988, 13, 50652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09621987342834473, "compression_ratio": 1.5568181818181819, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 33272, "start": 338.8, "end": 339.34000000000003, "text": " Oh, okay.", "tokens": [50669, 876, 11, 1392, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09621987342834473, "compression_ratio": 1.5568181818181819, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 33272, "start": 339.42, "end": 347.82000000000005, "text": " If a concept can be formalized in multiple reasonable ways, you can't just select your favorite by fiat or wait to see which one makes your data look best.", "tokens": [50700, 759, 257, 3410, 393, 312, 9860, 1602, 294, 3866, 10585, 2098, 11, 291, 393, 380, 445, 3048, 428, 2954, 538, 283, 7676, 420, 1699, 281, 536, 597, 472, 1669, 428, 1412, 574, 1151, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09621987342834473, "compression_ratio": 1.5568181818181819, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 33272, "start": 348.06, "end": 350.64000000000004, "text": " You have to put them in the arena and test them against each other.", "tokens": [51132, 509, 362, 281, 829, 552, 294, 264, 18451, 293, 1500, 552, 1970, 1184, 661, 13, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09621987342834473, "compression_ratio": 1.5568181818181819, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 33272, "start": 350.90000000000003, "end": 355.16, "text": " Bring your own competition to the match. I like that. But what about messy data?", "tokens": [51274, 12842, 428, 1065, 6211, 281, 264, 2995, 13, 286, 411, 300, 13, 583, 437, 466, 16191, 1412, 30, 51487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09621987342834473, "compression_ratio": 1.5568181818181819, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 35516, "start": 355.16, "end": 356.14000000000004, "text": " What do you mean?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 360, 291, 914, 30, 50414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10226744413375854, "compression_ratio": 1.7408637873754154, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305370902954363e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 35516, "start": 356.32000000000005, "end": 363.96000000000004, "text": " Like if I have a metric that works perfectly when I'm looking at a micro level, but the moment I zoom out on the data, the metric completely breaks down.", "tokens": [50423, 1743, 498, 286, 362, 257, 20678, 300, 1985, 6239, 562, 286, 478, 1237, 412, 257, 4532, 1496, 11, 457, 264, 1623, 286, 8863, 484, 322, 264, 1412, 11, 264, 20678, 2584, 9857, 760, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10226744413375854, "compression_ratio": 1.7408637873754154, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305370902954363e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 35516, "start": 364.48, "end": 366.12, "text": " Does that mean the concept wasn't real?", "tokens": [50831, 4402, 300, 914, 264, 3410, 2067, 380, 957, 30, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10226744413375854, "compression_ratio": 1.7408637873754154, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305370902954363e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 35516, "start": 366.32000000000005, "end": 374.88, "text": " That brings us perfectly to step three, which is stability. The construct must be stable across what the paper calls nuisance parameters.", "tokens": [50923, 663, 5607, 505, 6239, 281, 1823, 1045, 11, 597, 307, 11826, 13, 440, 7690, 1633, 312, 8351, 2108, 437, 264, 3035, 5498, 3822, 46852, 9834, 13, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10226744413375854, "compression_ratio": 1.7408637873754154, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305370902954363e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 35516, "start": 375.14000000000004, "end": 375.86, "text": " Nuisance parameters.", "tokens": [51364, 426, 8479, 719, 9834, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10226744413375854, "compression_ratio": 1.7408637873754154, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305370902954363e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 35516, "start": 375.92, "end": 380.20000000000005, "text": " Yeah. And a great example of a nuisance parameter is the coarse graining scale.", "tokens": [51403, 865, 13, 400, 257, 869, 1365, 295, 257, 3822, 46852, 13075, 307, 264, 39312, 1295, 1760, 4373, 13, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10226744413375854, "compression_ratio": 1.7408637873754154, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305370902954363e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 35516, "start": 380.34000000000003, "end": 383.24, "text": " Okay. Let's define coarse graining scale for the listener really quickly.", "tokens": [51624, 1033, 13, 961, 311, 6964, 39312, 1295, 1760, 4373, 337, 264, 31569, 534, 2661, 13, 51769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10226744413375854, "compression_ratio": 1.7408637873754154, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305370902954363e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 38324, "start": 383.24, "end": 387.88, "text": " Sure. Think of it like zooming in or out on a digital photograph.", "tokens": [50365, 4894, 13, 6557, 295, 309, 411, 48226, 294, 420, 484, 322, 257, 4562, 8348, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11436110529406317, "compression_ratio": 1.547945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127071687284777e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 38324, "start": 388.3, "end": 388.52, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50618, 1033, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11436110529406317, "compression_ratio": 1.547945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127071687284777e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 38324, "start": 388.62, "end": 397.34000000000003, "text": " If you zoom all the way in, you see individual pixels. If you zoom out, those pixels average together into a continuous shape.", "tokens": [50634, 759, 291, 8863, 439, 264, 636, 294, 11, 291, 536, 2609, 18668, 13, 759, 291, 8863, 484, 11, 729, 18668, 4274, 1214, 666, 257, 10957, 3909, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11436110529406317, "compression_ratio": 1.547945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127071687284777e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 38324, "start": 397.44, "end": 398.2, "text": " Right. It gets blurry.", "tokens": [51075, 1779, 13, 467, 2170, 37644, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11436110529406317, "compression_ratio": 1.547945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127071687284777e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 38324, "start": 398.5, "end": 404.88, "text": " Exactly. In physics, coarse graining is how much you blur the microscopic details to look at the macroscopic picture.", "tokens": [51128, 7587, 13, 682, 10649, 11, 39312, 1295, 1760, 307, 577, 709, 291, 14257, 264, 47897, 4365, 281, 574, 412, 264, 7912, 38006, 299, 3036, 13, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11436110529406317, "compression_ratio": 1.547945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127071687284777e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 40488, "start": 404.88, "end": 416.84, "text": " So, Flixian argues that if your groundbreaking new metric completely disappears just because you tweaked the coarse graining scale slightly, it's not a fundamental physical property.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 3235, 970, 952, 38218, 300, 498, 428, 42491, 777, 20678, 2584, 25527, 445, 570, 291, 6986, 7301, 264, 39312, 1295, 1760, 4373, 4748, 11, 309, 311, 406, 257, 8088, 4001, 4707, 13, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19688322691790824, "compression_ratio": 1.5283687943262412, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776330336917608e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 40488, "start": 416.98, "end": 417.48, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [50970, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19688322691790824, "compression_ratio": 1.5283687943262412, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776330336917608e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 40488, "start": 417.6, "end": 420.24, "text": " Yeah. It's just an artifact of how you process the data.", "tokens": [51001, 865, 13, 467, 311, 445, 364, 34806, 295, 577, 291, 1399, 264, 1412, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19688322691790824, "compression_ratio": 1.5283687943262412, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776330336917608e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 40488, "start": 420.38, "end": 421.42, "text": " That is so rigorous.", "tokens": [51140, 663, 307, 370, 29882, 13, 51192], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19688322691790824, "compression_ratio": 1.5283687943262412, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776330336917608e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 40488, "start": 421.82, "end": 422.0, "text": " Mm-hmm.", "tokens": [51212, 8266, 12, 10250, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19688322691790824, "compression_ratio": 1.5283687943262412, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776330336917608e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 40488, "start": 422.08, "end": 423.44, "text": " Okay. And what's the final hurdle?", "tokens": [51225, 1033, 13, 400, 437, 311, 264, 2572, 47423, 30, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19688322691790824, "compression_ratio": 1.5283687943262412, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776330336917608e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 40488, "start": 424.1, "end": 424.68, "text": " Step four.", "tokens": [51326, 5470, 1451, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19688322691790824, "compression_ratio": 1.5283687943262412, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776330336917608e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 40488, "start": 424.94, "end": 426.82, "text": " Step four is the ultimate filter.", "tokens": [51368, 5470, 1451, 307, 264, 9705, 6608, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19688322691790824, "compression_ratio": 1.5283687943262412, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776330336917608e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 40488, "start": 427.32, "end": 432.52, "text": " The new construct must improve prediction beyond a pre-existing baseline.", "tokens": [51487, 440, 777, 7690, 1633, 3470, 17630, 4399, 257, 659, 12, 36447, 20518, 13, 51747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19688322691790824, "compression_ratio": 1.5283687943262412, "no_speech_prob": 1.3776330336917608e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 43252, "start": 432.52, "end": 434.44, "text": " Meaning it has to actually be useful.", "tokens": [50365, 19948, 309, 575, 281, 767, 312, 4420, 13, 50461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0914790841597545, "compression_ratio": 1.5188679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 1.694140162357416e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 43252, "start": 434.74, "end": 445.15999999999997, "text": " Right. It can't just fit the data it was calibrated on. It must actually predict withheld future data better than the strongest, most boring conventional metrics we already have lying around.", "tokens": [50476, 1779, 13, 467, 393, 380, 445, 3318, 264, 1412, 309, 390, 21583, 5468, 322, 13, 467, 1633, 767, 6069, 365, 23504, 2027, 1412, 1101, 813, 264, 16595, 11, 881, 9989, 16011, 16367, 321, 1217, 362, 8493, 926, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0914790841597545, "compression_ratio": 1.5188679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 1.694140162357416e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 43252, "start": 445.65999999999997, "end": 450.12, "text": " Reconstruct, compare, stabilize, and predict. That is a brutal set of filters.", "tokens": [51022, 1300, 25279, 1757, 11, 6794, 11, 31870, 11, 293, 6069, 13, 663, 307, 257, 17878, 992, 295, 15995, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0914790841597545, "compression_ratio": 1.5188679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 1.694140162357416e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 43252, "start": 450.28, "end": 451.06, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51253, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0914790841597545, "compression_ratio": 1.5188679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 1.694140162357416e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 45106, "start": 451.06, "end": 456.64, "text": " But the thing that makes this deep dive so compelling is that the researcher didn't just write down these rules and walk away.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 551, 300, 1669, 341, 2452, 9192, 370, 20050, 307, 300, 264, 21751, 994, 380, 445, 2464, 760, 613, 4474, 293, 1792, 1314, 13, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12980237258108038, "compression_ratio": 1.6732283464566928, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359664475166905e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 45106, "start": 457.02, "end": 462.2, "text": " They actually applied this four-part test to a highly rigorous physical system.", "tokens": [50663, 814, 767, 6456, 341, 1451, 12, 6971, 1500, 281, 257, 5405, 29882, 4001, 1185, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12980237258108038, "compression_ratio": 1.6732283464566928, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359664475166905e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 45106, "start": 462.32, "end": 465.32, "text": " Yes. To see if their own theoretical construct could survive.", "tokens": [50928, 1079, 13, 1407, 536, 498, 641, 1065, 20864, 7690, 727, 7867, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12980237258108038, "compression_ratio": 1.6732283464566928, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359664475166905e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 45106, "start": 465.44, "end": 466.88, "text": " So let's get into the physics paper.", "tokens": [51084, 407, 718, 311, 483, 666, 264, 10649, 3035, 13, 51156], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12980237258108038, "compression_ratio": 1.6732283464566928, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359664475166905e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 45106, "start": 467.2, "end": 473.74, "text": " Yeah. The transition from the philosophy paper to the physics paper is where we see this methodology put into practice.", "tokens": [51172, 865, 13, 440, 6034, 490, 264, 10675, 3035, 281, 264, 10649, 3035, 307, 689, 321, 536, 341, 24850, 829, 666, 3124, 13, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12980237258108038, "compression_ratio": 1.6732283464566928, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359664475166905e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 47374, "start": 473.74, "end": 478.8, "text": " The test subject they chose is a system of active Brownian particles.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1500, 3983, 436, 5111, 307, 257, 1185, 295, 4967, 8030, 952, 10007, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144269204354501, "compression_ratio": 1.5430463576158941, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488006706477654e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 47374, "start": 479.18, "end": 479.24, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50637, 865, 13, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144269204354501, "compression_ratio": 1.5430463576158941, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488006706477654e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 47374, "start": 479.38, "end": 486.90000000000003, "text": " And these particles are undergoing something called motility-induced phase separation, which is often abbreviated as mityus.", "tokens": [50647, 400, 613, 10007, 366, 40033, 746, 1219, 2184, 1140, 12, 471, 41209, 5574, 14634, 11, 597, 307, 2049, 35839, 770, 382, 275, 507, 301, 13, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144269204354501, "compression_ratio": 1.5430463576158941, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488006706477654e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 47374, "start": 487.12, "end": 494.76, "text": " Mityus. Okay. For the listener, let's visualize this. Imagine a two-dimensional simulation filled with little circular disks.", "tokens": [51034, 376, 507, 301, 13, 1033, 13, 1171, 264, 31569, 11, 718, 311, 23273, 341, 13, 11739, 257, 732, 12, 18759, 16575, 6412, 365, 707, 16476, 41617, 13, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144269204354501, "compression_ratio": 1.5430463576158941, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488006706477654e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 47374, "start": 494.98, "end": 495.36, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51427, 1779, 13, 51446], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144269204354501, "compression_ratio": 1.5430463576158941, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488006706477654e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 47374, "start": 495.64, "end": 502.56, "text": " But they aren't just floating passively. They're active, meaning each disk has its own little internal engine propelling it forward.", "tokens": [51460, 583, 436, 3212, 380, 445, 12607, 1320, 3413, 13, 814, 434, 4967, 11, 3620, 1184, 12355, 575, 1080, 1065, 707, 6920, 2848, 25577, 2669, 309, 2128, 13, 51806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144269204354501, "compression_ratio": 1.5430463576158941, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488006706477654e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 50256, "start": 502.56, "end": 504.08, "text": " Like tiny bumper cars.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 5870, 23992, 5163, 13, 50441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11720777065195936, "compression_ratio": 1.5061728395061729, "no_speech_prob": 1.727917288418812e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 50256, "start": 504.46, "end": 507.72, "text": " Exactly. They're constantly moving around, bumping into each other.", "tokens": [50460, 7587, 13, 814, 434, 6460, 2684, 926, 11, 9961, 278, 666, 1184, 661, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11720777065195936, "compression_ratio": 1.5061728395061729, "no_speech_prob": 1.727917288418812e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 50256, "start": 508.12, "end": 512.98, "text": " And eventually, if you get enough of them in the same space, they cause a sort of microscopic traffic jam.", "tokens": [50643, 400, 4728, 11, 498, 291, 483, 1547, 295, 552, 294, 264, 912, 1901, 11, 436, 3082, 257, 1333, 295, 47897, 6419, 7872, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11720777065195936, "compression_ratio": 1.5061728395061729, "no_speech_prob": 1.727917288418812e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 50256, "start": 513.02, "end": 514.48, "text": " Yeah. They start crowding together.", "tokens": [50888, 865, 13, 814, 722, 6401, 3584, 1214, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11720777065195936, "compression_ratio": 1.5061728395061729, "no_speech_prob": 1.727917288418812e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 50256, "start": 514.66, "end": 519.08, "text": " They form these dense, solid-like clusters, separating themselves from the empty space.", "tokens": [50970, 814, 1254, 613, 18011, 11, 5100, 12, 4092, 23313, 11, 29279, 2969, 490, 264, 6707, 1901, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11720777065195936, "compression_ratio": 1.5061728395061729, "no_speech_prob": 1.727917288418812e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 50256, "start": 519.64, "end": 522.52, "text": " That specific clustering process is MIP-E-S.", "tokens": [51219, 663, 2685, 596, 48673, 1399, 307, 376, 9139, 12, 36, 12, 50, 13, 51363], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11720777065195936, "compression_ratio": 1.5061728395061729, "no_speech_prob": 1.727917288418812e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 52252, "start": 522.52, "end": 532.98, "text": " And the reason Flexion chose MIP-E-S as the testing ground is vital, it's because MIP-E-S is already incredibly well understood by existing kinetic and hydrodynamic theories.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 1778, 29208, 313, 5111, 376, 9139, 12, 36, 12, 50, 382, 264, 4997, 2727, 307, 11707, 11, 309, 311, 570, 376, 9139, 12, 36, 12, 50, 307, 1217, 6252, 731, 7320, 538, 6741, 27135, 293, 5796, 11452, 5216, 299, 13667, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1333983309634097, "compression_ratio": 1.6145038167938932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8973379724979145e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 52252, "start": 533.42, "end": 538.36, "text": " We already know exactly how particle density and collision rates drive this clustering.", "tokens": [50910, 492, 1217, 458, 2293, 577, 12359, 10305, 293, 24644, 6846, 3332, 341, 596, 48673, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1333983309634097, "compression_ratio": 1.6145038167938932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8973379724979145e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 52252, "start": 538.64, "end": 540.76, "text": " Right. So there is no mystery to solve here.", "tokens": [51171, 1779, 13, 407, 456, 307, 572, 11422, 281, 5039, 510, 13, 51277], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1333983309634097, "compression_ratio": 1.6145038167938932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8973379724979145e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 52252, "start": 541.02, "end": 541.4, "text": " Not at all.", "tokens": [51290, 1726, 412, 439, 13, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1333983309634097, "compression_ratio": 1.6145038167938932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8973379724979145e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 52252, "start": 541.46, "end": 542.54, "text": " And that is by design.", "tokens": [51312, 400, 300, 307, 538, 1715, 13, 51366], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1333983309634097, "compression_ratio": 1.6145038167938932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8973379724979145e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 52252, "start": 543.38, "end": 546.76, "text": " Flexion deliberately chose this because it constitutes a hard test.", "tokens": [51408, 29208, 313, 23506, 5111, 341, 570, 309, 44204, 257, 1152, 1500, 13, 51577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1333983309634097, "compression_ratio": 1.6145038167938932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8973379724979145e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 52252, "start": 546.92, "end": 547.52, "text": " A hard test.", "tokens": [51585, 316, 1152, 1500, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1333983309634097, "compression_ratio": 1.6145038167938932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8973379724979145e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 54752, "start": 547.52, "end": 550.6, "text": " Yeah. There is no explanatory vacuum to fill.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 821, 307, 572, 9045, 4745, 14224, 281, 2836, 13, 50519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14408760339441434, "compression_ratio": 1.4, "no_speech_prob": 2.1415649201911302e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 54752, "start": 551.46, "end": 558.96, "text": " When a scientific phenomenon is poorly understood, any new theory looks brilliant simply because there's no competition.", "tokens": [50562, 1133, 257, 8134, 14029, 307, 22271, 7320, 11, 604, 777, 5261, 1542, 10248, 2935, 570, 456, 311, 572, 6211, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14408760339441434, "compression_ratio": 1.4, "no_speech_prob": 2.1415649201911302e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 54752, "start": 559.36, "end": 562.98, "text": " Ah, right. It's easy to look like a genius in an empty room.", "tokens": [50957, 2438, 11, 558, 13, 467, 311, 1858, 281, 574, 411, 257, 14017, 294, 364, 6707, 1808, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14408760339441434, "compression_ratio": 1.4, "no_speech_prob": 2.1415649201911302e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 54752, "start": 563.04, "end": 567.8, "text": " Exactly. But here, massive, strong baselines already exist.", "tokens": [51141, 7587, 13, 583, 510, 11, 5994, 11, 2068, 987, 9173, 1217, 2514, 13, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14408760339441434, "compression_ratio": 1.4, "no_speech_prob": 2.1415649201911302e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 56780, "start": 567.8, "end": 576.56, "text": " So if a new theory about capacity or dissipation adds absolutely nothing to our ability to predict these clusters, it's highly informative.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 257, 777, 5261, 466, 6042, 420, 29544, 399, 10860, 3122, 1825, 281, 527, 3485, 281, 6069, 613, 23313, 11, 309, 311, 5405, 27759, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11161098641864324, "compression_ratio": 1.6346749226006192, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750126676304267e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 56780, "start": 577.06, "end": 579.88, "text": " It proves the new vocabulary didn't add predictive content.", "tokens": [50828, 467, 25019, 264, 777, 19864, 994, 380, 909, 35521, 2701, 13, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11161098641864324, "compression_ratio": 1.6346749226006192, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750126676304267e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 56780, "start": 580.02, "end": 585.9399999999999, "text": " Yes. Conversely, if it actually beats the existing density models, well, then it's an undeniable breakthrough.", "tokens": [50976, 1079, 13, 33247, 736, 11, 498, 309, 767, 16447, 264, 6741, 10305, 5245, 11, 731, 11, 550, 309, 311, 364, 674, 268, 9364, 22397, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11161098641864324, "compression_ratio": 1.6346749226006192, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750126676304267e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 56780, "start": 586.3, "end": 588.1999999999999, "text": " So they set the difficulty level to maximum.", "tokens": [51290, 407, 436, 992, 264, 10360, 1496, 281, 6674, 13, 51385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11161098641864324, "compression_ratio": 1.6346749226006192, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750126676304267e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 56780, "start": 588.3399999999999, "end": 588.74, "text": " They did.", "tokens": [51392, 814, 630, 13, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11161098641864324, "compression_ratio": 1.6346749226006192, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750126676304267e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 56780, "start": 589.18, "end": 596.9599999999999, "text": " And honoring step two of their own philosophical test to the rule that you must compare alternatives, the author didn't just test one generic version of capacity.", "tokens": [51434, 400, 38254, 1823, 732, 295, 641, 1065, 25066, 1500, 281, 264, 4978, 300, 291, 1633, 6794, 20478, 11, 264, 3793, 994, 380, 445, 1500, 472, 19577, 3037, 295, 6042, 13, 51823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11161098641864324, "compression_ratio": 1.6346749226006192, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750126676304267e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 59696, "start": 596.96, "end": 601.6, "text": " No, they built three competing mathematical operationalizations of it.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 11, 436, 3094, 1045, 15439, 18894, 16607, 14455, 295, 309, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15228622128265074, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011312063858197e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 59696, "start": 601.82, "end": 604.1600000000001, "text": " Just to see which, if any, held up.", "tokens": [50608, 1449, 281, 536, 597, 11, 498, 604, 11, 5167, 493, 13, 50725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15228622128265074, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011312063858197e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 59696, "start": 605.26, "end": 615.1600000000001, "text": " And looking at why they chose these three is fascinating because they represent totally different philosophical interpretations of what capacity even means in a physical space.", "tokens": [50780, 400, 1237, 412, 983, 436, 5111, 613, 1045, 307, 10343, 570, 436, 2906, 3879, 819, 25066, 37547, 295, 437, 6042, 754, 1355, 294, 257, 4001, 1901, 13, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15228622128265074, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011312063858197e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 59696, "start": 615.36, "end": 617.6, "text": " So true. Let's walk through them. What was the first one?", "tokens": [51285, 407, 2074, 13, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 552, 13, 708, 390, 264, 700, 472, 30, 51397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15228622128265074, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011312063858197e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 59696, "start": 617.9200000000001, "end": 619.76, "text": " The first was imposed capacity.", "tokens": [51413, 440, 700, 390, 26491, 6042, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15228622128265074, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011312063858197e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 59696, "start": 620.34, "end": 623.46, "text": " You can think of this as the raw potential built into the particle.", "tokens": [51534, 509, 393, 519, 295, 341, 382, 264, 8936, 3995, 3094, 666, 264, 12359, 13, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15228622128265074, "compression_ratio": 1.6273062730627306, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011312063858197e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 62346, "start": 623.46, "end": 630.4200000000001, "text": " It's essentially the propulsion speed limit assigned to the disk's internal engine, regardless of what it's bumping into.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 4476, 264, 49375, 3073, 4948, 13279, 281, 264, 12355, 311, 6920, 2848, 11, 10060, 295, 437, 309, 311, 9961, 278, 666, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16549580768474098, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.4607684636555596e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 62346, "start": 630.6600000000001, "end": 631.2800000000001, "text": " Okay. Makes sense.", "tokens": [50725, 1033, 13, 25245, 2020, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16549580768474098, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.4607684636555596e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 62346, "start": 631.7800000000001, "end": 635.5, "text": " But then they tested a second version, which was assigned realized capacity.", "tokens": [50781, 583, 550, 436, 8246, 257, 1150, 3037, 11, 597, 390, 13279, 5334, 6042, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16549580768474098, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.4607684636555596e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 62346, "start": 635.6600000000001, "end": 635.94, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50975, 1779, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16549580768474098, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.4607684636555596e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 62346, "start": 636.2, "end": 639.3000000000001, "text": " This one measures the actual kinetic reality of the particle.", "tokens": [51002, 639, 472, 8000, 264, 3539, 27135, 4103, 295, 264, 12359, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16549580768474098, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.4607684636555596e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 62346, "start": 639.96, "end": 645.5400000000001, "text": " It looks at the alignment between where the particle is trying to go and its actual true velocity.", "tokens": [51190, 467, 1542, 412, 264, 18515, 1296, 689, 264, 12359, 307, 1382, 281, 352, 293, 1080, 3539, 2074, 9269, 13, 51469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16549580768474098, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.4607684636555596e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 62346, "start": 645.88, "end": 649.1600000000001, "text": " And because these particles crash into each other, that matters.", "tokens": [51486, 400, 570, 613, 10007, 8252, 666, 1184, 661, 11, 300, 7001, 13, 51650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16549580768474098, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 1.4607684636555596e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 64916, "start": 649.16, "end": 655.64, "text": " Exactly. A particle might be pushing forward with all its might, but getting physically shoved backward by a denser cluster.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 316, 12359, 1062, 312, 7380, 2128, 365, 439, 1080, 1062, 11, 457, 1242, 9762, 2223, 937, 23897, 538, 257, 24505, 260, 13630, 13, 50689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13240194939947747, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.4547616583593381e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 64916, "start": 656.28, "end": 660.04, "text": " In that case, its realized capacity drops into negative numbers.", "tokens": [50721, 682, 300, 1389, 11, 1080, 5334, 6042, 11438, 666, 3671, 3547, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13240194939947747, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.4547616583593381e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 64916, "start": 660.2199999999999, "end": 663.56, "text": " Which is a very different interpretation than just looking at the internal engine.", "tokens": [50918, 3013, 307, 257, 588, 819, 14174, 813, 445, 1237, 412, 264, 6920, 2848, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13240194939947747, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.4547616583593381e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 64916, "start": 663.9, "end": 665.38, "text": " A completely different philosophy.", "tokens": [51102, 316, 2584, 819, 10675, 13, 51176], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13240194939947747, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.4547616583593381e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 64916, "start": 666.38, "end": 669.18, "text": " And the third variant was usable forward capacity.", "tokens": [51226, 400, 264, 2636, 17501, 390, 29975, 2128, 6042, 13, 51366], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13240194939947747, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.4547616583593381e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 66918, "start": 669.18, "end": 674.16, "text": " This one takes the realized capacity, but strictly ignores the negative numbers.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 472, 2516, 264, 5334, 6042, 11, 457, 20792, 5335, 2706, 264, 3671, 3547, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16501813185842415, "compression_ratio": 1.583617747440273, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722219754056964e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 66918, "start": 674.5999999999999, "end": 674.9799999999999, "text": " Oh, interesting.", "tokens": [50636, 876, 11, 1880, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16501813185842415, "compression_ratio": 1.583617747440273, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722219754056964e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 66918, "start": 675.2399999999999, "end": 678.12, "text": " Yeah. It only counts the positive forward progress being made.", "tokens": [50668, 865, 13, 467, 787, 14893, 264, 3353, 2128, 4205, 885, 1027, 13, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16501813185842415, "compression_ratio": 1.583617747440273, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722219754056964e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 66918, "start": 678.3599999999999, "end": 684.62, "text": " It's essentially asking, how much productive work is this particle actually achieving right now?", "tokens": [50824, 467, 311, 4476, 3365, 11, 577, 709, 13304, 589, 307, 341, 12359, 767, 19626, 558, 586, 30, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16501813185842415, "compression_ratio": 1.583617747440273, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722219754056964e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 66918, "start": 684.92, "end": 689.0799999999999, "text": " So by testing all three, the author honors their own rule.", "tokens": [51152, 407, 538, 4997, 439, 1045, 11, 264, 3793, 26884, 641, 1065, 4978, 13, 51360], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16501813185842415, "compression_ratio": 1.583617747440273, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722219754056964e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 66918, "start": 689.3399999999999, "end": 692.18, "text": " You don't just pick the definition that sounds best in your head.", "tokens": [51373, 509, 500, 380, 445, 1888, 264, 7123, 300, 3263, 1151, 294, 428, 1378, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16501813185842415, "compression_ratio": 1.583617747440273, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722219754056964e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 66918, "start": 692.38, "end": 692.56, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51525, 865, 13, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16501813185842415, "compression_ratio": 1.583617747440273, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722219754056964e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 66918, "start": 692.5999999999999, "end": 694.38, "text": " You make them fight it out in the simulation.", "tokens": [51536, 509, 652, 552, 2092, 309, 484, 294, 264, 16575, 13, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16501813185842415, "compression_ratio": 1.583617747440273, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722219754056964e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 66918, "start": 694.5799999999999, "end": 696.3599999999999, "text": " Exactly. Let the math decide.", "tokens": [51635, 7587, 13, 961, 264, 5221, 4536, 13, 51724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16501813185842415, "compression_ratio": 1.583617747440273, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722219754056964e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 69636, "start": 696.36, "end": 700.98, "text": " And they also brought that same rigor to a second concept, which was dissipation.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 436, 611, 3038, 300, 912, 42191, 281, 257, 1150, 3410, 11, 597, 390, 29544, 399, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13123392640498646, "compression_ratio": 1.662295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.4439677752109414e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 69636, "start": 701.64, "end": 707.0, "text": " Drawing from stochastic thermodynamics, they threw in two different estimators for dissipation.", "tokens": [50629, 20386, 278, 490, 342, 8997, 2750, 8810, 35483, 11, 436, 11918, 294, 732, 819, 8017, 3391, 337, 29544, 399, 13, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13123392640498646, "compression_ratio": 1.662295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.4439677752109414e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 69636, "start": 707.5, "end": 711.0600000000001, "text": " Okay. Stochastic thermodynamics sounds extremely intimidating.", "tokens": [50922, 1033, 13, 745, 8997, 2750, 8810, 35483, 3263, 4664, 29714, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13123392640498646, "compression_ratio": 1.662295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.4439677752109414e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 69636, "start": 711.34, "end": 713.02, "text": " What does that actually mean in this context?", "tokens": [51114, 708, 775, 300, 767, 914, 294, 341, 4319, 30, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13123392640498646, "compression_ratio": 1.662295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.4439677752109414e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 69636, "start": 713.42, "end": 719.6, "text": " It's basically the physics of microscopic systems where heat, energy transfer, and randomness all interact.", "tokens": [51218, 467, 311, 1936, 264, 10649, 295, 47897, 3652, 689, 3738, 11, 2281, 5003, 11, 293, 4974, 1287, 439, 4648, 13, 51527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13123392640498646, "compression_ratio": 1.662295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.4439677752109414e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 69636, "start": 719.76, "end": 720.0, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51535, 1033, 13, 51547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13123392640498646, "compression_ratio": 1.662295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.4439677752109414e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 69636, "start": 720.2, "end": 724.46, "text": " When you're dealing with tiny particles, they're constantly getting kicked around by random thermal noise.", "tokens": [51557, 1133, 291, 434, 6260, 365, 5870, 10007, 11, 436, 434, 6460, 1242, 14609, 926, 538, 4974, 15070, 5658, 13, 51770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13123392640498646, "compression_ratio": 1.662295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.4439677752109414e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 72446, "start": 724.46, "end": 728.46, "text": " Because of that randomness, energy transfer isn't perfectly deterministic.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 295, 300, 4974, 1287, 11, 2281, 5003, 1943, 380, 6239, 15957, 3142, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1560616890589396, "compression_ratio": 1.5043859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837540918133385e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 72446, "start": 728.9000000000001, "end": 730.5600000000001, "text": " It relies heavily on probability.", "tokens": [50587, 467, 30910, 10950, 322, 8482, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1560616890589396, "compression_ratio": 1.5043859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837540918133385e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 72446, "start": 731.2, "end": 745.74, "text": " So by pulling estimators from this field, Flixmein was essentially building an entire theoretical buffet of advanced metrics just to see if any single one of these complex dishes could beat the standard boring model of simple density.", "tokens": [50702, 407, 538, 8407, 8017, 3391, 490, 341, 2519, 11, 3235, 970, 1398, 259, 390, 4476, 2390, 364, 2302, 20864, 42904, 295, 7339, 16367, 445, 281, 536, 498, 604, 2167, 472, 295, 613, 3997, 10814, 727, 4224, 264, 3832, 9989, 2316, 295, 2199, 10305, 13, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1560616890589396, "compression_ratio": 1.5043859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837540918133385e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 74574, "start": 745.74, "end": 748.58, "text": " It's the ultimate defense against confirmation bias.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 264, 9705, 7654, 1970, 21871, 12577, 13, 50507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.141161650942083, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.53053221138566e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 74574, "start": 748.72, "end": 749.54, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [50514, 467, 534, 307, 13, 50555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.141161650942083, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.53053221138566e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 74574, "start": 749.66, "end": 751.74, "text": " But here's where the story gets kind of crazy.", "tokens": [50561, 583, 510, 311, 689, 264, 1657, 2170, 733, 295, 3219, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.141161650942083, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.53053221138566e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 74574, "start": 752.26, "end": 761.9, "text": " Before the researcher could even get to the grand finale of testing all these complex metrics, this obsessively rigorous methodology caught two massive traps.", "tokens": [50691, 4546, 264, 21751, 727, 754, 483, 281, 264, 2697, 23510, 295, 4997, 439, 613, 3997, 16367, 11, 341, 35803, 3413, 29882, 24850, 5415, 732, 5994, 24173, 13, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.141161650942083, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.53053221138566e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 74574, "start": 762.1, "end": 764.08, "text": " Oh, yeah. These bugs were wild.", "tokens": [51183, 876, 11, 1338, 13, 1981, 15120, 645, 4868, 13, 51282], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.141161650942083, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.53053221138566e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 74574, "start": 764.3, "end": 770.16, "text": " If a lesser study had been run without this level of paranoia, these traps would have completely ruined the results.", "tokens": [51293, 759, 257, 22043, 2979, 632, 668, 1190, 1553, 341, 1496, 295, 31416, 654, 11, 613, 24173, 576, 362, 2584, 17013, 264, 3542, 13, 51586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.141161650942083, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.53053221138566e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 74574, "start": 771.04, "end": 775.32, "text": " Seeing the scientific method catch its own mistakes behind the scenes is just incredible.", "tokens": [51630, 19703, 264, 8134, 3170, 3745, 1080, 1065, 8038, 2261, 264, 8026, 307, 445, 4651, 13, 51844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.141161650942083, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.53053221138566e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 77532, "start": 775.32, "end": 778.88, "text": " So the first trap they caught was a fundamental measurement artifact.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 700, 11487, 436, 5415, 390, 257, 8088, 13160, 34806, 13, 50543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391337364912033, "compression_ratio": 1.5884244372990353, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967531759296995e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 77532, "start": 779.1800000000001, "end": 780.22, "text": " Okay. Explain that one.", "tokens": [50558, 1033, 13, 39574, 300, 472, 13, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391337364912033, "compression_ratio": 1.5884244372990353, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967531759296995e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 77532, "start": 780.2800000000001, "end": 787.38, "text": " Well, initially, to figure out when the MIPS clustering had actually begun, they used a very common order parameter called FMAX.", "tokens": [50613, 1042, 11, 9105, 11, 281, 2573, 484, 562, 264, 13696, 6273, 596, 48673, 632, 767, 16009, 11, 436, 1143, 257, 588, 2689, 1668, 13075, 1219, 479, 9998, 55, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391337364912033, "compression_ratio": 1.5884244372990353, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967531759296995e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 77532, "start": 787.5200000000001, "end": 787.7600000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50975, 1779, 13, 50987], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391337364912033, "compression_ratio": 1.5884244372990353, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967531759296995e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 77532, "start": 787.94, "end": 790.34, "text": " This stands for the Particle Contact Cluster Fraction.", "tokens": [50996, 639, 7382, 337, 264, 4100, 3520, 30683, 2033, 8393, 1526, 2894, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391337364912033, "compression_ratio": 1.5884244372990353, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967531759296995e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 77532, "start": 790.6800000000001, "end": 794.08, "text": " It computes clustering based on a fixed contact distance cutoff.", "tokens": [51133, 467, 715, 1819, 596, 48673, 2361, 322, 257, 6806, 3385, 4560, 1723, 4506, 13, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391337364912033, "compression_ratio": 1.5884244372990353, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967531759296995e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 77532, "start": 794.44, "end": 796.22, "text": " That sounds perfectly logical.", "tokens": [51321, 663, 3263, 6239, 14978, 13, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391337364912033, "compression_ratio": 1.5884244372990353, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967531759296995e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 77532, "start": 796.48, "end": 799.5600000000001, "text": " Like, if the disks are close enough to touch, they're in a cluster.", "tokens": [51423, 1743, 11, 498, 264, 41617, 366, 1998, 1547, 281, 2557, 11, 436, 434, 294, 257, 13630, 13, 51577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391337364912033, "compression_ratio": 1.5884244372990353, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967531759296995e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 77532, "start": 800.08, "end": 801.8000000000001, "text": " If they aren't, they're just floating freely.", "tokens": [51603, 759, 436, 3212, 380, 11, 436, 434, 445, 12607, 16433, 13, 51689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1391337364912033, "compression_ratio": 1.5884244372990353, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967531759296995e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 80180, "start": 801.8, "end": 805.9799999999999, "text": " It sounds perfectly logical until, well, until you test its boundary.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 3263, 6239, 14978, 1826, 11, 731, 11, 1826, 291, 1500, 1080, 12866, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11242537749441046, "compression_ratio": 1.4190476190476191, "no_speech_prob": 1.920110988609669e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 80180, "start": 806.62, "end": 816.76, "text": " When Flixian ran a validity scan at a high packing fraction, this FMAX metric read exactly 1.000 at time zero.", "tokens": [50606, 1133, 3235, 970, 952, 5872, 257, 40943, 11049, 412, 257, 1090, 20815, 14135, 11, 341, 479, 9998, 55, 20678, 1401, 2293, 502, 13, 1360, 412, 565, 4018, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11242537749441046, "compression_ratio": 1.4190476190476191, "no_speech_prob": 1.920110988609669e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 80180, "start": 816.9, "end": 823.4799999999999, "text": " Wait. It was claiming 100% clustering before a single frame of dynamics had even occurred in the simulation.", "tokens": [51120, 3802, 13, 467, 390, 19232, 2319, 4, 596, 48673, 949, 257, 2167, 3920, 295, 15679, 632, 754, 11068, 294, 264, 16575, 13, 51449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11242537749441046, "compression_ratio": 1.4190476190476191, "no_speech_prob": 1.920110988609669e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 80180, "start": 823.74, "end": 824.18, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51462, 7587, 13, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11242537749441046, "compression_ratio": 1.4190476190476191, "no_speech_prob": 1.920110988609669e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 82418, "start": 824.18, "end": 828.0799999999999, "text": " Oh, wow. We should probably clarify what packing fraction means here.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 492, 820, 1391, 17594, 437, 20815, 14135, 1355, 510, 13, 50560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09115243444637376, "compression_ratio": 1.5914396887159532, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758287245220328e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 82418, "start": 828.4, "end": 832.88, "text": " It's just the percentage of the two-dimensional floor space that is physically covered by the disks, right?", "tokens": [50576, 467, 311, 445, 264, 9668, 295, 264, 732, 12, 18759, 4123, 1901, 300, 307, 9762, 5343, 538, 264, 41617, 11, 558, 30, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09115243444637376, "compression_ratio": 1.5914396887159532, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758287245220328e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 82418, "start": 832.9599999999999, "end": 838.26, "text": " That's right. So if you have a high packing fraction, say 80% of the space is covered in disks,", "tokens": [50804, 663, 311, 558, 13, 407, 498, 291, 362, 257, 1090, 20815, 14135, 11, 584, 4688, 4, 295, 264, 1901, 307, 5343, 294, 41617, 11, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09115243444637376, "compression_ratio": 1.5914396887159532, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758287245220328e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 82418, "start": 838.64, "end": 844.9, "text": " the typical space between any two particles is already below that fixed contact cutoff just based on geometry.", "tokens": [51088, 264, 7476, 1901, 1296, 604, 732, 10007, 307, 1217, 2507, 300, 6806, 3385, 1723, 4506, 445, 2361, 322, 18426, 13, 51401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09115243444637376, "compression_ratio": 1.5914396887159532, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758287245220328e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 82418, "start": 845.12, "end": 845.9599999999999, "text": " Because it's so crowded.", "tokens": [51412, 1436, 309, 311, 370, 21634, 13, 51454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09115243444637376, "compression_ratio": 1.5914396887159532, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758287245220328e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 84596, "start": 845.96, "end": 853.5600000000001, "text": " Yes. Any configuration, even if it's perfectly mixed and totally random, trivially satisfies the criterion for clustering.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 2639, 11694, 11, 754, 498, 309, 311, 6239, 7467, 293, 3879, 4974, 11, 1376, 85, 2270, 44271, 264, 46691, 337, 596, 48673, 13, 50745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10463847002936798, "compression_ratio": 1.6293706293706294, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484408239467174e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 84596, "start": 854.14, "end": 857.6600000000001, "text": " It was a geometric artifact disguised as a dynamical measurement.", "tokens": [50774, 467, 390, 257, 33246, 34806, 23333, 2640, 382, 257, 5999, 804, 13160, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10463847002936798, "compression_ratio": 1.6293706293706294, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484408239467174e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 84596, "start": 858.02, "end": 861.4000000000001, "text": " So if they hadn't been so paranoid about validating their baselines,", "tokens": [50968, 407, 498, 436, 8782, 380, 668, 370, 43948, 466, 7363, 990, 641, 987, 9173, 11, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10463847002936798, "compression_ratio": 1.6293706293706294, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484408239467174e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 84596, "start": 861.88, "end": 867.36, "text": " they could have easily published a paper claiming their new capacity metric perfectly predicted clustering.", "tokens": [51161, 436, 727, 362, 3612, 6572, 257, 3035, 19232, 641, 777, 6042, 20678, 6239, 19147, 596, 48673, 13, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10463847002936798, "compression_ratio": 1.6293706293706294, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484408239467174e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 84596, "start": 867.5400000000001, "end": 868.1800000000001, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [51444, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10463847002936798, "compression_ratio": 1.6293706293706294, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484408239467174e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 84596, "start": 868.38, "end": 871.34, "text": " When in reality, they were just predicting that the room was mathematically crowded.", "tokens": [51486, 1133, 294, 4103, 11, 436, 645, 445, 32884, 300, 264, 1808, 390, 44003, 21634, 13, 51634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10463847002936798, "compression_ratio": 1.6293706293706294, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484408239467174e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 87134, "start": 871.34, "end": 876.0400000000001, "text": " A less rigorous study absolutely would have published that artifact as a finding.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 1570, 29882, 2979, 3122, 576, 362, 6572, 300, 34806, 382, 257, 5006, 13, 50600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15256029531496382, "compression_ratio": 1.6619217081850535, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552927005834215e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 87134, "start": 876.6, "end": 882.5600000000001, "text": " But Fliction caught it, they discarded the metric, and they built a composite of relative density domain indicators.", "tokens": [50628, 583, 3235, 4105, 5415, 309, 11, 436, 45469, 264, 20678, 11, 293, 436, 3094, 257, 25557, 295, 4972, 10305, 9274, 22176, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15256029531496382, "compression_ratio": 1.6619217081850535, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552927005834215e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 87134, "start": 882.72, "end": 883.96, "text": " Okay, so how did that fix it?", "tokens": [50934, 1033, 11, 370, 577, 630, 300, 3191, 309, 30, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15256029531496382, "compression_ratio": 1.6619217081850535, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552927005834215e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 87134, "start": 884.44, "end": 890.0, "text": " They defined the clustering thresholds relative to each snapshot's own average density.", "tokens": [51020, 814, 7642, 264, 596, 48673, 14678, 82, 4972, 281, 1184, 30163, 311, 1065, 4274, 10305, 13, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15256029531496382, "compression_ratio": 1.6619217081850535, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552927005834215e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 87134, "start": 890.38, "end": 894.5600000000001, "text": " That way, a high packing fraction alone could never trigger a false positive.", "tokens": [51317, 663, 636, 11, 257, 1090, 20815, 14135, 3312, 727, 1128, 7875, 257, 7908, 3353, 13, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15256029531496382, "compression_ratio": 1.6619217081850535, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552927005834215e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 87134, "start": 894.74, "end": 895.72, "text": " That is so smart.", "tokens": [51535, 663, 307, 370, 4069, 13, 51584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15256029531496382, "compression_ratio": 1.6619217081850535, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552927005834215e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 87134, "start": 896.4000000000001, "end": 898.44, "text": " Okay, so that was error one, the measurement artifact.", "tokens": [51618, 1033, 11, 370, 300, 390, 6713, 472, 11, 264, 13160, 34806, 13, 51720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15256029531496382, "compression_ratio": 1.6619217081850535, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552927005834215e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 89844, "start": 898.44, "end": 902.1600000000001, "text": " But error two is arguably even wilder.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 6713, 732, 307, 26771, 754, 4868, 260, 13, 50551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15011848593657873, "compression_ratio": 1.6900369003690037, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482885798780767e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 89844, "start": 902.36, "end": 902.98, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [50561, 467, 534, 307, 13, 50592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15011848593657873, "compression_ratio": 1.6900369003690037, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482885798780767e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 89844, "start": 903.2, "end": 904.7600000000001, "text": " It was a causal intervention bug.", "tokens": [50603, 467, 390, 257, 38755, 13176, 7426, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15011848593657873, "compression_ratio": 1.6900369003690037, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482885798780767e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 89844, "start": 905.32, "end": 911.0200000000001, "text": " They built an intervention framework to see if manually changing the activity in a specific region of the simulation", "tokens": [50709, 814, 3094, 364, 13176, 8388, 281, 536, 498, 16945, 4473, 264, 5191, 294, 257, 2685, 4458, 295, 264, 16575, 50994], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15011848593657873, "compression_ratio": 1.6900369003690037, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482885798780767e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 89844, "start": 911.0200000000001, "end": 913.0200000000001, "text": " changed the clustering behavior.", "tokens": [50994, 3105, 264, 596, 48673, 5223, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15011848593657873, "compression_ratio": 1.6900369003690037, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482885798780767e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 89844, "start": 913.5200000000001, "end": 916.1, "text": " But they ran into a massive logic bug with the timing.", "tokens": [51119, 583, 436, 5872, 666, 257, 5994, 9952, 7426, 365, 264, 10822, 13, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15011848593657873, "compression_ratio": 1.6900369003690037, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482885798780767e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 89844, "start": 916.4000000000001, "end": 920.0, "text": " Yeah, so the simulation was designed to evaluate the intervention window.", "tokens": [51263, 865, 11, 370, 264, 16575, 390, 4761, 281, 13059, 264, 13176, 4910, 13, 51443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15011848593657873, "compression_ratio": 1.6900369003690037, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482885798780767e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 89844, "start": 920.48, "end": 926.4200000000001, "text": " For example, applying a pulse of elevated speed to the particles for exactly two time units.", "tokens": [51467, 1171, 1365, 11, 9275, 257, 17709, 295, 23457, 3073, 281, 264, 10007, 337, 2293, 732, 565, 6815, 13, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15011848593657873, "compression_ratio": 1.6900369003690037, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482885798780767e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 92642, "start": 926.42, "end": 929.7199999999999, "text": " This was supposed to be relative to the start of the experiment.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 390, 3442, 281, 312, 4972, 281, 264, 722, 295, 264, 5120, 13, 50530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14328702779916616, "compression_ratio": 1.5829145728643217, "no_speech_prob": 1.996596464548528e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 92642, "start": 930.3, "end": 937.1999999999999, "text": " But an early implementation of the code was evaluating the window against the simulation's absolute internal clock.", "tokens": [50559, 583, 364, 2440, 11420, 295, 264, 3089, 390, 27479, 264, 4910, 1970, 264, 16575, 311, 8236, 6920, 7830, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14328702779916616, "compression_ratio": 1.5829145728643217, "no_speech_prob": 1.996596464548528e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 92642, "start": 937.5, "end": 945.02, "text": " Meaning, if the simulation had a burn-in period just to let the particles settle into equilibrium before the actual experiment starts,", "tokens": [50919, 19948, 11, 498, 264, 16575, 632, 257, 5064, 12, 259, 2896, 445, 281, 718, 264, 10007, 11852, 666, 15625, 949, 264, 3539, 5120, 3719, 11, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14328702779916616, "compression_ratio": 1.5829145728643217, "no_speech_prob": 1.996596464548528e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 94502, "start": 945.02, "end": 951.66, "text": " that absolute clock might already be at a count of, say, 100 before the official test even begins.", "tokens": [50365, 300, 8236, 7830, 1062, 1217, 312, 412, 257, 1207, 295, 11, 584, 11, 2319, 949, 264, 4783, 1500, 754, 7338, 13, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13135448198639946, "compression_ratio": 1.6042553191489362, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898022052123316e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 94502, "start": 951.86, "end": 952.0799999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50707, 1079, 13, 50718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13135448198639946, "compression_ratio": 1.6042553191489362, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898022052123316e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 94502, "start": 952.24, "end": 959.06, "text": " So an intervention program to activate from time zero to time two was checking an internal clock that was already at 100.", "tokens": [50726, 407, 364, 13176, 1461, 281, 13615, 490, 565, 4018, 281, 565, 732, 390, 8568, 364, 6920, 7830, 300, 390, 1217, 412, 2319, 13, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13135448198639946, "compression_ratio": 1.6042553191489362, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898022052123316e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 94502, "start": 959.4, "end": 960.06, "text": " Oh, no.", "tokens": [51084, 876, 11, 572, 13, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13135448198639946, "compression_ratio": 1.6042553191489362, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898022052123316e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 94502, "start": 960.18, "end": 964.84, "text": " It never matched the condition, which meant the intervention pulse literally never activated.", "tokens": [51123, 467, 1128, 21447, 264, 4188, 11, 597, 4140, 264, 13176, 17709, 3736, 1128, 18157, 13, 51356], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13135448198639946, "compression_ratio": 1.6042553191489362, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898022052123316e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 94502, "start": 965.26, "end": 967.18, "text": " But how did they even realize that was happening?", "tokens": [51377, 583, 577, 630, 436, 754, 4325, 300, 390, 2737, 30, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13135448198639946, "compression_ratio": 1.6042553191489362, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898022052123316e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 96718, "start": 967.18, "end": 971.8, "text": " Because if you look at the output data and nothing changes, it's so easy to just assume,", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 498, 291, 574, 412, 264, 5598, 1412, 293, 1825, 2962, 11, 309, 311, 370, 1858, 281, 445, 6552, 11, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08728687579815204, "compression_ratio": 1.6842105263157894, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234910551332637e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 96718, "start": 971.9599999999999, "end": 973.64, "text": " oh, I guess my intervention had no effect.", "tokens": [50604, 1954, 11, 286, 2041, 452, 13176, 632, 572, 1802, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08728687579815204, "compression_ratio": 1.6842105263157894, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234910551332637e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 96718, "start": 973.7399999999999, "end": 977.18, "text": " And that is the hidden danger of computational causal inference.", "tokens": [50693, 400, 300, 307, 264, 7633, 4330, 295, 28270, 38755, 38253, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08728687579815204, "compression_ratio": 1.6842105263157894, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234910551332637e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 96718, "start": 977.6999999999999, "end": 982.9799999999999, "text": " An inactive intervention and a genuinely null causal effect look identical on a spreadsheet.", "tokens": [50891, 1107, 294, 12596, 13176, 293, 257, 17839, 18184, 38755, 1802, 574, 14800, 322, 257, 27733, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08728687579815204, "compression_ratio": 1.6842105263157894, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234910551332637e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 96718, "start": 983.14, "end": 984.1999999999999, "text": " That is terrifying.", "tokens": [51163, 663, 307, 18106, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08728687579815204, "compression_ratio": 1.6842105263157894, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234910551332637e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 96718, "start": 984.4, "end": 991.52, "text": " They caught the bug because they employed a zero-amplitude identity property test using common random numbers.", "tokens": [51226, 814, 5415, 264, 7426, 570, 436, 20115, 257, 4018, 12, 335, 564, 4377, 6575, 4707, 1500, 1228, 2689, 4974, 3547, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08728687579815204, "compression_ratio": 1.6842105263157894, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234910551332637e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 96718, "start": 991.9799999999999, "end": 996.3199999999999, "text": " Okay, let's break down common random numbers so we can fully appreciate how clever this is.", "tokens": [51605, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1821, 760, 2689, 4974, 3547, 370, 321, 393, 4498, 4449, 577, 13494, 341, 307, 13, 51822], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08728687579815204, "compression_ratio": 1.6842105263157894, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234910551332637e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 99632, "start": 996.32, "end": 1001.2600000000001, "text": " Sure. In a simulation driven by probabilities, you use random number generators.", "tokens": [50365, 4894, 13, 682, 257, 16575, 9555, 538, 33783, 11, 291, 764, 4974, 1230, 38662, 13, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15784724253528523, "compression_ratio": 1.7786259541984732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682368377332613e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 99632, "start": 1001.34, "end": 1001.5400000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50616, 1779, 13, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15784724253528523, "compression_ratio": 1.7786259541984732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682368377332613e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 99632, "start": 1001.7600000000001, "end": 1006.9200000000001, "text": " But you can seed those generators so they roll the exact same sequence of random numbers every time.", "tokens": [50637, 583, 291, 393, 8871, 729, 38662, 370, 436, 3373, 264, 1900, 912, 8310, 295, 4974, 3547, 633, 565, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15784724253528523, "compression_ratio": 1.7786259541984732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682368377332613e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 99632, "start": 1007.0600000000001, "end": 1007.7, "text": " Oh, okay.", "tokens": [50902, 876, 11, 1392, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15784724253528523, "compression_ratio": 1.7786259541984732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682368377332613e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 99632, "start": 1007.7, "end": 1015.1800000000001, "text": " So Flixian set up a treatment branch and a control branch of the simulation using identically seeded random numbers.", "tokens": [50934, 407, 3235, 970, 952, 992, 493, 257, 5032, 9819, 293, 257, 1969, 9819, 295, 264, 16575, 1228, 2473, 984, 8871, 292, 4974, 3547, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15784724253528523, "compression_ratio": 1.7786259541984732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682368377332613e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 99632, "start": 1015.82, "end": 1021.6, "text": " If you apply zero perturbation, meaning your treatment is mathematically identical to the control,", "tokens": [51340, 759, 291, 3079, 4018, 40468, 399, 11, 3620, 428, 5032, 307, 44003, 14800, 281, 264, 1969, 11, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15784724253528523, "compression_ratio": 1.7786259541984732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682368377332613e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 99632, "start": 1021.98, "end": 1024.92, "text": " the two branches must remain bit identical forever.", "tokens": [51648, 264, 732, 14770, 1633, 6222, 857, 14800, 5680, 13, 51795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15784724253528523, "compression_ratio": 1.7786259541984732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682368377332613e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 102492, "start": 1024.92, "end": 1028.3000000000002, "text": " And if they ever diverge, you know you have a bug in your code.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 498, 436, 1562, 18558, 432, 11, 291, 458, 291, 362, 257, 7426, 294, 428, 3089, 13, 50534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12742225877169905, "compression_ratio": 1.6958174904942966, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779790889415945e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 102492, "start": 1028.42, "end": 1030.24, "text": " Exactly. So they ran this check.", "tokens": [50540, 7587, 13, 407, 436, 5872, 341, 1520, 13, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12742225877169905, "compression_ratio": 1.6958174904942966, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779790889415945e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 102492, "start": 1030.7, "end": 1033.68, "text": " But to make sure the intervention machinery actually could work,", "tokens": [50654, 583, 281, 652, 988, 264, 13176, 27302, 767, 727, 589, 11, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12742225877169905, "compression_ratio": 1.6958174904942966, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779790889415945e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 102492, "start": 1033.98, "end": 1037.64, "text": " they tried a demonstration check with a massive perturbation.", "tokens": [50818, 436, 3031, 257, 16520, 1520, 365, 257, 5994, 40468, 399, 13, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12742225877169905, "compression_ratio": 1.6958174904942966, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779790889415945e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 102492, "start": 1037.74, "end": 1039.22, "text": " They cranked the dial way up.", "tokens": [51006, 814, 21263, 292, 264, 5502, 636, 493, 13, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12742225877169905, "compression_ratio": 1.6958174904942966, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779790889415945e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 102492, "start": 1039.3200000000002, "end": 1041.8200000000002, "text": " They cranked it up, looked at the particle trajectories,", "tokens": [51085, 814, 21263, 292, 309, 493, 11, 2956, 412, 264, 12359, 18257, 2083, 11, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12742225877169905, "compression_ratio": 1.6958174904942966, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779790889415945e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 102492, "start": 1041.98, "end": 1046.3000000000002, "text": " and realized the treatment branch and the control branch hadn't diverged by a single bit.", "tokens": [51218, 293, 5334, 264, 5032, 9819, 293, 264, 1969, 9819, 8782, 380, 18558, 3004, 538, 257, 2167, 857, 13, 51434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12742225877169905, "compression_ratio": 1.6958174904942966, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779790889415945e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 102492, "start": 1046.42, "end": 1047.46, "text": " The pulse never fired.", "tokens": [51440, 440, 17709, 1128, 11777, 13, 51492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12742225877169905, "compression_ratio": 1.6958174904942966, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779790889415945e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 102492, "start": 1047.74, "end": 1048.8400000000001, "text": " The pulse never fired.", "tokens": [51506, 440, 17709, 1128, 11777, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12742225877169905, "compression_ratio": 1.6958174904942966, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779790889415945e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 104884, "start": 1048.84, "end": 1055.0, "text": " And because they were inspecting the trajectories directly, they traced it back to the clock logic.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 570, 436, 645, 15018, 278, 264, 18257, 2083, 3838, 11, 436, 38141, 309, 646, 281, 264, 7830, 9952, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14617007328913761, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.622895719720352e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 104884, "start": 1055.3999999999999, "end": 1058.1999999999998, "text": " I want to pause here and connect this directly to you, the listener.", "tokens": [50693, 286, 528, 281, 10465, 510, 293, 1745, 341, 3838, 281, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 13, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14617007328913761, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.622895719720352e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 104884, "start": 1058.9399999999998, "end": 1067.0, "text": " Because this level of paranoia is exactly why you should always demand rigorous baselines when someone pitches you data.", "tokens": [50870, 1436, 341, 1496, 295, 31416, 654, 307, 2293, 983, 291, 820, 1009, 4733, 29882, 987, 9173, 562, 1580, 43110, 291, 1412, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14617007328913761, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.622895719720352e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 106700, "start": 1067.0, "end": 1068.26, "text": " Yes, always.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 1009, 13, 50428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15991812003286263, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.377634009473716e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 106700, "start": 1068.38, "end": 1073.58, "text": " Whether it's a new corporate marketing strategy, a proprietary health supplement, or an economic forecast.", "tokens": [50434, 8503, 309, 311, 257, 777, 10896, 6370, 5206, 11, 257, 38992, 1585, 15436, 11, 420, 364, 4836, 14330, 13, 50694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15991812003286263, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.377634009473716e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 106700, "start": 1073.94, "end": 1078.9, "text": " If the baseline is broken, if the intervention isn't even activating under the hood,", "tokens": [50712, 759, 264, 20518, 307, 5463, 11, 498, 264, 13176, 1943, 380, 754, 42481, 833, 264, 13376, 11, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15991812003286263, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.377634009473716e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 106700, "start": 1079.06, "end": 1083.24, "text": " or if the metric reads 100% success before the clock even starts,", "tokens": [50968, 420, 498, 264, 20678, 15700, 2319, 4, 2245, 949, 264, 7830, 754, 3719, 11, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15991812003286263, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.377634009473716e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 106700, "start": 1084.24, "end": 1088.16, "text": " every conclusion drawn from that data is fundamentally worthless.", "tokens": [51227, 633, 10063, 10117, 490, 300, 1412, 307, 17879, 34857, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15991812003286263, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.377634009473716e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 108816, "start": 1088.16, "end": 1094.0800000000002, "text": " It really brings home why the third and fourth steps of that four-part testability across nuisance parameters", "tokens": [50365, 467, 534, 5607, 1280, 983, 264, 2636, 293, 6409, 4439, 295, 300, 1451, 12, 6971, 1500, 2310, 2108, 3822, 46852, 9834, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12211071161123423, "compression_ratio": 1.6920821114369502, "no_speech_prob": 2.1091394689781717e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 108816, "start": 1094.0800000000002, "end": 1097.42, "text": " and predicting beyond baselines are completely non-negotiable.", "tokens": [50661, 293, 32884, 4399, 987, 9173, 366, 2584, 2107, 12, 28561, 8206, 712, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12211071161123423, "compression_ratio": 1.6920821114369502, "no_speech_prob": 2.1091394689781717e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 108816, "start": 1097.6000000000001, "end": 1101.4, "text": " Because if you don't fully understand how your baseline behaves under extreme conditions,", "tokens": [50837, 1436, 498, 291, 500, 380, 4498, 1223, 577, 428, 20518, 36896, 833, 8084, 4487, 11, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12211071161123423, "compression_ratio": 1.6920821114369502, "no_speech_prob": 2.1091394689781717e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 108816, "start": 1101.64, "end": 1103.42, "text": " you have no idea what you're actually measuring.", "tokens": [51039, 291, 362, 572, 1558, 437, 291, 434, 767, 13389, 13, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12211071161123423, "compression_ratio": 1.6920821114369502, "no_speech_prob": 2.1091394689781717e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 108816, "start": 1103.92, "end": 1109.0600000000002, "text": " So with the bugs squashed, the geometric artifacts fixed, and the rigorous setup finally in place,", "tokens": [51153, 407, 365, 264, 15120, 2339, 12219, 11, 264, 33246, 24617, 6806, 11, 293, 264, 29882, 8657, 2721, 294, 1081, 11, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12211071161123423, "compression_ratio": 1.6920821114369502, "no_speech_prob": 2.1091394689781717e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 108816, "start": 1109.52, "end": 1111.24, "text": " it was time for the climax of the paper.", "tokens": [51433, 309, 390, 565, 337, 264, 41329, 295, 264, 3035, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12211071161123423, "compression_ratio": 1.6920821114369502, "no_speech_prob": 2.1091394689781717e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 108816, "start": 1111.38, "end": 1112.52, "text": " The moment of truth.", "tokens": [51526, 440, 1623, 295, 3494, 13, 51583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12211071161123423, "compression_ratio": 1.6920821114369502, "no_speech_prob": 2.1091394689781717e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 108816, "start": 1112.52, "end": 1117.64, "text": " It was time to see if these complex capacity and dissipation fields actually predicted phase separation,", "tokens": [51583, 467, 390, 565, 281, 536, 498, 613, 3997, 6042, 293, 29544, 399, 7909, 767, 19147, 5574, 14634, 11, 51839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12211071161123423, "compression_ratio": 1.6920821114369502, "no_speech_prob": 2.1091394689781717e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 111764, "start": 1117.64, "end": 1119.8200000000002, "text": " better than just looking at simple density.", "tokens": [50365, 1101, 813, 445, 1237, 412, 2199, 10305, 13, 50474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2240727517457135, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271424753770079e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 111764, "start": 1120.46, "end": 1121.92, "text": " So what was the grand result?", "tokens": [50506, 407, 437, 390, 264, 2697, 1874, 30, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2240727517457135, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271424753770079e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 111764, "start": 1122.2, "end": 1123.14, "text": " The result was a null.", "tokens": [50593, 440, 1874, 390, 257, 18184, 13, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2240727517457135, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271424753770079e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 111764, "start": 1123.5400000000002, "end": 1124.0600000000002, "text": " A null.", "tokens": [50660, 316, 18184, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2240727517457135, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271424753770079e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 111764, "start": 1124.3600000000001, "end": 1128.48, "text": " Across every replication, across exhaustive parameter sweeps,", "tokens": [50701, 34527, 633, 39911, 11, 2108, 14687, 488, 13075, 2484, 10653, 11, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2240727517457135, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271424753770079e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 111764, "start": 1128.94, "end": 1136.7, "text": " none of the capacity or dissipation features showed any incremental predictive value beyond the conventional density observables.", "tokens": [50930, 6022, 295, 264, 6042, 420, 29544, 399, 4122, 4712, 604, 35759, 35521, 2158, 4399, 264, 16011, 10305, 9951, 2965, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2240727517457135, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271424753770079e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 111764, "start": 1136.8600000000001, "end": 1137.22, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51326, 3153, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2240727517457135, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271424753770079e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 111764, "start": 1137.48, "end": 1140.92, "text": " The simple density baseline did all of the predictive heavy lifting.", "tokens": [51357, 440, 2199, 10305, 20518, 630, 439, 295, 264, 35521, 4676, 15798, 13, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2240727517457135, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271424753770079e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 111764, "start": 1140.92, "end": 1142.2800000000002, "text": " A null result.", "tokens": [51529, 316, 18184, 1874, 13, 51597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2240727517457135, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271424753770079e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 111764, "start": 1142.66, "end": 1146.92, "text": " After all the mathematical theory, all the setup, all the philosophical nuance of imposed versus real,", "tokens": [51616, 2381, 439, 264, 18894, 5261, 11, 439, 264, 8657, 11, 439, 264, 25066, 42625, 295, 26491, 5717, 957, 11, 51829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2240727517457135, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271424753770079e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 114764, "start": 1147.64, "end": 1152.94, "text": " realized capacity, the shiny new buzzwords added absolutely nothing to the prediction.", "tokens": [50365, 5334, 6042, 11, 264, 16997, 777, 13036, 13832, 3869, 3122, 1825, 281, 264, 17630, 13, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19084932219307377, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.981063967385066e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 114764, "start": 1153.1000000000001, "end": 1153.44, "text": " Nothing.", "tokens": [50638, 6693, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19084932219307377, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.981063967385066e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 114764, "start": 1154.1000000000001, "end": 1156.46, "text": " And yet this is a phenomenal outcome for science.", "tokens": [50688, 400, 1939, 341, 307, 257, 17778, 9700, 337, 3497, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19084932219307377, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.981063967385066e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 114764, "start": 1156.6000000000001, "end": 1156.8000000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50813, 1779, 13, 50823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19084932219307377, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.981063967385066e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 114764, "start": 1157.0400000000002, "end": 1160.7, "text": " In the text, Fliction proudly describes this as a clean failure.", "tokens": [50835, 682, 264, 2487, 11, 3235, 4105, 33522, 15626, 341, 382, 257, 2541, 7763, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19084932219307377, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.981063967385066e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 114764, "start": 1160.92, "end": 1161.94, "text": " A clean failure.", "tokens": [51029, 316, 2541, 7763, 13, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19084932219307377, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.981063967385066e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 114764, "start": 1162.0400000000002, "end": 1162.74, "text": " I love that term.", "tokens": [51085, 286, 959, 300, 1433, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19084932219307377, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.981063967385066e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 114764, "start": 1162.8400000000001, "end": 1165.8400000000001, "text": " The mathematical fields they created were incredibly stable.", "tokens": [51125, 440, 18894, 7909, 436, 2942, 645, 6252, 8351, 13, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19084932219307377, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.981063967385066e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 114764, "start": 1166.26, "end": 1169.76, "text": " The coefficients held up perfectly across different coarse graining scales.", "tokens": [51296, 440, 31994, 5167, 493, 6239, 2108, 819, 39312, 1295, 1760, 17408, 13, 51471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19084932219307377, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.981063967385066e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 114764, "start": 1170.3200000000002, "end": 1172.7800000000002, "text": " There was just simply no predictive gain to be found.", "tokens": [51499, 821, 390, 445, 2935, 572, 35521, 6052, 281, 312, 1352, 13, 51622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19084932219307377, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.981063967385066e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 117278, "start": 1172.78, "end": 1179.84, "text": " The information contained in the capacity fields was entirely redundant with the information already present in the basic density configuration.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1589, 16212, 294, 264, 6042, 7909, 390, 7696, 40997, 365, 264, 1589, 1217, 1974, 294, 264, 3875, 10305, 11694, 13, 50718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16877520243326824, "compression_ratio": 1.6293103448275863, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924071936906374e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 117278, "start": 1180.3, "end": 1180.86, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50741, 7587, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16877520243326824, "compression_ratio": 1.6293103448275863, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924071936906374e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 117278, "start": 1181.5, "end": 1185.1399999999999, "text": " And this highlights one of the most impressive parts of the philosophical essay.", "tokens": [50801, 400, 341, 14254, 472, 295, 264, 881, 8992, 3166, 295, 264, 25066, 16238, 13, 50983], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16877520243326824, "compression_ratio": 1.6293103448275863, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924071936906374e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 117278, "start": 1185.6, "end": 1194.36, "text": " The author included a matrix, figure one, where they pre-registered their interpretation scheme before they ever looked at the simulation data.", "tokens": [51006, 440, 3793, 5556, 257, 8141, 11, 2573, 472, 11, 689, 436, 659, 12, 3375, 1964, 292, 641, 14174, 12232, 949, 436, 1562, 2956, 412, 264, 16575, 1412, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16877520243326824, "compression_ratio": 1.6293103448275863, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924071936906374e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 119436, "start": 1194.36, "end": 1197.8, "text": " That is the absolute gold standard of intellectual honesty.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 264, 8236, 3821, 3832, 295, 12576, 26839, 13, 50537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11903844396752047, "compression_ratio": 1.5791666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327315375761707e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 119436, "start": 1197.8999999999999, "end": 1198.6399999999999, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [50542, 467, 534, 307, 13, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11903844396752047, "compression_ratio": 1.5791666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327315375761707e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 119436, "start": 1198.82, "end": 1209.1399999999999, "text": " The matrix defined exactly what specific data outputs would constitute a strong success, a weak success, a conditional success, and a clean failure.", "tokens": [50588, 440, 8141, 7642, 2293, 437, 2685, 1412, 23930, 576, 41658, 257, 2068, 2245, 11, 257, 5336, 2245, 11, 257, 27708, 2245, 11, 293, 257, 2541, 7763, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11903844396752047, "compression_ratio": 1.5791666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327315375761707e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 119436, "start": 1209.3999999999999, "end": 1209.56, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51117, 1779, 13, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11903844396752047, "compression_ratio": 1.5791666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327315375761707e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 119436, "start": 1209.6999999999998, "end": 1218.2199999999998, "text": " By defining these categories before writing a single line of analysis code, they completely removed the ability to move the goalposts after the fact.", "tokens": [51132, 3146, 17827, 613, 10479, 949, 3579, 257, 2167, 1622, 295, 5215, 3089, 11, 436, 2584, 7261, 264, 3485, 281, 1286, 264, 3387, 23744, 82, 934, 264, 1186, 13, 51558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11903844396752047, "compression_ratio": 1.5791666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327315375761707e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 121822, "start": 1218.22, "end": 1219.74, "text": " Which is so tempting to do.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 307, 370, 37900, 281, 360, 13, 50441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09154095159512814, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 2.6148167832362734e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 121822, "start": 1219.98, "end": 1228.96, "text": " If you spend months building a brilliant theoretical capacity framework and the data comes back null, human nature makes you desperately want to find a silver lining.", "tokens": [50453, 759, 291, 3496, 2493, 2390, 257, 10248, 20864, 6042, 8388, 293, 264, 1412, 1487, 646, 18184, 11, 1952, 3687, 1669, 291, 23726, 528, 281, 915, 257, 8753, 19628, 13, 50902], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09154095159512814, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 2.6148167832362734e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 121822, "start": 1229.08, "end": 1229.66, "text": " Of course.", "tokens": [50908, 2720, 1164, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09154095159512814, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 2.6148167832362734e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 121822, "start": 1229.82, "end": 1235.22, "text": " You want to squint at the numbers and say, well, if you only look at this one specific angle on Tuesdays, it's a massive breakthrough.", "tokens": [50945, 509, 528, 281, 2339, 686, 412, 264, 3547, 293, 584, 11, 731, 11, 498, 291, 787, 574, 412, 341, 472, 2685, 5802, 322, 10017, 82, 11, 309, 311, 257, 5994, 22397, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09154095159512814, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 2.6148167832362734e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 121822, "start": 1235.58, "end": 1241.66, "text": " But because they pre-registered what failure looked like, they had no choice but to accept the clean failure.", "tokens": [51233, 583, 570, 436, 659, 12, 3375, 1964, 292, 437, 7763, 2956, 411, 11, 436, 632, 572, 3922, 457, 281, 3241, 264, 2541, 7763, 13, 51537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09154095159512814, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 2.6148167832362734e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 124166, "start": 1241.66, "end": 1250.46, "text": " The text explicitly states that the capacity reconstruction is not empirically justified for prediction in this specific system.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2487, 20803, 4368, 300, 264, 6042, 31565, 307, 406, 25790, 984, 27808, 337, 17630, 294, 341, 2685, 1185, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13824477725558812, "compression_ratio": 1.656, "no_speech_prob": 2.142022453507919e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 124166, "start": 1250.66, "end": 1256.46, "text": " It simply acts as a downstream expression of density, not an independent source of physical information.", "tokens": [50815, 467, 2935, 10672, 382, 257, 30621, 6114, 295, 10305, 11, 406, 364, 6695, 4009, 295, 4001, 1589, 13, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13824477725558812, "compression_ratio": 1.656, "no_speech_prob": 2.142022453507919e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 124166, "start": 1256.5600000000002, "end": 1257.1200000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51110, 7587, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13824477725558812, "compression_ratio": 1.656, "no_speech_prob": 2.142022453507919e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 124166, "start": 1257.26, "end": 1261.0800000000002, "text": " I do want to point out, though, that they didn't over-claim the failure either.", "tokens": [51145, 286, 360, 528, 281, 935, 484, 11, 1673, 11, 300, 436, 994, 380, 670, 12, 66, 10970, 264, 7763, 2139, 13, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13824477725558812, "compression_ratio": 1.656, "no_speech_prob": 2.142022453507919e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 124166, "start": 1261.26, "end": 1266.1000000000001, "text": " They didn't declare that the word capacity is useless forever across all fields of physics.", "tokens": [51345, 814, 994, 380, 19710, 300, 264, 1349, 6042, 307, 14115, 5680, 2108, 439, 7909, 295, 10649, 13, 51587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13824477725558812, "compression_ratio": 1.656, "no_speech_prob": 2.142022453507919e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 126610, "start": 1266.1, "end": 1266.58, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17294040219537143, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553466717679876e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 126610, "start": 1266.9199999999998, "end": 1270.26, "text": " They were meticulously precise about the boundaries of the finding.", "tokens": [50406, 814, 645, 41566, 25038, 13600, 466, 264, 13180, 295, 264, 5006, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17294040219537143, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553466717679876e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 126610, "start": 1270.86, "end": 1275.9199999999998, "text": " It is a scoped technical finding about one specific attempt in one parameter regime.", "tokens": [50603, 467, 307, 257, 795, 27277, 6191, 5006, 466, 472, 2685, 5217, 294, 472, 13075, 13120, 13, 50856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17294040219537143, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553466717679876e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 126610, "start": 1276.24, "end": 1279.98, "text": " In fact, they even went a step further and tested a causal pilot study.", "tokens": [50872, 682, 1186, 11, 436, 754, 1437, 257, 1823, 3052, 293, 8246, 257, 38755, 9691, 2979, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17294040219537143, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553466717679876e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 126610, "start": 1280.4199999999998, "end": 1287.76, "text": " This was an attempt to intervene and see if regions with identical densities but different capacities responded differently to perturbations.", "tokens": [51081, 639, 390, 364, 5217, 281, 30407, 293, 536, 498, 10682, 365, 14800, 24505, 1088, 457, 819, 39396, 15806, 7614, 281, 40468, 763, 13, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17294040219537143, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553466717679876e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 126610, "start": 1287.8799999999999, "end": 1289.08, "text": " Wait, how did they set that up?", "tokens": [51454, 3802, 11, 577, 630, 436, 992, 300, 493, 30, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17294040219537143, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553466717679876e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 126610, "start": 1289.1, "end": 1291.4199999999998, "text": " Because that sounds really tricky to isolate.", "tokens": [51515, 1436, 300, 3263, 534, 12414, 281, 25660, 13, 51631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17294040219537143, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553466717679876e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 126610, "start": 1291.82, "end": 1292.58, "text": " It is tricky.", "tokens": [51651, 467, 307, 12414, 13, 51689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17294040219537143, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553466717679876e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 126610, "start": 1292.8799999999999, "end": 1295.58, "text": " They used a matched region approach.", "tokens": [51704, 814, 1143, 257, 21447, 4458, 3109, 13, 51839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17294040219537143, "compression_ratio": 1.726643598615917, "no_speech_prob": 1.5553466717679876e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 129610, "start": 1296.1, "end": 1299.56, "text": " They found four specific pairs of regions in the simulation.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 1352, 1451, 2685, 15494, 295, 10682, 294, 264, 16575, 13, 50538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853596269038685, "compression_ratio": 1.7054794520547945, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616284949881211e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 129610, "start": 1300.4399999999998, "end": 1307.5, "text": " Inside each pair, the density was virtually identical, but the calculated capacity metrics were significantly different.", "tokens": [50582, 15123, 1184, 6119, 11, 264, 10305, 390, 14103, 14800, 11, 457, 264, 15598, 6042, 16367, 645, 10591, 819, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853596269038685, "compression_ratio": 1.7054794520547945, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616284949881211e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 129610, "start": 1307.6399999999999, "end": 1307.86, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50942, 1033, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853596269038685, "compression_ratio": 1.7054794520547945, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616284949881211e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 129610, "start": 1307.86, "end": 1314.86, "text": " They then pulsed those specific regions with extra activity to see if the local response magnitudes differed.", "tokens": [50953, 814, 550, 32295, 292, 729, 2685, 10682, 365, 2857, 5191, 281, 536, 498, 264, 2654, 4134, 4944, 16451, 743, 292, 13, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853596269038685, "compression_ratio": 1.7054794520547945, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616284949881211e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 129610, "start": 1314.98, "end": 1317.6, "text": " Did the regions with higher capacity react stronger?", "tokens": [51309, 2589, 264, 10682, 365, 2946, 6042, 4515, 7249, 30, 51440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853596269038685, "compression_ratio": 1.7054794520547945, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616284949881211e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 129610, "start": 1317.98, "end": 1319.6399999999999, "text": " It was entirely inconclusive.", "tokens": [51459, 467, 390, 7696, 20972, 66, 7233, 13, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853596269038685, "compression_ratio": 1.7054794520547945, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616284949881211e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 129610, "start": 1319.7199999999998, "end": 1319.9399999999998, "text": " Really?", "tokens": [51546, 4083, 30, 51557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853596269038685, "compression_ratio": 1.7054794520547945, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616284949881211e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 129610, "start": 1320.1, "end": 1320.28, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51565, 865, 13, 51574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853596269038685, "compression_ratio": 1.7054794520547945, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616284949881211e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 129610, "start": 1320.74, "end": 1325.84, "text": " Two of the pairs showed a response in one direction, and the other two pairs showed the exact opposite.", "tokens": [51597, 4453, 295, 264, 15494, 4712, 257, 4134, 294, 472, 3513, 11, 293, 264, 661, 732, 15494, 4712, 264, 1900, 6182, 13, 51852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14853596269038685, "compression_ratio": 1.7054794520547945, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616284949881211e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 132584, "start": 1325.84, "end": 1326.3999999999999, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 50393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13828741073608397, "compression_ratio": 1.50390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487949243762512e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 132584, "start": 1326.86, "end": 1330.0, "text": " Fliction openly admits the pilot study was underpowered.", "tokens": [50416, 3235, 4105, 23109, 46682, 264, 9691, 2979, 390, 833, 27178, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13828741073608397, "compression_ratio": 1.50390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487949243762512e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 132584, "start": 1330.76, "end": 1334.76, "text": " Four pairs simply isn't enough statistical weight to pull a signal from the noise.", "tokens": [50611, 7451, 15494, 2935, 1943, 380, 1547, 22820, 3364, 281, 2235, 257, 6358, 490, 264, 5658, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13828741073608397, "compression_ratio": 1.50390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487949243762512e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 132584, "start": 1334.8999999999999, "end": 1335.1, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [50818, 4894, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13828741073608397, "compression_ratio": 1.50390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487949243762512e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 132584, "start": 1335.28, "end": 1343.26, "text": " They acknowledge that whether capacity carries causal content beyond density remains an open, well-posed question awaiting a much larger study.", "tokens": [50837, 814, 10692, 300, 1968, 6042, 16402, 38755, 2701, 4399, 10305, 7023, 364, 1269, 11, 731, 12, 79, 1744, 1168, 43759, 257, 709, 4833, 2979, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13828741073608397, "compression_ratio": 1.50390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487949243762512e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 132584, "start": 1343.3999999999999, "end": 1344.04, "text": " We don't know yet.", "tokens": [51243, 492, 500, 380, 458, 1939, 13, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13828741073608397, "compression_ratio": 1.50390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487949243762512e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 132584, "start": 1344.12, "end": 1346.48, "text": " Our data is too small to say, so we will not make a claim.", "tokens": [51279, 2621, 1412, 307, 886, 1359, 281, 584, 11, 370, 321, 486, 406, 652, 257, 3932, 13, 51397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13828741073608397, "compression_ratio": 1.50390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487949243762512e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 132584, "start": 1346.6, "end": 1347.02, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51403, 7587, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13828741073608397, "compression_ratio": 1.50390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487949243762512e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 134702, "start": 1347.02, "end": 1348.26, "text": " It's incredibly refreshing.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 6252, 19772, 13, 50427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657864732562371, "compression_ratio": 1.4497354497354498, "no_speech_prob": 1.6941446075863231e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 134702, "start": 1348.86, "end": 1356.28, "text": " They even provided the exact experimental design a future, properly powered study would need to use to finally answer the question.", "tokens": [50457, 814, 754, 5649, 264, 1900, 17069, 1715, 257, 2027, 11, 6108, 17786, 2979, 576, 643, 281, 764, 281, 2721, 1867, 264, 1168, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657864732562371, "compression_ratio": 1.4497354497354498, "no_speech_prob": 1.6941446075863231e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 134702, "start": 1356.46, "end": 1363.66, "text": " It just demonstrates how a highly principled empirical workflow can yield incredibly informative negative results.", "tokens": [50837, 467, 445, 31034, 577, 257, 5405, 3681, 15551, 31886, 20993, 393, 11257, 6252, 27759, 3671, 3542, 13, 51197], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657864732562371, "compression_ratio": 1.4497354497354498, "no_speech_prob": 1.6941446075863231e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 136366, "start": 1363.66, "end": 1374.1200000000001, "text": " By meticulously forcing a concept to reconstruct, compare, stabilize, and predict, they systematically narrowed the space of viable theoretical claims.", "tokens": [50365, 3146, 41566, 25038, 19030, 257, 3410, 281, 31499, 11, 6794, 11, 31870, 11, 293, 6069, 11, 436, 39531, 9432, 292, 264, 1901, 295, 22024, 20864, 9441, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10976955967564736, "compression_ratio": 1.2905982905982907, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490477603228748e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 137412, "start": 1374.12, "end": 1377.6999999999998, "text": " So, let's bring this all the way back out of the physics simulation to wrap up.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 718, 311, 1565, 341, 439, 264, 636, 646, 484, 295, 264, 10649, 16575, 281, 7019, 493, 13, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469548543294271, "compression_ratio": 1.454954954954955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6941439570650196e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 137412, "start": 1378.04, "end": 1385.02, "text": " We've talked extensively about active Brownian particles and MAM piece, but the core takeaway here applies to almost everything.", "tokens": [50561, 492, 600, 2825, 32636, 466, 4967, 8030, 952, 10007, 293, 376, 2865, 2522, 11, 457, 264, 4965, 30681, 510, 13165, 281, 1920, 1203, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469548543294271, "compression_ratio": 1.454954954954955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6941439570650196e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 137412, "start": 1385.1999999999998, "end": 1385.9799999999998, "text": " It really does.", "tokens": [50919, 467, 534, 775, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469548543294271, "compression_ratio": 1.454954954954955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6941439570650196e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 137412, "start": 1386.36, "end": 1391.8999999999999, "text": " You, listening to this, now have a four-part framework to cut through the jargon in your own life.", "tokens": [50977, 509, 11, 4764, 281, 341, 11, 586, 362, 257, 1451, 12, 6971, 8388, 281, 1723, 807, 264, 15181, 10660, 294, 428, 1065, 993, 13, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469548543294271, "compression_ratio": 1.454954954954955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6941439570650196e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 139190, "start": 1391.9, "end": 1394.66, "text": " Reconstruct, compare, stabilize, predict.", "tokens": [50365, 1300, 25279, 1757, 11, 6794, 11, 31870, 11, 6069, 13, 50503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12715174357096354, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735348137327354e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 139190, "start": 1395.1200000000001, "end": 1399.18, "text": " If someone offers you a brand new metric, ask yourself the hard questions.", "tokens": [50526, 759, 1580, 7736, 291, 257, 3360, 777, 20678, 11, 1029, 1803, 264, 1152, 1651, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12715174357096354, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735348137327354e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 139190, "start": 1399.9, "end": 1404.3000000000002, "text": " Can this metric be clearly reconstructed from raw data without magical thinking?", "tokens": [50765, 1664, 341, 20678, 312, 4448, 31499, 292, 490, 8936, 1412, 1553, 12066, 1953, 30, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12715174357096354, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735348137327354e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 139190, "start": 1404.64, "end": 1407.3400000000001, "text": " Has it been compared against simpler existing alternatives?", "tokens": [51002, 8646, 309, 668, 5347, 1970, 18587, 6741, 20478, 30, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12715174357096354, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735348137327354e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 139190, "start": 1407.5600000000002, "end": 1410.16, "text": " Is it mathematically stable if I look at the data slightly differently?", "tokens": [51148, 1119, 309, 44003, 8351, 498, 286, 574, 412, 264, 1412, 4748, 7614, 30, 51278], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12715174357096354, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735348137327354e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 139190, "start": 1410.3200000000002, "end": 1414.52, "text": " And most importantly, does it actually predict the future better than what we were already doing?", "tokens": [51286, 400, 881, 8906, 11, 775, 309, 767, 6069, 264, 2027, 1101, 813, 437, 321, 645, 1217, 884, 30, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12715174357096354, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735348137327354e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 139190, "start": 1414.88, "end": 1419.64, "text": " If the answer to that last question is no, you're just looking at a new coat of paint on an old house.", "tokens": [51514, 759, 264, 1867, 281, 300, 1036, 1168, 307, 572, 11, 291, 434, 445, 1237, 412, 257, 777, 10690, 295, 4225, 322, 364, 1331, 1782, 13, 51752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12715174357096354, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735348137327354e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 141964, "start": 1419.64, "end": 1423.8000000000002, "text": " As Flixion says, new terminology is not new predictive content.", "tokens": [50365, 1018, 3235, 970, 313, 1619, 11, 777, 27575, 307, 406, 777, 35521, 2701, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20696038466233474, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016207678339444e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 141964, "start": 1424.68, "end": 1428.42, "text": " And I think there is immense unsung value in a clean failure.", "tokens": [50617, 400, 286, 519, 456, 307, 22920, 2693, 1063, 2158, 294, 257, 2541, 7763, 13, 50804], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20696038466233474, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016207678339444e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 141964, "start": 1429.3400000000001, "end": 1434.66, "text": " A rigorous clean failure is just as vital to the progression of human knowledge as a flashy breakthrough,", "tokens": [50850, 316, 29882, 2541, 7763, 307, 445, 382, 11707, 281, 264, 18733, 295, 1952, 3601, 382, 257, 47873, 22397, 11, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20696038466233474, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016207678339444e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 141964, "start": 1435.3000000000002, "end": 1438.18, "text": " because it maps the exact boundaries of what is actually true.", "tokens": [51148, 570, 309, 11317, 264, 1900, 13180, 295, 437, 307, 767, 2074, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20696038466233474, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016207678339444e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 141964, "start": 1438.5400000000002, "end": 1443.8400000000001, "text": " It stops future researchers from wandering down dead-end theoretical roads for decades.", "tokens": [51310, 467, 10094, 2027, 10309, 490, 26396, 760, 3116, 12, 521, 20864, 11344, 337, 7878, 13, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20696038466233474, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016207678339444e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 141964, "start": 1444.1200000000001, "end": 1444.6000000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51589, 7587, 13, 51613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20696038466233474, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016207678339444e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 141964, "start": 1444.76, "end": 1447.76, "text": " It is the dividing line between empirical science and pure rhetoric.", "tokens": [51621, 467, 307, 264, 26764, 1622, 1296, 31886, 3497, 293, 6075, 29604, 13, 51771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20696038466233474, "compression_ratio": 1.6083916083916083, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016207678339444e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 144776, "start": 1447.76, "end": 1454.36, "text": " When you pre-define your failure states, you allow physical reality to push back against your beautiful theories.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 291, 659, 12, 20595, 533, 428, 7763, 4368, 11, 291, 2089, 4001, 4103, 281, 2944, 646, 1970, 428, 2238, 13667, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305965312476297, "compression_ratio": 1.5932835820895523, "no_speech_prob": 1.63636985905935e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 144776, "start": 1454.82, "end": 1456.66, "text": " That is how real progress is made.", "tokens": [50718, 663, 307, 577, 957, 4205, 307, 1027, 13, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305965312476297, "compression_ratio": 1.5932835820895523, "no_speech_prob": 1.63636985905935e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 144776, "start": 1457.04, "end": 1459.44, "text": " Which leads me to a final thought I want to leave you with today.", "tokens": [50829, 3013, 6689, 385, 281, 257, 2572, 1194, 286, 528, 281, 1856, 291, 365, 965, 13, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305965312476297, "compression_ratio": 1.5932835820895523, "no_speech_prob": 1.63636985905935e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 144776, "start": 1459.78, "end": 1462.54, "text": " We've spent this deep dive talking about physical simulations.", "tokens": [50966, 492, 600, 4418, 341, 2452, 9192, 1417, 466, 4001, 35138, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305965312476297, "compression_ratio": 1.5932835820895523, "no_speech_prob": 1.63636985905935e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 144776, "start": 1462.86, "end": 1464.96, "text": " But let's apply this to something much more personal.", "tokens": [51120, 583, 718, 311, 3079, 341, 281, 746, 709, 544, 2973, 13, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305965312476297, "compression_ratio": 1.5932835820895523, "no_speech_prob": 1.63636985905935e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 144776, "start": 1465.34, "end": 1468.86, "text": " The modern obsession with wearable tech and personal data tracking.", "tokens": [51244, 440, 4363, 30521, 365, 3728, 712, 7553, 293, 2973, 1412, 11603, 13, 51420], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305965312476297, "compression_ratio": 1.5932835820895523, "no_speech_prob": 1.63636985905935e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 144776, "start": 1468.9, "end": 1469.94, "text": " Oh, that's a great example.", "tokens": [51422, 876, 11, 300, 311, 257, 869, 1365, 13, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1305965312476297, "compression_ratio": 1.5932835820895523, "no_speech_prob": 1.63636985905935e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 146994, "start": 1469.94, "end": 1476.8600000000001, "text": " Think about the devices on our wrists or our phones that give us daily readiness scores, sleep capacity metrics, or stress load indices.", "tokens": [50365, 6557, 466, 264, 5759, 322, 527, 41876, 420, 527, 10216, 300, 976, 505, 5212, 34954, 13444, 11, 2817, 6042, 16367, 11, 420, 4244, 3677, 43840, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12337961903324833, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.2989558430612225e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 146994, "start": 1477.3600000000001, "end": 1483.16, "text": " These companies have invented incredibly elegant, highly technical terminology to describe how we feel.", "tokens": [50736, 1981, 3431, 362, 14479, 6252, 21117, 11, 5405, 6191, 27575, 281, 6786, 577, 321, 841, 13, 51026], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12337961903324833, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.2989558430612225e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 146994, "start": 1483.3600000000001, "end": 1487.98, "text": " But if we force these complex algorithms through Flixion's four-part test,", "tokens": [51036, 583, 498, 321, 3464, 613, 3997, 14642, 807, 3235, 970, 313, 311, 1451, 12, 6971, 1500, 11, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12337961903324833, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.2989558430612225e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 146994, "start": 1488.78, "end": 1495.18, "text": " specifically the demand that they must predict outcomes better than a simple pre-existing baseline,", "tokens": [51307, 4682, 264, 4733, 300, 436, 1633, 6069, 10070, 1101, 813, 257, 2199, 659, 12, 36447, 20518, 11, 51627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12337961903324833, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.2989558430612225e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 146994, "start": 1495.38, "end": 1497.64, "text": " like just asking yourself, do I feel tired today?", "tokens": [51637, 411, 445, 3365, 1803, 11, 360, 286, 841, 5868, 965, 30, 51750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12337961903324833, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.2989558430612225e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 146994, "start": 1497.74, "end": 1499.22, "text": " Right, the simplest baseline possible.", "tokens": [51755, 1779, 11, 264, 22811, 20518, 1944, 13, 51829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12337961903324833, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.2989558430612225e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 149922, "start": 1499.22, "end": 1499.7, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13741674246611418, "compression_ratio": 1.3875, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616101719714061e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 149922, "start": 1500.14, "end": 1503.3600000000001, "text": " How many of these multi-billion dollar metrics would actually survive?", "tokens": [50411, 1012, 867, 295, 613, 4825, 12, 65, 11836, 7241, 16367, 576, 767, 7867, 30, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13741674246611418, "compression_ratio": 1.3875, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616101719714061e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 149922, "start": 1503.66, "end": 1507.16, "text": " It really makes you wonder how much of the personal data we obsess over every day", "tokens": [50587, 467, 534, 1669, 291, 2441, 577, 709, 295, 264, 2973, 1412, 321, 35803, 670, 633, 786, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13741674246611418, "compression_ratio": 1.3875, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616101719714061e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 149922, "start": 1507.16, "end": 1510.48, "text": " is actually a clean failure, quietly strapped to our wrists.", "tokens": [50762, 307, 767, 257, 2541, 7763, 11, 19141, 2148, 3320, 281, 527, 41876, 13, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13741674246611418, "compression_ratio": 1.3875, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616101719714061e-12}], "language": "en"}
