nd": 86.36, "text": " Some ancient attempt to mathematically inscribe our devotion", "tokens": [50665, 2188, 7832, 5217, 281, 44003, 1028, 8056, 527, 30671, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15952833159631039, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 1.8069345932708591e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 7670, "start": 86.36, "end": 88.56, "text": " into the very crust of the Earth itself.", "tokens": [50848, 666, 264, 588, 18156, 295, 264, 4755, 2564, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15952833159631039, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 1.8069345932708591e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 7670, "start": 88.74000000000001, "end": 91.08, "text": " It totally sounds like the premise of a, you know,", "tokens": [50967, 467, 3879, 3263, 411, 264, 22045, 295, 257, 11, 291, 458, 11, 51084], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15952833159631039, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 1.8069345932708591e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 7670, "start": 91.46000000000001, "end": 93.2, "text": " a high-concept science fiction novel.", "tokens": [51103, 257, 1090, 12, 1671, 1336, 3497, 13266, 7613, 13, 51190], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15952833159631039, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 1.8069345932708591e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 7670, "start": 93.24000000000001, "end": 93.86, "text": " It really does.", "tokens": [51192, 467, 534, 775, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15952833159631039, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 1.8069345932708591e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 7670, "start": 94.14, "end": 96.44, "text": " Well, what we are looking at today is not fiction.", "tokens": [51237, 1042, 11, 437, 321, 366, 1237, 412, 965, 307, 406, 13266, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15952833159631039, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 1.8069345932708591e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 7670, "start": 96.98, "end": 101.7, "text": " It is a highly rigorous, incredibly detailed engineering framework", "tokens": [51379, 467, 307, 257, 5405, 29882, 11, 6252, 9942, 7043, 8388, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15952833159631039, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 1.8069345932708591e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 10170, "start": 101.7, "end": 105.10000000000001, "text": " designed to actually build this.", "tokens": [50365, 4761, 281, 767, 1322, 341, 13, 50535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20454202379499162, "compression_ratio": 1.32, "no_speech_prob": 1.911693026102057e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 10170, "start": 105.44, "end": 107.56, "text": " Welcome to the deep dive, everyone.", "tokens": [50552, 4027, 281, 264, 2452, 9192, 11, 1518, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20454202379499162, "compression_ratio": 1.32, "no_speech_prob": 1.911693026102057e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 10170, "start": 108.12, "end": 110.94, "text": " Because today we are unpacking a document", "tokens": [50686, 1436, 965, 321, 366, 26699, 278, 257, 4166, 50827], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20454202379499162, "compression_ratio": 1.32, "no_speech_prob": 1.911693026102057e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 10170, "start": 110.94, "end": 115.06, "text": " that completely redefines the concept of thinking big.", "tokens": [50827, 300, 2584, 38818, 1652, 264, 3410, 295, 1953, 955, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20454202379499162, "compression_ratio": 1.32, "no_speech_prob": 1.911693026102057e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 11506, "start": 115.56, "end": 116.98, "text": " Understatement of the century, honestly.", "tokens": [50390, 6974, 19435, 1712, 295, 264, 4901, 11, 6095, 13, 50461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645983937960952, "compression_ratio": 1.5639344262295083, "no_speech_prob": 1.629993340822311e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 11506, "start": 117.48, "end": 119.94, "text": " So if you are listening right now, whether you're on your commute,", "tokens": [50486, 407, 498, 291, 366, 4764, 558, 586, 11, 1968, 291, 434, 322, 428, 36750, 11, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645983937960952, "compression_ratio": 1.5639344262295083, "no_speech_prob": 1.629993340822311e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 11506, "start": 120.12, "end": 123.86, "text": " making dinner, or just trying to wrap your head around the future of humanity,", "tokens": [50618, 1455, 6148, 11, 420, 445, 1382, 281, 7019, 428, 1378, 926, 264, 2027, 295, 10243, 11, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645983937960952, "compression_ratio": 1.5639344262295083, "no_speech_prob": 1.629993340822311e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 11506, "start": 124.28, "end": 126.98, "text": " we are going to explore a mind-bending paper", "tokens": [50826, 321, 366, 516, 281, 6839, 257, 1575, 12, 65, 2029, 3035, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645983937960952, "compression_ratio": 1.5639344262295083, "no_speech_prob": 1.629993340822311e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 11506, "start": 126.98, "end": 129.58, "text": " from an independent researcher known as Flixian.", "tokens": [50961, 490, 364, 6695, 21751, 2570, 382, 3235, 970, 952, 13, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645983937960952, "compression_ratio": 1.5639344262295083, "no_speech_prob": 1.629993340822311e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 11506, "start": 129.7, "end": 129.96, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51097, 1779, 13, 51110], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645983937960952, "compression_ratio": 1.5639344262295083, "no_speech_prob": 1.629993340822311e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 11506, "start": 130.38, "end": 131.88, "text": " It's dated July 2026,", "tokens": [51131, 467, 311, 23804, 7370, 945, 10880, 11, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645983937960952, "compression_ratio": 1.5639344262295083, "no_speech_prob": 1.629993340822311e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 11506, "start": 132.08, "end": 134.64000000000001, "text": " and it's called the Orthodromic Infrastructure Blueprint.", "tokens": [51216, 293, 309, 311, 1219, 264, 27554, 378, 4397, 299, 38425, 2885, 2177, 29017, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645983937960952, "compression_ratio": 1.5639344262295083, "no_speech_prob": 1.629993340822311e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 11506, "start": 135.1, "end": 138.1, "text": " And I think it is vital to establish right at the top", "tokens": [51367, 400, 286, 519, 309, 307, 11707, 281, 8327, 558, 412, 264, 1192, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645983937960952, "compression_ratio": 1.5639344262295083, "no_speech_prob": 1.629993340822311e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 11506, "start": 138.1, "end": 141.58, "text": " what this blueprint is, what it is not.", "tokens": [51517, 437, 341, 35868, 307, 11, 437, 309, 307, 406, 13, 51691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645983937960952, "compression_ratio": 1.5639344262295083, "no_speech_prob": 1.629993340822311e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 11506, "start": 141.72, "end": 142.14000000000001, "text": " Oh, definitely.", "tokens": [51698, 876, 11, 2138, 13, 51719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1645983937960952, "compression_ratio": 1.5639344262295083, "no_speech_prob": 1.629993340822311e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 14214, "start": 142.14, "end": 145.73999999999998, "text": " We are not talking about blueprints for a new high-speed rail line here.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 366, 406, 1417, 466, 888, 23547, 47523, 337, 257, 777, 1090, 12, 22746, 8765, 1622, 510, 13, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14709491877592812, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.585886370142342e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 14214, "start": 145.79999999999998, "end": 146.79999999999998, "text": " Right. It's not a train track.", "tokens": [50548, 1779, 13, 467, 311, 406, 257, 3847, 2837, 13, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14709491877592812, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.585886370142342e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 14214, "start": 147.04, "end": 147.45999999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50610, 7587, 13, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14709491877592812, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.585886370142342e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 14214, "start": 147.64, "end": 151.55999999999997, "text": " We aren't talking about how to construct a better water pipeline", "tokens": [50640, 492, 3212, 380, 1417, 466, 577, 281, 7690, 257, 1101, 1281, 15517, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14709491877592812, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.585886370142342e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 14214, "start": 151.55999999999997, "end": 154.57999999999998, "text": " or, you know, a safer nuclear power grid.", "tokens": [50836, 420, 11, 291, 458, 11, 257, 15856, 8179, 1347, 10748, 13, 50987], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14709491877592812, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.585886370142342e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 14214, "start": 154.66, "end": 156.67999999999998, "text": " So what are we actually looking at, then?", "tokens": [50991, 407, 437, 366, 321, 767, 1237, 412, 11, 550, 30, 51092], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14709491877592812, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.585886370142342e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 14214, "start": 157.1, "end": 161.56, "text": " We are looking at a mathematical and architectural specification", "tokens": [51113, 492, 366, 1237, 412, 257, 18894, 293, 26621, 31256, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14709491877592812, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.585886370142342e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 14214, "start": 161.56, "end": 165.27999999999997, "text": " for a planetary-scale infrastructure system.", "tokens": [51336, 337, 257, 35788, 12, 20033, 6896, 1185, 13, 51522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14709491877592812, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.585886370142342e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 14214, "start": 165.6, "end": 166.04, "text": " Planetary.", "tokens": [51538, 22146, 822, 13, 51560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14709491877592812, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.585886370142342e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 14214, "start": 166.2, "end": 167.2, "text": " Yes, planetary.", "tokens": [51568, 1079, 11, 35788, 13, 51618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14709491877592812, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.585886370142342e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 14214, "start": 167.66, "end": 169.79999999999998, "text": " One designed from the ground up to last,", "tokens": [51641, 1485, 4761, 490, 264, 2727, 493, 281, 1036, 11, 51748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14709491877592812, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.585886370142342e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 14214, "start": 169.79999999999998, "end": 171.95999999999998, "text": " not just for decades, but across centuries.", "tokens": [51748, 406, 445, 337, 7878, 11, 457, 2108, 13926, 13, 51856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14709491877592812, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.585886370142342e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 17214, "start": 172.14, "end": 172.61999999999998, "text": " Centuries.", "tokens": [50365, 3408, 8318, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 17214, "start": 173.05999999999997, "end": 173.5, "text": " Plural.", "tokens": [50411, 2149, 1807, 13, 50433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 17214, "start": 174.0, "end": 175.64, "text": " I mean, we are talking about a system", "tokens": [50458, 286, 914, 11, 321, 366, 1417, 466, 257, 1185, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 17214, "start": 175.64, "end": 179.29999999999998, "text": " that will outlive the countries that literally build it.", "tokens": [50540, 300, 486, 484, 45273, 264, 3517, 300, 3736, 1322, 309, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 17214, "start": 179.38, "end": 179.85999999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50727, 7587, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 17214, "start": 180.01999999999998, "end": 182.23999999999998, "text": " But how do you even begin to plan something like that?", "tokens": [50759, 583, 577, 360, 291, 754, 1841, 281, 1393, 746, 411, 300, 30, 50870], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 17214, "start": 182.27999999999997, "end": 183.23999999999998, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this.", "tokens": [50872, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 17214, "start": 183.55999999999997, "end": 185.23999999999998, "text": " Because the very first thing the blueprint does", "tokens": [50936, 1436, 264, 588, 700, 551, 264, 35868, 775, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 17214, "start": 185.23999999999998, "end": 188.6, "text": " is completely tear down our normal definition", "tokens": [51020, 307, 2584, 12556, 760, 527, 2710, 7123, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 17214, "start": 188.6, "end": 189.94, "text": " of a construction project.", "tokens": [51188, 295, 257, 6435, 1716, 13, 51255], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 17214, "start": 190.07999999999998, "end": 191.7, "text": " It really throws out the whole playbook.", "tokens": [51262, 467, 534, 19251, 484, 264, 1379, 862, 2939, 13, 51343], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 17214, "start": 191.79999999999998, "end": 191.98, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51348, 1779, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 17214, "start": 192.16, "end": 194.27999999999997, "text": " Usually when we build something, say a bridge,", "tokens": [51366, 11419, 562, 321, 1322, 746, 11, 584, 257, 7283, 11, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 17214, "start": 194.42, "end": 195.88, "text": " we care about the concrete, right?", "tokens": [51479, 321, 1127, 466, 264, 9859, 11, 558, 30, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 17214, "start": 195.88, "end": 198.11999999999998, "text": " We care about the steel cables, the asphalt.", "tokens": [51552, 492, 1127, 466, 264, 8269, 17555, 11, 264, 46076, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17337504677150561, "compression_ratio": 1.6221498371335505, "no_speech_prob": 1.402282912184305e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 19812, "start": 198.12, "end": 200.04, "text": " We care about the physical machines.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1127, 466, 264, 4001, 8379, 13, 50461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 19812, "start": 200.24, "end": 200.88, "text": " Sure, the materials.", "tokens": [50471, 4894, 11, 264, 5319, 13, 50503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 19812, "start": 201.34, "end": 205.1, "text": " But this blueprint says, you know, forget the machine.", "tokens": [50526, 583, 341, 35868, 1619, 11, 291, 458, 11, 2870, 264, 3479, 13, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 19812, "start": 205.74, "end": 206.98000000000002, "text": " We aren't building machines.", "tokens": [50746, 492, 3212, 380, 2390, 8379, 13, 50808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 19812, "start": 207.38, "end": 209.04, "text": " We are building spatial relationships.", "tokens": [50828, 492, 366, 2390, 23598, 6159, 13, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 19812, "start": 209.64000000000001, "end": 209.84, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50941, 865, 13, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 19812, "start": 210.08, "end": 213.14000000000001, "text": " The paper draws this incredibly hard,", "tokens": [50963, 440, 3035, 20045, 341, 6252, 1152, 11, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 19812, "start": 213.34, "end": 215.5, "text": " unforgiving line between two concepts.", "tokens": [51126, 31411, 15441, 1622, 1296, 732, 10392, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 19812, "start": 215.68, "end": 215.82, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51243, 1033, 13, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 19812, "start": 216.08, "end": 216.44, "text": " What are they?", "tokens": [51263, 708, 366, 436, 30, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 19812, "start": 216.54000000000002, "end": 218.8, "text": " The physical implementation and the corridor.", "tokens": [51286, 440, 4001, 11420, 293, 264, 25602, 13, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 19812, "start": 219.14000000000001, "end": 220.32, "text": " Implementation versus corridor.", "tokens": [51416, 4331, 781, 19631, 5717, 25602, 13, 51475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 19812, "start": 220.5, "end": 220.92000000000002, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51484, 7587, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 19812, "start": 221.12, "end": 222.9, "text": " The implementation is whatever technology", "tokens": [51515, 440, 11420, 307, 2035, 2899, 51604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 19812, "start": 222.9, "end": 224.78, "text": " you just happen to be using at the time.", "tokens": [51604, 291, 445, 1051, 281, 312, 1228, 412, 264, 565, 13, 51698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2207947254180908, "compression_ratio": 1.687732342007435, "no_speech_prob": 1.573304746031734e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 22478, "start": 224.78, "end": 227.5, "text": " Like whatever we have right now in 2026.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 2035, 321, 362, 558, 586, 294, 945, 10880, 13, 50501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 22478, "start": 227.9, "end": 228.04, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50521, 1779, 13, 50528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 22478, "start": 228.26, "end": 230.7, "text": " Today, that might be a concrete water pipe", "tokens": [50539, 2692, 11, 300, 1062, 312, 257, 9859, 1281, 11240, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 22478, "start": 230.7, "end": 233.08, "text": " or, I don't know, a magnetic levitation train.", "tokens": [50661, 420, 11, 286, 500, 380, 458, 11, 257, 12688, 20445, 4614, 3847, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 22478, "start": 233.56, "end": 236.32, "text": " Tomorrow, it might be an evacuated hyperloop tube", "tokens": [50804, 17499, 11, 309, 1062, 312, 364, 20245, 27275, 9848, 46623, 9917, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 22478, "start": 236.32, "end": 238.12, "text": " or a geothermal tap.", "tokens": [50942, 420, 257, 1519, 47280, 5119, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 22478, "start": 238.22, "end": 238.38, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51037, 1779, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 22478, "start": 238.44, "end": 238.88, "text": " It changes.", "tokens": [51048, 467, 2962, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 22478, "start": 239.12, "end": 239.86, "text": " It always changes.", "tokens": [51082, 467, 1009, 2962, 13, 51119], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 22478, "start": 240.3, "end": 242.46, "text": " So the blueprint fundamentally does not care", "tokens": [51141, 407, 264, 35868, 17879, 775, 406, 1127, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 22478, "start": 242.46, "end": 243.4, "text": " about your technology.", "tokens": [51249, 466, 428, 2899, 13, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 22478, "start": 243.54, "end": 244.62, "text": " It cares about the corridor.", "tokens": [51303, 467, 12310, 466, 264, 25602, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 22478, "start": 244.84, "end": 245.58, "text": " The reserved space.", "tokens": [51368, 440, 24819, 1901, 13, 51405], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 22478, "start": 245.74, "end": 246.04, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51413, 1079, 13, 51428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 22478, "start": 246.2, "end": 248.7, "text": " The corridor is just a reserved spatial volume.", "tokens": [51436, 440, 25602, 307, 445, 257, 24819, 23598, 5523, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 22478, "start": 248.86, "end": 249.92000000000002, "text": " It is pure geometry.", "tokens": [51569, 467, 307, 6075, 18426, 13, 51622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 22478, "start": 250.16, "end": 250.46, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51634, 3153, 13, 51649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1851314968532986, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920843202815727e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 25046, "start": 250.46, "end": 254.62, "text": " And the author explicitly states that the invariant element,", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 3793, 20803, 4368, 300, 264, 33270, 394, 4478, 11, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1539421404822398, "compression_ratio": 1.6227758007117439, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764388472538364e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 25046, "start": 254.92000000000002, "end": 256.86, "text": " the thing that must never, ever change,", "tokens": [50588, 264, 551, 300, 1633, 1128, 11, 1562, 1319, 11, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1539421404822398, "compression_ratio": 1.6227758007117439, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764388472538364e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 25046, "start": 257.18, "end": 259.46000000000004, "text": " is the geometric and topological relationship", "tokens": [50701, 307, 264, 33246, 293, 1192, 4383, 2480, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1539421404822398, "compression_ratio": 1.6227758007117439, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764388472538364e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 25046, "start": 259.46000000000004, "end": 261.62, "text": " among those corridors, nodes, and interfaces.", "tokens": [50815, 3654, 729, 46920, 11, 13891, 11, 293, 28416, 13, 50923], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1539421404822398, "compression_ratio": 1.6227758007117439, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764388472538364e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 25046, "start": 261.94, "end": 263.38, "text": " So it's about holding the space.", "tokens": [50939, 407, 309, 311, 466, 5061, 264, 1901, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1539421404822398, "compression_ratio": 1.6227758007117439, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764388472538364e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 25046, "start": 263.76, "end": 264.24, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51030, 7587, 13, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1539421404822398, "compression_ratio": 1.6227758007117439, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764388472538364e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 25046, "start": 264.82, "end": 267.5, "text": " This paper is ultimately about solving a deep problem", "tokens": [51083, 639, 3035, 307, 6284, 466, 12606, 257, 2452, 1154, 51217], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1539421404822398, "compression_ratio": 1.6227758007117439, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764388472538364e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 25046, "start": 267.5, "end": 269.34000000000003, "text": " of human coordination over time.", "tokens": [51217, 295, 1952, 21252, 670, 565, 13, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1539421404822398, "compression_ratio": 1.6227758007117439, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764388472538364e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 25046, "start": 269.66, "end": 270.94, "text": " It is a protocol.", "tokens": [51325, 467, 307, 257, 10336, 13, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1539421404822398, "compression_ratio": 1.6227758007117439, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764388472538364e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 25046, "start": 271.14, "end": 272.42, "text": " A protocol, like for computers.", "tokens": [51399, 316, 10336, 11, 411, 337, 10807, 13, 51463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1539421404822398, "compression_ratio": 1.6227758007117439, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764388472538364e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 25046, "start": 272.76, "end": 273.56, "text": " Exactly like that.", "tokens": [51480, 7587, 411, 300, 13, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1539421404822398, "compression_ratio": 1.6227758007117439, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764388472538364e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 25046, "start": 273.68, "end": 273.88, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51526, 1779, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1539421404822398, "compression_ratio": 1.6227758007117439, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764388472538364e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 25046, "start": 273.98, "end": 276.58, "text": " It's laying down a framework to ensure that a civilization", "tokens": [51541, 467, 311, 14903, 760, 257, 8388, 281, 5586, 300, 257, 18036, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1539421404822398, "compression_ratio": 1.6227758007117439, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764388472538364e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 27658, "start": 276.58, "end": 281.28, "text": " in the 22nd or 23rd century can plug their highly advanced,", "tokens": [50365, 294, 264, 5853, 273, 420, 6673, 7800, 4901, 393, 5452, 641, 5405, 7339, 11, 50600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15154225373071087, "compression_ratio": 1.5364238410596027, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729477592043e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 27658, "start": 281.5, "end": 285.4, "text": " unimaginable tech into the exact same physical corridors", "tokens": [50611, 517, 44976, 712, 7553, 666, 264, 1900, 912, 4001, 46920, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15154225373071087, "compression_ratio": 1.5364238410596027, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729477592043e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 27658, "start": 285.4, "end": 288.2, "text": " laid out by a civilization in the 21st century.", "tokens": [50806, 9897, 484, 538, 257, 18036, 294, 264, 5080, 372, 4901, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15154225373071087, "compression_ratio": 1.5364238410596027, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729477592043e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 27658, "start": 288.44, "end": 291.21999999999997, "text": " I was really trying to wrap my head around this concept of,", "tokens": [50958, 286, 390, 534, 1382, 281, 7019, 452, 1378, 926, 341, 3410, 295, 11, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15154225373071087, "compression_ratio": 1.5364238410596027, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729477592043e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 27658, "start": 291.53999999999996, "end": 293.97999999999996, "text": " you know, separating the space from the technology.", "tokens": [51113, 291, 458, 11, 29279, 264, 1901, 490, 264, 2899, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15154225373071087, "compression_ratio": 1.5364238410596027, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729477592043e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 27658, "start": 294.52, "end": 297.0, "text": " And I immediately thought of the Manhattan City grid in New York.", "tokens": [51262, 400, 286, 4258, 1194, 295, 264, 23633, 4392, 10748, 294, 1873, 3609, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15154225373071087, "compression_ratio": 1.5364238410596027, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729477592043e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 27658, "start": 297.09999999999997, "end": 298.26, "text": " Oh, that's a brilliant example.", "tokens": [51391, 876, 11, 300, 311, 257, 10248, 1365, 13, 51449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15154225373071087, "compression_ratio": 1.5364238410596027, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729477592043e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 27658, "start": 298.46, "end": 298.68, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51459, 1779, 13, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15154225373071087, "compression_ratio": 1.5364238410596027, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729477592043e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 27658, "start": 299.02, "end": 300.21999999999997, "text": " If you go back to 1811,", "tokens": [51487, 759, 291, 352, 646, 281, 2443, 5348, 11, 51547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15154225373071087, "compression_ratio": 1.5364238410596027, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729477592043e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 27658, "start": 300.64, "end": 303.96, "text": " the city commissioners laid out this massive abstract grid", "tokens": [51568, 264, 2307, 9221, 433, 9897, 484, 341, 5994, 12649, 10748, 51734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15154225373071087, "compression_ratio": 1.5364238410596027, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729477592043e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 30396, "start": 303.96, "end": 309.53999999999996, "text": " of streets and avenues over what was mostly just farmland and swamps.", "tokens": [50365, 295, 8481, 293, 43039, 670, 437, 390, 5240, 445, 5421, 1661, 293, 1693, 23150, 13, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15138572692871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5684931506849316, "no_speech_prob": 1.383241069428942e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 30396, "start": 309.7, "end": 311.58, "text": " Yeah, mostly just rocks and mud at that point.", "tokens": [50652, 865, 11, 5240, 445, 10989, 293, 8933, 412, 300, 935, 13, 50746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15138572692871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5684931506849316, "no_speech_prob": 1.383241069428942e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 30396, "start": 311.65999999999997, "end": 311.94, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50750, 7587, 13, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15138572692871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5684931506849316, "no_speech_prob": 1.383241069428942e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 30396, "start": 312.21999999999997, "end": 314.26, "text": " And they had absolutely no idea what the future held.", "tokens": [50778, 400, 436, 632, 3122, 572, 1558, 437, 264, 2027, 5167, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15138572692871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5684931506849316, "no_speech_prob": 1.383241069428942e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 30396, "start": 314.32, "end": 314.76, "text": " None at all.", "tokens": [50883, 14492, 412, 439, 13, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15138572692871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5684931506849316, "no_speech_prob": 1.383241069428942e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 30396, "start": 314.84, "end": 317.35999999999996, "text": " I mean, the commissioners of 1811 were designing for a world", "tokens": [50909, 286, 914, 11, 264, 9221, 433, 295, 2443, 5348, 645, 14685, 337, 257, 1002, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15138572692871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5684931506849316, "no_speech_prob": 1.383241069428942e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 30396, "start": 317.35999999999996, "end": 319.79999999999995, "text": " of horse-drawn carriages, dirt roads,", "tokens": [51035, 295, 6832, 12, 67, 29603, 1032, 30891, 11, 11483, 11344, 11, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15138572692871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5684931506849316, "no_speech_prob": 1.383241069428942e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 30396, "start": 320.02, "end": 322.21999999999997, "text": " maybe some early steam power if they were visionary.", "tokens": [51168, 1310, 512, 2440, 11952, 1347, 498, 436, 645, 49442, 13, 51278], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15138572692871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5684931506849316, "no_speech_prob": 1.383241069428942e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 30396, "start": 322.7, "end": 322.96, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51302, 1779, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15138572692871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5684931506849316, "no_speech_prob": 1.383241069428942e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 30396, "start": 323.38, "end": 326.64, "text": " But because they laid down a rigid spatial protocol,", "tokens": [51336, 583, 570, 436, 9897, 760, 257, 22195, 23598, 10336, 11, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15138572692871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5684931506849316, "no_speech_prob": 1.383241069428942e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 30396, "start": 327.09999999999997, "end": 330.82, "text": " this strict grid of right angles and specific widths,", "tokens": [51522, 341, 10910, 10748, 295, 558, 14708, 293, 2685, 11402, 82, 11, 51708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15138572692871094, "compression_ratio": 1.5684931506849316, "no_speech_prob": 1.383241069428942e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 33082, "start": 330.82, "end": 335.4, "text": " that same exact abstract framework adapted to everything that came later.", "tokens": [50365, 300, 912, 1900, 12649, 8388, 20871, 281, 1203, 300, 1361, 1780, 13, 50594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 33082, "start": 335.46, "end": 337.32, "text": " It just absorbed the new technology.", "tokens": [50597, 467, 445, 20799, 264, 777, 2899, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 33082, "start": 337.56, "end": 337.9, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50702, 7587, 13, 50719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 33082, "start": 338.15999999999997, "end": 339.3, "text": " It handled cobblestones.", "tokens": [50732, 467, 18033, 39527, 5199, 34853, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 33082, "start": 339.5, "end": 339.7, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50799, 865, 13, 50809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 33082, "start": 339.86, "end": 342.2, "text": " Then it handled the Model T Ford on asphalt.", "tokens": [50817, 1396, 309, 18033, 264, 17105, 314, 11961, 322, 46076, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 33082, "start": 342.68, "end": 346.78, "text": " Then it handled massive modern electric cars and skyscrapers.", "tokens": [50958, 1396, 309, 18033, 5994, 4363, 5210, 5163, 293, 48227, 66, 4007, 433, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 33082, "start": 346.84, "end": 347.5, "text": " And the subways.", "tokens": [51166, 400, 264, 1422, 942, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 33082, "start": 347.8, "end": 348.08, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51214, 1079, 13, 51228], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 33082, "start": 348.44, "end": 351.28, "text": " And most importantly, it allowed for subways to be dug underneath.", "tokens": [51246, 400, 881, 8906, 11, 309, 4350, 337, 1422, 942, 281, 312, 22954, 7223, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 33082, "start": 351.78, "end": 353.28, "text": " The founders in 1811,", "tokens": [51413, 440, 25608, 294, 2443, 5348, 11, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 33082, "start": 353.5, "end": 356.48, "text": " they didn't mandate the technology that would eventually run on their avenues.", "tokens": [51499, 436, 994, 380, 23885, 264, 2899, 300, 576, 4728, 1190, 322, 641, 43039, 13, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 33082, "start": 356.7, "end": 356.88, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51659, 865, 13, 51668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 33082, "start": 356.88, "end": 358.68, "text": " They just legally mandated the space.", "tokens": [51668, 814, 445, 21106, 47563, 264, 1901, 13, 51758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 33082, "start": 358.76, "end": 359.58, "text": " They protected the corridor.", "tokens": [51762, 814, 10594, 264, 25602, 13, 51803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20468401737350353, "compression_ratio": 1.74496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 1.6077181903481619e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 35958, "start": 359.58, "end": 360.76, "text": " They protected the corridor.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 10594, 264, 25602, 13, 50424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 35958, "start": 361.08, "end": 364.41999999999996, "text": " The Manhattan analogy is a fantastic way to conceptualize it.", "tokens": [50440, 440, 23633, 21663, 307, 257, 5456, 636, 281, 24106, 1125, 309, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 35958, "start": 364.46, "end": 365.21999999999997, "text": " Though I will say,", "tokens": [50609, 10404, 286, 486, 584, 11, 50647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 35958, "start": 365.53999999999996, "end": 367.8, "text": " the blueprint we are discussing takes that logic", "tokens": [50663, 264, 35868, 321, 366, 10850, 2516, 300, 9952, 50776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 35958, "start": 367.8, "end": 370.91999999999996, "text": " to a planetary mathematically formalized extreme.", "tokens": [50776, 281, 257, 35788, 44003, 9860, 1602, 8084, 13, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 35958, "start": 371.24, "end": 371.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50948, 1779, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 35958, "start": 371.59999999999997, "end": 373.0, "text": " Because Manhattan is just one island.", "tokens": [50966, 1436, 23633, 307, 445, 472, 6077, 13, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 35958, "start": 373.21999999999997, "end": 373.65999999999997, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51047, 7587, 13, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 35958, "start": 373.94, "end": 376.88, "text": " And the paper even provides a strict mathematical formulation", "tokens": [51083, 400, 264, 3035, 754, 6417, 257, 10910, 18894, 37642, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 35958, "start": 376.88, "end": 379.88, "text": " for this idea of intergenerational compatibility.", "tokens": [51230, 337, 341, 1558, 295, 728, 21848, 1478, 34237, 13, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 35958, "start": 380.14, "end": 380.46, "text": " Oh yeah.", "tokens": [51393, 876, 1338, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 35958, "start": 380.56, "end": 381.97999999999996, "text": " The math in this thing is intense.", "tokens": [51414, 440, 5221, 294, 341, 551, 307, 9447, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 35958, "start": 382.36, "end": 382.78, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51504, 467, 307, 13, 51525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 35958, "start": 382.94, "end": 385.76, "text": " Now, without getting bogged down in reading formulas on the air,", "tokens": [51533, 823, 11, 1553, 1242, 26132, 3004, 760, 294, 3760, 30546, 322, 264, 1988, 11, 51674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 35958, "start": 385.88, "end": 387.78, "text": " the logic is incredibly elegant.", "tokens": [51680, 264, 9952, 307, 6252, 21117, 13, 51775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1594441062525699, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640798350274e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 38778, "start": 387.78, "end": 392.82, "text": " Think about how frustrating it is when a technology company changes the shape of a charging cable.", "tokens": [50365, 6557, 466, 577, 16522, 309, 307, 562, 257, 2899, 2237, 2962, 264, 3909, 295, 257, 11379, 8220, 13, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16079471376207138, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689084788954923e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 38778, "start": 392.85999999999996, "end": 394.32, "text": " Oh, it is the absolute worst.", "tokens": [50619, 876, 11, 309, 307, 264, 8236, 5855, 13, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16079471376207138, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689084788954923e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 38778, "start": 394.46, "end": 394.64, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50699, 1779, 13, 50708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16079471376207138, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689084788954923e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 38778, "start": 394.78, "end": 398.79999999999995, "text": " You have a drawer full of perfectly good electronics that are essentially bricks,", "tokens": [50715, 509, 362, 257, 24039, 1577, 295, 6239, 665, 20611, 300, 366, 4476, 25497, 11, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16079471376207138, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689084788954923e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 38778, "start": 399.0, "end": 401.5, "text": " because, you know, the new plug doesn't fit the old port.", "tokens": [50926, 570, 11, 291, 458, 11, 264, 777, 5452, 1177, 380, 3318, 264, 1331, 2436, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16079471376207138, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689084788954923e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 38778, "start": 401.96, "end": 402.44, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51074, 48746, 736, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16079471376207138, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689084788954923e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 38778, "start": 402.88, "end": 406.67999999999995, "text": " Now, scale that frustration up to a planetary water and power grid.", "tokens": [51120, 823, 11, 4373, 300, 20491, 493, 281, 257, 35788, 1281, 293, 1347, 10748, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16079471376207138, "compression_ratio": 1.51931330472103, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689084788954923e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 40668, "start": 406.68, "end": 407.6, "text": " Oh, man.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 587, 13, 50411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22759785763053006, "compression_ratio": 1.4227272727272726, "no_speech_prob": 2.4272190160545826e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 40668, "start": 407.8, "end": 407.94, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50421, 1779, 13, 50428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22759785763053006, "compression_ratio": 1.4227272727272726, "no_speech_prob": 2.4272190160545826e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 40668, "start": 408.3, "end": 415.0, "text": " If we pour a trillion tons of concrete today to build a massive global pipeline,", "tokens": [50446, 759, 321, 2016, 257, 18723, 9131, 295, 9859, 965, 281, 1322, 257, 5994, 4338, 15517, 11, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22759785763053006, "compression_ratio": 1.4227272727272726, "no_speech_prob": 2.4272190160545826e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 40668, "start": 415.28000000000003, "end": 418.54, "text": " and we optimize it perfectly for 2026 technology,", "tokens": [50795, 293, 321, 19719, 309, 6239, 337, 945, 10880, 2899, 11, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22759785763053006, "compression_ratio": 1.4227272727272726, "no_speech_prob": 2.4272190160545826e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 40668, "start": 418.86, "end": 424.24, "text": " we are basically forcing the year 2300 to use our outdated charging cable.", "tokens": [50974, 321, 366, 1936, 19030, 264, 1064, 6673, 628, 281, 764, 527, 36313, 11379, 8220, 13, 51243], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22759785763053006, "compression_ratio": 1.4227272727272726, "no_speech_prob": 2.4272190160545826e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 40668, "start": 424.32, "end": 425.22, "text": " We'd be trapping them.", "tokens": [51247, 492, 1116, 312, 944, 3759, 552, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22759785763053006, "compression_ratio": 1.4227272727272726, "no_speech_prob": 2.4272190160545826e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 40668, "start": 425.42, "end": 425.84000000000003, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51302, 7587, 13, 51323], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22759785763053006, "compression_ratio": 1.4227272727272726, "no_speech_prob": 2.4272190160545826e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 40668, "start": 426.32, "end": 429.54, "text": " The blueprint uses a mathematical shorthand to forbid this.", "tokens": [51347, 440, 35868, 4960, 257, 18894, 402, 2652, 474, 281, 34117, 341, 13, 51508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22759785763053006, "compression_ratio": 1.4227272727272726, "no_speech_prob": 2.4272190160545826e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 42954, "start": 429.54, "end": 433.64000000000004, "text": " It essentially states that the goal is not to clone the technology.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 4476, 4368, 300, 264, 3387, 307, 406, 281, 26506, 264, 2899, 13, 50570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1477349786197438, "compression_ratio": 1.6480446927374302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754377612186345e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 42954, "start": 434.28000000000003, "end": 437.46000000000004, "text": " Implementation B does not need to equal implementation A.", "tokens": [50602, 4331, 781, 19631, 363, 775, 406, 643, 281, 2681, 11420, 316, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1477349786197438, "compression_ratio": 1.6480446927374302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754377612186345e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 42954, "start": 437.96000000000004, "end": 443.84000000000003, "text": " Instead, it says implementation B must be compatible with implementation A under the rules of the spatial protocol.", "tokens": [50786, 7156, 11, 309, 1619, 11420, 363, 1633, 312, 18218, 365, 11420, 316, 833, 264, 4474, 295, 264, 23598, 10336, 13, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1477349786197438, "compression_ratio": 1.6480446927374302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754377612186345e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 42954, "start": 444.08000000000004, "end": 446.78000000000003, "text": " So the new puzzle piece just has to fit the old slot.", "tokens": [51092, 407, 264, 777, 12805, 2522, 445, 575, 281, 3318, 264, 1331, 14747, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1477349786197438, "compression_ratio": 1.6480446927374302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754377612186345e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 44678, "start": 446.78, "end": 448.67999999999995, "text": " That is the perfect way to phrase it.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 264, 2176, 636, 281, 9535, 309, 13, 50460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14534408054994732, "compression_ratio": 1.6597510373443984, "no_speech_prob": 2.584362194732459e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 44678, "start": 449.26, "end": 454.59999999999997, "text": " There must exist a finite sequence of permitted adapters or replacement operations", "tokens": [50489, 821, 1633, 2514, 257, 19362, 8310, 295, 28658, 23169, 1559, 420, 14419, 7705, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14534408054994732, "compression_ratio": 1.6597510373443984, "no_speech_prob": 2.584362194732459e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 44678, "start": 454.59999999999997, "end": 461.11999999999995, "text": " that joins the new tech to the old tech without violating the protected spatial volume of the corridor.", "tokens": [50756, 300, 24397, 264, 777, 7553, 281, 264, 1331, 7553, 1553, 42201, 264, 10594, 23598, 5523, 295, 264, 25602, 13, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14534408054994732, "compression_ratio": 1.6597510373443984, "no_speech_prob": 2.584362194732459e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 44678, "start": 461.41999999999996, "end": 462.38, "text": " That makes total sense.", "tokens": [51097, 663, 1669, 3217, 2020, 13, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14534408054994732, "compression_ratio": 1.6597510373443984, "no_speech_prob": 2.584362194732459e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 44678, "start": 462.59999999999997, "end": 465.96, "text": " This prevents the hubris of premature optimization.", "tokens": [51156, 639, 22367, 264, 11838, 5714, 295, 34877, 19618, 13, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14534408054994732, "compression_ratio": 1.6597510373443984, "no_speech_prob": 2.584362194732459e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 44678, "start": 466.55999999999995, "end": 467.79999999999995, "text": " We aren't freezing technology.", "tokens": [51354, 492, 3212, 380, 20200, 2899, 13, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14534408054994732, "compression_ratio": 1.6597510373443984, "no_speech_prob": 2.584362194732459e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 44678, "start": 468.08, "end": 472.52, "text": " We are creating a permanent theater for technology to evolve within.", "tokens": [51430, 492, 366, 4084, 257, 10996, 10612, 337, 2899, 281, 16693, 1951, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14534408054994732, "compression_ratio": 1.6597510373443984, "no_speech_prob": 2.584362194732459e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 47252, "start": 472.52, "end": 477.97999999999996, "text": " And to make sure this isn't just a bunch of philosophical poetry about the future,", "tokens": [50365, 400, 281, 652, 988, 341, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 3840, 295, 25066, 15155, 466, 264, 2027, 11, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0857552486917247, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556607430537329e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 47252, "start": 478.32, "end": 482.03999999999996, "text": " the blueprint uses some of the strictest semantic discipline I've ever seen.", "tokens": [50655, 264, 35868, 4960, 512, 295, 264, 10910, 377, 47982, 13635, 286, 600, 1562, 1612, 13, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0857552486917247, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556607430537329e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 47252, "start": 482.12, "end": 483.88, "text": " Oh, it is incredibly rigorous.", "tokens": [50845, 876, 11, 309, 307, 6252, 29882, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0857552486917247, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556607430537329e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 47252, "start": 484.12, "end": 487.41999999999996, "text": " It reads like a binding legal contract mixed with the physics textbook.", "tokens": [50945, 467, 15700, 411, 257, 17359, 5089, 4364, 7467, 365, 264, 10649, 25591, 13, 51110], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0857552486917247, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556607430537329e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 47252, "start": 488.15999999999997, "end": 493.53999999999996, "text": " There is a whole section detailing the exact difference between the words shall, should, and may.", "tokens": [51147, 821, 307, 257, 1379, 3541, 42459, 264, 1900, 2649, 1296, 264, 2283, 4393, 11, 820, 11, 293, 815, 13, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0857552486917247, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556607430537329e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 47252, "start": 493.64, "end": 497.0, "text": " Which is absolutely vital for any serious engineering specification.", "tokens": [51421, 3013, 307, 3122, 11707, 337, 604, 3156, 7043, 31256, 13, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0857552486917247, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556607430537329e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 47252, "start": 497.32, "end": 501.68, "text": " I mean, words have to mean something concrete when you are coordinating across continents and centuries.", "tokens": [51605, 286, 914, 11, 2283, 362, 281, 914, 746, 9859, 562, 291, 366, 37824, 2108, 38598, 293, 13926, 13, 51823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0857552486917247, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556607430537329e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 50168, "start": 501.68, "end": 504.48, "text": " So shall means it is a mandatory condition, right?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 4393, 1355, 309, 307, 257, 22173, 4188, 11, 558, 30, 50505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17168913737382038, "compression_ratio": 1.562015503875969, "no_speech_prob": 2.0685439038742315e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 50168, "start": 504.56, "end": 506.14, "text": " You have to do it to comply with the blueprint.", "tokens": [50509, 509, 362, 281, 360, 309, 281, 27956, 365, 264, 35868, 13, 50588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17168913737382038, "compression_ratio": 1.562015503875969, "no_speech_prob": 2.0685439038742315e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 50168, "start": 506.36, "end": 506.46, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50599, 1779, 13, 50604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17168913737382038, "compression_ratio": 1.562015503875969, "no_speech_prob": 2.0685439038742315e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 50168, "start": 506.84000000000003, "end": 511.92, "text": " Should is a strong recommendation, but you can deviate if you have, like, documented justification.", "tokens": [50623, 6454, 307, 257, 2068, 11879, 11, 457, 291, 393, 1905, 13024, 498, 291, 362, 11, 411, 11, 23007, 31591, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17168913737382038, "compression_ratio": 1.562015503875969, "no_speech_prob": 2.0685439038742315e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 50168, "start": 512.62, "end": 514.76, "text": " And may is just completely optional.", "tokens": [50912, 400, 815, 307, 445, 2584, 17312, 13, 51019], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17168913737382038, "compression_ratio": 1.562015503875969, "no_speech_prob": 2.0685439038742315e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 50168, "start": 515.02, "end": 515.48, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51032, 7587, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17168913737382038, "compression_ratio": 1.562015503875969, "no_speech_prob": 2.0685439038742315e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 50168, "start": 515.92, "end": 518.54, "text": " But here is the kicker, and I love this.", "tokens": [51077, 583, 510, 307, 264, 4437, 260, 11, 293, 286, 959, 341, 13, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17168913737382038, "compression_ratio": 1.562015503875969, "no_speech_prob": 2.0685439038742315e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 50168, "start": 519.52, "end": 527.74, "text": " The document demands that every single requirement formulated with the word shall must be physically testable.", "tokens": [51257, 440, 4166, 15107, 300, 633, 2167, 11695, 48936, 365, 264, 1349, 4393, 1633, 312, 9762, 1500, 712, 13, 51668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17168913737382038, "compression_ratio": 1.562015503875969, "no_speech_prob": 2.0685439038742315e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 52774, "start": 527.74, "end": 531.74, "text": " Yes, because if you cannot measure it, it is not an engineering specification.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 570, 498, 291, 2644, 3481, 309, 11, 309, 307, 406, 364, 7043, 31256, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16496801376342773, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 2.1588410312883832e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 52774, "start": 532.76, "end": 532.84, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50616, 1779, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16496801376342773, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 2.1588410312883832e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 52774, "start": 532.92, "end": 534.2, "text": " It is just an aspiration.", "tokens": [50624, 467, 307, 445, 364, 44565, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16496801376342773, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 2.1588410312883832e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 52774, "start": 534.88, "end": 539.32, "text": " If a protocol says the corridor shall be very safe, well, that is meaningless.", "tokens": [50722, 759, 257, 10336, 1619, 264, 25602, 4393, 312, 588, 3273, 11, 731, 11, 300, 307, 33232, 13, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16496801376342773, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 2.1588410312883832e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 52774, "start": 539.52, "end": 539.62, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50954, 1779, 13, 50959], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16496801376342773, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 2.1588410312883832e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 52774, "start": 539.76, "end": 540.82, "text": " What is safe?", "tokens": [50966, 708, 307, 3273, 30, 51019], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16496801376342773, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 2.1588410312883832e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 52774, "start": 540.94, "end": 541.24, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51025, 7587, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16496801376342773, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 2.1588410312883832e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 52774, "start": 541.78, "end": 551.9, "text": " If it instead says the structural boundary of the corridor shall withstand a localized pressure anomaly of 500 megapascals, well, that is a testable, measurable predicate.", "tokens": [51067, 759, 309, 2602, 1619, 264, 15067, 12866, 295, 264, 25602, 4393, 31311, 257, 44574, 3321, 42737, 295, 5923, 34733, 4806, 1124, 11, 731, 11, 300, 307, 257, 1500, 712, 11, 43615, 3852, 8700, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16496801376342773, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 2.1588410312883832e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 52774, "start": 552.1, "end": 553.42, "text": " You can actually build a test for that.", "tokens": [51583, 509, 393, 767, 1322, 257, 1500, 337, 300, 13, 51649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16496801376342773, "compression_ratio": 1.6744186046511629, "no_speech_prob": 2.1588410312883832e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 55342, "start": 553.42, "end": 558.3399999999999, "text": " The blueprint requires a documented decision procedure for every single mandatory rule.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 35868, 7029, 257, 23007, 3537, 10747, 337, 633, 2167, 22173, 4978, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11053015969016335, "compression_ratio": 1.549090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354611229677188e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 55342, "start": 558.42, "end": 563.0799999999999, "text": " Because hoping for the best doesn't keep a planetary hyperloop from imploding in the year 2150.", "tokens": [50615, 1436, 7159, 337, 264, 1151, 1177, 380, 1066, 257, 35788, 9848, 46623, 490, 8484, 8616, 294, 264, 1064, 5080, 2803, 13, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11053015969016335, "compression_ratio": 1.549090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354611229677188e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 55342, "start": 563.36, "end": 564.26, "text": " No, it does not.", "tokens": [50862, 883, 11, 309, 775, 406, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11053015969016335, "compression_ratio": 1.549090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354611229677188e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 55342, "start": 564.5, "end": 565.5999999999999, "text": " You need hard math.", "tokens": [50919, 509, 643, 1152, 5221, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11053015969016335, "compression_ratio": 1.549090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354611229677188e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 55342, "start": 565.74, "end": 565.9799999999999, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50981, 865, 13, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11053015969016335, "compression_ratio": 1.549090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354611229677188e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 55342, "start": 566.0999999999999, "end": 575.7199999999999, "text": " And this extreme rigor carries over into how the blueprint addresses physical reality, especially when we start talking about building models versus building the real thing.", "tokens": [50999, 400, 341, 8084, 42191, 16402, 670, 666, 577, 264, 35868, 16862, 4001, 4103, 11, 2318, 562, 321, 722, 1417, 466, 2390, 5245, 5717, 2390, 264, 957, 551, 13, 51480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11053015969016335, "compression_ratio": 1.549090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354611229677188e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 55342, "start": 575.76, "end": 575.9399999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51482, 1779, 13, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11053015969016335, "compression_ratio": 1.549090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354611229677188e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 55342, "start": 576.02, "end": 576.88, "text": " The scaling issue.", "tokens": [51495, 440, 21589, 2734, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11053015969016335, "compression_ratio": 1.549090909090909, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354611229677188e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 57688, "start": 576.88, "end": 580.5, "text": " Yeah, I was reading this section and a really basic question popped into my head.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 286, 390, 3760, 341, 3541, 293, 257, 534, 3875, 1168, 21545, 666, 452, 1378, 13, 50546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14001995451906893, "compression_ratio": 1.5827067669172932, "no_speech_prob": 1.989105494898391e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 57688, "start": 581.18, "end": 590.16, "text": " The text explicitly states that local governments or engineers can build small demonstrators, you know, regional surveys of this protocol to test it out.", "tokens": [50580, 440, 2487, 20803, 4368, 300, 2654, 11280, 420, 11955, 393, 1322, 1359, 5516, 34886, 11, 291, 458, 11, 10964, 22711, 295, 341, 10336, 281, 1500, 309, 484, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14001995451906893, "compression_ratio": 1.5827067669172932, "no_speech_prob": 1.989105494898391e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 57688, "start": 590.3, "end": 591.4399999999999, "text": " They can and they should.", "tokens": [51036, 814, 393, 293, 436, 820, 13, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14001995451906893, "compression_ratio": 1.5827067669172932, "no_speech_prob": 1.989105494898391e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 57688, "start": 591.8, "end": 595.0, "text": " You want to prove the concept locally before deploying it globally.", "tokens": [51111, 509, 528, 281, 7081, 264, 3410, 16143, 949, 34198, 309, 18958, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14001995451906893, "compression_ratio": 1.5827067669172932, "no_speech_prob": 1.989105494898391e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 57688, "start": 595.24, "end": 595.54, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51283, 1779, 13, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14001995451906893, "compression_ratio": 1.5827067669172932, "no_speech_prob": 1.989105494898391e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 57688, "start": 596.2, "end": 601.36, "text": " But the text is also incredibly strict about warning against the dangers of scaling.", "tokens": [51331, 583, 264, 2487, 307, 611, 6252, 10910, 466, 9164, 1970, 264, 27701, 295, 21589, 13, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14001995451906893, "compression_ratio": 1.5827067669172932, "no_speech_prob": 1.989105494898391e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 60136, "start": 601.36, "end": 604.48, "text": " And I'm thinking about this in terms of toys, actually.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 286, 478, 1953, 466, 341, 294, 2115, 295, 13753, 11, 767, 13, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15533326012747628, "compression_ratio": 1.599337748344371, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832402020672041e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 60136, "start": 604.48, "end": 604.9, "text": " Oh, nice.", "tokens": [50521, 876, 11, 1481, 13, 50542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15533326012747628, "compression_ratio": 1.599337748344371, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832402020672041e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 60136, "start": 605.04, "end": 605.32, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50549, 1033, 13, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15533326012747628, "compression_ratio": 1.599337748344371, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832402020672041e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 60136, "start": 605.48, "end": 605.98, "text": " Let's hear it.", "tokens": [50571, 961, 311, 1568, 309, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15533326012747628, "compression_ratio": 1.599337748344371, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832402020672041e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 60136, "start": 606.08, "end": 606.24, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50601, 865, 13, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15533326012747628, "compression_ratio": 1.599337748344371, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832402020672041e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 60136, "start": 606.36, "end": 613.54, "text": " Like, if I'm sitting on my living room floor and I build a really cool, structurally sound bridge out of standard Legos.", "tokens": [50615, 1743, 11, 498, 286, 478, 3798, 322, 452, 2647, 1808, 4123, 293, 286, 1322, 257, 534, 1627, 11, 6594, 6512, 1626, 7283, 484, 295, 3832, 7470, 329, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15533326012747628, "compression_ratio": 1.599337748344371, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832402020672041e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 60136, "start": 613.6, "end": 613.84, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50977, 1779, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15533326012747628, "compression_ratio": 1.599337748344371, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832402020672041e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 60136, "start": 614.28, "end": 622.62, "text": " Why can't I just take that exact same design, manufactured giant, building-sized Legos, and build the exact same bridge 10,000 times larger?", "tokens": [51011, 1545, 393, 380, 286, 445, 747, 300, 1900, 912, 1715, 11, 25738, 7410, 11, 2390, 12, 20614, 7470, 329, 11, 293, 1322, 264, 1900, 912, 7283, 1266, 11, 1360, 1413, 4833, 30, 51428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15533326012747628, "compression_ratio": 1.599337748344371, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832402020672041e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 60136, "start": 622.76, "end": 623.5600000000001, "text": " I mean, it works small.", "tokens": [51435, 286, 914, 11, 309, 1985, 1359, 13, 51475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15533326012747628, "compression_ratio": 1.599337748344371, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832402020672041e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 60136, "start": 623.64, "end": 624.5, "text": " Why wouldn't it work big?", "tokens": [51479, 1545, 2759, 380, 309, 589, 955, 30, 51522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15533326012747628, "compression_ratio": 1.599337748344371, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832402020672041e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 60136, "start": 624.74, "end": 628.4, "text": " It is one of the most intuitive traps in all of structural engineering.", "tokens": [51534, 467, 307, 472, 295, 264, 881, 21769, 24173, 294, 439, 295, 15067, 7043, 13, 51717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15533326012747628, "compression_ratio": 1.599337748344371, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832402020672041e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 62840, "start": 628.4, "end": 631.6999999999999, "text": " We assume that a shape is just a shape, regardless of its size.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 6552, 300, 257, 3909, 307, 445, 257, 3909, 11, 10060, 295, 1080, 2744, 13, 50530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1417862270189368, "compression_ratio": 1.6297709923664123, "no_speech_prob": 1.4666982905975345e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 62840, "start": 631.8199999999999, "end": 631.9, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50536, 1779, 13, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1417862270189368, "compression_ratio": 1.6297709923664123, "no_speech_prob": 1.4666982905975345e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 62840, "start": 631.98, "end": 632.76, "text": " A square is a square.", "tokens": [50544, 316, 3732, 307, 257, 3732, 13, 50583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1417862270189368, "compression_ratio": 1.6297709923664123, "no_speech_prob": 1.4666982905975345e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 62840, "start": 632.9, "end": 639.22, "text": " But you run headfirst into one of the most unforgiving realities of physics, which is the square cube law.", "tokens": [50590, 583, 291, 1190, 1378, 29581, 666, 472, 295, 264, 881, 31411, 15441, 27785, 295, 10649, 11, 597, 307, 264, 3732, 13728, 2101, 13, 50906], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1417862270189368, "compression_ratio": 1.6297709923664123, "no_speech_prob": 1.4666982905975345e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 62840, "start": 639.38, "end": 640.66, "text": " The square cube law.", "tokens": [50914, 440, 3732, 13728, 2101, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1417862270189368, "compression_ratio": 1.6297709923664123, "no_speech_prob": 1.4666982905975345e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 62840, "start": 640.88, "end": 641.1999999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50989, 1079, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1417862270189368, "compression_ratio": 1.6297709923664123, "no_speech_prob": 1.4666982905975345e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 62840, "start": 641.64, "end": 645.38, "text": " The laws of physics simply do not allow you to scale up those Legos.", "tokens": [51027, 440, 6064, 295, 10649, 2935, 360, 406, 2089, 291, 281, 4373, 493, 729, 7470, 329, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1417862270189368, "compression_ratio": 1.6297709923664123, "no_speech_prob": 1.4666982905975345e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 62840, "start": 645.8, "end": 646.02, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51235, 1033, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1417862270189368, "compression_ratio": 1.6297709923664123, "no_speech_prob": 1.4666982905975345e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 62840, "start": 646.18, "end": 650.76, "text": " Break that down for me, because this completely shattered my understanding of how massive structures are actually built.", "tokens": [51254, 16925, 300, 760, 337, 385, 11, 570, 341, 2584, 35209, 452, 3701, 295, 577, 5994, 9227, 366, 767, 3094, 13, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1417862270189368, "compression_ratio": 1.6297709923664123, "no_speech_prob": 1.4666982905975345e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 62840, "start": 650.84, "end": 651.0, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51487, 1033, 13, 51495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1417862270189368, "compression_ratio": 1.6297709923664123, "no_speech_prob": 1.4666982905975345e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 65100, "start": 651.0, "end": 658.72, "text": " Let's visualize a simple object, a solid cube of concrete that is exactly one meter tall, one meter wide, and one meter deep.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 23273, 257, 2199, 2657, 11, 257, 5100, 13728, 295, 9859, 300, 307, 2293, 472, 9255, 6764, 11, 472, 9255, 4874, 11, 293, 472, 9255, 2452, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852336536754263, "compression_ratio": 1.6186046511627907, "no_speech_prob": 1.610256090793516e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 65100, "start": 658.8, "end": 659.04, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50755, 1033, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852336536754263, "compression_ratio": 1.6186046511627907, "no_speech_prob": 1.610256090793516e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 65100, "start": 659.14, "end": 659.5, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [50772, 5803, 309, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852336536754263, "compression_ratio": 1.6186046511627907, "no_speech_prob": 1.610256090793516e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 65100, "start": 659.68, "end": 663.46, "text": " Now, let's say we want to scale that cube up by a factor of 10.", "tokens": [50799, 823, 11, 718, 311, 584, 321, 528, 281, 4373, 300, 13728, 493, 538, 257, 5952, 295, 1266, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852336536754263, "compression_ratio": 1.6186046511627907, "no_speech_prob": 1.610256090793516e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 65100, "start": 663.82, "end": 667.28, "text": " We want to build a version that is 10 meters on every side.", "tokens": [51006, 492, 528, 281, 1322, 257, 3037, 300, 307, 1266, 8146, 322, 633, 1252, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852336536754263, "compression_ratio": 1.6186046511627907, "no_speech_prob": 1.610256090793516e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 65100, "start": 667.42, "end": 667.72, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51186, 1033, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852336536754263, "compression_ratio": 1.6186046511627907, "no_speech_prob": 1.610256090793516e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 65100, "start": 667.82, "end": 670.06, "text": " So a 10 by 10 by 10 giant cube.", "tokens": [51206, 407, 257, 1266, 538, 1266, 538, 1266, 7410, 13728, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852336536754263, "compression_ratio": 1.6186046511627907, "no_speech_prob": 1.610256090793516e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 65100, "start": 670.22, "end": 670.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51326, 1779, 13, 51340], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852336536754263, "compression_ratio": 1.6186046511627907, "no_speech_prob": 1.610256090793516e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 65100, "start": 670.62, "end": 672.4, "text": " Now, let's look at the math of scaling.", "tokens": [51346, 823, 11, 718, 311, 574, 412, 264, 5221, 295, 21589, 13, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14852336536754263, "compression_ratio": 1.6186046511627907, "no_speech_prob": 1.610256090793516e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 67240, "start": 672.4, "end": 680.54, "text": " The mass of an object, its total volume and weight, grows by the cube of the scale factor, because, you know, it occupies three dimensions.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2758, 295, 364, 2657, 11, 1080, 3217, 5523, 293, 3364, 11, 13156, 538, 264, 13728, 295, 264, 4373, 5952, 11, 570, 11, 291, 458, 11, 309, 8073, 530, 1045, 12819, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15552930831909179, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664801491204305e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 67240, "start": 680.72, "end": 680.86, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50781, 1033, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15552930831909179, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664801491204305e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 67240, "start": 681.04, "end": 682.28, "text": " So our scale factor is 10.", "tokens": [50797, 407, 527, 4373, 5952, 307, 1266, 13, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15552930831909179, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664801491204305e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 67240, "start": 682.6, "end": 686.78, "text": " 10 to the third power, 10 times 10 times 10 is 1,000.", "tokens": [50875, 1266, 281, 264, 2636, 1347, 11, 1266, 1413, 1266, 1413, 1266, 307, 502, 11, 1360, 13, 51084], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15552930831909179, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664801491204305e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 67240, "start": 687.06, "end": 691.84, "text": " Your new giant cube is 1,000 times heavier than your original small cube.", "tokens": [51098, 2260, 777, 7410, 13728, 307, 502, 11, 1360, 1413, 18279, 813, 428, 3380, 1359, 13728, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15552930831909179, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664801491204305e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 67240, "start": 692.0, "end": 693.22, "text": " 1,000 times heavier.", "tokens": [51345, 502, 11, 1360, 1413, 18279, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15552930831909179, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664801491204305e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 67240, "start": 693.28, "end": 695.1999999999999, "text": " I mean, that's a massive jump in weight.", "tokens": [51409, 286, 914, 11, 300, 311, 257, 5994, 3012, 294, 3364, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15552930831909179, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664801491204305e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 67240, "start": 695.34, "end": 695.74, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51512, 467, 307, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15552930831909179, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664801491204305e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 67240, "start": 696.0, "end": 698.0, "text": " But here is the fatal flaw.", "tokens": [51545, 583, 510, 307, 264, 24069, 13717, 13, 51645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15552930831909179, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4664801491204305e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 69800, "start": 698.0, "end": 706.72, "text": " The cross-sectional area, the two-dimensional footprint at the bottom that has to actually support all that weight against the ground, well, that only grows by the square of the scale factor.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3278, 12, 11963, 304, 1859, 11, 264, 732, 12, 18759, 24222, 412, 264, 2767, 300, 575, 281, 767, 1406, 439, 300, 3364, 1970, 264, 2727, 11, 731, 11, 300, 787, 13156, 538, 264, 3732, 295, 264, 4373, 5952, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0987557117069993, "compression_ratio": 1.6596638655462186, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858792144080036e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 69800, "start": 707.02, "end": 708.12, "text": " Because it's only two dimensions.", "tokens": [50816, 1436, 309, 311, 787, 732, 12819, 13, 50871], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0987557117069993, "compression_ratio": 1.6596638655462186, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858792144080036e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 69800, "start": 708.3, "end": 708.58, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50880, 7587, 13, 50894], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0987557117069993, "compression_ratio": 1.6596638655462186, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858792144080036e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 69800, "start": 708.98, "end": 709.92, "text": " Length times width.", "tokens": [50914, 441, 4206, 1413, 11402, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0987557117069993, "compression_ratio": 1.6596638655462186, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858792144080036e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 69800, "start": 710.36, "end": 713.28, "text": " So 10 squared, 10 times 10 is only 100.", "tokens": [50983, 407, 1266, 8889, 11, 1266, 1413, 1266, 307, 787, 2319, 13, 51129], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0987557117069993, "compression_ratio": 1.6596638655462186, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858792144080036e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 69800, "start": 713.56, "end": 714.14, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [51143, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0987557117069993, "compression_ratio": 1.6596638655462186, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858792144080036e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 69800, "start": 714.38, "end": 719.32, "text": " So the weight went up by 1,000 times, but the base supporting it only got 100 times bigger.", "tokens": [51184, 407, 264, 3364, 1437, 493, 538, 502, 11, 1360, 1413, 11, 457, 264, 3096, 7231, 309, 787, 658, 2319, 1413, 3801, 13, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0987557117069993, "compression_ratio": 1.6596638655462186, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858792144080036e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 71932, "start": 719.32, "end": 729.22, "text": " Which means the compressive stress generated by its own self-weight, you know, the total weight divided by the supporting area, increases linearly with the scale.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 1355, 264, 14778, 488, 4244, 10833, 538, 1080, 1065, 2698, 12, 12329, 11, 291, 458, 11, 264, 3217, 3364, 6666, 538, 264, 7231, 1859, 11, 8637, 43586, 365, 264, 4373, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09029867047461394, "compression_ratio": 1.6014492753623188, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722625466505711e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 71932, "start": 729.36, "end": 730.9200000000001, "text": " It scales by a factor of 10.", "tokens": [50867, 467, 17408, 538, 257, 5952, 295, 1266, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09029867047461394, "compression_ratio": 1.6014492753623188, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722625466505711e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 71932, "start": 731.0400000000001, "end": 733.4200000000001, "text": " So it's just pushing down way harder on itself.", "tokens": [50951, 407, 309, 311, 445, 7380, 760, 636, 6081, 322, 2564, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09029867047461394, "compression_ratio": 1.6014492753623188, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722625466505711e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 71932, "start": 733.62, "end": 734.1400000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51080, 7587, 13, 51106], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09029867047461394, "compression_ratio": 1.6014492753623188, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722625466505711e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 71932, "start": 734.6, "end": 743.1800000000001, "text": " Your giant Lego bridge would generate so much internal stress that it would crush itself under its own weight long before you ever tried to drive a train over it.", "tokens": [51129, 2260, 7410, 28761, 7283, 576, 8460, 370, 709, 6920, 4244, 300, 309, 576, 10321, 2564, 833, 1080, 1065, 3364, 938, 949, 291, 1562, 3031, 281, 3332, 257, 3847, 670, 309, 13, 51558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09029867047461394, "compression_ratio": 1.6014492753623188, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722625466505711e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 71932, "start": 743.24, "end": 744.1600000000001, "text": " Just from standing there.", "tokens": [51561, 1449, 490, 4877, 456, 13, 51607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09029867047461394, "compression_ratio": 1.6014492753623188, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722625466505711e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 71932, "start": 744.3000000000001, "end": 744.62, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51614, 1079, 13, 51630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09029867047461394, "compression_ratio": 1.6014492753623188, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722625466505711e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 74462, "start": 744.62, "end": 747.32, "text": " The structural material would literally shatter.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 15067, 2527, 576, 3736, 402, 1161, 13, 50500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1830906449702748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867158671586716, "no_speech_prob": 1.642370375982971e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 74462, "start": 748.14, "end": 753.12, "text": " As Fickshian writes in the document, structural similarity does not imply mechanical similarity.", "tokens": [50541, 1018, 479, 618, 2716, 952, 13657, 294, 264, 4166, 11, 15067, 32194, 775, 406, 33616, 12070, 32194, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1830906449702748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867158671586716, "no_speech_prob": 1.642370375982971e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 74462, "start": 753.3, "end": 756.34, "text": " You know, I think there's a classic biology example for this too, right?", "tokens": [50799, 509, 458, 11, 286, 519, 456, 311, 257, 7230, 14956, 1365, 337, 341, 886, 11, 558, 30, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1830906449702748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867158671586716, "no_speech_prob": 1.642370375982971e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 74462, "start": 756.38, "end": 756.9, "text": " With animals.", "tokens": [50953, 2022, 4882, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1830906449702748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867158671586716, "no_speech_prob": 1.642370375982971e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 74462, "start": 757.04, "end": 757.8, "text": " Ah, yes.", "tokens": [50986, 2438, 11, 2086, 13, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1830906449702748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867158671586716, "no_speech_prob": 1.642370375982971e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 74462, "start": 758.02, "end": 758.22, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51035, 865, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1830906449702748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867158671586716, "no_speech_prob": 1.642370375982971e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 74462, "start": 758.58, "end": 759.5, "text": " The mouse and the elephant.", "tokens": [51063, 440, 9719, 293, 264, 19791, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1830906449702748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867158671586716, "no_speech_prob": 1.642370375982971e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 74462, "start": 759.66, "end": 761.22, "text": " It is the exact same principle.", "tokens": [51117, 467, 307, 264, 1900, 912, 8665, 13, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1830906449702748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867158671586716, "no_speech_prob": 1.642370375982971e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 74462, "start": 761.52, "end": 761.78, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51210, 1779, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1830906449702748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867158671586716, "no_speech_prob": 1.642370375982971e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 74462, "start": 762.12, "end": 768.08, "text": " Because if you take a tiny little mouse, which has these like delicate, almost translucent little leg bones.", "tokens": [51240, 1436, 498, 291, 747, 257, 5870, 707, 9719, 11, 597, 575, 613, 411, 21417, 11, 1920, 48236, 707, 1676, 10491, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1830906449702748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867158671586716, "no_speech_prob": 1.642370375982971e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 74462, "start": 768.2, "end": 768.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51544, 1779, 13, 51559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1830906449702748, "compression_ratio": 1.5867158671586716, "no_speech_prob": 1.642370375982971e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 76850, "start": 768.5, "end": 777.18, "text": " And you wave a magic wand and scale that exact mouse up to the size of an African elephant, it wouldn't become a terrifying giant monster.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 291, 5772, 257, 5585, 14304, 293, 4373, 300, 1900, 9719, 493, 281, 264, 2744, 295, 364, 7312, 19791, 11, 309, 2759, 380, 1813, 257, 18106, 7410, 10090, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09677269773663215, "compression_ratio": 1.7192307692307693, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126232715660496e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 76850, "start": 777.76, "end": 779.12, "text": " It would immediately collapse.", "tokens": [50828, 467, 576, 4258, 15584, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09677269773663215, "compression_ratio": 1.7192307692307693, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126232715660496e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 76850, "start": 779.34, "end": 781.0, "text": " Its bones would instantly shatter.", "tokens": [50907, 6953, 10491, 576, 13518, 402, 1161, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09677269773663215, "compression_ratio": 1.7192307692307693, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126232715660496e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 76850, "start": 781.34, "end": 786.98, "text": " The mass of its giant body would have scaled up by the cube, but the thickness of its bones would have only scaled by the square.", "tokens": [51007, 440, 2758, 295, 1080, 7410, 1772, 576, 362, 36039, 493, 538, 264, 13728, 11, 457, 264, 14855, 295, 1080, 10491, 576, 362, 787, 36039, 538, 264, 3732, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09677269773663215, "compression_ratio": 1.7192307692307693, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126232715660496e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 76850, "start": 787.14, "end": 788.56, "text": " So the bones just can't take it.", "tokens": [51297, 407, 264, 10491, 445, 393, 380, 747, 309, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09677269773663215, "compression_ratio": 1.7192307692307693, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126232715660496e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 76850, "start": 788.72, "end": 792.68, "text": " They wouldn't be nearly thick enough to handle the exponentially larger weight.", "tokens": [51376, 814, 2759, 380, 312, 6217, 5060, 1547, 281, 4813, 264, 37330, 4833, 3364, 13, 51574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09677269773663215, "compression_ratio": 1.7192307692307693, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126232715660496e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 79268, "start": 792.68, "end": 796.4399999999999, "text": " That is why a real elephant doesn't look like a giant mouse.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 983, 257, 957, 19791, 1177, 380, 574, 411, 257, 7410, 9719, 13, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1478844652272234, "compression_ratio": 1.5757575757575757, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610560804082962e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 79268, "start": 796.7399999999999, "end": 796.76, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50568, 1779, 13, 50569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1478844652272234, "compression_ratio": 1.5757575757575757, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610560804082962e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 79268, "start": 796.9399999999999, "end": 800.06, "text": " An elephant has those massive, dense tree trunk legs.", "tokens": [50578, 1107, 19791, 575, 729, 5994, 11, 18011, 4230, 19849, 5668, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1478844652272234, "compression_ratio": 1.5757575757575757, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610560804082962e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 79268, "start": 800.16, "end": 800.64, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50739, 7587, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1478844652272234, "compression_ratio": 1.5757575757575757, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610560804082962e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 79268, "start": 801.3199999999999, "end": 806.26, "text": " Its biology had to fundamentally redesign its structural supports to handle the scale.", "tokens": [50797, 6953, 14956, 632, 281, 17879, 39853, 1080, 15067, 9346, 281, 4813, 264, 4373, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1478844652272234, "compression_ratio": 1.5757575757575757, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610560804082962e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 79268, "start": 806.4, "end": 814.4599999999999, "text": " And this is why the blueprint makes a massive, crucial distinction between what it calls topological modularity and mechanical scaling.", "tokens": [51051, 400, 341, 307, 983, 264, 35868, 1669, 257, 5994, 11, 11462, 16844, 1296, 437, 309, 5498, 1192, 4383, 31111, 507, 293, 12070, 21589, 13, 51454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1478844652272234, "compression_ratio": 1.5757575757575757, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610560804082962e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 79268, "start": 814.64, "end": 815.0799999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51463, 1079, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1478844652272234, "compression_ratio": 1.5757575757575757, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610560804082962e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 79268, "start": 815.1999999999999, "end": 818.02, "text": " That is the core takeaway of the square cube law section.", "tokens": [51491, 663, 307, 264, 4965, 30681, 295, 264, 3732, 13728, 2101, 3541, 13, 51632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1478844652272234, "compression_ratio": 1.5757575757575757, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610560804082962e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 81802, "start": 818.02, "end": 821.3, "text": " Topological modularity is about how the network connects.", "tokens": [50365, 8840, 4383, 31111, 507, 307, 466, 577, 264, 3209, 16967, 13, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259863148564877, "compression_ratio": 1.7582781456953642, "no_speech_prob": 1.81754231890624e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 81802, "start": 821.56, "end": 822.4399999999999, "text": " The abstract map.", "tokens": [50542, 440, 12649, 4471, 13, 50586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259863148564877, "compression_ratio": 1.7582781456953642, "no_speech_prob": 1.81754231890624e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 81802, "start": 822.62, "end": 825.62, "text": " Node A connects to node B, which connects to node C.", "tokens": [50595, 38640, 316, 16967, 281, 9984, 363, 11, 597, 16967, 281, 9984, 383, 13, 50745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259863148564877, "compression_ratio": 1.7582781456953642, "no_speech_prob": 1.81754231890624e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 81802, "start": 825.6999999999999, "end": 825.84, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50749, 1779, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259863148564877, "compression_ratio": 1.7582781456953642, "no_speech_prob": 1.81754231890624e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 81802, "start": 825.92, "end": 826.92, "text": " The theoretical lines.", "tokens": [50760, 440, 20864, 3876, 13, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259863148564877, "compression_ratio": 1.7582781456953642, "no_speech_prob": 1.81754231890624e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 81802, "start": 827.0, "end": 827.26, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50814, 1079, 13, 50827], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259863148564877, "compression_ratio": 1.7582781456953642, "no_speech_prob": 1.81754231890624e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 81802, "start": 827.6, "end": 833.64, "text": " That map, that topological graph, can be preserved perfectly from a tiny classroom model all the way up to a planetary grid.", "tokens": [50844, 663, 4471, 11, 300, 1192, 4383, 4295, 11, 393, 312, 22242, 6239, 490, 257, 5870, 7419, 2316, 439, 264, 636, 493, 281, 257, 35788, 10748, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259863148564877, "compression_ratio": 1.7582781456953642, "no_speech_prob": 1.81754231890624e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 81802, "start": 833.92, "end": 834.8199999999999, "text": " You can scale the map.", "tokens": [51160, 509, 393, 4373, 264, 4471, 13, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259863148564877, "compression_ratio": 1.7582781456953642, "no_speech_prob": 1.81754231890624e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 81802, "start": 835.02, "end": 836.62, "text": " But you cannot scale the mechanics.", "tokens": [51215, 583, 291, 2644, 4373, 264, 12939, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259863148564877, "compression_ratio": 1.7582781456953642, "no_speech_prob": 1.81754231890624e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 81802, "start": 836.88, "end": 838.28, "text": " Mechanical scaling is impossible.", "tokens": [51308, 30175, 804, 21589, 307, 6243, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259863148564877, "compression_ratio": 1.7582781456953642, "no_speech_prob": 1.81754231890624e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 81802, "start": 838.8199999999999, "end": 845.24, "text": " The material realization, the actual physical stuff you build with, has to completely change as the scale changes.", "tokens": [51405, 440, 2527, 25138, 11, 264, 3539, 4001, 1507, 291, 1322, 365, 11, 575, 281, 2584, 1319, 382, 264, 4373, 2962, 13, 51726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259863148564877, "compression_ratio": 1.7582781456953642, "no_speech_prob": 1.81754231890624e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 81802, "start": 845.34, "end": 846.12, "text": " Because of the physics.", "tokens": [51731, 1436, 295, 264, 10649, 13, 51770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259863148564877, "compression_ratio": 1.7582781456953642, "no_speech_prob": 1.81754231890624e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 81802, "start": 846.38, "end": 846.86, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51783, 48746, 736, 13, 51807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259863148564877, "compression_ratio": 1.7582781456953642, "no_speech_prob": 1.81754231890624e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 84686, "start": 846.86, "end": 862.16, "text": " The engineers of the 22nd century are going to use completely different advanced materials, entirely new load paths, and different thermal management systems to build their version of the corridor than we would use to build a small demonstrator today.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 11955, 295, 264, 5853, 273, 4901, 366, 516, 281, 764, 2584, 819, 7339, 5319, 11, 7696, 777, 3677, 14518, 11, 293, 819, 15070, 4592, 3652, 281, 1322, 641, 3037, 295, 264, 25602, 813, 321, 576, 764, 281, 1322, 257, 1359, 5516, 19802, 965, 13, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06346001016332749, "compression_ratio": 1.6917293233082706, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232393033888126e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 84686, "start": 862.36, "end": 865.98, "text": " So the blueprint gives them the map, but not the materials.", "tokens": [51140, 407, 264, 35868, 2709, 552, 264, 4471, 11, 457, 406, 264, 5319, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06346001016332749, "compression_ratio": 1.6917293233082706, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232393033888126e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 84686, "start": 866.3000000000001, "end": 875.0600000000001, "text": " The globally invariant protocol dictates where the connection happens, but it humbly leaves the how up to the specific era of building it.", "tokens": [51337, 440, 18958, 33270, 394, 10336, 12569, 1024, 689, 264, 4984, 2314, 11, 457, 309, 1484, 25021, 5510, 264, 577, 493, 281, 264, 2685, 4249, 295, 2390, 309, 13, 51775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06346001016332749, "compression_ratio": 1.6917293233082706, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232393033888126e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 87506, "start": 875.06, "end": 876.92, "text": " Okay, here's where it gets really interesting.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 510, 311, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 1880, 13, 50458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16619495391845704, "compression_ratio": 1.38125, "no_speech_prob": 3.33132002885983e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 87506, "start": 877.3399999999999, "end": 886.3, "text": " Because we've established that the physical materials will change, but the spatial footprint, this global spatial skeleton, has to stay exactly the same for centuries.", "tokens": [50479, 1436, 321, 600, 7545, 300, 264, 4001, 5319, 486, 1319, 11, 457, 264, 23598, 24222, 11, 341, 4338, 23598, 25204, 11, 575, 281, 1754, 2293, 264, 912, 337, 13926, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16619495391845704, "compression_ratio": 1.38125, "no_speech_prob": 3.33132002885983e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 87506, "start": 886.42, "end": 886.68, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50933, 1779, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16619495391845704, "compression_ratio": 1.38125, "no_speech_prob": 3.33132002885983e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 88668, "start": 886.68, "end": 890.4599999999999, "text": " So, um, what exactly is the shape of this planetary footprint?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 1105, 11, 437, 2293, 307, 264, 3909, 295, 341, 35788, 24222, 30, 50554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13316331969367134, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182191863225228e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 88668, "start": 890.66, "end": 894.0999999999999, "text": " If we are literally drawing a map for the centuries, what are we drawing?", "tokens": [50564, 759, 321, 366, 3736, 6316, 257, 4471, 337, 264, 13926, 11, 437, 366, 321, 6316, 30, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13316331969367134, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182191863225228e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 88668, "start": 894.52, "end": 901.8, "text": " To understand the shape of the network, we have to look at the first massive mathematical approximation the blueprint makes, which is the reference sphere.", "tokens": [50757, 1407, 1223, 264, 3909, 295, 264, 3209, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 264, 700, 5994, 18894, 28023, 264, 35868, 1669, 11, 597, 307, 264, 6408, 16687, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13316331969367134, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182191863225228e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 88668, "start": 902.0799999999999, "end": 903.02, "text": " The reference sphere.", "tokens": [51135, 440, 6408, 16687, 13, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13316331969367134, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182191863225228e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 88668, "start": 903.2399999999999, "end": 903.56, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51193, 1079, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13316331969367134, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182191863225228e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 88668, "start": 904.2199999999999, "end": 909.28, "text": " The entire geometric framework begins by treating the planet Earth as a perfect sphere.", "tokens": [51242, 440, 2302, 33246, 8388, 7338, 538, 15083, 264, 5054, 4755, 382, 257, 2176, 16687, 13, 51495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13316331969367134, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182191863225228e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 88668, "start": 909.78, "end": 912.12, "text": " Now, obviously, we know the Earth is not perfectly spherical.", "tokens": [51520, 823, 11, 2745, 11, 321, 458, 264, 4755, 307, 406, 6239, 37300, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13316331969367134, "compression_ratio": 1.724264705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182191863225228e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 91212, "start": 912.12, "end": 912.8, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19199276814418556, "compression_ratio": 1.5679012345679013, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528932708433148e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 91212, "start": 912.9, "end": 914.16, "text": " It's an oblate spheroid.", "tokens": [50404, 467, 311, 364, 1111, 17593, 637, 16218, 327, 13, 50467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19199276814418556, "compression_ratio": 1.5679012345679013, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528932708433148e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 91212, "start": 914.46, "end": 915.62, "text": " It bulges at the equator.", "tokens": [50482, 467, 6493, 2880, 412, 264, 45544, 13, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19199276814418556, "compression_ratio": 1.5679012345679013, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528932708433148e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 91212, "start": 915.84, "end": 916.38, "text": " It's bumpy.", "tokens": [50551, 467, 311, 49400, 13, 50578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19199276814418556, "compression_ratio": 1.5679012345679013, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528932708433148e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 91212, "start": 916.58, "end": 917.92, "text": " It has the Mariana Trench.", "tokens": [50588, 467, 575, 264, 2039, 8497, 314, 4442, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19199276814418556, "compression_ratio": 1.5679012345679013, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528932708433148e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 91212, "start": 918.12, "end": 919.22, "text": " It has Mount Everest.", "tokens": [50665, 467, 575, 8426, 47591, 13, 50720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19199276814418556, "compression_ratio": 1.5679012345679013, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528932708433148e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 91212, "start": 919.64, "end": 921.98, "text": " I mean, it's a textured, messy rock.", "tokens": [50741, 286, 914, 11, 309, 311, 257, 48656, 11, 16191, 3727, 13, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19199276814418556, "compression_ratio": 1.5679012345679013, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528932708433148e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 91212, "start": 922.16, "end": 922.54, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50867, 7587, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19199276814418556, "compression_ratio": 1.5679012345679013, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528932708433148e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 91212, "start": 923.14, "end": 929.82, "text": " But the perfect sphere is the correct initial mathematical object to define the idealized network.", "tokens": [50916, 583, 264, 2176, 16687, 307, 264, 3006, 5883, 18894, 2657, 281, 6964, 264, 7157, 1602, 3209, 13, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19199276814418556, "compression_ratio": 1.5679012345679013, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528932708433148e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 91212, "start": 930.26, "end": 935.66, "text": " You have to start with a pristine geometric layer before you deal with the messy reality of the terrain.", "tokens": [51272, 509, 362, 281, 722, 365, 257, 582, 42745, 33246, 4583, 949, 291, 2028, 365, 264, 16191, 4103, 295, 264, 17674, 13, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19199276814418556, "compression_ratio": 1.5679012345679013, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528932708433148e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 91212, "start": 936.02, "end": 936.5600000000001, "text": " Makes sense.", "tokens": [51560, 25245, 2020, 13, 51587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19199276814418556, "compression_ratio": 1.5679012345679013, "no_speech_prob": 2.3528932708433148e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 93656, "start": 936.56, "end": 942.6999999999999, "text": " And on this perfect sphere, the blueprint dictates that the primary planetary highways must be orthodromes.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 322, 341, 2176, 16687, 11, 264, 35868, 12569, 1024, 300, 264, 6194, 35788, 43747, 1633, 312, 19052, 378, 4397, 279, 13, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09444205172650226, "compression_ratio": 1.6726190476190477, "no_speech_prob": 1.377967726902407e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 93656, "start": 943.0799999999999, "end": 943.4799999999999, "text": " Orthodromes.", "tokens": [50691, 27554, 378, 4397, 279, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09444205172650226, "compression_ratio": 1.6726190476190477, "no_speech_prob": 1.377967726902407e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 93656, "start": 943.56, "end": 946.88, "text": " Okay, that sounds intimidating, but it is basically just a great circle, isn't it?", "tokens": [50715, 1033, 11, 300, 3263, 29714, 11, 457, 309, 307, 1936, 445, 257, 869, 6329, 11, 1943, 380, 309, 30, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09444205172650226, "compression_ratio": 1.6726190476190477, "no_speech_prob": 1.377967726902407e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 93656, "start": 946.92, "end": 950.4399999999999, "text": " Like, the absolute shortest path between any two points on a sphere.", "tokens": [50883, 1743, 11, 264, 8236, 31875, 3100, 1296, 604, 732, 2793, 322, 257, 16687, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09444205172650226, "compression_ratio": 1.6726190476190477, "no_speech_prob": 1.377967726902407e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 93656, "start": 950.6199999999999, "end": 952.0999999999999, "text": " Yes, that's exactly what it is.", "tokens": [51068, 1079, 11, 300, 311, 2293, 437, 309, 307, 13, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09444205172650226, "compression_ratio": 1.6726190476190477, "no_speech_prob": 1.377967726902407e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 93656, "start": 952.1999999999999, "end": 960.26, "text": " If you have ever taken a long international flight, say, from New York to London, and you look at the flight path on the little screen on the back of the seat, the line always looks curved.", "tokens": [51147, 759, 291, 362, 1562, 2726, 257, 938, 5058, 7018, 11, 584, 11, 490, 1873, 3609, 281, 7042, 11, 293, 291, 574, 412, 264, 7018, 3100, 322, 264, 707, 2568, 322, 264, 646, 295, 264, 6121, 11, 264, 1622, 1009, 1542, 24991, 13, 51550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09444205172650226, "compression_ratio": 1.6726190476190477, "no_speech_prob": 1.377967726902407e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 93656, "start": 960.3599999999999, "end": 960.68, "text": " Oh, yeah.", "tokens": [51555, 876, 11, 1338, 13, 51571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09444205172650226, "compression_ratio": 1.6726190476190477, "no_speech_prob": 1.377967726902407e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 93656, "start": 960.76, "end": 961.64, "text": " It arcs way up north.", "tokens": [51575, 467, 10346, 82, 636, 493, 6830, 13, 51619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09444205172650226, "compression_ratio": 1.6726190476190477, "no_speech_prob": 1.377967726902407e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 93656, "start": 961.6999999999999, "end": 961.9, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51622, 1779, 13, 51632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09444205172650226, "compression_ratio": 1.6726190476190477, "no_speech_prob": 1.377967726902407e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 93656, "start": 962.26, "end": 963.92, "text": " That curve is an orthodrome.", "tokens": [51650, 663, 7605, 307, 364, 19052, 378, 11505, 13, 51733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09444205172650226, "compression_ratio": 1.6726190476190477, "no_speech_prob": 1.377967726902407e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 96392, "start": 963.92, "end": 968.54, "text": " It is the straightest possible line you can draw across a curved surface.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 2997, 377, 1944, 1622, 291, 393, 2642, 2108, 257, 24991, 3753, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1374268337171905, "compression_ratio": 1.7242798353909465, "no_speech_prob": 1.284100104893826e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 96392, "start": 969.02, "end": 982.4799999999999, "text": " I always pictured it like if you had a giant sword and you slice the earth perfectly in half straight through the absolute dead center of the core, the ring that you leave on the surface is a great circle.", "tokens": [50620, 286, 1009, 49896, 309, 411, 498, 291, 632, 257, 7410, 10576, 293, 291, 13153, 264, 4120, 6239, 294, 1922, 2997, 807, 264, 8236, 3116, 3056, 295, 264, 4965, 11, 264, 4875, 300, 291, 1856, 322, 264, 3753, 307, 257, 869, 6329, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1374268337171905, "compression_ratio": 1.7242798353909465, "no_speech_prob": 1.284100104893826e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 96392, "start": 982.6999999999999, "end": 983.42, "text": " Like the equator.", "tokens": [51304, 1743, 264, 45544, 13, 51340], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1374268337171905, "compression_ratio": 1.7242798353909465, "no_speech_prob": 1.284100104893826e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 96392, "start": 983.64, "end": 985.9799999999999, "text": " The equator slices the earth perfectly in half.", "tokens": [51351, 440, 45544, 19793, 264, 4120, 6239, 294, 1922, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1374268337171905, "compression_ratio": 1.7242798353909465, "no_speech_prob": 1.284100104893826e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 96392, "start": 986.2199999999999, "end": 990.74, "text": " That is a, well, highly aggressive but very accurate way to visualize it.", "tokens": [51480, 663, 307, 257, 11, 731, 11, 5405, 10762, 457, 588, 8559, 636, 281, 23273, 309, 13, 51706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1374268337171905, "compression_ratio": 1.7242798353909465, "no_speech_prob": 1.284100104893826e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 99074, "start": 990.74, "end": 996.96, "text": " Any plane that passes through the exact center of the sphere creates a great circle on the surface.", "tokens": [50365, 2639, 5720, 300, 11335, 807, 264, 1900, 3056, 295, 264, 16687, 7829, 257, 869, 6329, 322, 264, 3753, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14494501942335958, "compression_ratio": 1.7385892116182573, "no_speech_prob": 1.1510604752337783e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 99074, "start": 997.5600000000001, "end": 1002.24, "text": " And the blueprint represents an orthodrome mathematically as an unoriented great circle.", "tokens": [50706, 400, 264, 35868, 8855, 364, 19052, 378, 11505, 44003, 382, 364, 517, 27414, 869, 6329, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14494501942335958, "compression_ratio": 1.7385892116182573, "no_speech_prob": 1.1510604752337783e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 99074, "start": 1002.74, "end": 1006.1, "text": " Unoriented meaning we don't care about the direction of traffic yet.", "tokens": [50965, 1156, 27414, 3620, 321, 500, 380, 1127, 466, 264, 3513, 295, 6419, 1939, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14494501942335958, "compression_ratio": 1.7385892116182573, "no_speech_prob": 1.1510604752337783e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 99074, "start": 1006.1800000000001, "end": 1006.42, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51137, 12753, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14494501942335958, "compression_ratio": 1.7385892116182573, "no_speech_prob": 1.1510604752337783e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 99074, "start": 1006.5600000000001, "end": 1012.0600000000001, "text": " The mathematics at this stage don't care if the water or the trains are flowing east or flowing west.", "tokens": [51156, 440, 18666, 412, 341, 3233, 500, 380, 1127, 498, 264, 1281, 420, 264, 16329, 366, 13974, 10648, 420, 13974, 7009, 13, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14494501942335958, "compression_ratio": 1.7385892116182573, "no_speech_prob": 1.1510604752337783e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 99074, "start": 1012.16, "end": 1014.38, "text": " It just cares about the spatial ring itself.", "tokens": [51436, 467, 445, 12310, 466, 264, 23598, 4875, 2564, 13, 51547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14494501942335958, "compression_ratio": 1.7385892116182573, "no_speech_prob": 1.1510604752337783e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 99074, "start": 1014.58, "end": 1014.78, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51557, 1033, 13, 51567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14494501942335958, "compression_ratio": 1.7385892116182573, "no_speech_prob": 1.1510604752337783e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 101478, "start": 1014.78, "end": 1018.8199999999999, "text": " In advanced geometry, if you have a great circle, you can define it by a normal vector.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 7339, 18426, 11, 498, 291, 362, 257, 869, 6329, 11, 291, 393, 6964, 309, 538, 257, 2710, 8062, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0988967259724935, "compression_ratio": 1.711340206185567, "no_speech_prob": 2.6949352038146968e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 101478, "start": 1019.02, "end": 1019.54, "text": " Which is what?", "tokens": [50577, 3013, 307, 437, 30, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0988967259724935, "compression_ratio": 1.711340206185567, "no_speech_prob": 2.6949352038146968e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 101478, "start": 1019.88, "end": 1023.76, "text": " An arrow pointing straight out from the center of the plane that cuts the earth in half.", "tokens": [50620, 1107, 11610, 12166, 2997, 484, 490, 264, 3056, 295, 264, 5720, 300, 9992, 264, 4120, 294, 1922, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0988967259724935, "compression_ratio": 1.711340206185567, "no_speech_prob": 2.6949352038146968e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 101478, "start": 1024.02, "end": 1029.2, "text": " An arrow pointing up and an arrow pointing down to find the exact same ring.", "tokens": [50827, 1107, 11610, 12166, 493, 293, 364, 11610, 12166, 760, 281, 915, 264, 1900, 912, 4875, 13, 51086], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0988967259724935, "compression_ratio": 1.711340206185567, "no_speech_prob": 2.6949352038146968e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 101478, "start": 1029.3999999999999, "end": 1032.84, "text": " The parameter space for this isn't your standard 3D space.", "tokens": [51096, 440, 13075, 1901, 337, 341, 1943, 380, 428, 3832, 805, 35, 1901, 13, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0988967259724935, "compression_ratio": 1.711340206185567, "no_speech_prob": 2.6949352038146968e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 101478, "start": 1032.98, "end": 1042.76, "text": " It's what mathematicians call the real projective plane where antipodal points, points on exact opposite sides of the sphere, are treated as the same mathematical entity.", "tokens": [51275, 467, 311, 437, 32811, 2567, 818, 264, 957, 1716, 488, 5720, 689, 2511, 647, 378, 304, 2793, 11, 2793, 322, 1900, 6182, 4881, 295, 264, 16687, 11, 366, 8668, 382, 264, 912, 18894, 13977, 13, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0988967259724935, "compression_ratio": 1.711340206185567, "no_speech_prob": 2.6949352038146968e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 104276, "start": 1042.76, "end": 1047.06, "text": " Okay, so we have these massive, perfect rings slicing the earth in half.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 321, 362, 613, 5994, 11, 2176, 11136, 46586, 264, 4120, 294, 1922, 13, 50580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024243054089244, "compression_ratio": 1.6097560975609757, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037849859597888e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 104276, "start": 1047.18, "end": 1050.7, "text": " But here is the thing about drawing multiple straight lines on a sphere.", "tokens": [50586, 583, 510, 307, 264, 551, 466, 6316, 3866, 2997, 3876, 322, 257, 16687, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024243054089244, "compression_ratio": 1.6097560975609757, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037849859597888e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 104276, "start": 1050.9, "end": 1051.2, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50772, 1079, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024243054089244, "compression_ratio": 1.6097560975609757, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037849859597888e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 104276, "start": 1051.56, "end": 1064.04, "text": " If you take any two distinct great circles, let's say the equator, which runs horizontal, and a line of longitude that runs vertical through the poles, they will always inevitably intersect.", "tokens": [50805, 759, 291, 747, 604, 732, 10644, 869, 13040, 11, 718, 311, 584, 264, 45544, 11, 597, 6676, 12750, 11, 293, 257, 1622, 295, 938, 4377, 300, 6676, 9429, 807, 264, 24760, 11, 436, 486, 1009, 28171, 27815, 13, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024243054089244, "compression_ratio": 1.6097560975609757, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037849859597888e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 104276, "start": 1064.22, "end": 1064.68, "text": " No way.", "tokens": [51438, 883, 636, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024243054089244, "compression_ratio": 1.6097560975609757, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037849859597888e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 104276, "start": 1064.76, "end": 1066.0, "text": " And they don't just intersect once.", "tokens": [51465, 400, 436, 500, 380, 445, 27815, 1564, 13, 51527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024243054089244, "compression_ratio": 1.6097560975609757, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037849859597888e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 104276, "start": 1066.14, "end": 1070.04, "text": " They always intersect at exactly two points on opposite sides of the planet.", "tokens": [51534, 814, 1009, 27815, 412, 2293, 732, 2793, 322, 6182, 4881, 295, 264, 5054, 13, 51729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024243054089244, "compression_ratio": 1.6097560975609757, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037849859597888e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 107004, "start": 1070.04, "end": 1074.36, "text": " You cannot draw two great circles on a sphere without them crossing twice.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 2644, 2642, 732, 869, 13040, 322, 257, 16687, 1553, 552, 14712, 6091, 13, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14554187830756693, "compression_ratio": 1.5737704918032787, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106028186482768e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 107004, "start": 1074.48, "end": 1075.78, "text": " It's mathematically impossible.", "tokens": [50587, 467, 311, 44003, 6243, 13, 50652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14554187830756693, "compression_ratio": 1.5737704918032787, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106028186482768e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 107004, "start": 1075.8999999999999, "end": 1076.08, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50658, 1779, 13, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14554187830756693, "compression_ratio": 1.5737704918032787, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106028186482768e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 107004, "start": 1076.22, "end": 1078.96, "text": " This gives us one of the foundational theorems in the text.", "tokens": [50674, 639, 2709, 505, 472, 295, 264, 32195, 10299, 2592, 294, 264, 2487, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14554187830756693, "compression_ratio": 1.5737704918032787, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106028186482768e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 107004, "start": 1079.96, "end": 1084.08, "text": " Two distinct great circles intersect in exactly two antipodal points.", "tokens": [50861, 4453, 10644, 869, 13040, 27815, 294, 2293, 732, 2511, 647, 378, 304, 2793, 13, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14554187830756693, "compression_ratio": 1.5737704918032787, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106028186482768e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 107004, "start": 1084.56, "end": 1086.86, "text": " The mathematics guarantee this intersection.", "tokens": [51091, 440, 18666, 10815, 341, 15236, 13, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14554187830756693, "compression_ratio": 1.5737704918032787, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106028186482768e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 108686, "start": 1086.86, "end": 1096.6999999999998, "text": " And furthermore, the text proves that the absolute shortest path between those two intersection nodes is simply the shorter arc of the great circle connecting them.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 3052, 3138, 11, 264, 2487, 25019, 300, 264, 8236, 31875, 3100, 1296, 729, 732, 15236, 13891, 307, 2935, 264, 11639, 10346, 295, 264, 869, 6329, 11015, 552, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13588787449730766, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.644982757121772e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 108686, "start": 1097.1, "end": 1101.52, "text": " This network of intersecting rings is the ultimate global skeleton.", "tokens": [50877, 639, 3209, 295, 27815, 278, 11136, 307, 264, 9705, 4338, 25204, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13588787449730766, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.644982757121772e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 108686, "start": 1101.9199999999998, "end": 1102.3, "text": " But wait.", "tokens": [51118, 583, 1699, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13588787449730766, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.644982757121772e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 108686, "start": 1103.0, "end": 1105.6399999999999, "text": " We talked about how the earth is a messy, bumpy rock.", "tokens": [51172, 492, 2825, 466, 577, 264, 4120, 307, 257, 16191, 11, 49400, 3727, 13, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13588787449730766, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.644982757121772e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 108686, "start": 1106.0, "end": 1106.56, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51322, 467, 307, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13588787449730766, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.644982757121772e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 110656, "start": 1106.56, "end": 1117.74, "text": " You can draw a perfect mathematical great circle on a whiteboard, but when you actually go to build a continent-spanning tunnel or pipeline along that line, you are going to hit reality.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 2642, 257, 2176, 18894, 869, 6329, 322, 257, 2418, 3787, 11, 457, 562, 291, 767, 352, 281, 1322, 257, 18932, 12, 4952, 282, 773, 13186, 420, 15517, 2051, 300, 1622, 11, 291, 366, 516, 281, 2045, 4103, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10418256493501885, "compression_ratio": 1.7696335078534031, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782083977010751e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 110656, "start": 1117.8999999999999, "end": 1118.76, "text": " You certainly will.", "tokens": [50932, 509, 3297, 486, 13, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10418256493501885, "compression_ratio": 1.7696335078534031, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782083977010751e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 110656, "start": 1118.82, "end": 1120.08, "text": " You are going to hit the Alps.", "tokens": [50978, 509, 366, 516, 281, 2045, 264, 967, 1878, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10418256493501885, "compression_ratio": 1.7696335078534031, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782083977010751e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 110656, "start": 1120.4199999999998, "end": 1122.78, "text": " You are going to hit a deeply populated city center.", "tokens": [51058, 509, 366, 516, 281, 2045, 257, 8760, 32998, 2307, 3056, 13, 51176], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10418256493501885, "compression_ratio": 1.7696335078534031, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782083977010751e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 110656, "start": 1123.22, "end": 1125.1599999999999, "text": " You are going to hit a protected national park.", "tokens": [51198, 509, 366, 516, 281, 2045, 257, 10594, 4048, 3884, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10418256493501885, "compression_ratio": 1.7696335078534031, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782083977010751e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 112516, "start": 1125.16, "end": 1130.88, "text": " I mean, you can't just bulldoze a perfectly straight line through the middle of the Himalayas just because the math says so.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 914, 11, 291, 393, 380, 445, 4693, 2595, 1381, 257, 6239, 2997, 1622, 807, 264, 2808, 295, 264, 5920, 35951, 296, 445, 570, 264, 5221, 1619, 370, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401844055672002, "compression_ratio": 1.7484076433121019, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370912008483284e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 112516, "start": 1131.22, "end": 1136.98, "text": " And this is where the blueprint proves it is an actual engineering document and not just, you know, a mathematical fantasy.", "tokens": [50668, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 35868, 25019, 309, 307, 364, 3539, 7043, 4166, 293, 406, 445, 11, 291, 458, 11, 257, 18894, 13861, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401844055672002, "compression_ratio": 1.7484076433121019, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370912008483284e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 112516, "start": 1137.3000000000002, "end": 1142.8000000000002, "text": " It introduces a vital distinction between the reference layer and the realization layer.", "tokens": [50972, 467, 31472, 257, 11707, 16844, 1296, 264, 6408, 4583, 293, 264, 25138, 4583, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401844055672002, "compression_ratio": 1.7484076433121019, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370912008483284e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 112516, "start": 1142.88, "end": 1144.5800000000002, "text": " I thought this part was absolutely brilliant.", "tokens": [51251, 286, 1194, 341, 644, 390, 3122, 10248, 13, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401844055672002, "compression_ratio": 1.7484076433121019, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370912008483284e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 112516, "start": 1144.72, "end": 1147.9, "text": " It is a masterstroke of systemic realism, really.", "tokens": [51343, 467, 307, 257, 4505, 42706, 295, 23789, 38484, 11, 534, 13, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401844055672002, "compression_ratio": 1.7484076433121019, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370912008483284e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 112516, "start": 1148.4, "end": 1152.44, "text": " The reference layer is that invisible, mathematically perfect great circle.", "tokens": [51527, 440, 6408, 4583, 307, 300, 14603, 11, 44003, 2176, 869, 6329, 13, 51729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401844055672002, "compression_ratio": 1.7484076433121019, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370912008483284e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 112516, "start": 1152.8400000000001, "end": 1154.8400000000001, "text": " It lives in the realm of pure geometry.", "tokens": [51749, 467, 2909, 294, 264, 15355, 295, 6075, 18426, 13, 51849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13401844055672002, "compression_ratio": 1.7484076433121019, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370912008483284e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 115484, "start": 1154.84, "end": 1161.06, "text": " But the realization layer is where the actual concrete gets poured, where the rocks get dug, and where the cities live.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 25138, 4583, 307, 689, 264, 3539, 9859, 2170, 23270, 11, 689, 264, 10989, 483, 22954, 11, 293, 689, 264, 6486, 1621, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13035804820510577, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622698005731463e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 115484, "start": 1161.6599999999999, "end": 1162.58, "text": " So how do they interact?", "tokens": [50706, 407, 577, 360, 436, 4648, 30, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13035804820510577, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622698005731463e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 115484, "start": 1162.82, "end": 1165.08, "text": " Like, if the pure math hits a mountain, what happens?", "tokens": [50764, 1743, 11, 498, 264, 6075, 5221, 8664, 257, 6937, 11, 437, 2314, 30, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13035804820510577, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622698005731463e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 115484, "start": 1165.3, "end": 1172.76, "text": " The blueprint allows the physical implementation, the actual tunnel or pipeline, to physically detour around the mountain.", "tokens": [50888, 440, 35868, 4045, 264, 4001, 11420, 11, 264, 3539, 13186, 420, 15517, 11, 281, 9762, 1141, 396, 926, 264, 6937, 13, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13035804820510577, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622698005731463e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 115484, "start": 1173.02, "end": 1173.26, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51274, 1033, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13035804820510577, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622698005731463e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 115484, "start": 1173.4599999999998, "end": 1176.86, "text": " It can weave around the borders of a protected ecological zone.", "tokens": [51296, 467, 393, 29145, 926, 264, 16287, 295, 257, 10594, 31054, 6668, 13, 51466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13035804820510577, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622698005731463e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 115484, "start": 1177.12, "end": 1180.8, "text": " It can snake its way carefully through a dense metropolitan area.", "tokens": [51479, 467, 393, 12650, 1080, 636, 7500, 807, 257, 18011, 44645, 1859, 13, 51663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13035804820510577, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622698005731463e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 118080, "start": 1180.8, "end": 1187.62, "text": " But to maintain the integrity of the entire global network, it must formally register that deviation", "tokens": [50365, 583, 281, 6909, 264, 16000, 295, 264, 2302, 4338, 3209, 11, 309, 1633, 25983, 7280, 300, 25163, 50706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.3876963570004418, "compression_ratio": 1.1627906976744187, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050221489730896e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 118762, "start": 1187.62, "end": 1192.78, "text": " as a bypass, and it must stay mathematically tethered to that invisible great circle.", "tokens": [50365, 382, 257, 24996, 11, 293, 309, 1633, 1754, 44003, 256, 1666, 292, 281, 300, 14603, 869, 6329, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17953729157400602, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832400936469869e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 118762, "start": 1192.78, "end": 1194.8799999999999, "text": " You know, it's almost like walking a dog on a leash.", "tokens": [50623, 509, 458, 11, 309, 311, 1920, 411, 4494, 257, 3000, 322, 257, 41616, 13, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17953729157400602, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832400936469869e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 118762, "start": 1195.6, "end": 1196.4799999999998, "text": " Oh, how so?", "tokens": [50764, 876, 11, 577, 370, 30, 50808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17953729157400602, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832400936469869e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 118762, "start": 1197.08, "end": 1198.7399999999998, "text": " The invisible great circle is the person, right?", "tokens": [50838, 440, 14603, 869, 6329, 307, 264, 954, 11, 558, 30, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17953729157400602, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832400936469869e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 118762, "start": 1199.1399999999999, "end": 1200.6399999999999, "text": " Walking in a perfectly straight line.", "tokens": [50941, 26964, 294, 257, 6239, 2997, 1622, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17953729157400602, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832400936469869e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 118762, "start": 1201.1, "end": 1202.9599999999998, "text": " And the physical corridor is the dog.", "tokens": [51039, 400, 264, 4001, 25602, 307, 264, 3000, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17953729157400602, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832400936469869e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 118762, "start": 1203.3, "end": 1203.58, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51149, 1779, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17953729157400602, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832400936469869e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 118762, "start": 1203.6399999999999, "end": 1207.1999999999998, "text": " The dog can weave left to sniff a tree or dart right to go around a puddle.", "tokens": [51166, 440, 3000, 393, 29145, 1411, 281, 31101, 257, 4230, 420, 39010, 558, 281, 352, 926, 257, 14166, 2285, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17953729157400602, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832400936469869e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 120720, "start": 1207.2, "end": 1212.94, "text": " But it is always tied back to that straight central path, and eventually it has to come back to the center.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 309, 307, 1009, 9601, 646, 281, 300, 2997, 5777, 3100, 11, 293, 4728, 309, 575, 281, 808, 646, 281, 264, 3056, 13, 50652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13267795528684342, "compression_ratio": 1.6552901023890785, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881604621155066e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 120720, "start": 1213.3600000000001, "end": 1215.16, "text": " That is a very grounded way to look at it.", "tokens": [50673, 663, 307, 257, 588, 23535, 636, 281, 574, 412, 309, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13267795528684342, "compression_ratio": 1.6552901023890785, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881604621155066e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 120720, "start": 1215.8600000000001, "end": 1220.42, "text": " By separating the idealized geometric line from the terrain-dependent physical route,", "tokens": [50798, 3146, 29279, 264, 7157, 1602, 33246, 1622, 490, 264, 17674, 12, 36763, 317, 4001, 7955, 11, 51026], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13267795528684342, "compression_ratio": 1.6552901023890785, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881604621155066e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 120720, "start": 1220.72, "end": 1226.68, "text": " the blueprint prevents local geographical obstacles from destroying the global topological network.", "tokens": [51041, 264, 35868, 22367, 2654, 39872, 17735, 490, 19926, 264, 4338, 1192, 4383, 3209, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13267795528684342, "compression_ratio": 1.6552901023890785, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881604621155066e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 120720, "start": 1226.72, "end": 1227.56, "text": " So you don't break the math.", "tokens": [51341, 407, 291, 500, 380, 1821, 264, 5221, 13, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13267795528684342, "compression_ratio": 1.6552901023890785, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881604621155066e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 120720, "start": 1228.06, "end": 1228.56, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51408, 7587, 13, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13267795528684342, "compression_ratio": 1.6552901023890785, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881604621155066e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 120720, "start": 1228.72, "end": 1233.8600000000001, "text": " You don't lose the global identity of the corridor just because you had to route around a lake in Switzerland.", "tokens": [51441, 509, 500, 380, 3624, 264, 4338, 6575, 295, 264, 25602, 445, 570, 291, 632, 281, 7955, 926, 257, 11001, 294, 23312, 13, 51698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13267795528684342, "compression_ratio": 1.6552901023890785, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881604621155066e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 123386, "start": 1233.86, "end": 1241.6799999999998, "text": " The network remains mathematically concurrent on a planetary scale while remaining flexible on a regional scale.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3209, 7023, 44003, 37702, 322, 257, 35788, 4373, 1339, 8877, 11358, 322, 257, 10964, 4373, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1301968018213908, "compression_ratio": 1.5962145110410095, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074917225979534e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 123386, "start": 1241.9199999999998, "end": 1247.74, "text": " And we shouldn't picture this corridor as just a tiny, thin wire stretched across the globe, right?", "tokens": [50768, 400, 321, 4659, 380, 3036, 341, 25602, 382, 445, 257, 5870, 11, 5862, 6234, 23563, 2108, 264, 15371, 11, 558, 30, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1301968018213908, "compression_ratio": 1.5962145110410095, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074917225979534e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 123386, "start": 1248.02, "end": 1249.6, "text": " It's not a one-dimensional line.", "tokens": [51073, 467, 311, 406, 257, 472, 12, 18759, 1622, 13, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1301968018213908, "compression_ratio": 1.5962145110410095, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074917225979534e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 123386, "start": 1249.7199999999998, "end": 1250.4799999999998, "text": " No, not at all.", "tokens": [51158, 883, 11, 406, 412, 439, 13, 51196], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1301968018213908, "compression_ratio": 1.5962145110410095, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074917225979534e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 123386, "start": 1250.56, "end": 1253.3799999999999, "text": " The blueprint calls it an orthodromic corridor tube.", "tokens": [51200, 440, 35868, 5498, 309, 364, 19052, 378, 4397, 299, 25602, 9917, 13, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1301968018213908, "compression_ratio": 1.5962145110410095, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074917225979534e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 123386, "start": 1254.1799999999998, "end": 1255.34, "text": " It has a physical width.", "tokens": [51381, 467, 575, 257, 4001, 11402, 13, 51439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1301968018213908, "compression_ratio": 1.5962145110410095, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074917225979534e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 123386, "start": 1255.9799999999998, "end": 1260.52, "text": " So imagine a two-dimensional band, like a massive strip of tape wrapping all the way around the Earth", "tokens": [51471, 407, 3811, 257, 732, 12, 18759, 4116, 11, 411, 257, 5994, 12828, 295, 7314, 21993, 439, 264, 636, 926, 264, 4755, 51698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1301968018213908, "compression_ratio": 1.5962145110410095, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074917225979534e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 123386, "start": 1260.52, "end": 1263.74, "text": " with that invisible great circle running dead center through it.", "tokens": [51698, 365, 300, 14603, 869, 6329, 2614, 3116, 3056, 807, 309, 13, 51859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1301968018213908, "compression_ratio": 1.5962145110410095, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074917225979534e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 126386, "start": 1263.86, "end": 1264.12, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.151277990226286, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830383437084096e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 126386, "start": 1264.28, "end": 1272.1, "text": " The corridor has a defined spatial volume, and the text provides the exact derivation for the surface area this tube consumes on the planet.", "tokens": [50386, 440, 25602, 575, 257, 7642, 23598, 5523, 11, 293, 264, 2487, 6417, 264, 1900, 10151, 399, 337, 264, 3753, 1859, 341, 9917, 48823, 322, 264, 5054, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.151277990226286, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830383437084096e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 126386, "start": 1272.36, "end": 1275.58, "text": " Without reading the calculus out loud, if you define an angular half-width,", "tokens": [50790, 9129, 3760, 264, 33400, 484, 6588, 11, 498, 291, 6964, 364, 24413, 1922, 12, 21271, 11, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.151277990226286, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830383437084096e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 126386, "start": 1275.7199999999998, "end": 1279.74, "text": " which is basically how far left and right from the center line the corridor extends,", "tokens": [50958, 597, 307, 1936, 577, 1400, 1411, 293, 558, 490, 264, 3056, 1622, 264, 25602, 26448, 11, 51159], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.151277990226286, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830383437084096e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 126386, "start": 1280.3999999999999, "end": 1282.6999999999998, "text": " you can integrate that over the sphere's surface.", "tokens": [51192, 291, 393, 13365, 300, 670, 264, 16687, 311, 3753, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.151277990226286, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830383437084096e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 128270, "start": 1282.7, "end": 1286.28, "text": " What does that actually mean for the size of these things, like, on practical terms?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 775, 300, 767, 914, 337, 264, 2744, 295, 613, 721, 11, 411, 11, 322, 8496, 2115, 30, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13880687564998478, "compression_ratio": 1.6989795918367347, "no_speech_prob": 1.5848701474460714e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 128270, "start": 1286.72, "end": 1292.1200000000001, "text": " It means that if the width of the corridor is relatively small compared to the sheer size of the Earth,", "tokens": [50566, 467, 1355, 300, 498, 264, 11402, 295, 264, 25602, 307, 7226, 1359, 5347, 281, 264, 23061, 2744, 295, 264, 4755, 11, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13880687564998478, "compression_ratio": 1.6989795918367347, "no_speech_prob": 1.5848701474460714e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 128270, "start": 1292.3400000000001, "end": 1300.56, "text": " the total area of this global tube essentially simplifies to the circumference of the Earth multiplied by the total width of the corridor.", "tokens": [50847, 264, 3217, 1859, 295, 341, 4338, 9917, 4476, 6883, 11221, 281, 264, 7125, 5158, 295, 264, 4755, 17207, 538, 264, 3217, 11402, 295, 264, 25602, 13, 51258], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13880687564998478, "compression_ratio": 1.6989795918367347, "no_speech_prob": 1.5848701474460714e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 128270, "start": 1300.88, "end": 1301.14, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51274, 1033, 13, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13880687564998478, "compression_ratio": 1.6989795918367347, "no_speech_prob": 1.5848701474460714e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 130114, "start": 1301.14, "end": 1306.94, "text": " It gives planners a highly specific, measurable spatial footprint to reserve.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 2709, 49674, 257, 5405, 2685, 11, 43615, 23598, 24222, 281, 17824, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14455385208129884, "compression_ratio": 1.4656862745098038, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325114445351561e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 130114, "start": 1307.1000000000001, "end": 1307.3400000000001, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50663, 1033, 13, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14455385208129884, "compression_ratio": 1.4656862745098038, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325114445351561e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 130114, "start": 1307.42, "end": 1308.64, "text": " So we have our global skeleton.", "tokens": [50679, 407, 321, 362, 527, 4338, 25204, 13, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14455385208129884, "compression_ratio": 1.4656862745098038, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325114445351561e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 130114, "start": 1308.88, "end": 1312.4, "text": " We have these massive continent-spanning rings wrapping the planet,", "tokens": [50752, 492, 362, 613, 5994, 18932, 12, 4952, 282, 773, 11136, 21993, 264, 5054, 11, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14455385208129884, "compression_ratio": 1.4656862745098038, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325114445351561e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 130114, "start": 1312.88, "end": 1317.9, "text": " establishing these protected spatial tubes that can detour around mountains but always return to the math.", "tokens": [50952, 22494, 613, 10594, 23598, 21458, 300, 393, 1141, 396, 926, 10233, 457, 1009, 2736, 281, 264, 5221, 13, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14455385208129884, "compression_ratio": 1.4656862745098038, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325114445351561e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 130114, "start": 1318.0, "end": 1318.2800000000002, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51208, 12753, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14455385208129884, "compression_ratio": 1.4656862745098038, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325114445351561e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 131828, "start": 1318.28, "end": 1323.6399999999999, "text": " But the obvious next question is, how many of these giant rings do we actually need?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 6322, 958, 1168, 307, 11, 577, 867, 295, 613, 7410, 11136, 360, 321, 767, 643, 30, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13893658115017798, "compression_ratio": 1.6348684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.741903496443875e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 131828, "start": 1323.72, "end": 1324.58, "text": " That is the big question.", "tokens": [50637, 663, 307, 264, 955, 1168, 13, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13893658115017798, "compression_ratio": 1.6348684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.741903496443875e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 131828, "start": 1324.66, "end": 1324.8, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50684, 1779, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13893658115017798, "compression_ratio": 1.6348684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.741903496443875e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 131828, "start": 1325.04, "end": 1331.8799999999999, "text": " If we want to wrap the entire planet in a functional network, are we talking about hundreds of rings, thousands?", "tokens": [50703, 759, 321, 528, 281, 7019, 264, 2302, 5054, 294, 257, 11745, 3209, 11, 366, 321, 1417, 466, 6779, 295, 11136, 11, 5383, 30, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13893658115017798, "compression_ratio": 1.6348684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.741903496443875e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 131828, "start": 1332.18, "end": 1332.48, "text": " Mm-hmm.", "tokens": [51060, 8266, 12, 10250, 13, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13893658115017798, "compression_ratio": 1.6348684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.741903496443875e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 131828, "start": 1332.58, "end": 1335.22, "text": " And how do they intersect to create something useful?", "tokens": [51080, 400, 577, 360, 436, 27815, 281, 1884, 746, 4420, 30, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13893658115017798, "compression_ratio": 1.6348684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.741903496443875e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 131828, "start": 1335.54, "end": 1340.96, "text": " This brings us to the core architectural decision of the entire blueprint, the nine-circle arrangement.", "tokens": [51228, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 4965, 26621, 3537, 295, 264, 2302, 35868, 11, 264, 4949, 12, 23568, 2160, 17620, 13, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13893658115017798, "compression_ratio": 1.6348684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.741903496443875e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 131828, "start": 1341.2, "end": 1341.86, "text": " Just nine.", "tokens": [51511, 1449, 4949, 13, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13893658115017798, "compression_ratio": 1.6348684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.741903496443875e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 131828, "start": 1341.86, "end": 1346.52, "text": " The author does not just throw dozens of rings at the planet randomly to see what sticks.", "tokens": [51544, 440, 3793, 775, 406, 445, 3507, 18431, 295, 11136, 412, 264, 5054, 16979, 281, 536, 437, 12518, 13, 51777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13893658115017798, "compression_ratio": 1.6348684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.741903496443875e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 134652, "start": 1346.52, "end": 1354.96, "text": " The blueprint explicitly specifies exactly nine primary orthodromes, just nine rings to structure the entire globe.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 35868, 20803, 1608, 11221, 2293, 4949, 6194, 19052, 378, 4397, 279, 11, 445, 4949, 11136, 281, 3877, 264, 2302, 15371, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1511440427284541, "compression_ratio": 1.645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430492371325103e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 134652, "start": 1355.06, "end": 1355.82, "text": " It feels so elegant.", "tokens": [50792, 467, 3417, 370, 21117, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1511440427284541, "compression_ratio": 1.645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430492371325103e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 134652, "start": 1356.08, "end": 1356.54, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [50843, 467, 307, 13, 50866], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1511440427284541, "compression_ratio": 1.645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430492371325103e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 134652, "start": 1356.66, "end": 1360.0, "text": " And they are strictly divided into two functional categories.", "tokens": [50872, 400, 436, 366, 20792, 6666, 666, 732, 11745, 10479, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1511440427284541, "compression_ratio": 1.645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430492371325103e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 134652, "start": 1360.76, "end": 1364.52, "text": " Five of them are completely fixed in place, and four of them are flexible.", "tokens": [51077, 9436, 295, 552, 366, 2584, 6806, 294, 1081, 11, 293, 1451, 295, 552, 366, 11358, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1511440427284541, "compression_ratio": 1.645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430492371325103e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 134652, "start": 1364.8, "end": 1365.02, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51279, 1033, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1511440427284541, "compression_ratio": 1.645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430492371325103e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 134652, "start": 1365.2, "end": 1369.74, "text": " Let's look at the five fixed rings first because they form the absolute anchor of the whole system.", "tokens": [51299, 961, 311, 574, 412, 264, 1732, 6806, 11136, 700, 570, 436, 1254, 264, 8236, 18487, 295, 264, 1379, 1185, 13, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1511440427284541, "compression_ratio": 1.645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430492371325103e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 134652, "start": 1369.8, "end": 1370.08, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51529, 1033, 13, 51543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1511440427284541, "compression_ratio": 1.645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430492371325103e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 134652, "start": 1370.08, "end": 1375.8799999999999, "text": " We have one reference equator that's easy to visualize, just the standard belt around the middle of the Earth.", "tokens": [51543, 492, 362, 472, 6408, 45544, 300, 311, 1858, 281, 23273, 11, 445, 264, 3832, 10750, 926, 264, 2808, 295, 264, 4755, 13, 51833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1511440427284541, "compression_ratio": 1.645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430492371325103e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 134652, "start": 1375.96, "end": 1376.48, "text": " That's one.", "tokens": [51837, 663, 311, 472, 13, 51863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1511440427284541, "compression_ratio": 1.645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.9430492371325103e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 137652, "start": 1376.52, "end": 1376.7, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16950891037617832, "compression_ratio": 1.6451612903225807, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839948931158475e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 137652, "start": 1377.1399999999999, "end": 1379.34, "text": " Then we have four polar meridian circles.", "tokens": [50396, 1396, 321, 362, 1451, 12367, 3551, 34681, 13040, 13, 50506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16950891037617832, "compression_ratio": 1.6451612903225807, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839948931158475e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 137652, "start": 1379.92, "end": 1383.5, "text": " So imagine you are an astronaut looking straight down at the North Pole.", "tokens": [50535, 407, 3811, 291, 366, 364, 18516, 1237, 2997, 760, 412, 264, 4067, 34212, 13, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16950891037617832, "compression_ratio": 1.6451612903225807, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839948931158475e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 137652, "start": 1383.6, "end": 1383.84, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50719, 1033, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16950891037617832, "compression_ratio": 1.6451612903225807, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839948931158475e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 137652, "start": 1384.1399999999999, "end": 1390.32, "text": " You draw a massive great circle that slices straight through the pole, cutting the Earth into left and right hemispheres.", "tokens": [50746, 509, 2642, 257, 5994, 869, 6329, 300, 19793, 2997, 807, 264, 13208, 11, 6492, 264, 4755, 666, 1411, 293, 558, 8636, 7631, 19464, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16950891037617832, "compression_ratio": 1.6451612903225807, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839948931158475e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 137652, "start": 1390.66, "end": 1395.52, "text": " Then you draw another one, cutting it top and bottom, making a big X or a cross.", "tokens": [51072, 1396, 291, 2642, 1071, 472, 11, 6492, 309, 1192, 293, 2767, 11, 1455, 257, 955, 1783, 420, 257, 3278, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16950891037617832, "compression_ratio": 1.6451612903225807, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839948931158475e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 137652, "start": 1395.52, "end": 1399.08, "text": " You now have two polar circles intersecting at 90 degrees.", "tokens": [51315, 509, 586, 362, 732, 12367, 13040, 27815, 278, 412, 4289, 5310, 13, 51493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16950891037617832, "compression_ratio": 1.6451612903225807, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839948931158475e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 137652, "start": 1399.46, "end": 1399.58, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51512, 1779, 13, 51518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16950891037617832, "compression_ratio": 1.6451612903225807, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839948931158475e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 137652, "start": 1400.1, "end": 1401.22, "text": " Now, bisect those.", "tokens": [51544, 823, 11, 7393, 557, 729, 13, 51600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16950891037617832, "compression_ratio": 1.6451612903225807, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839948931158475e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 137652, "start": 1402.06, "end": 1404.06, "text": " Draw two more rings perfectly between them.", "tokens": [51642, 20386, 732, 544, 11136, 6239, 1296, 552, 13, 51742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16950891037617832, "compression_ratio": 1.6451612903225807, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839948931158475e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 140406, "start": 1404.06, "end": 1410.4199999999998, "text": " You end up with four lines slicing through the pole, perfectly spaced exactly 45 degrees apart.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 917, 493, 365, 1451, 3876, 46586, 807, 264, 13208, 11, 6239, 43766, 2293, 6905, 5310, 4936, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17206651736528444, "compression_ratio": 1.2357723577235773, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171612660098589e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 140406, "start": 1410.62, "end": 1413.1399999999999, "text": " Or in mathematical terms, pi over four radians.", "tokens": [50693, 1610, 294, 18894, 2115, 11, 3895, 670, 1451, 2843, 2567, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17206651736528444, "compression_ratio": 1.2357723577235773, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171612660098589e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 140406, "start": 1413.26, "end": 1413.56, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [50825, 12753, 13, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17206651736528444, "compression_ratio": 1.2357723577235773, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171612660098589e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 141356, "start": 1413.56, "end": 1424.6, "text": " And because all four of those meridian circles meet at the exact same spot, the North Pole and subsequently the South Pole, we immediately encounter a scenario that breaks the standard rules of geometry.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 570, 439, 1451, 295, 729, 3551, 34681, 13040, 1677, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 4008, 11, 264, 4067, 34212, 293, 26514, 264, 4242, 34212, 11, 321, 4258, 8593, 257, 9005, 300, 9857, 264, 3832, 4474, 295, 18426, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11001016655746772, "compression_ratio": 1.396103896103896, "no_speech_prob": 2.1006137367746147e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 141356, "start": 1424.86, "end": 1425.6599999999999, "text": " Yes, we do.", "tokens": [50930, 1079, 11, 321, 360, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11001016655746772, "compression_ratio": 1.396103896103896, "no_speech_prob": 2.1006137367746147e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 142566, "start": 1425.66, "end": 1431.92, "text": " In what mathematicians call a general position, you usually never have more than two circles crossing at the exact same spot.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 437, 32811, 2567, 818, 257, 2674, 2535, 11, 291, 2673, 1128, 362, 544, 813, 732, 13040, 14712, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 4008, 13, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11439451516843309, "compression_ratio": 1.3541666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6012083152439072e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 142566, "start": 1432.16, "end": 1435.3600000000001, "text": " It's like a standard four-way stop on a road, two lines cross.", "tokens": [50690, 467, 311, 411, 257, 3832, 1451, 12, 676, 1590, 322, 257, 3060, 11, 732, 3876, 3278, 13, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11439451516843309, "compression_ratio": 1.3541666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6012083152439072e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 142566, "start": 1435.44, "end": 1435.64, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50854, 1779, 13, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11439451516843309, "compression_ratio": 1.3541666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6012083152439072e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 143564, "start": 1435.64, "end": 1443.2, "text": " But here, at the poles, we have four distinct planetary rings, all converging at the exact same geographic point.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 510, 11, 412, 264, 24760, 11, 321, 362, 1451, 10644, 35788, 11136, 11, 439, 9652, 3249, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 32318, 935, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12821066206780032, "compression_ratio": 1.4184782608695652, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169179710423531e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 143564, "start": 1443.3400000000001, "end": 1447.98, "text": " The blueprint calls this a multi-way intersection, a node with a multiplicity of four.", "tokens": [50750, 440, 35868, 5498, 341, 257, 4825, 12, 676, 15236, 11, 257, 9984, 365, 257, 17596, 507, 295, 1451, 13, 50982], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12821066206780032, "compression_ratio": 1.4184782608695652, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169179710423531e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 143564, "start": 1448.24, "end": 1451.3200000000002, "text": " It's like an eight-way, massive, global roundabout.", "tokens": [50995, 467, 311, 411, 364, 3180, 12, 676, 11, 5994, 11, 4338, 3098, 21970, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12821066206780032, "compression_ratio": 1.4184782608695652, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169179710423531e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 143564, "start": 1451.5, "end": 1451.98, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51158, 7587, 13, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12821066206780032, "compression_ratio": 1.4184782608695652, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169179710423531e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 145198, "start": 1451.98, "end": 1461.28, "text": " So, if we have these nine rings crisscrossing the globe, how do we figure out how many actual regions or chunks of land this creates on the surface of the Earth?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 498, 321, 362, 613, 4949, 11136, 941, 891, 35418, 278, 264, 15371, 11, 577, 360, 321, 2573, 484, 577, 867, 3539, 10682, 420, 24004, 295, 2117, 341, 7829, 322, 264, 3753, 295, 264, 4755, 30, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15235027737087672, "compression_ratio": 1.6366782006920415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892530568119677e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 145198, "start": 1461.38, "end": 1461.54, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50835, 1779, 13, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15235027737087672, "compression_ratio": 1.6366782006920415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892530568119677e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 145198, "start": 1461.58, "end": 1462.5, "text": " How many neighborhoods do we get?", "tokens": [50845, 1012, 867, 20052, 360, 321, 483, 30, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15235027737087672, "compression_ratio": 1.6366782006920415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892530568119677e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 145198, "start": 1462.76, "end": 1469.06, "text": " To solve this, the blueprint reaches for one of the most beautiful and fundamental rules in all of topology.", "tokens": [50904, 1407, 5039, 341, 11, 264, 35868, 14235, 337, 472, 295, 264, 881, 2238, 293, 8088, 4474, 294, 439, 295, 1192, 1793, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15235027737087672, "compression_ratio": 1.6366782006920415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892530568119677e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 145198, "start": 1469.74, "end": 1471.64, "text": " Euler's formula for a sphere.", "tokens": [51253, 462, 26318, 311, 8513, 337, 257, 16687, 13, 51348], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15235027737087672, "compression_ratio": 1.6366782006920415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892530568119677e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 145198, "start": 1471.88, "end": 1473.1200000000001, "text": " Oh, Euler's formula.", "tokens": [51360, 876, 11, 462, 26318, 311, 8513, 13, 51422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15235027737087672, "compression_ratio": 1.6366782006920415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892530568119677e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 145198, "start": 1473.24, "end": 1474.92, "text": " You might remember this from high school geometry.", "tokens": [51428, 509, 1062, 1604, 341, 490, 1090, 1395, 18426, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15235027737087672, "compression_ratio": 1.6366782006920415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892530568119677e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 145198, "start": 1475.14, "end": 1475.8, "text": " Oh, man.", "tokens": [51523, 876, 11, 587, 13, 51556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15235027737087672, "compression_ratio": 1.6366782006920415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892530568119677e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 145198, "start": 1475.9, "end": 1476.42, "text": " It's been a minute.", "tokens": [51561, 467, 311, 668, 257, 3456, 13, 51587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15235027737087672, "compression_ratio": 1.6366782006920415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892530568119677e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 145198, "start": 1476.56, "end": 1477.98, "text": " Vertices, edges, faces.", "tokens": [51594, 21044, 1473, 11, 8819, 11, 8475, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15235027737087672, "compression_ratio": 1.6366782006920415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892530568119677e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 145198, "start": 1478.2, "end": 1478.38, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51676, 1779, 13, 51685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15235027737087672, "compression_ratio": 1.6366782006920415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892530568119677e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 147838, "start": 1478.38, "end": 1478.94, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09833559525751434, "compression_ratio": 1.6783216783216783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489056435016857e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 147838, "start": 1479.2800000000002, "end": 1483.98, "text": " The classic formula is V minus E plus F equals two.", "tokens": [50410, 440, 7230, 8513, 307, 691, 3175, 462, 1804, 479, 6915, 732, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09833559525751434, "compression_ratio": 1.6783216783216783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489056435016857e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 147838, "start": 1484.24, "end": 1484.46, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50658, 1033, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09833559525751434, "compression_ratio": 1.6783216783216783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489056435016857e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 147838, "start": 1484.5600000000002, "end": 1497.1200000000001, "text": " That stands for vertices, which are the points where lines intersect, minus edges, the line segments connecting the points, plus faces, the enclosed regions or shapes created by those lines, always equals exactly two.", "tokens": [50674, 663, 7382, 337, 32053, 11, 597, 366, 264, 2793, 689, 3876, 27815, 11, 3175, 8819, 11, 264, 1622, 19904, 11015, 264, 2793, 11, 1804, 8475, 11, 264, 42089, 10682, 420, 10854, 2942, 538, 729, 3876, 11, 1009, 6915, 2293, 732, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09833559525751434, "compression_ratio": 1.6783216783216783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489056435016857e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 147838, "start": 1497.3000000000002, "end": 1497.94, "text": " Always two.", "tokens": [51311, 11270, 732, 13, 51343], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09833559525751434, "compression_ratio": 1.6783216783216783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489056435016857e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 147838, "start": 1498.0200000000002, "end": 1503.8600000000001, "text": " It doesn't matter how you draw the lines on the sphere, as long as they connect, that underlying relationship never changes.", "tokens": [51347, 467, 1177, 380, 1871, 577, 291, 2642, 264, 3876, 322, 264, 16687, 11, 382, 938, 382, 436, 1745, 11, 300, 14217, 2480, 1128, 2962, 13, 51639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09833559525751434, "compression_ratio": 1.6783216783216783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489056435016857e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 147838, "start": 1504.5200000000002, "end": 1507.7800000000002, "text": " It is a fundamental topological invariant of our universe.", "tokens": [51672, 467, 307, 257, 8088, 1192, 4383, 33270, 394, 295, 527, 6445, 13, 51835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09833559525751434, "compression_ratio": 1.6783216783216783, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489056435016857e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 150778, "start": 1507.78, "end": 1508.62, "text": " That is wild.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 4868, 13, 50407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11147323309206496, "compression_ratio": 1.451219512195122, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671536334263547e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 150778, "start": 1508.78, "end": 1521.8999999999999, "text": " And fliction adapts this classic formula to account for these massive multiweight intersections at the poles, providing a rigorous way to calculate the exact number of cells or faces created by these nine intersecting rings.", "tokens": [50415, 400, 932, 4105, 23169, 1373, 341, 7230, 8513, 281, 2696, 337, 613, 5994, 4825, 12329, 47664, 412, 264, 24760, 11, 6530, 257, 29882, 636, 281, 8873, 264, 1900, 1230, 295, 5438, 420, 8475, 2942, 538, 613, 4949, 27815, 278, 11136, 13, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11147323309206496, "compression_ratio": 1.451219512195122, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671536334263547e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 152190, "start": 1521.9, "end": 1524.02, "text": " So let's visualize this together right now.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 718, 311, 23273, 341, 1214, 558, 586, 13, 50471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10703168417278089, "compression_ratio": 1.5395348837209302, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884400356864446e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 152190, "start": 1524.24, "end": 1538.64, "text": " If we have our five fixed rings, and let's assume for a moment that our four flexible rings are placed in a standard general position, meaning they are tilted and shifted so they only cross one another in normal pairs, avoiding massive pileups.", "tokens": [50482, 759, 321, 362, 527, 1732, 6806, 11136, 11, 293, 718, 311, 6552, 337, 257, 1623, 300, 527, 1451, 11358, 11136, 366, 7074, 294, 257, 3832, 2674, 2535, 11, 3620, 436, 366, 43229, 293, 18892, 370, 436, 787, 3278, 472, 1071, 294, 2710, 15494, 11, 20220, 5994, 14375, 7528, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10703168417278089, "compression_ratio": 1.5395348837209302, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884400356864446e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 152190, "start": 1538.72, "end": 1538.8400000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51206, 1779, 13, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10703168417278089, "compression_ratio": 1.5395348837209302, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884400356864446e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 152190, "start": 1538.94, "end": 1540.3200000000002, "text": " No extra multiweight intersections.", "tokens": [51217, 883, 2857, 4825, 12329, 47664, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10703168417278089, "compression_ratio": 1.5395348837209302, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884400356864446e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 154032, "start": 1540.32, "end": 1549.0, "text": " If we wrap the globe in these nine rings, how many major intersection nodes connecting highways and massive neighborhoods do we actually get?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 321, 7019, 264, 15371, 294, 613, 4949, 11136, 11, 577, 867, 2563, 15236, 13891, 11015, 43747, 293, 5994, 20052, 360, 321, 767, 483, 30, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09829468727111816, "compression_ratio": 1.517094017094017, "no_speech_prob": 1.554641940355872e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 154032, "start": 1549.1, "end": 1552.78, "text": " The blueprint provides a corollary for this exact calculation.", "tokens": [50804, 440, 35868, 6417, 257, 1181, 1833, 822, 337, 341, 1900, 17108, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09829468727111816, "compression_ratio": 1.517094017094017, "no_speech_prob": 1.554641940355872e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 154032, "start": 1553.1599999999999, "end": 1561.84, "text": " For an arrangement of any number n of great circles in a general position, the math tells us that the number of vertices is n times n minus one.", "tokens": [51007, 1171, 364, 17620, 295, 604, 1230, 297, 295, 869, 13040, 294, 257, 2674, 2535, 11, 264, 5221, 5112, 505, 300, 264, 1230, 295, 32053, 307, 297, 1413, 297, 3175, 472, 13, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09829468727111816, "compression_ratio": 1.517094017094017, "no_speech_prob": 1.554641940355872e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 154032, "start": 1562.2, "end": 1562.48, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51459, 1033, 13, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09829468727111816, "compression_ratio": 1.517094017094017, "no_speech_prob": 1.554641940355872e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 156248, "start": 1562.48, "end": 1569.8, "text": " The number of edges is double that, so can times n minus one, and the number of faces is n squared minus n plus two.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1230, 295, 8819, 307, 3834, 300, 11, 370, 393, 1413, 297, 3175, 472, 11, 293, 264, 1230, 295, 8475, 307, 297, 8889, 3175, 297, 1804, 732, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12370895517283473, "compression_ratio": 1.4742268041237114, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034041057365946e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 156248, "start": 1569.94, "end": 1570.1, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50738, 1033, 13, 50746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12370895517283473, "compression_ratio": 1.4742268041237114, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034041057365946e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 156248, "start": 1570.16, "end": 1571.46, "text": " Let me follow the math here out loud.", "tokens": [50749, 961, 385, 1524, 264, 5221, 510, 484, 6588, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12370895517283473, "compression_ratio": 1.4742268041237114, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034041057365946e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 156248, "start": 1571.52, "end": 1572.9, "text": " We have nine rings, so n is nine.", "tokens": [50817, 492, 362, 4949, 11136, 11, 370, 297, 307, 4949, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12370895517283473, "compression_ratio": 1.4742268041237114, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034041057365946e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 156248, "start": 1573.02, "end": 1573.2, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50892, 1779, 13, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12370895517283473, "compression_ratio": 1.4742268041237114, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034041057365946e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 156248, "start": 1573.46, "end": 1576.94, "text": " For vertices, the major intersections, it's nine times eight, so that's 72.", "tokens": [50914, 1171, 32053, 11, 264, 2563, 47664, 11, 309, 311, 4949, 1413, 3180, 11, 370, 300, 311, 18731, 13, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12370895517283473, "compression_ratio": 1.4742268041237114, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034041057365946e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 156248, "start": 1577.22, "end": 1577.44, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51102, 12753, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12370895517283473, "compression_ratio": 1.4742268041237114, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034041057365946e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 157744, "start": 1577.44, "end": 1581.6000000000001, "text": " There are exactly 72 major global intersection nodes on the planet.", "tokens": [50365, 821, 366, 2293, 18731, 2563, 4338, 15236, 13891, 322, 264, 5054, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13130081460831014, "compression_ratio": 1.5907335907335907, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423724359670988e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 157744, "start": 1582.1000000000001, "end": 1587.38, "text": " For edges, the massive highway segments connecting those nodes, it's double, so 144 segments.", "tokens": [50598, 1171, 8819, 11, 264, 5994, 17205, 19904, 11015, 729, 13891, 11, 309, 311, 3834, 11, 370, 45218, 19904, 13, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13130081460831014, "compression_ratio": 1.5907335907335907, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423724359670988e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 157744, "start": 1587.78, "end": 1595.3600000000001, "text": " And for the faces, the enclosed cells or regions of the planet, nine squared is 81, minus nine is 72, plus two is 74.", "tokens": [50882, 400, 337, 264, 8475, 11, 264, 42089, 5438, 420, 10682, 295, 264, 5054, 11, 4949, 8889, 307, 30827, 11, 3175, 4949, 307, 18731, 11, 1804, 732, 307, 28868, 13, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13130081460831014, "compression_ratio": 1.5907335907335907, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423724359670988e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 157744, "start": 1595.8200000000002, "end": 1604.76, "text": " So this system carves the entire surface of the Earth up into exactly 74 massive distinct neighborhoods bordered by these corridors.", "tokens": [51284, 407, 341, 1185, 1032, 977, 264, 2302, 3753, 295, 264, 4755, 493, 666, 2293, 28868, 5994, 10644, 20052, 25872, 4073, 538, 613, 46920, 13, 51731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13130081460831014, "compression_ratio": 1.5907335907335907, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423724359670988e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 160476, "start": 1604.76, "end": 1611.78, "text": " That is exactly right, and what is profoundly fascinating here is how the system handles what it calls topological stability.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 2293, 558, 11, 293, 437, 307, 39954, 10343, 510, 307, 577, 264, 1185, 18722, 437, 309, 5498, 1192, 4383, 11826, 13, 50716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1579707682817832, "compression_ratio": 1.584033613445378, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764423167007884e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 160476, "start": 1612.08, "end": 1612.3, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50731, 1033, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1579707682817832, "compression_ratio": 1.584033613445378, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764423167007884e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 160476, "start": 1612.3799999999999, "end": 1612.8, "text": " What is that?", "tokens": [50746, 708, 307, 300, 30, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1579707682817832, "compression_ratio": 1.584033613445378, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764423167007884e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 160476, "start": 1612.98, "end": 1614.92, "text": " You mentioned the four flexible rings earlier.", "tokens": [50776, 509, 2835, 264, 1451, 11358, 11136, 3071, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1579707682817832, "compression_ratio": 1.584033613445378, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764423167007884e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 160476, "start": 1615.36, "end": 1618.74, "text": " The blueprint does not permanently lock those four rings in place.", "tokens": [50895, 440, 35868, 775, 406, 24042, 4017, 729, 1451, 11136, 294, 1081, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1579707682817832, "compression_ratio": 1.584033613445378, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764423167007884e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 160476, "start": 1618.8799999999999, "end": 1624.2, "text": " It allows regional and global planners to literally slide these four rings around the globe.", "tokens": [51071, 467, 4045, 10964, 293, 4338, 49674, 281, 3736, 4137, 613, 1451, 11136, 926, 264, 15371, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1579707682817832, "compression_ratio": 1.584033613445378, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764423167007884e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 160476, "start": 1624.32, "end": 1625.06, "text": " They can just move them.", "tokens": [51343, 814, 393, 445, 1286, 552, 13, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1579707682817832, "compression_ratio": 1.584033613445378, "no_speech_prob": 2.0764423167007884e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 162506, "start": 1625.06, "end": 1634.9199999999998, "text": " Yes, they can tilt them on their axis, shift their angles, rotate them to better cover massive population centers, or to intentionally avoid dangerous tectonic fault lines.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 436, 393, 18446, 552, 322, 641, 10298, 11, 5513, 641, 14708, 11, 13121, 552, 281, 1101, 2060, 5994, 4415, 10898, 11, 420, 281, 22062, 5042, 5795, 535, 349, 11630, 7441, 3876, 13, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09195114482532848, "compression_ratio": 1.597972972972973, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414740439633536e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 162506, "start": 1635.06, "end": 1642.28, "text": " But if you start sliding these massive continent-spanning rings around, aren't you completely destroying the geometric perfection we just calculated?", "tokens": [50865, 583, 498, 291, 722, 21169, 613, 5994, 18932, 12, 4952, 282, 773, 11136, 926, 11, 3212, 380, 291, 2584, 19926, 264, 33246, 19708, 321, 445, 15598, 30, 51226], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09195114482532848, "compression_ratio": 1.597972972972973, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414740439633536e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 162506, "start": 1642.4199999999998, "end": 1643.52, "text": " I mean, doesn't the math break?", "tokens": [51233, 286, 914, 11, 1177, 380, 264, 5221, 1821, 30, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09195114482532848, "compression_ratio": 1.597972972972973, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414740439633536e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 162506, "start": 1643.6599999999999, "end": 1645.12, "text": " That is the magic of topology.", "tokens": [51295, 663, 307, 264, 5585, 295, 1192, 1793, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09195114482532848, "compression_ratio": 1.597972972972973, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414740439633536e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 162506, "start": 1645.3799999999999, "end": 1649.74, "text": " As you slide a ring, yes, the physical length of the 144 edges will stretch and shrink.", "tokens": [51381, 1018, 291, 4137, 257, 4875, 11, 2086, 11, 264, 4001, 4641, 295, 264, 45218, 8819, 486, 5985, 293, 23060, 13, 51599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09195114482532848, "compression_ratio": 1.597972972972973, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414740439633536e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 164974, "start": 1649.74, "end": 1653.92, "text": " The actual square mileage of those 74 faces will expand and contract.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3539, 3732, 43121, 295, 729, 28868, 8475, 486, 5268, 293, 4364, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12859706878662108, "compression_ratio": 1.592885375494071, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279150115942499e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 164974, "start": 1654.24, "end": 1662.96, "text": " But the graph itself, the abstract topological map of which node connects to which other node, stays exactly mathematically identical.", "tokens": [50590, 583, 264, 4295, 2564, 11, 264, 12649, 1192, 4383, 4471, 295, 597, 9984, 16967, 281, 597, 661, 9984, 11, 10834, 2293, 44003, 14800, 13, 51026], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12859706878662108, "compression_ratio": 1.592885375494071, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279150115942499e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 164974, "start": 1663.16, "end": 1663.34, "text": " Really?", "tokens": [51036, 4083, 30, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12859706878662108, "compression_ratio": 1.592885375494071, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279150115942499e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 164974, "start": 1663.58, "end": 1663.9, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51057, 1079, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12859706878662108, "compression_ratio": 1.592885375494071, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279150115942499e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 164974, "start": 1664.36, "end": 1669.02, "text": " It is like drawing a network on a rubber balloon and then stretching the balloon.", "tokens": [51096, 467, 307, 411, 6316, 257, 3209, 322, 257, 11593, 16994, 293, 550, 19632, 264, 16994, 13, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12859706878662108, "compression_ratio": 1.592885375494071, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279150115942499e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 164974, "start": 1669.44, "end": 1672.46, "text": " The shapes warp, but the connections remain true.", "tokens": [51350, 440, 10854, 36030, 11, 457, 264, 9271, 6222, 2074, 13, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12859706878662108, "compression_ratio": 1.592885375494071, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279150115942499e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 164974, "start": 1672.82, "end": 1675.94, "text": " Until you stretch it so far that you break the rules.", "tokens": [51519, 9088, 291, 5985, 309, 370, 1400, 300, 291, 1821, 264, 4474, 13, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12859706878662108, "compression_ratio": 1.592885375494071, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279150115942499e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 167594, "start": 1675.94, "end": 1676.5800000000002, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 50397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15763144536849555, "compression_ratio": 1.6590909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661699588788824e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 167594, "start": 1677.0, "end": 1686.2, "text": " If you are sliding one of those flexible rings, and you slide it so far that it accidentally crosses right over a spot where two other rings are already intersecting.", "tokens": [50418, 759, 291, 366, 21169, 472, 295, 729, 11358, 11136, 11, 293, 291, 4137, 309, 370, 1400, 300, 309, 15715, 28467, 558, 670, 257, 4008, 689, 732, 661, 11136, 366, 1217, 27815, 278, 13, 50878], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15763144536849555, "compression_ratio": 1.6590909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661699588788824e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 167594, "start": 1686.2, "end": 1688.14, "text": " You create a new multi-way intersection.", "tokens": [50878, 509, 1884, 257, 777, 4825, 12, 676, 15236, 13, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15763144536849555, "compression_ratio": 1.6590909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661699588788824e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 167594, "start": 1688.3, "end": 1688.56, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50983, 1079, 13, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15763144536849555, "compression_ratio": 1.6590909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661699588788824e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 167594, "start": 1688.8, "end": 1691.7, "text": " You hit what the math calls a degeneracy.", "tokens": [51008, 509, 2045, 437, 264, 5221, 5498, 257, 40520, 2551, 13, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15763144536849555, "compression_ratio": 1.6590909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661699588788824e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 167594, "start": 1692.3200000000002, "end": 1699.16, "text": " The moment three circles cross at the same point instead of two, the mathematical topology of the entire planet physically changes.", "tokens": [51184, 440, 1623, 1045, 13040, 3278, 412, 264, 912, 935, 2602, 295, 732, 11, 264, 18894, 1192, 1793, 295, 264, 2302, 5054, 9762, 2962, 13, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15763144536849555, "compression_ratio": 1.6590909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661699588788824e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 167594, "start": 1699.44, "end": 1699.88, "text": " Oh, right.", "tokens": [51540, 876, 11, 558, 13, 51562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15763144536849555, "compression_ratio": 1.6590909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661699588788824e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 167594, "start": 1699.9, "end": 1701.5, "text": " The number of vertices drops.", "tokens": [51563, 440, 1230, 295, 32053, 11438, 13, 51643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15763144536849555, "compression_ratio": 1.6590909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661699588788824e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 170150, "start": 1701.5, "end": 1708.06, "text": " Fliction writes that moving a ring within a stable topological chamber, just stretching the rubber band, is perfectly fine.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 13657, 300, 2684, 257, 4875, 1951, 257, 8351, 1192, 4383, 13610, 11, 445, 19632, 264, 11593, 4116, 11, 307, 6239, 2489, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14224485314410665, "compression_ratio": 1.6341463414634145, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383336102014033e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 170150, "start": 1708.14, "end": 1709.42, "text": " It's just a local deformation.", "tokens": [50697, 467, 311, 445, 257, 2654, 34364, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14224485314410665, "compression_ratio": 1.6341463414634145, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383336102014033e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 170150, "start": 1709.64, "end": 1709.78, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50772, 1033, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14224485314410665, "compression_ratio": 1.6341463414634145, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383336102014033e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 170150, "start": 1709.92, "end": 1719.58, "text": " But the moment you slide that ring across another intersection, crossing that discriminant set and changing the graph type, that is considered an explicit massive architectural revision.", "tokens": [50786, 583, 264, 1623, 291, 4137, 300, 4875, 2108, 1071, 15236, 11, 14712, 300, 20828, 394, 992, 293, 4473, 264, 4295, 2010, 11, 300, 307, 4888, 364, 13691, 5994, 26621, 34218, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14224485314410665, "compression_ratio": 1.6341463414634145, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383336102014033e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 170150, "start": 1719.8, "end": 1720.6, "text": " Because you broke the map.", "tokens": [51280, 1436, 291, 6902, 264, 4471, 13, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14224485314410665, "compression_ratio": 1.6341463414634145, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383336102014033e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 170150, "start": 1720.82, "end": 1727.22, "text": " That requires a complete global protocol update because you have fundamentally altered the DNA of the planetary map.", "tokens": [51331, 663, 7029, 257, 3566, 4338, 10336, 5623, 570, 291, 362, 17879, 28783, 264, 8272, 295, 264, 35788, 4471, 13, 51651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14224485314410665, "compression_ratio": 1.6341463414634145, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383336102014033e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 170150, "start": 1727.4, "end": 1729.14, "text": " So what does this all mean in plain English?", "tokens": [51660, 407, 437, 775, 341, 439, 914, 294, 11121, 3669, 30, 51747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14224485314410665, "compression_ratio": 1.6341463414634145, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383336102014033e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 172914, "start": 1729.14, "end": 1742.68, "text": " It means we have a planetary architecture that is rigid enough to last for centuries, but flexible enough that we can stretch and warp it to fit the actual lived geography of humanity without destroying the underlying map.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1355, 321, 362, 257, 35788, 9482, 300, 307, 22195, 1547, 281, 1036, 337, 13926, 11, 457, 11358, 1547, 300, 321, 393, 5985, 293, 36030, 309, 281, 3318, 264, 3539, 5152, 26695, 295, 10243, 1553, 19926, 264, 14217, 4471, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15657024582227072, "compression_ratio": 1.5280898876404494, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773407327860587e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 172914, "start": 1742.92, "end": 1743.3200000000002, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51054, 7587, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15657024582227072, "compression_ratio": 1.5280898876404494, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773407327860587e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 172914, "start": 1743.5, "end": 1746.38, "text": " We have a robust, adaptable global skeleton.", "tokens": [51083, 492, 362, 257, 13956, 11, 6231, 712, 4338, 25204, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15657024582227072, "compression_ratio": 1.5280898876404494, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773407327860587e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 172914, "start": 1746.68, "end": 1747.0600000000002, "text": " But hold on.", "tokens": [51242, 583, 1797, 322, 13, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15657024582227072, "compression_ratio": 1.5280898876404494, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773407327860587e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 172914, "start": 1747.1000000000001, "end": 1748.1000000000001, "text": " I'm looking at the scale of this.", "tokens": [51263, 286, 478, 1237, 412, 264, 4373, 295, 341, 13, 51313], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15657024582227072, "compression_ratio": 1.5280898876404494, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773407327860587e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 172914, "start": 1748.5400000000002, "end": 1753.16, "text": " We just calculated that there are only 72 major intersection nodes worldwide.", "tokens": [51335, 492, 445, 15598, 300, 456, 366, 787, 18731, 2563, 15236, 13891, 13485, 13, 51566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15657024582227072, "compression_ratio": 1.5280898876404494, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773407327860587e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 172914, "start": 1753.48, "end": 1753.72, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51582, 1779, 13, 51594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15657024582227072, "compression_ratio": 1.5280898876404494, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773407327860587e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 175372, "start": 1753.72, "end": 1755.9, "text": " 72 nodes to cover the entire Earth.", "tokens": [50365, 18731, 13891, 281, 2060, 264, 2302, 4755, 13, 50474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1435778754098075, "compression_ratio": 1.6454183266932272, "no_speech_prob": 1.489575498538065e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 175372, "start": 1756.02, "end": 1759.18, "text": " That means these nodes are going to be thousands and thousands of miles apart.", "tokens": [50480, 663, 1355, 613, 13891, 366, 516, 281, 312, 5383, 293, 5383, 295, 6193, 4936, 13, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1435778754098075, "compression_ratio": 1.6454183266932272, "no_speech_prob": 1.489575498538065e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 175372, "start": 1759.44, "end": 1759.98, "text": " Very far apart.", "tokens": [50651, 4372, 1400, 4936, 13, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1435778754098075, "compression_ratio": 1.6454183266932272, "no_speech_prob": 1.489575498538065e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 175372, "start": 1760.18, "end": 1769.04, "text": " So if I live in a regular town in the middle of one of those 74 giant faces, one of those massive global neighborhoods, how on earth do I connect to this system?", "tokens": [50688, 407, 498, 286, 1621, 294, 257, 3890, 3954, 294, 264, 2808, 295, 472, 295, 729, 28868, 7410, 8475, 11, 472, 295, 729, 5994, 4338, 20052, 11, 577, 322, 4120, 360, 286, 1745, 281, 341, 1185, 30, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1435778754098075, "compression_ratio": 1.6454183266932272, "no_speech_prob": 1.489575498538065e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 175372, "start": 1769.18, "end": 1775.1200000000001, "text": " Like how does my local water utility or my local power grid know which of those 72 nodes is my node?", "tokens": [51138, 1743, 577, 775, 452, 2654, 1281, 14877, 420, 452, 2654, 1347, 10748, 458, 597, 295, 729, 18731, 13891, 307, 452, 9984, 30, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1435778754098075, "compression_ratio": 1.6454183266932272, "no_speech_prob": 1.489575498538065e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 175372, "start": 1775.56, "end": 1776.46, "text": " Where do I plug in?", "tokens": [51457, 2305, 360, 286, 5452, 294, 30, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1435778754098075, "compression_ratio": 1.6454183266932272, "no_speech_prob": 1.489575498538065e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 177646, "start": 1776.46, "end": 1780.54, "text": " That is the glaring problem with only having a global skeleton.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 264, 1563, 1921, 1154, 365, 787, 1419, 257, 4338, 25204, 13, 50569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20150431238039576, "compression_ratio": 1.5903614457831325, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773431180308382e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 177646, "start": 1781.42, "end": 1790.0, "text": " The orthodromes give us the massive intercontinental highways, but as you rightly point out, they are utterly insufficient for actually serving local populations.", "tokens": [50613, 440, 19052, 378, 4397, 279, 976, 505, 264, 5994, 728, 9000, 38653, 43747, 11, 457, 382, 291, 32879, 935, 484, 11, 436, 366, 30251, 41709, 337, 767, 8148, 2654, 12822, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20150431238039576, "compression_ratio": 1.5903614457831325, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773431180308382e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 177646, "start": 1790.06, "end": 1790.2, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51045, 1779, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20150431238039576, "compression_ratio": 1.5903614457831325, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773431180308382e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 177646, "start": 1790.26, "end": 1791.0, "text": " You need off-ramps.", "tokens": [51055, 509, 643, 766, 12, 81, 23150, 13, 51092], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20150431238039576, "compression_ratio": 1.5903614457831325, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773431180308382e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 177646, "start": 1791.3600000000001, "end": 1793.04, "text": " We need a second layer of geometry.", "tokens": [51110, 492, 643, 257, 1150, 4583, 295, 18426, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20150431238039576, "compression_ratio": 1.5903614457831325, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773431180308382e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 177646, "start": 1793.3, "end": 1794.4, "text": " We need the connective tissue.", "tokens": [51207, 492, 643, 264, 1745, 488, 12404, 13, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20150431238039576, "compression_ratio": 1.5903614457831325, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773431180308382e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 177646, "start": 1794.94, "end": 1798.94, "text": " And this is where the blueprint introduces spherical service geometry.", "tokens": [51289, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 35868, 31472, 37300, 2643, 18426, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20150431238039576, "compression_ratio": 1.5903614457831325, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773431180308382e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 177646, "start": 1799.1000000000001, "end": 1799.22, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51497, 3153, 13, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20150431238039576, "compression_ratio": 1.5903614457831325, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773431180308382e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 179922, "start": 1799.22, "end": 1805.58, "text": " Specifically, it uses two mathematical concepts, Voronoi cells and the Delaunay complex.", "tokens": [50365, 26058, 11, 309, 4960, 732, 18894, 10392, 11, 12231, 266, 4869, 5438, 293, 264, 413, 4053, 409, 320, 3997, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16921365672144398, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553989945656712e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 179922, "start": 1805.7, "end": 1805.98, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50689, 1033, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16921365672144398, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553989945656712e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 179922, "start": 1806.18, "end": 1807.14, "text": " Voronoi patterns.", "tokens": [50713, 12231, 266, 4869, 8294, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16921365672144398, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553989945656712e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 179922, "start": 1807.26, "end": 1808.22, "text": " I actually love these.", "tokens": [50767, 286, 767, 959, 613, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16921365672144398, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553989945656712e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 179922, "start": 1808.38, "end": 1808.9, "text": " You do.", "tokens": [50823, 509, 360, 13, 50849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16921365672144398, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553989945656712e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 179922, "start": 1809.06, "end": 1809.2, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50857, 865, 13, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16921365672144398, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553989945656712e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 179922, "start": 1809.26, "end": 1810.6200000000001, "text": " You see them in nature all the time.", "tokens": [50867, 509, 536, 552, 294, 3687, 439, 264, 565, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16921365672144398, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553989945656712e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 179922, "start": 1810.78, "end": 1811.0, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50943, 865, 13, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16921365672144398, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553989945656712e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 179922, "start": 1811.06, "end": 1820.32, "text": " If you look at the spots on a giraffe or the way mud cracks when it dries in the sun or the intricate web of a dragonfly's wing, those are all Voronoi patterns.", "tokens": [50957, 759, 291, 574, 412, 264, 10681, 322, 257, 49897, 420, 264, 636, 8933, 21770, 562, 309, 33997, 294, 264, 3295, 420, 264, 38015, 3670, 295, 257, 12165, 14061, 311, 11162, 11, 729, 366, 439, 12231, 266, 4869, 8294, 13, 51420], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16921365672144398, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553989945656712e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 179922, "start": 1820.44, "end": 1821.1200000000001, "text": " That's very true.", "tokens": [51426, 663, 311, 588, 2074, 13, 51460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16921365672144398, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553989945656712e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 179922, "start": 1821.1200000000001, "end": 1825.46, "text": " It's basically a mathematical way of dividing up space based on who is closest to what.", "tokens": [51460, 467, 311, 1936, 257, 18894, 636, 295, 26764, 493, 1901, 2361, 322, 567, 307, 13699, 281, 437, 13, 51677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16921365672144398, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553989945656712e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 179922, "start": 1825.98, "end": 1828.98, "text": " That is a perfect intuitive way to understand it.", "tokens": [51703, 663, 307, 257, 2176, 21769, 636, 281, 1223, 309, 13, 51853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16921365672144398, "compression_ratio": 1.7080536912751678, "no_speech_prob": 1.7553989945656712e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 182922, "start": 1829.22, "end": 1830.6000000000001, "text": " Let's use a very human example.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 764, 257, 588, 1952, 1365, 13, 50434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11313840384795287, "compression_ratio": 1.5970695970695972, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171442440357509e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 182922, "start": 1831.2, "end": 1835.8600000000001, "text": " Imagine a city with 10 different pizza delivery restaurants scattered randomly around town.", "tokens": [50464, 11739, 257, 2307, 365, 1266, 819, 8298, 8982, 11486, 21986, 16979, 926, 3954, 13, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11313840384795287, "compression_ratio": 1.5970695970695972, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171442440357509e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 182922, "start": 1835.92, "end": 1836.6000000000001, "text": " Best city ever.", "tokens": [50700, 9752, 2307, 1562, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11313840384795287, "compression_ratio": 1.5970695970695972, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171442440357509e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 182922, "start": 1836.98, "end": 1837.28, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50753, 1779, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11313840384795287, "compression_ratio": 1.5970695970695972, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171442440357509e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 182922, "start": 1837.6200000000001, "end": 1846.4, "text": " If you want to draw a map that assigns every single house in the city to the pizza place that is closest to them, you are drawing a Voronoi diagram.", "tokens": [50785, 759, 291, 528, 281, 2642, 257, 4471, 300, 6269, 82, 633, 2167, 1782, 294, 264, 2307, 281, 264, 8298, 1081, 300, 307, 13699, 281, 552, 11, 291, 366, 6316, 257, 12231, 266, 4869, 10686, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11313840384795287, "compression_ratio": 1.5970695970695972, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171442440357509e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 182922, "start": 1846.76, "end": 1850.04, "text": " You draw boundary lines exactly halfway between each restaurant.", "tokens": [51242, 509, 2642, 12866, 3876, 2293, 15461, 1296, 1184, 6383, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11313840384795287, "compression_ratio": 1.5970695970695972, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171442440357509e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 182922, "start": 1850.04, "end": 1853.48, "text": " So you end up with these polygon-shaped territories covering the city.", "tokens": [51406, 407, 291, 917, 493, 365, 613, 48242, 12, 23103, 25195, 10322, 264, 2307, 13, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11313840384795287, "compression_ratio": 1.5970695970695972, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171442440357509e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 182922, "start": 1853.6000000000001, "end": 1853.98, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51584, 1079, 13, 51603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11313840384795287, "compression_ratio": 1.5970695970695972, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171442440357509e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 185398, "start": 1853.98, "end": 1860.3600000000001, "text": " If my house is inside polygon A, I know for a mathematical fact that restaurant A is my closest option.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 452, 1782, 307, 1854, 48242, 316, 11, 286, 458, 337, 257, 18894, 1186, 300, 6383, 316, 307, 452, 13699, 3614, 13, 50684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1597114520126514, "compression_ratio": 1.5381355932203389, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830478846875275e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 185398, "start": 1860.58, "end": 1861.14, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50695, 7587, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1597114520126514, "compression_ratio": 1.5381355932203389, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830478846875275e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 185398, "start": 1861.68, "end": 1865.02, "text": " Now take that exact same logic and apply it to a planetary sphere.", "tokens": [50750, 823, 747, 300, 1900, 912, 9952, 293, 3079, 309, 281, 257, 35788, 16687, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1597114520126514, "compression_ratio": 1.5381355932203389, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830478846875275e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 185398, "start": 1865.56, "end": 1869.78, "text": " We have our 72 massive intersection nodes from the primary skeleton.", "tokens": [50944, 492, 362, 527, 18731, 5994, 15236, 13891, 490, 264, 6194, 25204, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1597114520126514, "compression_ratio": 1.5381355932203389, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830478846875275e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 185398, "start": 1870.28, "end": 1875.92, "text": " We can assign every single square inch on Earth to its nearest node based on geodesic distance.", "tokens": [51180, 492, 393, 6269, 633, 2167, 3732, 7227, 322, 4755, 281, 1080, 23831, 9984, 2361, 322, 1519, 4789, 299, 4560, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1597114520126514, "compression_ratio": 1.5381355932203389, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830478846875275e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 185398, "start": 1876.1200000000001, "end": 1876.96, "text": " Geodesic distance.", "tokens": [51472, 2876, 4789, 299, 4560, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1597114520126514, "compression_ratio": 1.5381355932203389, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830478846875275e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 187696, "start": 1876.96, "end": 1880.7, "text": " The absolute shortest path across the curved surface of the globe.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 8236, 31875, 3100, 2108, 264, 24991, 3753, 295, 264, 15371, 13, 50552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12999241087171767, "compression_ratio": 1.668103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.4151299489867375e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 187696, "start": 1881.3400000000001, "end": 1884.78, "text": " That defined territory is the node's spherical Voronoi cell.", "tokens": [50584, 663, 7642, 11360, 307, 264, 9984, 311, 37300, 12231, 266, 4869, 2815, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12999241087171767, "compression_ratio": 1.668103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.4151299489867375e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 187696, "start": 1884.92, "end": 1885.1000000000001, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50763, 1033, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12999241087171767, "compression_ratio": 1.668103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.4151299489867375e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 187696, "start": 1885.3, "end": 1890.6000000000001, "text": " The blueprint proves mathematically that every unweighted spherical Voronoi cell is spherically convex.", "tokens": [50782, 440, 35868, 25019, 44003, 300, 633, 517, 12329, 292, 37300, 12231, 266, 4869, 2815, 307, 637, 511, 984, 42432, 13, 51047], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12999241087171767, "compression_ratio": 1.668103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.4151299489867375e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 187696, "start": 1891.1200000000001, "end": 1897.98, "text": " It guarantees that every town, every city, every farm on Earth falls into exactly one cleanly defined surface territory.", "tokens": [51073, 467, 32567, 300, 633, 3954, 11, 633, 2307, 11, 633, 5421, 322, 4755, 8804, 666, 2293, 472, 2541, 356, 7642, 3753, 11360, 13, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12999241087171767, "compression_ratio": 1.668103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.4151299489867375e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 187696, "start": 1898.08, "end": 1899.08, "text": " So everyone knows their hub.", "tokens": [51421, 407, 1518, 3255, 641, 11838, 13, 51471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12999241087171767, "compression_ratio": 1.668103448275862, "no_speech_prob": 1.4151299489867375e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 189908, "start": 1899.08, "end": 1899.52, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1352443394698496, "compression_ratio": 1.6771929824561405, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414748029048743e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 189908, "start": 1900.02, "end": 1905.9399999999998, "text": " If you live inside that territory, all your local water, power, and data route to that territory is central node.", "tokens": [50412, 759, 291, 1621, 1854, 300, 11360, 11, 439, 428, 2654, 1281, 11, 1347, 11, 293, 1412, 7955, 281, 300, 11360, 307, 5777, 9984, 13, 50708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1352443394698496, "compression_ratio": 1.6771929824561405, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414748029048743e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 189908, "start": 1906.24, "end": 1906.46, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50723, 1033, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1352443394698496, "compression_ratio": 1.6771929824561405, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414748029048743e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 189908, "start": 1906.54, "end": 1908.54, "text": " So we've mapped out the surface territories.", "tokens": [50738, 407, 321, 600, 33318, 484, 264, 3753, 25195, 13, 50838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1352443394698496, "compression_ratio": 1.6771929824561405, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414748029048743e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 189908, "start": 1908.96, "end": 1912.26, "text": " But what if the node in my territory goes offline?", "tokens": [50859, 583, 437, 498, 264, 9984, 294, 452, 11360, 1709, 21857, 30, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1352443394698496, "compression_ratio": 1.6771929824561405, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414748029048743e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 189908, "start": 1912.76, "end": 1918.74, "text": " Or what if I need to send data to the town right next to me, but they're in a different Voronoi cell?", "tokens": [51049, 1610, 437, 498, 286, 643, 281, 2845, 1412, 281, 264, 3954, 558, 958, 281, 385, 11, 457, 436, 434, 294, 257, 819, 12231, 266, 4869, 2815, 30, 51348], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1352443394698496, "compression_ratio": 1.6771929824561405, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414748029048743e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 189908, "start": 1919.52, "end": 1925.34, "text": " Do I have to send my data all the way up to the Global Orthodrome Highway, down the ring, and back into their territory?", "tokens": [51387, 1144, 286, 362, 281, 2845, 452, 1412, 439, 264, 636, 493, 281, 264, 14465, 27554, 378, 11505, 30911, 11, 760, 264, 4875, 11, 293, 646, 666, 641, 11360, 30, 51678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1352443394698496, "compression_ratio": 1.6771929824561405, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414748029048743e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 189908, "start": 1925.6399999999999, "end": 1927.4399999999998, "text": " That seems hugely inefficient.", "tokens": [51693, 663, 2544, 27417, 43495, 13, 51783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1352443394698496, "compression_ratio": 1.6771929824561405, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414748029048743e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 192744, "start": 1927.44, "end": 1933.38, "text": " It would be, which is why we need the second half of this mathematical pairing, the spherical Delaunay complex.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 576, 312, 11, 597, 307, 983, 321, 643, 264, 1150, 1922, 295, 341, 18894, 32735, 11, 264, 37300, 413, 4053, 409, 320, 3997, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14435321406314247, "compression_ratio": 1.5740072202166064, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886488530248653e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 192744, "start": 1933.52, "end": 1934.2, "text": " Your connective tissue.", "tokens": [50669, 2260, 1745, 488, 12404, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14435321406314247, "compression_ratio": 1.5740072202166064, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886488530248653e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 192744, "start": 1934.42, "end": 1934.6200000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50714, 1779, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14435321406314247, "compression_ratio": 1.5740072202166064, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886488530248653e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 192744, "start": 1935.04, "end": 1941.06, "text": " Once we have our Voronoi pizza delivery zones mapped out, we can draw what is called a dual graph.", "tokens": [50745, 3443, 321, 362, 527, 12231, 266, 4869, 8298, 8982, 16025, 33318, 484, 11, 321, 393, 2642, 437, 307, 1219, 257, 11848, 4295, 13, 51046], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14435321406314247, "compression_ratio": 1.5740072202166064, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886488530248653e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 192744, "start": 1941.54, "end": 1943.28, "text": " This is our secondary network layer.", "tokens": [51070, 639, 307, 527, 11396, 3209, 4583, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14435321406314247, "compression_ratio": 1.5740072202166064, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886488530248653e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 192744, "start": 1943.54, "end": 1944.38, "text": " The rule is simple.", "tokens": [51170, 440, 4978, 307, 2199, 13, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14435321406314247, "compression_ratio": 1.5740072202166064, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886488530248653e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 192744, "start": 1945.22, "end": 1953.1000000000001, "text": " If two Voronoi service territories physically touch, if they share a border wall, you draw a line connecting their two central nodes.", "tokens": [51254, 759, 732, 12231, 266, 4869, 2643, 25195, 9762, 2557, 11, 498, 436, 2073, 257, 7838, 2929, 11, 291, 2642, 257, 1622, 11015, 641, 732, 5777, 13891, 13, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14435321406314247, "compression_ratio": 1.5740072202166064, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886488530248653e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 192744, "start": 1953.42, "end": 1953.72, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [51664, 2438, 13, 51679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14435321406314247, "compression_ratio": 1.5740072202166064, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886488530248653e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 195372, "start": 1953.72, "end": 1957.88, "text": " So it's not a global ring, it's just a direct local bridge between next-door neighbors.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 309, 311, 406, 257, 4338, 4875, 11, 309, 311, 445, 257, 2047, 2654, 7283, 1296, 958, 12, 10441, 12512, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17772791657266737, "compression_ratio": 1.483568075117371, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893217309767335e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 195372, "start": 1958.08, "end": 1958.52, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50583, 48746, 736, 13, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17772791657266737, "compression_ratio": 1.483568075117371, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893217309767335e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 195372, "start": 1958.84, "end": 1962.1000000000001, "text": " Two nodes are Delaunay adjacent if their surface regions share a boundary.", "tokens": [50621, 4453, 13891, 366, 413, 4053, 409, 320, 24441, 498, 641, 3753, 10682, 2073, 257, 12866, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17772791657266737, "compression_ratio": 1.483568075117371, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893217309767335e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 195372, "start": 1962.44, "end": 1964.78, "text": " You connect those nodes with a secondary physical link.", "tokens": [50801, 509, 1745, 729, 13891, 365, 257, 11396, 4001, 2113, 13, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17772791657266737, "compression_ratio": 1.483568075117371, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893217309767335e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 195372, "start": 1965.3600000000001, "end": 1969.76, "text": " This gives us the complete three-layer connectivity model that the blueprint dictates.", "tokens": [50947, 639, 2709, 505, 264, 3566, 1045, 12, 8376, 260, 21095, 2316, 300, 264, 35868, 12569, 1024, 13, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17772791657266737, "compression_ratio": 1.483568075117371, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893217309767335e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 196976, "start": 1969.76, "end": 1977.56, "text": " Layer one is the primary layer, the massive great circle orthodromic skeleton circling the whole planet.", "tokens": [50365, 35166, 472, 307, 264, 6194, 4583, 11, 264, 5994, 869, 6329, 19052, 378, 4397, 299, 25204, 3510, 1688, 264, 1379, 5054, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11723894278208415, "compression_ratio": 1.4971098265895955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102642223098096e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 196976, "start": 1978.04, "end": 1985.74, "text": " Layer two is the secondary layer, the Delaunay connective tissue that bridges neighboring surface zones directly, providing vital local redundancy.", "tokens": [50779, 35166, 732, 307, 264, 11396, 4583, 11, 264, 413, 4053, 409, 320, 1745, 488, 12404, 300, 21114, 31521, 3753, 16025, 3838, 11, 6530, 11707, 2654, 27830, 6717, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11723894278208415, "compression_ratio": 1.4971098265895955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102642223098096e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 196976, "start": 1985.82, "end": 1986.04, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51168, 1779, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11723894278208415, "compression_ratio": 1.4971098265895955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102642223098096e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 198604, "start": 1986.04, "end": 1994.78, "text": " And layer three is the tertiary layer, the highly localized regional realization routes, the actual pipes running under my street.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 4583, 1045, 307, 264, 38726, 29104, 4583, 11, 264, 5405, 44574, 10964, 25138, 18242, 11, 264, 3539, 21882, 2614, 833, 452, 4838, 13, 50802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1215705326625279, "compression_ratio": 1.547945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423717854457953e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 198604, "start": 1994.8999999999999, "end": 1995.22, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50808, 7587, 13, 50824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1215705326625279, "compression_ratio": 1.547945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423717854457953e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 198604, "start": 1995.46, "end": 2000.12, "text": " The overarching design principle here is fixed skeleton adaptive tissue.", "tokens": [50836, 440, 45501, 1715, 8665, 510, 307, 6806, 25204, 27912, 12404, 13, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1215705326625279, "compression_ratio": 1.547945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423717854457953e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 198604, "start": 2000.24, "end": 2000.94, "text": " I like that phrase.", "tokens": [51075, 286, 411, 300, 9535, 13, 51110], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1215705326625279, "compression_ratio": 1.547945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423717854457953e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 198604, "start": 2001.1599999999999, "end": 2006.8, "text": " The massive great circles preserve the global identity and intercontinental coordination across centuries.", "tokens": [51121, 440, 5994, 869, 13040, 15665, 264, 4338, 6575, 293, 728, 9000, 38653, 21252, 2108, 13926, 13, 51403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1215705326625279, "compression_ratio": 1.547945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423717854457953e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 200680, "start": 2006.8, "end": 2011.54, "text": " But the Delaunay connective tissue minimizes local service separation.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 413, 4053, 409, 320, 1745, 488, 12404, 4464, 5660, 2654, 2643, 14634, 13, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15756380874498754, "compression_ratio": 1.51953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686404862020776e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 200680, "start": 2011.82, "end": 2013.4199999999998, "text": " So you don't always have to go to the main highway.", "tokens": [50616, 407, 291, 500, 380, 1009, 362, 281, 352, 281, 264, 2135, 17205, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15756380874498754, "compression_ratio": 1.51953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686404862020776e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 200680, "start": 2013.58, "end": 2013.84, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50704, 1779, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15756380874498754, "compression_ratio": 1.51953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686404862020776e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 200680, "start": 2014.2, "end": 2022.34, "text": " If you need a backup route between two nearby nodes, you don't commission a brand new 10,000-mile planetary great circle.", "tokens": [50735, 759, 291, 643, 257, 14807, 7955, 1296, 732, 11184, 13891, 11, 291, 500, 380, 9221, 257, 3360, 777, 1266, 11, 1360, 12, 44927, 35788, 869, 6329, 13, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15756380874498754, "compression_ratio": 1.51953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686404862020776e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 200680, "start": 2022.56, "end": 2024.58, "text": " You just use a local Delaunay edge.", "tokens": [51153, 509, 445, 764, 257, 2654, 413, 4053, 409, 320, 4691, 13, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15756380874498754, "compression_ratio": 1.51953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686404862020776e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 200680, "start": 2024.78, "end": 2025.02, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51264, 1033, 13, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15756380874498754, "compression_ratio": 1.51953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686404862020776e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 200680, "start": 2025.26, "end": 2027.04, "text": " This all sounds incredibly elegant.", "tokens": [51288, 639, 439, 3263, 6252, 21117, 13, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15756380874498754, "compression_ratio": 1.51953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686404862020776e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 200680, "start": 2027.58, "end": 2028.82, "text": " But I have to push back on something here.", "tokens": [51404, 583, 286, 362, 281, 2944, 646, 322, 746, 510, 13, 51466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15756380874498754, "compression_ratio": 1.51953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686404862020776e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 200680, "start": 2028.82, "end": 2029.02, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51466, 1033, 13, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15756380874498754, "compression_ratio": 1.51953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686404862020776e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 200680, "start": 2029.1399999999999, "end": 2029.56, "text": " Push back.", "tokens": [51482, 18229, 646, 13, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15756380874498754, "compression_ratio": 1.51953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686404862020776e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 202956, "start": 2029.56, "end": 2037.58, "text": " If this is a perfectly planned, mathematically optimized planetary blueprint, why does it look like dragonfly wings or cracked mud?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 341, 307, 257, 6239, 8589, 11, 44003, 26941, 35788, 35868, 11, 983, 775, 309, 574, 411, 12165, 14061, 11405, 420, 25140, 8933, 30, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12082950070373014, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729538982087177e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 202956, "start": 2038.06, "end": 2038.52, "text": " What do you mean?", "tokens": [50790, 708, 360, 291, 914, 30, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12082950070373014, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729538982087177e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 202956, "start": 2038.84, "end": 2048.24, "text": " Why not just cover the Earth in identical, perfectly repeating, flawless hexagons, like a giant game of Settlers of Catan or a massive honeycomb?", "tokens": [50829, 1545, 406, 445, 2060, 264, 4755, 294, 14800, 11, 6239, 18617, 11, 45693, 23291, 559, 892, 11, 411, 257, 7410, 1216, 295, 318, 3093, 11977, 295, 9565, 282, 420, 257, 5994, 8330, 38763, 30, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12082950070373014, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729538982087177e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 202956, "start": 2048.82, "end": 2051.7, "text": " Why do some regions get slightly different shapes or sizes?", "tokens": [51328, 1545, 360, 512, 10682, 483, 4748, 819, 10854, 420, 11602, 30, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12082950070373014, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729538982087177e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 202956, "start": 2052.04, "end": 2053.14, "text": " Why is there variation?", "tokens": [51489, 1545, 307, 456, 12990, 30, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12082950070373014, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729538982087177e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 202956, "start": 2053.6, "end": 2056.16, "text": " Why can't we just mandate perfect uniformity?", "tokens": [51567, 1545, 393, 380, 321, 445, 23885, 2176, 9452, 507, 30, 51695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12082950070373014, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729538982087177e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 202956, "start": 2056.24, "end": 2057.7, "text": " Because the universe will not let you.", "tokens": [51699, 1436, 264, 6445, 486, 406, 718, 291, 13, 51772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12082950070373014, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729538982087177e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 202956, "start": 2057.88, "end": 2058.24, "text": " Really?", "tokens": [51781, 4083, 30, 51799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12082950070373014, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729538982087177e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 205824, "start": 2058.24, "end": 2064.04, "text": " And this brings us to what I consider the most beautiful, humbling mathematical truth in the entire blueprint.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 5607, 505, 281, 437, 286, 1949, 264, 881, 2238, 11, 1484, 18262, 18894, 3494, 294, 264, 2302, 35868, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11699195072568697, "compression_ratio": 1.7466666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050194384676584e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 205824, "start": 2064.58, "end": 2070.6, "text": " You physically, mathematically cannot cover a sphere purely in perfect hexagons.", "tokens": [50682, 509, 9762, 11, 44003, 2644, 2060, 257, 16687, 17491, 294, 2176, 23291, 559, 892, 13, 50983], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11699195072568697, "compression_ratio": 1.7466666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050194384676584e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 205824, "start": 2070.74, "end": 2071.56, "text": " Wait, you can't?", "tokens": [50990, 3802, 11, 291, 393, 380, 30, 51031], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11699195072568697, "compression_ratio": 1.7466666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050194384676584e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 205824, "start": 2071.58, "end": 2072.4199999999996, "text": " It is impossible.", "tokens": [51032, 467, 307, 6243, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11699195072568697, "compression_ratio": 1.7466666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050194384676584e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 205824, "start": 2072.66, "end": 2074.4199999999996, "text": " It is a concept called the curvature defect.", "tokens": [51086, 467, 307, 257, 3410, 1219, 264, 37638, 16445, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11699195072568697, "compression_ratio": 1.7466666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050194384676584e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 205824, "start": 2074.54, "end": 2075.3599999999997, "text": " The curvature defect.", "tokens": [51180, 440, 37638, 16445, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11699195072568697, "compression_ratio": 1.7466666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050194384676584e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 205824, "start": 2075.56, "end": 2077.1, "text": " Okay, you can't just wrap a sphere in hexes.", "tokens": [51231, 1033, 11, 291, 393, 380, 445, 7019, 257, 16687, 294, 23291, 279, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11699195072568697, "compression_ratio": 1.7466666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050194384676584e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 205824, "start": 2077.14, "end": 2077.62, "text": " You cannot.", "tokens": [51310, 509, 2644, 13, 51334], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11699195072568697, "compression_ratio": 1.7466666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050194384676584e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 205824, "start": 2077.8199999999997, "end": 2080.04, "text": " And the blueprint walks us through exactly why.", "tokens": [51344, 400, 264, 35868, 12896, 505, 807, 2293, 983, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11699195072568697, "compression_ratio": 1.7466666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050194384676584e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 205824, "start": 2080.22, "end": 2081.8199999999997, "text": " Let's look at a flat surface first.", "tokens": [51464, 961, 311, 574, 412, 257, 4962, 3753, 700, 13, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11699195072568697, "compression_ratio": 1.7466666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050194384676584e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 205824, "start": 2081.9399999999996, "end": 2082.2599999999998, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51550, 1033, 13, 51566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11699195072568697, "compression_ratio": 1.7466666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050194384676584e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 205824, "start": 2082.4599999999996, "end": 2086.52, "text": " If you want to tile a flat floor with perfect hexagons, you can do it forever.", "tokens": [51576, 759, 291, 528, 281, 20590, 257, 4962, 4123, 365, 2176, 23291, 559, 892, 11, 291, 393, 360, 309, 5680, 13, 51779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11699195072568697, "compression_ratio": 1.7466666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050194384676584e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 205824, "start": 2086.74, "end": 2087.08, "text": " Why?", "tokens": [51790, 1545, 30, 51807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11699195072568697, "compression_ratio": 1.7466666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050194384676584e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 208708, "start": 2087.08, "end": 2091.54, "text": " Because a perfect hexagon has internal angles of 120 degrees.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 257, 2176, 23291, 6709, 575, 6920, 14708, 295, 10411, 5310, 13, 50588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18631991361960387, "compression_ratio": 1.5181347150259068, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507043790730866e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 208708, "start": 2091.92, "end": 2092.02, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50607, 1779, 13, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18631991361960387, "compression_ratio": 1.5181347150259068, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507043790730866e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 208708, "start": 2092.16, "end": 2099.12, "text": " If you put three of them together at a single point, 120 plus 120 plus 120 equals exactly 360 degrees.", "tokens": [50619, 759, 291, 829, 1045, 295, 552, 1214, 412, 257, 2167, 935, 11, 10411, 1804, 10411, 1804, 10411, 6915, 2293, 13898, 5310, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18631991361960387, "compression_ratio": 1.5181347150259068, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507043790730866e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 208708, "start": 2099.2999999999997, "end": 2102.54, "text": " It forms a perfect flat circle around that point.", "tokens": [50976, 467, 6422, 257, 2176, 4962, 6329, 926, 300, 935, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18631991361960387, "compression_ratio": 1.5181347150259068, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507043790730866e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 208708, "start": 2102.66, "end": 2104.18, "text": " It lays completely flat on the ground.", "tokens": [51144, 467, 32714, 2584, 4962, 322, 264, 2727, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18631991361960387, "compression_ratio": 1.5181347150259068, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507043790730866e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 208708, "start": 2104.2799999999997, "end": 2104.42, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51225, 1033, 13, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18631991361960387, "compression_ratio": 1.5181347150259068, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507043790730866e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 208708, "start": 2104.5, "end": 2105.58, "text": " Making total sense so far.", "tokens": [51236, 14595, 3217, 2020, 370, 1400, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18631991361960387, "compression_ratio": 1.5181347150259068, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507043790730866e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 210558, "start": 2105.58, "end": 2107.22, "text": " 360 degrees means it's flat.", "tokens": [50365, 13898, 5310, 1355, 309, 311, 4962, 13, 50447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24759649193805197, "compression_ratio": 1.3630573248407643, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549042951979898e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 210558, "start": 2107.22, "end": 2109.2799999999997, "text": " But a planet is not flat.", "tokens": [50447, 583, 257, 5054, 307, 406, 4962, 13, 50550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24759649193805197, "compression_ratio": 1.3630573248407643, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549042951979898e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 210558, "start": 2109.46, "end": 2111.0, "text": " It has positive curvature.", "tokens": [50559, 467, 575, 3353, 37638, 13, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24759649193805197, "compression_ratio": 1.3630573248407643, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549042951979898e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 210558, "start": 2111.24, "end": 2112.54, "text": " It curves back on itself.", "tokens": [50648, 467, 19490, 646, 322, 2564, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24759649193805197, "compression_ratio": 1.3630573248407643, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549042951979898e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 210558, "start": 2113.12, "end": 2117.22, "text": " To wrap a sheet of material around a sphere, you cannot have it lay flat.", "tokens": [50742, 1407, 7019, 257, 8193, 295, 2527, 926, 257, 16687, 11, 291, 2644, 362, 309, 2360, 4962, 13, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24759649193805197, "compression_ratio": 1.3630573248407643, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549042951979898e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 210558, "start": 2117.34, "end": 2118.44, "text": " You have to pinch it.", "tokens": [50953, 509, 362, 281, 14614, 309, 13, 51008], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24759649193805197, "compression_ratio": 1.3630573248407643, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549042951979898e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 210558, "start": 2118.72, "end": 2119.08, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [51022, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24759649193805197, "compression_ratio": 1.3630573248407643, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549042951979898e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 211908, "start": 2119.08, "end": 2123.12, "text": " You have to remove some of those degrees to force the material to curl inward.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 281, 4159, 512, 295, 729, 5310, 281, 3464, 264, 2527, 281, 22591, 29876, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15942717202102083, "compression_ratio": 1.511111111111111, "no_speech_prob": 1.4322052658416462e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 211908, "start": 2123.7, "end": 2125.5, "text": " The blueprint derives this mathematically.", "tokens": [50596, 440, 35868, 1163, 1539, 341, 44003, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15942717202102083, "compression_ratio": 1.511111111111111, "no_speech_prob": 1.4322052658416462e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 211908, "start": 2126.04, "end": 2130.74, "text": " If you assume the network triangulates the sphere and you run it through Euler's relation again,", "tokens": [50713, 759, 291, 6552, 264, 3209, 19335, 26192, 264, 16687, 293, 291, 1190, 309, 807, 462, 26318, 311, 9721, 797, 11, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15942717202102083, "compression_ratio": 1.511111111111111, "no_speech_prob": 1.4322052658416462e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 211908, "start": 2130.74, "end": 2140.08, "text": " you find that the total combinatorial degree defect from a perfect flat hexagonal grid is always, inevitably, exactly 12.", "tokens": [50948, 291, 915, 300, 264, 3217, 2512, 31927, 831, 4314, 16445, 490, 257, 2176, 4962, 23291, 6709, 304, 10748, 307, 1009, 11, 28171, 11, 2293, 2272, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15942717202102083, "compression_ratio": 1.511111111111111, "no_speech_prob": 1.4322052658416462e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 214008, "start": 2140.08, "end": 2142.22, "text": " The defect is exactly 12.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 16445, 307, 2293, 2272, 13, 50472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12646132707595825, "compression_ratio": 1.7420494699646643, "no_speech_prob": 1.943034708823399e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 214008, "start": 2142.5, "end": 2144.96, "text": " What does that actually look like in physical reality?", "tokens": [50486, 708, 775, 300, 767, 574, 411, 294, 4001, 4103, 30, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12646132707595825, "compression_ratio": 1.7420494699646643, "no_speech_prob": 1.943034708823399e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 214008, "start": 2145.22, "end": 2152.06, "text": " To create a sphere, you must have a total deficit equivalent to 12 vertices that only connect to five shapes instead of six.", "tokens": [50622, 1407, 1884, 257, 16687, 11, 291, 1633, 362, 257, 3217, 22132, 10344, 281, 2272, 32053, 300, 787, 1745, 281, 1732, 10854, 2602, 295, 2309, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12646132707595825, "compression_ratio": 1.7420494699646643, "no_speech_prob": 1.943034708823399e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 214008, "start": 2152.56, "end": 2154.8199999999997, "text": " Think of a traditional black and white soccer ball.", "tokens": [50989, 6557, 295, 257, 5164, 2211, 293, 2418, 15469, 2594, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12646132707595825, "compression_ratio": 1.7420494699646643, "no_speech_prob": 1.943034708823399e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 214008, "start": 2155.02, "end": 2156.36, "text": " What shapes is it made of?", "tokens": [51112, 708, 10854, 307, 309, 1027, 295, 30, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12646132707595825, "compression_ratio": 1.7420494699646643, "no_speech_prob": 1.943034708823399e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 214008, "start": 2156.44, "end": 2157.98, "text": " It looks like mostly white hexagons.", "tokens": [51183, 467, 1542, 411, 5240, 2418, 23291, 559, 892, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12646132707595825, "compression_ratio": 1.7420494699646643, "no_speech_prob": 1.943034708823399e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 214008, "start": 2158.2, "end": 2159.54, "text": " It is mostly hexagons.", "tokens": [51271, 467, 307, 5240, 23291, 559, 892, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12646132707595825, "compression_ratio": 1.7420494699646643, "no_speech_prob": 1.943034708823399e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 214008, "start": 2159.6, "end": 2162.44, "text": " But if you take a soccer ball and physically count the panels,", "tokens": [51341, 583, 498, 291, 747, 257, 15469, 2594, 293, 9762, 1207, 264, 13419, 11, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12646132707595825, "compression_ratio": 1.7420494699646643, "no_speech_prob": 1.943034708823399e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 214008, "start": 2162.7599999999998, "end": 2168.04, "text": " you will find exactly 12 black pentagons interspersed among all those white hexagons.", "tokens": [51499, 291, 486, 915, 2293, 2272, 2211, 16834, 559, 892, 728, 4952, 433, 292, 3654, 439, 729, 2418, 23291, 559, 892, 13, 51763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12646132707595825, "compression_ratio": 1.7420494699646643, "no_speech_prob": 1.943034708823399e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 216804, "start": 2168.04, "end": 2170.12, "text": " Oh, wow. I'd have thought about that.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 286, 1116, 362, 1194, 466, 300, 13, 50469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14324174045531218, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105084288063008e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 216804, "start": 2170.4, "end": 2175.7799999999997, "text": " Without those 12 five-sided pentagons, the leather would lay perfectly flat on the factory floor.", "tokens": [50483, 9129, 729, 2272, 1732, 12, 30941, 16834, 559, 892, 11, 264, 12821, 576, 2360, 6239, 4962, 322, 264, 9265, 4123, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14324174045531218, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105084288063008e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 216804, "start": 2176.18, "end": 2177.7, "text": " It would never curl up into a ball.", "tokens": [50772, 467, 576, 1128, 22591, 493, 666, 257, 2594, 13, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14324174045531218, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105084288063008e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 216804, "start": 2178.3, "end": 2183.42, "text": " The positive curvature of the sphere physically forces exceptional nodes into existence.", "tokens": [50878, 440, 3353, 37638, 295, 264, 16687, 9762, 5874, 19279, 13891, 666, 9123, 13, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14324174045531218, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105084288063008e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 216804, "start": 2183.72, "end": 2184.74, "text": " That is astonishing.", "tokens": [51149, 663, 307, 35264, 13, 51200], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14324174045531218, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105084288063008e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 216804, "start": 2185.2, "end": 2189.04, "text": " The math of a sphere literally demands imperfection to exist.", "tokens": [51223, 440, 5221, 295, 257, 16687, 3736, 15107, 26714, 313, 281, 2514, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14324174045531218, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105084288063008e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 216804, "start": 2189.2599999999998, "end": 2193.62, "text": " Flickshinn calls this principle uniformity without forced uniformity.", "tokens": [51426, 3235, 618, 2716, 7729, 5498, 341, 8665, 9452, 507, 1553, 7579, 9452, 507, 13, 51644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14324174045531218, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105084288063008e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 216804, "start": 2194.06, "end": 2196.2599999999998, "text": " You cannot fight the geometry of the planet.", "tokens": [51666, 509, 2644, 2092, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 5054, 13, 51776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14324174045531218, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105084288063008e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 216804, "start": 2196.2599999999998, "end": 2197.86, "text": " You have to build in harmony with it.", "tokens": [51776, 509, 362, 281, 1322, 294, 19410, 365, 309, 13, 51856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14324174045531218, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105084288063008e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 219804, "start": 2198.04, "end": 2204.5, "text": " Those 12 forced mathematical exceptions, the pentagons, naturally become high centrality hubs.", "tokens": [50365, 3950, 2272, 7579, 18894, 22847, 11, 264, 16834, 559, 892, 11, 8195, 1813, 1090, 32199, 1860, 46870, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682519331210997, "compression_ratio": 1.5253456221198156, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080595835286538e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 219804, "start": 2204.96, "end": 2208.0, "text": " They become geometric singularities in the infrastructure network.", "tokens": [50711, 814, 1813, 33246, 20010, 1088, 294, 264, 6896, 3209, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682519331210997, "compression_ratio": 1.5253456221198156, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080595835286538e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 219804, "start": 2208.5, "end": 2211.92, "text": " The planet itself dictates that not all nodes are created equal.", "tokens": [50888, 440, 5054, 2564, 12569, 1024, 300, 406, 439, 13891, 366, 2942, 2681, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682519331210997, "compression_ratio": 1.5253456221198156, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080595835286538e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 219804, "start": 2212.08, "end": 2214.7799999999997, "text": " Okay, so the planet forces our hand on the shape of the grid.", "tokens": [51067, 1033, 11, 370, 264, 5054, 5874, 527, 1011, 322, 264, 3909, 295, 264, 10748, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682519331210997, "compression_ratio": 1.5253456221198156, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080595835286538e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 219804, "start": 2215.44, "end": 2217.38, "text": " But we do have some control, right?", "tokens": [51235, 583, 321, 360, 362, 512, 1969, 11, 558, 30, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682519331210997, "compression_ratio": 1.5253456221198156, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080595835286538e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 219804, "start": 2217.46, "end": 2217.82, "text": " We do.", "tokens": [51336, 492, 360, 13, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682519331210997, "compression_ratio": 1.5253456221198156, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080595835286538e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 221782, "start": 2217.82, "end": 2224.2400000000002, "text": " We mentioned earlier that out of the nine primary rings, five are locked to the poles and equator, but four are flexible.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 2835, 3071, 300, 484, 295, 264, 4949, 6194, 11136, 11, 1732, 366, 9376, 281, 264, 24760, 293, 45544, 11, 457, 1451, 366, 11358, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10629809136484183, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794588944031962e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 221782, "start": 2224.4, "end": 2225.6200000000003, "text": " We get to choose where to put them.", "tokens": [50694, 492, 483, 281, 2826, 689, 281, 829, 552, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10629809136484183, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794588944031962e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 221782, "start": 2225.7000000000003, "end": 2226.34, "text": " We can tilt them.", "tokens": [50759, 492, 393, 18446, 552, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10629809136484183, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794588944031962e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 221782, "start": 2226.44, "end": 2227.26, "text": " We can rotate them.", "tokens": [50796, 492, 393, 13121, 552, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10629809136484183, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794588944031962e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 221782, "start": 2227.44, "end": 2227.6000000000004, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50846, 1079, 13, 50854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10629809136484183, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794588944031962e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 221782, "start": 2227.78, "end": 2229.34, "text": " So how do we actually make that choice?", "tokens": [50863, 407, 577, 360, 321, 767, 652, 300, 3922, 30, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10629809136484183, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794588944031962e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 221782, "start": 2229.48, "end": 2236.86, "text": " If you have the power to place a continent-spanning mega highway, how do you make that choice fairly for all 8 billion people on Earth?", "tokens": [50948, 759, 291, 362, 264, 1347, 281, 1081, 257, 18932, 12, 4952, 282, 773, 17986, 17205, 11, 577, 360, 291, 652, 300, 3922, 6457, 337, 439, 1649, 5218, 561, 322, 4755, 30, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10629809136484183, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794588944031962e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 223686, "start": 2236.86, "end": 2243.26, "text": " We have to move from arbitrary aesthetic placement into the realm of explicit measurable objectives.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 281, 1286, 490, 23211, 20092, 17257, 666, 264, 15355, 295, 13691, 43615, 15961, 13, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2156954056177384, "compression_ratio": 1.325925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.201343169908442e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 223686, "start": 2243.6800000000003, "end": 2247.6400000000003, "text": " And this is where the blueprint introduces multi-objective optimization.", "tokens": [50706, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 35868, 31472, 4825, 12, 41070, 488, 19618, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2156954056177384, "compression_ratio": 1.325925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.201343169908442e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 223686, "start": 2248.32, "end": 2248.34, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50938, 1033, 13, 50939], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2156954056177384, "compression_ratio": 1.325925925925926, "no_speech_prob": 1.201343169908442e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 224834, "start": 2248.34, "end": 2254.06, "text": " Those four flexible rings give global planners exactly eight continuous dials to play with.", "tokens": [50365, 3950, 1451, 11358, 11136, 976, 4338, 49674, 2293, 3180, 10957, 5502, 82, 281, 862, 365, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12428520773058739, "compression_ratio": 1.6298932384341638, "no_speech_prob": 1.629232556157878e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 224834, "start": 2254.7200000000003, "end": 2259.02, "text": " Mathematically, these are the latitude and azimuth for the pole of each of the four great circles.", "tokens": [50684, 15776, 40197, 11, 613, 366, 264, 45436, 293, 7883, 332, 2910, 337, 264, 13208, 295, 1184, 295, 264, 1451, 869, 13040, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12428520773058739, "compression_ratio": 1.6298932384341638, "no_speech_prob": 1.629232556157878e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 224834, "start": 2259.1600000000003, "end": 2265.1400000000003, "text": " So we have eight massive dials we can spin to tilt and rotate these four huge rings around the globe.", "tokens": [50906, 407, 321, 362, 3180, 5994, 5502, 82, 321, 393, 6060, 281, 18446, 293, 13121, 613, 1451, 2603, 11136, 926, 264, 15371, 13, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12428520773058739, "compression_ratio": 1.6298932384341638, "no_speech_prob": 1.629232556157878e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 224834, "start": 2265.34, "end": 2268.86, "text": " And obviously we want to find the best position for them.", "tokens": [51215, 400, 2745, 321, 528, 281, 915, 264, 1151, 2535, 337, 552, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12428520773058739, "compression_ratio": 1.6298932384341638, "no_speech_prob": 1.629232556157878e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 224834, "start": 2269.1000000000004, "end": 2272.6400000000003, "text": " But best means something completely different depending on who you ask.", "tokens": [51403, 583, 1151, 1355, 746, 2584, 819, 5413, 322, 567, 291, 1029, 13, 51580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12428520773058739, "compression_ratio": 1.6298932384341638, "no_speech_prob": 1.629232556157878e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 224834, "start": 2272.7200000000003, "end": 2273.1400000000003, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51584, 7587, 13, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12428520773058739, "compression_ratio": 1.6298932384341638, "no_speech_prob": 1.629232556157878e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 224834, "start": 2273.4, "end": 2274.7400000000002, "text": " Best is highly subjective.", "tokens": [51618, 9752, 307, 5405, 25972, 13, 51685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12428520773058739, "compression_ratio": 1.6298932384341638, "no_speech_prob": 1.629232556157878e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 227474, "start": 2274.74, "end": 2279.72, "text": " If you look at the optimization functional provided in the text, it isn't just one mathematical goal.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 574, 412, 264, 19618, 11745, 5649, 294, 264, 2487, 11, 309, 1943, 380, 445, 472, 18894, 3387, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12028863000088051, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 1.598310459677288e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 227474, "start": 2280.2, "end": 2282.74, "text": " It is a complex vector of competing costs.", "tokens": [50638, 467, 307, 257, 3997, 8062, 295, 15439, 5497, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12028863000088051, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 1.598310459677288e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 227474, "start": 2282.9799999999996, "end": 2283.22, "text": " Likewise.", "tokens": [50777, 30269, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12028863000088051, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 1.598310459677288e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 227474, "start": 2283.4199999999996, "end": 2291.18, "text": " You have to balance population density, tectonic fault lines, ecological reserves, freshwater hydrology, and orbital launch trajectories.", "tokens": [50799, 509, 362, 281, 4772, 4415, 10305, 11, 535, 349, 11630, 7441, 3876, 11, 31054, 27483, 11, 50234, 15435, 4987, 88, 11, 293, 27677, 4025, 18257, 2083, 13, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12028863000088051, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 1.598310459677288e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 227474, "start": 2291.4799999999996, "end": 2297.12, "text": " So if I'm a planner and I decide to heavily weight equatorial space launches because we are building a massive space elevator,", "tokens": [51202, 407, 498, 286, 478, 257, 31268, 293, 286, 4536, 281, 10950, 3364, 45544, 831, 1901, 31841, 570, 321, 366, 2390, 257, 5994, 1901, 18782, 11, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12028863000088051, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 1.598310459677288e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 227474, "start": 2297.7, "end": 2302.16, "text": " I might tilt the rings in a way that totally ruins high-latitude water distribution for northern countries.", "tokens": [51513, 286, 1062, 18446, 264, 11136, 294, 257, 636, 300, 3879, 24747, 1090, 12, 14087, 4377, 1281, 7316, 337, 14197, 3517, 13, 51736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12028863000088051, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 1.598310459677288e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 227474, "start": 2302.56, "end": 2303.04, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51756, 7587, 13, 51780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12028863000088051, "compression_ratio": 1.6144578313253013, "no_speech_prob": 1.598310459677288e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 230304, "start": 2303.04, "end": 2305.72, "text": " You are always trading one benefit for another cost.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 366, 1009, 9529, 472, 5121, 337, 1071, 2063, 13, 50499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15923132590197642, "compression_ratio": 1.5755395683453237, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236379645276355e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 230304, "start": 2305.86, "end": 2307.22, "text": " Let's do a thought experiment with this.", "tokens": [50506, 961, 311, 360, 257, 1194, 5120, 365, 341, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15923132590197642, "compression_ratio": 1.5755395683453237, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236379645276355e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 230304, "start": 2307.32, "end": 2307.98, "text": " Okay, let's hear it.", "tokens": [50579, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1568, 309, 13, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15923132590197642, "compression_ratio": 1.5755395683453237, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236379645276355e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 230304, "start": 2308.56, "end": 2313.34, "text": " If you are listening right now, imagine you have your hand on one of these eight dials.", "tokens": [50641, 759, 291, 366, 4764, 558, 586, 11, 3811, 291, 362, 428, 1011, 322, 472, 295, 613, 3180, 5502, 82, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15923132590197642, "compression_ratio": 1.5755395683453237, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236379645276355e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 230304, "start": 2313.9, "end": 2316.62, "text": " You have the power to place this massive corridor.", "tokens": [50908, 509, 362, 264, 1347, 281, 1081, 341, 5994, 25602, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15923132590197642, "compression_ratio": 1.5755395683453237, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236379645276355e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 230304, "start": 2317.7599999999998, "end": 2327.6, "text": " Do you tilt it so it runs directly through New York City, prioritizing the dense population center so millions of people have instant access to water and power?", "tokens": [51101, 1144, 291, 18446, 309, 370, 309, 6676, 3838, 807, 1873, 3609, 4392, 11, 14846, 3319, 264, 18011, 4415, 3056, 370, 6803, 295, 561, 362, 9836, 2105, 281, 1281, 293, 1347, 30, 51593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15923132590197642, "compression_ratio": 1.5755395683453237, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236379645276355e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 230304, "start": 2328.06, "end": 2329.18, "text": " Seems like a good idea.", "tokens": [51616, 22524, 411, 257, 665, 1558, 13, 51672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15923132590197642, "compression_ratio": 1.5755395683453237, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236379645276355e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 232918, "start": 2329.18, "end": 2343.18, "text": " That sounds great, but wait, tilting it toward New York forces the other side of that great circle to slice directly through the mid-Atlantic ridge a massive tectonic fault line under the ocean that could snap your corridor in half during an earthquake.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 3263, 869, 11, 457, 1699, 11, 8440, 783, 309, 7361, 1873, 3609, 5874, 264, 661, 1252, 295, 300, 869, 6329, 281, 13153, 3838, 807, 264, 2062, 12, 18684, 75, 7128, 34651, 257, 5994, 535, 349, 11630, 7441, 1622, 833, 264, 7810, 300, 727, 13650, 428, 25602, 294, 1922, 1830, 364, 18778, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11654753763167584, "compression_ratio": 1.4364640883977902, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947675901546333e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 232918, "start": 2343.4199999999996, "end": 2343.6, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51077, 1779, 13, 51086], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11654753763167584, "compression_ratio": 1.4364640883977902, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947675901546333e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 234360, "start": 2343.6, "end": 2348.72, "text": " So do you prioritize the people or do you prioritize the structural safety?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 360, 291, 25164, 264, 561, 420, 360, 291, 25164, 264, 15067, 4514, 30, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15107206197885367, "compression_ratio": 1.244186046511628, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794610628075412e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 234360, "start": 2348.86, "end": 2350.22, "text": " You cannot have both perfectly.", "tokens": [50628, 509, 2644, 362, 1293, 6239, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15107206197885367, "compression_ratio": 1.244186046511628, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794610628075412e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 235022, "start": 2350.22, "end": 2357.0, "text": " This inherent conflict is why the blueprint introduces a crucial ethical and design principle called Pareto transparency.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 26387, 6596, 307, 983, 264, 35868, 31472, 257, 11462, 18890, 293, 1715, 8665, 1219, 31189, 1353, 17131, 13, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08948862786386527, "compression_ratio": 1.467741935483871, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039918959015464e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 235022, "start": 2357.9599999999996, "end": 2366.7799999999997, "text": " The text explicitly states that no single configuration should ever be presented to the public as uniquely dictated by pure geometry or objective math.", "tokens": [50752, 440, 2487, 20803, 4368, 300, 572, 2167, 11694, 820, 1562, 312, 8212, 281, 264, 1908, 382, 31474, 12569, 770, 538, 6075, 18426, 420, 10024, 5221, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08948862786386527, "compression_ratio": 1.467741935483871, "no_speech_prob": 1.6039918959015464e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 236678, "start": 2366.78, "end": 2367.7200000000003, "text": " Because that's a lie.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 300, 311, 257, 4544, 13, 50412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505756974220276, "compression_ratio": 1.5565610859728507, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758188582822632e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 236678, "start": 2368.02, "end": 2368.6400000000003, "text": " It is a lie.", "tokens": [50427, 467, 307, 257, 4544, 13, 50458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505756974220276, "compression_ratio": 1.5565610859728507, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758188582822632e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 236678, "start": 2369.4, "end": 2373.78, "text": " The final location depends entirely on human, political, and ethical weightings.", "tokens": [50496, 440, 2572, 4914, 5946, 7696, 322, 1952, 11, 3905, 11, 293, 18890, 3364, 1109, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505756974220276, "compression_ratio": 1.5565610859728507, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758188582822632e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 236678, "start": 2374.7200000000003, "end": 2387.2200000000003, "text": " A configuration is considered Pareto optimal when you reach a point where you cannot improve one metric, like getting closer to New York, without mathematically worsening another, like getting closer to an earthquake zone.", "tokens": [50762, 316, 11694, 307, 4888, 31189, 1353, 16252, 562, 291, 2524, 257, 935, 689, 291, 2644, 3470, 472, 20678, 11, 411, 1242, 4966, 281, 1873, 3609, 11, 1553, 44003, 47567, 4559, 1071, 11, 411, 1242, 4966, 281, 364, 18778, 6668, 13, 51387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505756974220276, "compression_ratio": 1.5565610859728507, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758188582822632e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 236678, "start": 2387.3, "end": 2387.6000000000004, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51391, 1033, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505756974220276, "compression_ratio": 1.5565610859728507, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758188582822632e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 238760, "start": 2387.6, "end": 2392.38, "text": " The blueprint demands that planners publicly preserve this Pareto frontier.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 35868, 15107, 300, 49674, 14843, 15665, 341, 31189, 1353, 35853, 13, 50604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19710064697265625, "compression_ratio": 1.6253776435045317, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674123240647098e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 238760, "start": 2392.94, "end": 2397.2799999999997, "text": " They must explicitly disclose the ethical weights they use to pick a specific layout.", "tokens": [50632, 814, 1633, 20803, 36146, 264, 18890, 17443, 436, 764, 281, 1888, 257, 2685, 13333, 13, 50849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19710064697265625, "compression_ratio": 1.6253776435045317, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674123240647098e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 238760, "start": 2397.7, "end": 2398.52, "text": " I really appreciate that.", "tokens": [50870, 286, 534, 4449, 300, 13, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19710064697265625, "compression_ratio": 1.6253776435045317, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674123240647098e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 238760, "start": 2398.72, "end": 2401.36, "text": " It's essentially saying show your work and show your bias.", "tokens": [50921, 467, 311, 4476, 1566, 855, 428, 589, 293, 855, 428, 12577, 13, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19710064697265625, "compression_ratio": 1.6253776435045317, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674123240647098e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 238760, "start": 2401.52, "end": 2401.62, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51061, 865, 13, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19710064697265625, "compression_ratio": 1.6253776435045317, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674123240647098e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 238760, "start": 2401.9, "end": 2405.44, "text": " Don't hide behind a supercomputer and say the algorithm made me do it.", "tokens": [51080, 1468, 380, 6479, 2261, 257, 36708, 293, 584, 264, 9284, 1027, 385, 360, 309, 13, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19710064697265625, "compression_ratio": 1.6253776435045317, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674123240647098e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 238760, "start": 2405.5, "end": 2406.12, "text": " It's just math.", "tokens": [51260, 467, 311, 445, 5221, 13, 51291], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19710064697265625, "compression_ratio": 1.6253776435045317, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674123240647098e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 238760, "start": 2406.2599999999998, "end": 2406.44, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51298, 865, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19710064697265625, "compression_ratio": 1.6253776435045317, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674123240647098e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 238760, "start": 2406.56, "end": 2409.7999999999997, "text": " Admit that you decided the coastal population was worth the earthquake risk.", "tokens": [51313, 1999, 3508, 300, 291, 3047, 264, 25050, 4415, 390, 3163, 264, 18778, 3148, 13, 51475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19710064697265625, "compression_ratio": 1.6253776435045317, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674123240647098e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 238760, "start": 2409.92, "end": 2412.2799999999997, "text": " It enforces honesty in planetary engineering.", "tokens": [51481, 467, 25495, 887, 26839, 294, 35788, 7043, 13, 51599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19710064697265625, "compression_ratio": 1.6253776435045317, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674123240647098e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 238760, "start": 2412.64, "end": 2416.92, "text": " But this raises an incredibly important, almost existential question.", "tokens": [51617, 583, 341, 19658, 364, 6252, 1021, 11, 1920, 37133, 1168, 13, 51831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19710064697265625, "compression_ratio": 1.6253776435045317, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674123240647098e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 241692, "start": 2416.92, "end": 2417.5, "text": " Which is?", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 307, 30, 50394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12918494902935224, "compression_ratio": 1.5670498084291187, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674074451549336e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 241692, "start": 2417.9, "end": 2423.02, "text": " How do you accurately weight an optimization for population when the network is supposed to endure for centuries?", "tokens": [50414, 1012, 360, 291, 20095, 3364, 364, 19618, 337, 4415, 562, 264, 3209, 307, 3442, 281, 24732, 337, 13926, 30, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12918494902935224, "compression_ratio": 1.5670498084291187, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674074451549336e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 241692, "start": 2423.6, "end": 2424.06, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [50699, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12918494902935224, "compression_ratio": 1.5670498084291187, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674074451549336e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 241692, "start": 2424.28, "end": 2437.92, "text": " Yeah, because if sea levels rise by a meter or if climate change radically shifts the arable agricultural zones over the next 300 years, the massive population centers of 2026 are absolutely not going to be the population centers of 2326.", "tokens": [50733, 865, 11, 570, 498, 4158, 4358, 6272, 538, 257, 9255, 420, 498, 5659, 1319, 35508, 19201, 264, 15186, 638, 19587, 16025, 670, 264, 958, 6641, 924, 11, 264, 5994, 4415, 10898, 295, 945, 10880, 366, 3122, 406, 516, 281, 312, 264, 4415, 10898, 295, 6673, 10880, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12918494902935224, "compression_ratio": 1.5670498084291187, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674074451549336e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 241692, "start": 2438.76, "end": 2439.14, "text": " Men at all.", "tokens": [51457, 6685, 412, 439, 13, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12918494902935224, "compression_ratio": 1.5670498084291187, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674074451549336e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 241692, "start": 2439.1800000000003, "end": 2439.88, "text": " People are going to move.", "tokens": [51478, 3432, 366, 516, 281, 1286, 13, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12918494902935224, "compression_ratio": 1.5670498084291187, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674074451549336e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 243988, "start": 2439.88, "end": 2451.58, "text": " So if we optimize this permanent 1,000-year skeleton based strictly on a map of where people live today, that optimization is going to fail catastrophically in a few generations.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 321, 19719, 341, 10996, 502, 11, 1360, 12, 5294, 25204, 2361, 20792, 322, 257, 4471, 295, 689, 561, 1621, 965, 11, 300, 19618, 307, 516, 281, 3061, 28363, 984, 294, 257, 1326, 10593, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15125248530139662, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 2.5042444246753393e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 243988, "start": 2452.1400000000003, "end": 2454.9, "text": " You've hit on the exact flaw of short-term optimization.", "tokens": [50978, 509, 600, 2045, 322, 264, 1900, 13717, 295, 2099, 12, 7039, 19618, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15125248530139662, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 2.5042444246753393e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 243988, "start": 2455.52, "end": 2459.98, "text": " If you optimize perfectly for the present, you create fragility for the future.", "tokens": [51147, 759, 291, 19719, 6239, 337, 264, 1974, 11, 291, 1884, 9241, 1140, 337, 264, 2027, 13, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15125248530139662, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 2.5042444246753393e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 245998, "start": 2459.98, "end": 2467.62, "text": " And this is where the text moves away from simple nominal optimization and introduces robust stochastic optimization.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 2487, 6067, 1314, 490, 2199, 41641, 19618, 293, 31472, 13956, 342, 8997, 2750, 19618, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1622150892852455, "compression_ratio": 1.6141078838174274, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359662105905337e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 245998, "start": 2468.04, "end": 2470.46, "text": " Stochastic meaning involving probability and randomness.", "tokens": [50768, 745, 8997, 2750, 3620, 17030, 8482, 293, 4974, 1287, 13, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1622150892852455, "compression_ratio": 1.6141078838174274, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359662105905337e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 245998, "start": 2470.54, "end": 2470.76, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50893, 1079, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1622150892852455, "compression_ratio": 1.6141078838174274, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359662105905337e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 245998, "start": 2471.32, "end": 2475.52, "text": " Fliction introduces a concept here that I absolutely love, and it applies far beyond engineering.", "tokens": [50932, 3235, 4105, 31472, 257, 3410, 510, 300, 286, 3122, 959, 11, 293, 309, 13165, 1400, 4399, 7043, 13, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1622150892852455, "compression_ratio": 1.6141078838174274, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359662105905337e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 245998, "start": 2475.78, "end": 2478.4, "text": " It's called long-horizon minimax regret.", "tokens": [51155, 467, 311, 1219, 938, 12, 2335, 24057, 4464, 2797, 10879, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1622150892852455, "compression_ratio": 1.6141078838174274, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359662105905337e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 245998, "start": 2478.72, "end": 2479.64, "text": " Minimax regret.", "tokens": [51302, 2829, 332, 2797, 10879, 13, 51348], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1622150892852455, "compression_ratio": 1.6141078838174274, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359662105905337e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 245998, "start": 2479.88, "end": 2482.34, "text": " Minimizing the maximum regret you could possibly have.", "tokens": [51360, 2829, 332, 3319, 264, 6674, 10879, 291, 727, 6264, 362, 13, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1622150892852455, "compression_ratio": 1.6141078838174274, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359662105905337e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 248234, "start": 2482.34, "end": 2482.7000000000003, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15197533574597588, "compression_ratio": 1.641350210970464, "no_speech_prob": 2.371652570512528e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 248234, "start": 2483.04, "end": 2489.86, "text": " Instead of trying to guess exactly what the world will look like in 300 years and optimizing perfectly for that single guess, the math shifts.", "tokens": [50400, 7156, 295, 1382, 281, 2041, 2293, 437, 264, 1002, 486, 574, 411, 294, 6641, 924, 293, 40425, 6239, 337, 300, 2167, 2041, 11, 264, 5221, 19201, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15197533574597588, "compression_ratio": 1.641350210970464, "no_speech_prob": 2.371652570512528e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 248234, "start": 2489.86, "end": 2496.86, "text": " You optimize to minimize the worst-case cost across a massive set of highly uncertain futures.", "tokens": [50741, 509, 19719, 281, 17522, 264, 5855, 12, 9765, 2063, 2108, 257, 5994, 992, 295, 5405, 11308, 26071, 13, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15197533574597588, "compression_ratio": 1.641350210970464, "no_speech_prob": 2.371652570512528e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 248234, "start": 2497.4, "end": 2502.1800000000003, "text": " It is an infrastructure philosophy based on profound humility regarding the future.", "tokens": [51118, 467, 307, 364, 6896, 10675, 2361, 322, 14382, 27106, 8595, 264, 2027, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15197533574597588, "compression_ratio": 1.641350210970464, "no_speech_prob": 2.371652570512528e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 248234, "start": 2502.6400000000003, "end": 2504.42, "text": " Humility regarding the future.", "tokens": [51380, 12877, 1140, 8595, 264, 2027, 13, 51469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15197533574597588, "compression_ratio": 1.641350210970464, "no_speech_prob": 2.371652570512528e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 248234, "start": 2504.52, "end": 2506.2200000000003, "text": " That is such a powerful phrase.", "tokens": [51474, 663, 307, 1270, 257, 4005, 9535, 13, 51559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15197533574597588, "compression_ratio": 1.641350210970464, "no_speech_prob": 2.371652570512528e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 250622, "start": 2506.22, "end": 2517.1, "text": " The design principle states that we should actively avoid decisions whose apparent present advantage relies heavily on narrow assumptions about future climates, technologies, or political organizations.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1715, 8665, 4368, 300, 321, 820, 13022, 5042, 5327, 6104, 18335, 1974, 5002, 30910, 10950, 322, 9432, 17695, 466, 2027, 5644, 1024, 11, 7943, 11, 420, 3905, 6150, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08074885433159985, "compression_ratio": 1.593939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 1.519171073660619e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 250622, "start": 2517.4399999999996, "end": 2518.5, "text": " Because we just don't know.", "tokens": [50926, 1436, 321, 445, 500, 380, 458, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08074885433159985, "compression_ratio": 1.593939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 1.519171073660619e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 250622, "start": 2518.64, "end": 2518.8599999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50986, 1779, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08074885433159985, "compression_ratio": 1.593939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 1.519171073660619e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 250622, "start": 2519.02, "end": 2529.2, "text": " We should prefer a configuration that minimizes irreversible regret across a wide range of possible futures, rather than chasing a razor's edge maximum efficiency for today.", "tokens": [51005, 492, 820, 4382, 257, 11694, 300, 4464, 5660, 16014, 840, 964, 10879, 2108, 257, 4874, 3613, 295, 1944, 26071, 11, 2831, 813, 17876, 257, 30478, 311, 4691, 6674, 10493, 337, 965, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08074885433159985, "compression_ratio": 1.593939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 1.519171073660619e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 250622, "start": 2529.8199999999997, "end": 2535.66, "text": " It is the mathematical equivalent of buying insurance instead of gambling your life savings on a single stock tip.", "tokens": [51545, 467, 307, 264, 18894, 10344, 295, 6382, 7214, 2602, 295, 27077, 428, 993, 13454, 322, 257, 2167, 4127, 4125, 13, 51837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08074885433159985, "compression_ratio": 1.593939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 1.519171073660619e-12}, {"id": 809, "seek": 253566, "start": 2535.66, "end": 2536.2999999999997, "text": " I love that.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 959, 300, 13, 50397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13854025460623362, "compression_ratio": 1.639240506329114, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420309102848645e-12}, {"id": 810, "seek": 253566, "start": 2536.8399999999997, "end": 2539.3399999999997, "text": " We are reserving these giant spatial tubes.", "tokens": [50424, 492, 366, 725, 20186, 613, 7410, 23598, 21458, 13, 50549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13854025460623362, "compression_ratio": 1.639240506329114, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420309102848645e-12}, {"id": 811, "seek": 253566, "start": 2539.5, "end": 2542.58, "text": " We are placing them carefully to avoid massive regret for our great-grandchildren.", "tokens": [50557, 492, 366, 17221, 552, 7500, 281, 5042, 5994, 10879, 337, 527, 869, 12, 32902, 21172, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13854025460623362, "compression_ratio": 1.639240506329114, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420309102848645e-12}, {"id": 812, "seek": 253566, "start": 2543.18, "end": 2544.96, "text": " But what actually happens inside the tube?", "tokens": [50741, 583, 437, 767, 2314, 1854, 264, 9917, 30, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13854025460623362, "compression_ratio": 1.639240506329114, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420309102848645e-12}, {"id": 813, "seek": 253566, "start": 2545.06, "end": 2545.72, "text": " Inside it.", "tokens": [50835, 15123, 309, 13, 50868], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13854025460623362, "compression_ratio": 1.639240506329114, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420309102848645e-12}, {"id": 814, "seek": 253566, "start": 2545.7599999999998, "end": 2546.6, "text": " We've drawn the map.", "tokens": [50870, 492, 600, 10117, 264, 4471, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13854025460623362, "compression_ratio": 1.639240506329114, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420309102848645e-12}, {"id": 815, "seek": 253566, "start": 2546.68, "end": 2548.0, "text": " We've optimized the global grid.", "tokens": [50916, 492, 600, 26941, 264, 4338, 10748, 13, 50982], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13854025460623362, "compression_ratio": 1.639240506329114, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420309102848645e-12}, {"id": 816, "seek": 253566, "start": 2548.1, "end": 2550.02, "text": " But now, let's zoom all the way down.", "tokens": [50987, 583, 586, 11, 718, 311, 8863, 439, 264, 636, 760, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13854025460623362, "compression_ratio": 1.639240506329114, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420309102848645e-12}, {"id": 817, "seek": 253566, "start": 2550.2799999999997, "end": 2551.48, "text": " Let's get our boots in the dirt.", "tokens": [51096, 961, 311, 483, 527, 15194, 294, 264, 11483, 13, 51156], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13854025460623362, "compression_ratio": 1.639240506329114, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420309102848645e-12}, {"id": 818, "seek": 253566, "start": 2551.58, "end": 2557.2, "text": " Let's look at a single one-mile patch of this physical 3D corridor itself.", "tokens": [51161, 961, 311, 574, 412, 257, 2167, 472, 12, 44927, 9972, 295, 341, 4001, 805, 35, 25602, 2564, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13854025460623362, "compression_ratio": 1.639240506329114, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420309102848645e-12}, {"id": 819, "seek": 253566, "start": 2557.46, "end": 2560.24, "text": " This brings us to the operational reality of the system.", "tokens": [51455, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 16607, 4103, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 51594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13854025460623362, "compression_ratio": 1.639240506329114, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420309102848645e-12}, {"id": 820, "seek": 253566, "start": 2561.0, "end": 2564.62, "text": " The text introduces the concept of the operational microcell.", "tokens": [51632, 440, 2487, 31472, 264, 3410, 295, 264, 16607, 4532, 4164, 13, 51813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13854025460623362, "compression_ratio": 1.639240506329114, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420309102848645e-12}, {"id": 821, "seek": 253566, "start": 2564.8399999999997, "end": 2565.08, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51824, 1033, 13, 51836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13854025460623362, "compression_ratio": 1.639240506329114, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420309102848645e-12}, {"id": 822, "seek": 256508, "start": 2565.08, "end": 2579.14, "text": " This is the highly specific geographical zone where the orthodromic cell, the global geometric highway skeleton, physically overlaps with the Voronoi cell, the nearest node local service territory.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 264, 5405, 2685, 39872, 6668, 689, 264, 19052, 378, 4397, 299, 2815, 11, 264, 4338, 33246, 17205, 25204, 11, 9762, 15986, 2382, 365, 264, 12231, 266, 4869, 2815, 11, 264, 23831, 9984, 2654, 2643, 11360, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10171434527537862, "compression_ratio": 1.5359116022099448, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612943237928388e-12}, {"id": 823, "seek": 256508, "start": 2579.38, "end": 2583.3199999999997, "text": " So this is where the massive global ambition meets local city planning.", "tokens": [51080, 407, 341, 307, 689, 264, 5994, 4338, 22814, 13961, 2654, 2307, 5038, 13, 51277], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10171434527537862, "compression_ratio": 1.5359116022099448, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612943237928388e-12}, {"id": 824, "seek": 256508, "start": 2583.54, "end": 2583.98, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51288, 7587, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10171434527537862, "compression_ratio": 1.5359116022099448, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612943237928388e-12}, {"id": 825, "seek": 258398, "start": 2583.98, "end": 2594.46, "text": " It tells a regional engineer exactly what mathematical boundary structures their specific region, and exactly which primary node they are responsible for interfacing with.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 5112, 257, 10964, 11403, 2293, 437, 18894, 12866, 9227, 641, 2685, 4458, 11, 293, 2293, 597, 6194, 9984, 436, 366, 6250, 337, 14510, 5615, 365, 13, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08819586297740108, "compression_ratio": 1.6167883211678833, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045720524840434e-12}, {"id": 826, "seek": 258398, "start": 2594.8, "end": 2600.96, "text": " And as we zoom in on the corridor curve itself, the text introduces a vital tool called the orthonormal moving frame.", "tokens": [50906, 400, 382, 321, 8863, 294, 322, 264, 25602, 7605, 2564, 11, 264, 2487, 31472, 257, 11707, 2290, 1219, 264, 420, 11943, 24440, 2684, 3920, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08819586297740108, "compression_ratio": 1.6167883211678833, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045720524840434e-12}, {"id": 827, "seek": 258398, "start": 2601.28, "end": 2608.52, "text": " Because we aren't just drawing a flat line on a piece of paper, we are literally wrapping a three-dimensional tube around the curved surface of a sphere.", "tokens": [51230, 1436, 321, 3212, 380, 445, 6316, 257, 4962, 1622, 322, 257, 2522, 295, 3035, 11, 321, 366, 3736, 21993, 257, 1045, 12, 18759, 9917, 926, 264, 24991, 3753, 295, 257, 16687, 13, 51592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08819586297740108, "compression_ratio": 1.6167883211678833, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045720524840434e-12}, {"id": 828, "seek": 260852, "start": 2608.52, "end": 2608.92, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16785802841186523, "compression_ratio": 1.586080586080586, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881543905833407e-12}, {"id": 829, "seek": 260852, "start": 2609.34, "end": 2615.02, "text": " To manage this mathematically, the framework uses three distinct vectors at every single point along the path.", "tokens": [50406, 1407, 3067, 341, 44003, 11, 264, 8388, 4960, 1045, 10644, 18875, 412, 633, 2167, 935, 2051, 264, 3100, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16785802841186523, "compression_ratio": 1.586080586080586, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881543905833407e-12}, {"id": 830, "seek": 260852, "start": 2615.42, "end": 2617.18, "text": " Tangent, normal, and binormal.", "tokens": [50710, 22063, 317, 11, 2710, 11, 293, 5171, 24440, 13, 50798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16785802841186523, "compression_ratio": 1.586080586080586, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881543905833407e-12}, {"id": 831, "seek": 260852, "start": 2617.66, "end": 2619.3, "text": " Often called the TNB frame.", "tokens": [50822, 20043, 1219, 264, 314, 45, 33, 3920, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16785802841186523, "compression_ratio": 1.586080586080586, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881543905833407e-12}, {"id": 832, "seek": 260852, "start": 2619.38, "end": 2619.52, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50908, 1033, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16785802841186523, "compression_ratio": 1.586080586080586, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881543905833407e-12}, {"id": 833, "seek": 260852, "start": 2619.6, "end": 2620.42, "text": " Help me visualize this.", "tokens": [50919, 10773, 385, 23273, 341, 13, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16785802841186523, "compression_ratio": 1.586080586080586, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881543905833407e-12}, {"id": 834, "seek": 260852, "start": 2620.48, "end": 2623.58, "text": " Let's imagine I'm sitting in a roller coaster car on a track that wraps around the Earth.", "tokens": [50963, 961, 311, 3811, 286, 478, 3798, 294, 257, 15948, 28442, 1032, 322, 257, 2837, 300, 25831, 926, 264, 4755, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16785802841186523, "compression_ratio": 1.586080586080586, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881543905833407e-12}, {"id": 835, "seek": 260852, "start": 2623.8, "end": 2624.1, "text": " Perfect.", "tokens": [51129, 10246, 13, 51144], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16785802841186523, "compression_ratio": 1.586080586080586, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881543905833407e-12}, {"id": 836, "seek": 260852, "start": 2624.62, "end": 2628.98, "text": " The tangent vector points straight ahead, exactly along the path of the tracks.", "tokens": [51170, 440, 27747, 8062, 2793, 2997, 2286, 11, 2293, 2051, 264, 3100, 295, 264, 10218, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16785802841186523, "compression_ratio": 1.586080586080586, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881543905833407e-12}, {"id": 837, "seek": 260852, "start": 2629.16, "end": 2630.62, "text": " It is the direction of travel.", "tokens": [51397, 467, 307, 264, 3513, 295, 3147, 13, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16785802841186523, "compression_ratio": 1.586080586080586, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881543905833407e-12}, {"id": 838, "seek": 260852, "start": 2630.74, "end": 2631.02, "text": " Forward.", "tokens": [51476, 35524, 13, 51490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16785802841186523, "compression_ratio": 1.586080586080586, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881543905833407e-12}, {"id": 839, "seek": 260852, "start": 2631.16, "end": 2631.44, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [51497, 5803, 309, 13, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16785802841186523, "compression_ratio": 1.586080586080586, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881543905833407e-12}, {"id": 840, "seek": 263144, "start": 2631.44, "end": 2637.52, "text": " The normal vector points straight out from the exact center of the Earth, right through your seat, and up through your head.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2710, 8062, 2793, 2997, 484, 490, 264, 1900, 3056, 295, 264, 4755, 11, 558, 807, 428, 6121, 11, 293, 493, 807, 428, 1378, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13857988967108972, "compression_ratio": 1.711297071129707, "no_speech_prob": 2.494852631776401e-12}, {"id": 841, "seek": 263144, "start": 2637.7400000000002, "end": 2641.82, "text": " It defines absolute up relative to gravity at that specific spot.", "tokens": [50680, 467, 23122, 8236, 493, 4972, 281, 12110, 412, 300, 2685, 4008, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13857988967108972, "compression_ratio": 1.711297071129707, "no_speech_prob": 2.494852631776401e-12}, {"id": 842, "seek": 263144, "start": 2641.9, "end": 2642.14, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50888, 1033, 13, 50900], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13857988967108972, "compression_ratio": 1.711297071129707, "no_speech_prob": 2.494852631776401e-12}, {"id": 843, "seek": 263144, "start": 2642.3, "end": 2642.94, "text": " Forward and up.", "tokens": [50908, 35524, 293, 493, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13857988967108972, "compression_ratio": 1.711297071129707, "no_speech_prob": 2.494852631776401e-12}, {"id": 844, "seek": 263144, "start": 2643.2000000000003, "end": 2648.16, "text": " And the binormal vector points dead sideways, exactly perpendicular to both forward and up.", "tokens": [50953, 400, 264, 5171, 24440, 8062, 2793, 3116, 26092, 11, 2293, 26734, 281, 1293, 2128, 293, 493, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13857988967108972, "compression_ratio": 1.711297071129707, "no_speech_prob": 2.494852631776401e-12}, {"id": 845, "seek": 263144, "start": 2648.3, "end": 2652.92, "text": " It defines the physical width of the corridor spreading out to your left and right on the surface.", "tokens": [51208, 467, 23122, 264, 4001, 11402, 295, 264, 25602, 15232, 484, 281, 428, 1411, 293, 558, 322, 264, 3753, 13, 51439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13857988967108972, "compression_ratio": 1.711297071129707, "no_speech_prob": 2.494852631776401e-12}, {"id": 846, "seek": 263144, "start": 2653.18, "end": 2653.4, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51452, 1033, 13, 51463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13857988967108972, "compression_ratio": 1.711297071129707, "no_speech_prob": 2.494852631776401e-12}, {"id": 847, "seek": 265340, "start": 2653.4, "end": 2665.4, "text": " The blueprint proves that this frame remains perfectly orthonormal, meaning all three arrows stay exactly 90 degrees to each other at every single point along the entire global network.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 35868, 25019, 300, 341, 3920, 7023, 6239, 420, 11943, 24440, 11, 3620, 439, 1045, 19669, 1754, 2293, 4289, 5310, 281, 1184, 661, 412, 633, 2167, 935, 2051, 264, 2302, 4338, 3209, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11420038148954317, "compression_ratio": 1.5182186234817814, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487989359242894e-12}, {"id": 848, "seek": 265340, "start": 2665.6, "end": 2670.0, "text": " So we have this perfectly defined 3D volume stretching across continents.", "tokens": [50975, 407, 321, 362, 341, 6239, 7642, 805, 35, 5523, 19632, 2108, 38598, 13, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11420038148954317, "compression_ratio": 1.5182186234817814, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487989359242894e-12}, {"id": 849, "seek": 265340, "start": 2670.1600000000003, "end": 2676.46, "text": " And earlier we talked about intergenerational compatibility, putting advanced future tech into this old space.", "tokens": [51203, 400, 3071, 321, 2825, 466, 728, 21848, 1478, 34237, 11, 3372, 7339, 2027, 7553, 666, 341, 1331, 1901, 13, 51518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11420038148954317, "compression_ratio": 1.5182186234817814, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487989359242894e-12}, {"id": 850, "seek": 265340, "start": 2676.7200000000003, "end": 2676.9, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51531, 1079, 13, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11420038148954317, "compression_ratio": 1.5182186234817814, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487989359242894e-12}, {"id": 851, "seek": 267690, "start": 2676.9, "end": 2682.7200000000003, "text": " But what about putting multiple different types of technology into the exact same space at the exact same time?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 437, 466, 3372, 3866, 819, 3467, 295, 2899, 666, 264, 1900, 912, 1901, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 565, 30, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.126160888671875, "compression_ratio": 1.6064981949458483, "no_speech_prob": 1.769175301050141e-12}, {"id": 852, "seek": 267690, "start": 2683.2000000000003, "end": 2690.96, "text": " We were talking about running water pipes, high voltage power lines, massive data trunks, and potentially hyperloop transit all through the same corridor.", "tokens": [50680, 492, 645, 1417, 466, 2614, 1281, 21882, 11, 1090, 8352, 1347, 3876, 11, 5994, 1412, 504, 17627, 11, 293, 7263, 9848, 46623, 17976, 439, 807, 264, 912, 25602, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.126160888671875, "compression_ratio": 1.6064981949458483, "no_speech_prob": 1.769175301050141e-12}, {"id": 853, "seek": 267690, "start": 2691.1600000000003, "end": 2697.32, "text": " Which introduces one of the most critical, non-negotiable safety protocols in the entire blueprint.", "tokens": [51078, 3013, 31472, 472, 295, 264, 881, 4924, 11, 2107, 12, 28561, 8206, 712, 4514, 20618, 294, 264, 2302, 35868, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.126160888671875, "compression_ratio": 1.6064981949458483, "no_speech_prob": 1.769175301050141e-12}, {"id": 854, "seek": 267690, "start": 2697.84, "end": 2700.78, "text": " The text calls this spatial co-location.", "tokens": [51412, 440, 2487, 5498, 341, 23598, 598, 12, 5842, 399, 13, 51559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.126160888671875, "compression_ratio": 1.6064981949458483, "no_speech_prob": 1.769175301050141e-12}, {"id": 855, "seek": 267690, "start": 2700.82, "end": 2701.98, "text": " Co-location meaning they're together.", "tokens": [51561, 3066, 12, 5842, 399, 3620, 436, 434, 1214, 13, 51619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.126160888671875, "compression_ratio": 1.6064981949458483, "no_speech_prob": 1.769175301050141e-12}, {"id": 856, "seek": 270198, "start": 2701.98, "end": 2722.28, "text": " But when it couples it with a terrifying warning, just because water, electricity, transportation, and data are sharing the exact same spatial tube to save on costs and minimize ecological impact, they must absolutely, under no circumstances, share the same functional identification or failure boundary.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 562, 309, 20368, 309, 365, 257, 18106, 9164, 11, 445, 570, 1281, 11, 10356, 11, 11328, 11, 293, 1412, 366, 5414, 264, 1900, 912, 23598, 9917, 281, 3155, 322, 5497, 293, 17522, 31054, 2712, 11, 436, 1633, 3122, 11, 833, 572, 9121, 11, 2073, 264, 912, 11745, 22065, 420, 7763, 12866, 13, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15325715590496453, "compression_ratio": 1.5964912280701755, "no_speech_prob": 2.167616563672481e-12}, {"id": 857, "seek": 270198, "start": 2722.54, "end": 2724.28, "text": " It's like renting a giant apartment.", "tokens": [51393, 467, 311, 411, 40598, 257, 7410, 9587, 13, 51480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15325715590496453, "compression_ratio": 1.5964912280701755, "no_speech_prob": 2.167616563672481e-12}, {"id": 858, "seek": 270198, "start": 2724.46, "end": 2724.66, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51489, 1779, 13, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15325715590496453, "compression_ratio": 1.5964912280701755, "no_speech_prob": 2.167616563672481e-12}, {"id": 859, "seek": 270198, "start": 2724.9, "end": 2729.14, "text": " The corridor is a massive multi-bedroom apartment, and you rent it out to four different roommates.", "tokens": [51511, 440, 25602, 307, 257, 5994, 4825, 12, 2883, 2861, 9587, 11, 293, 291, 6214, 309, 484, 281, 1451, 819, 46886, 13, 51723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15325715590496453, "compression_ratio": 1.5964912280701755, "no_speech_prob": 2.167616563672481e-12}, {"id": 860, "seek": 270198, "start": 2729.32, "end": 2729.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51732, 1779, 13, 51741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15325715590496453, "compression_ratio": 1.5964912280701755, "no_speech_prob": 2.167616563672481e-12}, {"id": 861, "seek": 272950, "start": 2729.5, "end": 2734.14, "text": " You've got water, power, data, and transit all living under one roof.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 600, 658, 1281, 11, 1347, 11, 1412, 11, 293, 17976, 439, 2647, 833, 472, 8418, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12733549776330458, "compression_ratio": 1.6622516556291391, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189549921676426e-12}, {"id": 862, "seek": 272950, "start": 2734.28, "end": 2736.02, "text": " They share the red, they share the footprint.", "tokens": [50604, 814, 2073, 264, 2182, 11, 436, 2073, 264, 24222, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12733549776330458, "compression_ratio": 1.6622516556291391, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189549921676426e-12}, {"id": 863, "seek": 272950, "start": 2736.22, "end": 2737.1, "text": " It's highly efficient.", "tokens": [50701, 467, 311, 5405, 7148, 13, 50745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12733549776330458, "compression_ratio": 1.6622516556291391, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189549921676426e-12}, {"id": 864, "seek": 272950, "start": 2737.64, "end": 2745.4, "text": " But if the transit roommate leaves the stove on and starts a massive grease fire in the kitchen, the other roommates need absolute firewall protection.", "tokens": [50772, 583, 498, 264, 17976, 31692, 5510, 264, 19263, 322, 293, 3719, 257, 5994, 24867, 2610, 294, 264, 6525, 11, 264, 661, 46886, 643, 8236, 36109, 6334, 13, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12733549776330458, "compression_ratio": 1.6622516556291391, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189549921676426e-12}, {"id": 865, "seek": 272950, "start": 2745.82, "end": 2749.66, "text": " You cannot let the whole apartment burn down just because one roommate made a mistake.", "tokens": [51181, 509, 2644, 718, 264, 1379, 9587, 5064, 760, 445, 570, 472, 31692, 1027, 257, 6146, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12733549776330458, "compression_ratio": 1.6622516556291391, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189549921676426e-12}, {"id": 866, "seek": 272950, "start": 2750.14, "end": 2752.4, "text": " That is an incredibly accurate analogy.", "tokens": [51397, 663, 307, 364, 6252, 8559, 21663, 13, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12733549776330458, "compression_ratio": 1.6622516556291391, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189549921676426e-12}, {"id": 867, "seek": 272950, "start": 2752.68, "end": 2757.04, "text": " The blueprint is deeply concerned with the mathematical danger of cascading failure.", "tokens": [51524, 440, 35868, 307, 8760, 5922, 365, 264, 18894, 4330, 295, 3058, 66, 8166, 7763, 13, 51742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12733549776330458, "compression_ratio": 1.6622516556291391, "no_speech_prob": 1.5189549921676426e-12}, {"id": 868, "seek": 275704, "start": 2757.04, "end": 2763.16, "text": " Let's say you have a linear mass acceleration track, a high-speed magnetic transit system running down the corridor.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 584, 291, 362, 257, 8213, 2758, 17162, 2837, 11, 257, 1090, 12, 22746, 12688, 17976, 1185, 2614, 760, 264, 25602, 13, 50671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14085896809895834, "compression_ratio": 1.1717171717171717, "no_speech_prob": 1.249464941233125e-12}, {"id": 869, "seek": 276316, "start": 2763.16, "end": 2776.68, "text": " If that system suffers a catastrophic explosive failure, the blast radius and the thermal shock cannot be allowed to breach and contaminate the primary freshwater conduit running 30 feet away parallel to it.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 300, 1185, 33776, 257, 34915, 24630, 7763, 11, 264, 12035, 15845, 293, 264, 15070, 5588, 2644, 312, 4350, 281, 31086, 293, 27562, 473, 264, 6194, 50234, 15504, 270, 2614, 2217, 3521, 1314, 8952, 281, 309, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06677816808223724, "compression_ratio": 1.4930232558139536, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686122527783455e-12}, {"id": 870, "seek": 276316, "start": 2776.7599999999998, "end": 2781.7, "text": " Because then you don't just have a transit disaster, you have millions of people suddenly without drinking water.", "tokens": [51045, 1436, 550, 291, 500, 380, 445, 362, 257, 17976, 11293, 11, 291, 362, 6803, 295, 561, 5800, 1553, 7583, 1281, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06677816808223724, "compression_ratio": 1.4930232558139536, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686122527783455e-12}, {"id": 871, "seek": 278170, "start": 2781.7, "end": 2782.14, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1595362424850464, "compression_ratio": 1.455497382198953, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858796480888726e-12}, {"id": 872, "seek": 278170, "start": 2782.64, "end": 2790.96, "text": " To enforce this, the blueprint uses Menger's theorem, a concept from graph theory that evaluates edge disjoint and vertex disjoint paths.", "tokens": [50412, 1407, 24825, 341, 11, 264, 35868, 4960, 6685, 1321, 311, 20904, 11, 257, 3410, 490, 4295, 5261, 300, 6133, 1024, 4691, 717, 48613, 293, 28162, 717, 48613, 14518, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1595362424850464, "compression_ratio": 1.455497382198953, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858796480888726e-12}, {"id": 873, "seek": 278170, "start": 2791.22, "end": 2792.3199999999997, "text": " What does that mean practically?", "tokens": [50841, 708, 775, 300, 914, 15667, 30, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1595362424850464, "compression_ratio": 1.455497382198953, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858796480888726e-12}, {"id": 874, "seek": 278170, "start": 2792.7, "end": 2798.02, "text": " It mandates that every critical node pair in the network must have guaranteed physical redundancy.", "tokens": [50915, 467, 48662, 300, 633, 4924, 9984, 6119, 294, 264, 3209, 1633, 362, 18031, 4001, 27830, 6717, 13, 51181], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1595362424850464, "compression_ratio": 1.455497382198953, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858796480888726e-12}, {"id": 875, "seek": 279802, "start": 2798.02, "end": 2807.8, "text": " Spatial proximity, living in the same apartment, has to be violently mathematically balanced against physical separation, blast shielding, and emergency isolation valves.", "tokens": [50365, 1738, 267, 831, 27632, 11, 2647, 294, 264, 912, 9587, 11, 575, 281, 312, 46728, 44003, 13902, 1970, 4001, 14634, 11, 12035, 10257, 278, 11, 293, 7473, 16001, 34950, 13, 50854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12166043900951896, "compression_ratio": 1.5522388059701493, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686435219681606e-12}, {"id": 876, "seek": 279802, "start": 2808.04, "end": 2809.62, "text": " So what does this all mean for us?", "tokens": [50866, 407, 437, 775, 341, 439, 914, 337, 505, 30, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12166043900951896, "compression_ratio": 1.5522388059701493, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686435219681606e-12}, {"id": 877, "seek": 279802, "start": 2810.04, "end": 2820.56, "text": " Why should you, listening to this right now, care about spherical trigonometry, voronoi pizza zones, the curvature defect of a soccer ball, and the explosive shielding of giant Legos?", "tokens": [50966, 1545, 820, 291, 11, 4764, 281, 341, 558, 586, 11, 1127, 466, 37300, 35386, 266, 34730, 11, 4245, 266, 4869, 8298, 16025, 11, 264, 37638, 16445, 295, 257, 15469, 2594, 11, 293, 264, 24630, 10257, 278, 295, 7410, 7470, 329, 30, 51492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12166043900951896, "compression_ratio": 1.5522388059701493, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686435219681606e-12}, {"id": 878, "seek": 279802, "start": 2820.7, "end": 2821.48, "text": " Right, why does it matter?", "tokens": [51499, 1779, 11, 983, 775, 309, 1871, 30, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12166043900951896, "compression_ratio": 1.5522388059701493, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686435219681606e-12}, {"id": 879, "seek": 282148, "start": 2821.48, "end": 2826.2, "text": " Why did we just spend an hour deep diving into a blueprint for the year 2300?", "tokens": [50365, 1545, 630, 321, 445, 3496, 364, 1773, 2452, 20241, 666, 257, 35868, 337, 264, 1064, 6673, 628, 30, 50601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09106162586043366, "compression_ratio": 1.6137931034482758, "no_speech_prob": 1.9815522920435535e-12}, {"id": 880, "seek": 282148, "start": 2826.92, "end": 2836.7, "text": " I think it's because this document, the Orthodromic Infrastructure Blueprint, is arguably one of the greatest masterclasses in pure systems thinking I have ever read.", "tokens": [50637, 286, 519, 309, 311, 570, 341, 4166, 11, 264, 27554, 378, 4397, 299, 38425, 2885, 2177, 29017, 11, 307, 26771, 472, 295, 264, 6636, 4505, 11665, 279, 294, 6075, 3652, 1953, 286, 362, 1562, 1401, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09106162586043366, "compression_ratio": 1.6137931034482758, "no_speech_prob": 1.9815522920435535e-12}, {"id": 881, "seek": 282148, "start": 2836.82, "end": 2839.1, "text": " It forces a profound shift in perspective.", "tokens": [51132, 467, 5874, 257, 14382, 5513, 294, 4585, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09106162586043366, "compression_ratio": 1.6137931034482758, "no_speech_prob": 1.9815522920435535e-12}, {"id": 882, "seek": 282148, "start": 2839.4, "end": 2839.92, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [51261, 467, 775, 13, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09106162586043366, "compression_ratio": 1.6137931034482758, "no_speech_prob": 1.9815522920435535e-12}, {"id": 883, "seek": 282148, "start": 2840.04, "end": 2848.48, "text": " It forces us to separate our ultimate goals, the geometry, the protocol, the human connections, from our current tools, the physical machinery of the present day.", "tokens": [51293, 467, 5874, 505, 281, 4994, 527, 9705, 5493, 11, 264, 18426, 11, 264, 10336, 11, 264, 1952, 9271, 11, 490, 527, 2190, 3873, 11, 264, 4001, 27302, 295, 264, 1974, 786, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09106162586043366, "compression_ratio": 1.6137931034482758, "no_speech_prob": 1.9815522920435535e-12}, {"id": 884, "seek": 282148, "start": 2848.72, "end": 2849.28, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51727, 7587, 13, 51755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09106162586043366, "compression_ratio": 1.6137931034482758, "no_speech_prob": 1.9815522920435535e-12}, {"id": 885, "seek": 284928, "start": 2849.28, "end": 2852.0, "text": " And that is a mindset you can apply to literally anything.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 300, 307, 257, 12543, 291, 393, 3079, 281, 3736, 1340, 13, 50501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0817818374633789, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783455492758946e-12}, {"id": 886, "seek": 284928, "start": 2852.32, "end": 2857.6600000000003, "text": " You can apply it to your business strategy, to your community urban planning, or even to your own personal life.", "tokens": [50517, 509, 393, 3079, 309, 281, 428, 1606, 5206, 11, 281, 428, 1768, 9681, 5038, 11, 420, 754, 281, 428, 1065, 2973, 993, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0817818374633789, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783455492758946e-12}, {"id": 887, "seek": 284928, "start": 2858.1000000000004, "end": 2865.84, "text": " The lesson is, don't build something so rigid and hyper-optimized for today that your future self cannot adapt it for tomorrow.", "tokens": [50806, 440, 6898, 307, 11, 500, 380, 1322, 746, 370, 22195, 293, 9848, 12, 5747, 332, 1602, 337, 965, 300, 428, 2027, 2698, 2644, 6231, 309, 337, 4153, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0817818374633789, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783455492758946e-12}, {"id": 888, "seek": 284928, "start": 2866.5400000000004, "end": 2868.1800000000003, "text": " Separate the space from the implementation.", "tokens": [51228, 43480, 473, 264, 1901, 490, 264, 11420, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0817818374633789, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783455492758946e-12}, {"id": 889, "seek": 284928, "start": 2868.94, "end": 2872.96, "text": " It is about building a scaffolding for future generations rather than a cage.", "tokens": [51348, 467, 307, 466, 2390, 257, 44094, 278, 337, 2027, 10593, 2831, 813, 257, 17302, 13, 51549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0817818374633789, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783455492758946e-12}, {"id": 890, "seek": 284928, "start": 2873.36, "end": 2877.78, "text": " We want to give them the foundation to build upon without dictating exactly what they must build.", "tokens": [51569, 492, 528, 281, 976, 552, 264, 7030, 281, 1322, 3564, 1553, 12569, 990, 2293, 437, 436, 1633, 1322, 13, 51790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0817818374633789, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783455492758946e-12}, {"id": 891, "seek": 284928, "start": 2877.88, "end": 2878.84, "text": " So well said.", "tokens": [51795, 407, 731, 848, 13, 51843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0817818374633789, "compression_ratio": 1.7083333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4783455492758946e-12}, {"id": 892, "seek": 287884, "start": 2878.84, "end": 2886.1400000000003, "text": " But if we connect this all the way back to the absolute biggest picture possible, it leaves me with a thought that borders on the profound.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 321, 1745, 341, 439, 264, 636, 646, 281, 264, 8236, 3880, 3036, 1944, 11, 309, 5510, 385, 365, 257, 1194, 300, 16287, 322, 264, 14382, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17769426981608072, "compression_ratio": 1.4438775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.460769547857732e-12}, {"id": 893, "seek": 287884, "start": 2886.3, "end": 2886.8, "text": " Let's hear it.", "tokens": [50738, 961, 311, 1568, 309, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17769426981608072, "compression_ratio": 1.4438775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.460769547857732e-12}, {"id": 894, "seek": 287884, "start": 2887.04, "end": 2887.54, "text": " Bring us home.", "tokens": [50775, 12842, 505, 1280, 13, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17769426981608072, "compression_ratio": 1.4438775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.460769547857732e-12}, {"id": 895, "seek": 287884, "start": 2887.76, "end": 2889.6600000000003, "text": " Think back to the scenario you opened with.", "tokens": [50811, 6557, 646, 281, 264, 9005, 291, 5625, 365, 13, 50906], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17769426981608072, "compression_ratio": 1.4438775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.460769547857732e-12}, {"id": 896, "seek": 287884, "start": 2890.08, "end": 2892.58, "text": " Imagine humanity actually manages to coordinate.", "tokens": [50927, 11739, 10243, 767, 22489, 281, 15670, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17769426981608072, "compression_ratio": 1.4438775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.460769547857732e-12}, {"id": 897, "seek": 287884, "start": 2893.26, "end": 2894.08, "text": " We build this.", "tokens": [51086, 492, 1322, 341, 13, 51127], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17769426981608072, "compression_ratio": 1.4438775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.460769547857732e-12}, {"id": 898, "seek": 287884, "start": 2894.1600000000003, "end": 2894.36, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51131, 1033, 13, 51141], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17769426981608072, "compression_ratio": 1.4438775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.460769547857732e-12}, {"id": 899, "seek": 289436, "start": 2894.36, "end": 2899.2000000000003, "text": " Over the next hundred years, we lay down these nine massive orthodromic rings.", "tokens": [50365, 4886, 264, 958, 3262, 924, 11, 321, 2360, 760, 613, 4949, 5994, 19052, 378, 4397, 299, 11136, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18985929489135742, "compression_ratio": 1.5055555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.324220464185566e-12}, {"id": 900, "seek": 289436, "start": 2899.42, "end": 2901.1600000000003, "text": " We pour the planetary skeleton.", "tokens": [50618, 492, 2016, 264, 35788, 25204, 13, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18985929489135742, "compression_ratio": 1.5055555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.324220464185566e-12}, {"id": 901, "seek": 289436, "start": 2901.4, "end": 2902.2200000000003, "text": " We optimize it.", "tokens": [50717, 492, 19719, 309, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18985929489135742, "compression_ratio": 1.5055555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.324220464185566e-12}, {"id": 902, "seek": 289436, "start": 2902.28, "end": 2902.86, "text": " We shield it.", "tokens": [50761, 492, 10257, 309, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18985929489135742, "compression_ratio": 1.5055555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.324220464185566e-12}, {"id": 903, "seek": 289436, "start": 2902.92, "end": 2904.6, "text": " We run our civilizations through it.", "tokens": [50793, 492, 1190, 527, 40749, 807, 309, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18985929489135742, "compression_ratio": 1.5055555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.324220464185566e-12}, {"id": 904, "seek": 289436, "start": 2904.7000000000003, "end": 2904.92, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50882, 1779, 13, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18985929489135742, "compression_ratio": 1.5055555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.324220464185566e-12}, {"id": 905, "seek": 289436, "start": 2905.1, "end": 2907.3, "text": " But then say our civilization falls.", "tokens": [50902, 583, 550, 584, 527, 18036, 8804, 13, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18985929489135742, "compression_ratio": 1.5055555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.324220464185566e-12}, {"id": 906, "seek": 289436, "start": 2907.6200000000003, "end": 2910.06, "text": " Climate, war, time, whatever it is, we fade away.", "tokens": [51028, 27025, 11, 1516, 11, 565, 11, 2035, 309, 307, 11, 321, 21626, 1314, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18985929489135742, "compression_ratio": 1.5055555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.324220464185566e-12}, {"id": 907, "seek": 291006, "start": 2910.06, "end": 2919.46, "text": " What happens 10,000 years later, a future civilization entirely disconnected from us or perhaps an alien archaeological team arrives on Earth.", "tokens": [50365, 708, 2314, 1266, 11, 1360, 924, 1780, 11, 257, 2027, 18036, 7696, 29426, 490, 505, 420, 4317, 364, 12319, 42139, 1469, 20116, 322, 4755, 13, 50835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22929532187325613, "compression_ratio": 1.3006993006993006, "no_speech_prob": 1.4434400940135927e-12}, {"id": 908, "seek": 291006, "start": 2919.58, "end": 2919.7999999999997, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50841, 865, 13, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22929532187325613, "compression_ratio": 1.3006993006993006, "no_speech_prob": 1.4434400940135927e-12}, {"id": 909, "seek": 291006, "start": 2919.92, "end": 2921.7, "text": " They start digging through the crust.", "tokens": [50858, 814, 722, 17343, 807, 264, 18156, 13, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22929532187325613, "compression_ratio": 1.3006993006993006, "no_speech_prob": 1.4434400940135927e-12}, {"id": 910, "seek": 292170, "start": 2921.7, "end": 2928.72, "text": " And they unearth these massive, continuous, mathematically perfect rings circling the globe.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 436, 2251, 18352, 613, 5994, 11, 10957, 11, 44003, 2176, 11136, 3510, 1688, 264, 15371, 13, 50716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15277177409121864, "compression_ratio": 1.2342342342342343, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050162942813582e-12}, {"id": 911, "seek": 292170, "start": 2928.8799999999997, "end": 2929.54, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [50724, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 50757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15277177409121864, "compression_ratio": 1.2342342342342343, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050162942813582e-12}, {"id": 912, "seek": 292170, "start": 2929.62, "end": 2930.66, "text": " I see where you're going with this.", "tokens": [50761, 286, 536, 689, 291, 434, 516, 365, 341, 13, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15277177409121864, "compression_ratio": 1.2342342342342343, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050162942813582e-12}, {"id": 913, "seek": 293066, "start": 