: 1.5884146341463414, "no_speech_prob": 1.2448412526483432e-12}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 6.86, "end": 8.72, "text": " Okay, sounds awful, but I'm with you.", "tokens": [50708, 1033, 11, 3263, 11232, 11, 457, 286, 478, 365, 291, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.100457184074461, "compression_ratio": 1.5884146341463414, "no_speech_prob": 1.2448412526483432e-12}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 8.78, "end": 13.68, "text": " Right. Now imagine a computer algorithm is just looking at a snapshot of this elevator.", "tokens": [50804, 1779, 13, 823, 3811, 257, 3820, 9284, 307, 445, 1237, 412, 257, 30163, 295, 341, 18782, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.100457184074461, "compression_ratio": 1.5884146341463414, "no_speech_prob": 1.2448412526483432e-12}, {"id": 3, "seek": 0, "start": 13.68, "end": 19.64, "text": " It sees 50 people, all physically pressed up against each other, and it concludes, based on that data,", "tokens": [51049, 467, 8194, 2625, 561, 11, 439, 9762, 17355, 493, 1970, 1184, 661, 11, 293, 309, 24643, 11, 2361, 322, 300, 1412, 11, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.100457184074461, "compression_ratio": 1.5884146341463414, "no_speech_prob": 1.2448412526483432e-12}, {"id": 4, "seek": 0, "start": 20.04, "end": 23.64, "text": " that they are this incredibly tight-knit family who deeply love each other.", "tokens": [51367, 300, 436, 366, 341, 6252, 4524, 12, 5457, 270, 1605, 567, 8760, 959, 1184, 661, 13, 51547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.100457184074461, "compression_ratio": 1.5884146341463414, "no_speech_prob": 1.2448412526483432e-12}, {"id": 5, "seek": 0, "start": 23.84, "end": 25.14, "text": " Just because they're physically touching.", "tokens": [51557, 1449, 570, 436, 434, 9762, 11175, 13, 51622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.100457184074461, "compression_ratio": 1.5884146341463414, "no_speech_prob": 1.2448412526483432e-12}, {"id": 6, "seek": 0, "start": 25.3, "end": 29.38, "text": " Exactly. It's measuring the physical space, not the social reality.", "tokens": [51630, 7587, 13, 467, 311, 13389, 264, 4001, 1901, 11, 406, 264, 2093, 4103, 13, 51834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.100457184074461, "compression_ratio": 1.5884146341463414, "no_speech_prob": 1.2448412526483432e-12}, {"id": 7, "seek": 3000, "start": 30.0, "end": 38.26, "text": " And today we are looking at how supposedly rigorous scientific metrics can completely lie to us in the exact same way.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 965, 321, 366, 1237, 412, 577, 20581, 29882, 8134, 16367, 393, 2584, 4544, 281, 505, 294, 264, 1900, 912, 636, 13, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11964155126501012, "compression_ratio": 1.6082474226804124, "no_speech_prob": 6.794337770350822e-13}, {"id": 8, "seek": 3000, "start": 38.26, "end": 42.86, "text": " Yeah, by basically just measuring the box we're trapped in instead of the actual physics of what we're doing.", "tokens": [50778, 865, 11, 538, 1936, 445, 13389, 264, 2424, 321, 434, 14994, 294, 2602, 295, 264, 3539, 10649, 295, 437, 321, 434, 884, 13, 51008], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11964155126501012, "compression_ratio": 1.6082474226804124, "no_speech_prob": 6.794337770350822e-13}, {"id": 9, "seek": 3000, "start": 43.46, "end": 48.56, "text": " Welcome to the deep dive. Today we are talking about the illusion of measurement.", "tokens": [51038, 4027, 281, 264, 2452, 9192, 13, 2692, 321, 366, 1417, 466, 264, 18854, 295, 13160, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11964155126501012, "compression_ratio": 1.6082474226804124, "no_speech_prob": 6.794337770350822e-13}, {"id": 10, "seek": 3000, "start": 49.24, "end": 55.260000000000005, "text": " Because, you know, have you ever read an article or maybe a scientific paper that just throws around these heavy, important-sounding terms?", "tokens": [51327, 1436, 11, 291, 458, 11, 362, 291, 1562, 1401, 364, 7222, 420, 1310, 257, 8134, 3035, 300, 445, 19251, 926, 613, 4676, 11, 1021, 12, 82, 24625, 2115, 30, 51628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11964155126501012, "compression_ratio": 1.6082474226804124, "no_speech_prob": 6.794337770350822e-13}, {"id": 11, "seek": 3000, "start": 55.94, "end": 56.68, "text": " Oh, all the time.", "tokens": [51662, 876, 11, 439, 264, 565, 13, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11964155126501012, "compression_ratio": 1.6082474226804124, "no_speech_prob": 6.794337770350822e-13}, {"id": 12, "seek": 5668, "start": 56.68, "end": 63.78, "text": " Words like capacity or agency, resilience, utility, things like that.", "tokens": [50365, 32857, 411, 6042, 420, 7934, 11, 19980, 11, 14877, 11, 721, 411, 300, 13, 50720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10466327117039607, "compression_ratio": 1.5714285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.345435590195676e-12}, {"id": 13, "seek": 5668, "start": 63.84, "end": 71.8, "text": " You're reading along, feeling very informed, and then you just stop and realize, wait, I have absolutely no idea how anyone is actually measuring those things.", "tokens": [50723, 509, 434, 3760, 2051, 11, 2633, 588, 11740, 11, 293, 550, 291, 445, 1590, 293, 4325, 11, 1699, 11, 286, 362, 3122, 572, 1558, 577, 2878, 307, 767, 13389, 729, 721, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10466327117039607, "compression_ratio": 1.5714285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.345435590195676e-12}, {"id": 14, "seek": 5668, "start": 72.0, "end": 75.53999999999999, "text": " It is the absolute definition of theoretical muddy waters.", "tokens": [51131, 467, 307, 264, 8236, 7123, 295, 20864, 38540, 12975, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10466327117039607, "compression_ratio": 1.5714285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.345435590195676e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 5668, "start": 76.24, "end": 76.53999999999999, "text": " Hmm.", "tokens": [51343, 8239, 13, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10466327117039607, "compression_ratio": 1.5714285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.345435590195676e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 5668, "start": 76.84, "end": 79.66, "text": " I mean, these words do a tremendous amount of heavy lifting in our minds.", "tokens": [51373, 286, 914, 11, 613, 2283, 360, 257, 10048, 2372, 295, 4676, 15798, 294, 527, 9634, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10466327117039607, "compression_ratio": 1.5714285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.345435590195676e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 5668, "start": 79.72, "end": 80.24, "text": " You really do.", "tokens": [51517, 509, 534, 360, 13, 51543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10466327117039607, "compression_ratio": 1.5714285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.345435590195676e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 5668, "start": 80.32, "end": 81.3, "text": " They sound structural, right?", "tokens": [51547, 814, 1626, 15067, 11, 558, 30, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10466327117039607, "compression_ratio": 1.5714285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.345435590195676e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 5668, "start": 81.44, "end": 81.62, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51603, 865, 13, 51612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10466327117039607, "compression_ratio": 1.5714285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.345435590195676e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 8162, "start": 81.62, "end": 83.60000000000001, "text": " Like load-bearing pillars in an argument.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 3677, 12, 650, 1921, 26729, 294, 364, 6770, 13, 50464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14478363387886134, "compression_ratio": 1.4931506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.2253014358351577e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 8162, "start": 83.72, "end": 83.88000000000001, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50470, 865, 13, 50478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14478363387886134, "compression_ratio": 1.4931506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.2253014358351577e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 8162, "start": 83.88000000000001, "end": 93.24000000000001, "text": " But when you try to pin them down to a hard number or, you know, ask for the specific ruler being used to measure them, they have a tendency to just sort of evaporate into thin air.", "tokens": [50478, 583, 562, 291, 853, 281, 5447, 552, 760, 281, 257, 1152, 1230, 420, 11, 291, 458, 11, 1029, 337, 264, 2685, 19661, 885, 1143, 281, 3481, 552, 11, 436, 362, 257, 18187, 281, 445, 1333, 295, 26315, 473, 666, 5862, 1988, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14478363387886134, "compression_ratio": 1.4931506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.2253014358351577e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 8162, "start": 93.82000000000001, "end": 96.12, "text": " And that is the mission for this deep dive.", "tokens": [50975, 400, 300, 307, 264, 4447, 337, 341, 2452, 9192, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14478363387886134, "compression_ratio": 1.4931506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.2253014358351577e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 8162, "start": 96.52000000000001, "end": 99.32000000000001, "text": " We are setting a trap for scientific buzzwords today.", "tokens": [51110, 492, 366, 3287, 257, 11487, 337, 8134, 13036, 13832, 965, 13, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14478363387886134, "compression_ratio": 1.4931506849315068, "no_speech_prob": 1.2253014358351577e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 9932, "start": 99.32, "end": 106.91999999999999, "text": " We've got two really fascinating documents from July 2026 from an independent researcher known as Flitschian.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 600, 658, 732, 534, 10343, 8512, 490, 7370, 945, 10880, 490, 364, 6695, 21751, 2570, 382, 3235, 1208, 339, 952, 13, 50745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17288346724076706, "compression_ratio": 1.4260089686098654, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245780983150214e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 9932, "start": 107.11999999999999, "end": 107.32, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50755, 865, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17288346724076706, "compression_ratio": 1.4260089686098654, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245780983150214e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 9932, "start": 107.5, "end": 108.5, "text": " These are incredible reads.", "tokens": [50774, 1981, 366, 4651, 15700, 13, 50824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17288346724076706, "compression_ratio": 1.4260089686098654, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245780983150214e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 9932, "start": 108.6, "end": 110.36, "text": " The first one is this methodological essay.", "tokens": [50829, 440, 700, 472, 307, 341, 3170, 4383, 16238, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17288346724076706, "compression_ratio": 1.4260089686098654, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245780983150214e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 9932, "start": 110.47999999999999, "end": 115.5, "text": " It's called Prediction Before Interpretation, a Criterion for Field-like Constructs in Complex Systems.", "tokens": [50923, 467, 311, 1219, 32969, 4105, 4546, 5751, 6629, 399, 11, 257, 4779, 1681, 313, 337, 17952, 12, 4092, 8574, 1757, 82, 294, 41184, 27059, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17288346724076706, "compression_ratio": 1.4260089686098654, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245780983150214e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 9932, "start": 115.69999999999999, "end": 116.44, "text": " It's quite a title.", "tokens": [51184, 467, 311, 1596, 257, 4876, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17288346724076706, "compression_ratio": 1.4260089686098654, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245780983150214e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 9932, "start": 116.8, "end": 117.19999999999999, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51239, 467, 307, 13, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17288346724076706, "compression_ratio": 1.4260089686098654, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245780983150214e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 11720, "start": 117.2, "end": 126.8, "text": " And then the second one is its companion empirical paper, which is Capacity Dissipation and the Onset of Motility-Induced Phase Separation.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 550, 264, 1150, 472, 307, 1080, 22363, 31886, 3035, 11, 597, 307, 8363, 19008, 413, 891, 647, 399, 293, 264, 1282, 3854, 295, 8956, 1140, 12, 21790, 41209, 24432, 43480, 399, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.112110595703125, "compression_ratio": 1.433179723502304, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552528661964439e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 11720, "start": 126.98, "end": 136.68, "text": " And look, the journey through these two documents, it is going to fundamentally change how you evaluate scientific claims or, well, even business frameworks.", "tokens": [50854, 400, 574, 11, 264, 4671, 807, 613, 732, 8512, 11, 309, 307, 516, 281, 17879, 1319, 577, 291, 13059, 8134, 9441, 420, 11, 731, 11, 754, 1606, 29834, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.112110595703125, "compression_ratio": 1.433179723502304, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552528661964439e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 11720, "start": 136.74, "end": 137.3, "text": " Oh, for sure.", "tokens": [51342, 876, 11, 337, 988, 13, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.112110595703125, "compression_ratio": 1.433179723502304, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552528661964439e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 13730, "start": 137.3, "end": 142.56, "text": " Really, any domain where people invent new vocabulary to describe complex phenomena.", "tokens": [50365, 4083, 11, 604, 9274, 689, 561, 7962, 777, 19864, 281, 6786, 3997, 22004, 13, 50628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12923324501121436, "compression_ratio": 1.5116279069767442, "no_speech_prob": 1.367239980086532e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 13730, "start": 142.68, "end": 142.92000000000002, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50634, 865, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12923324501121436, "compression_ratio": 1.5116279069767442, "no_speech_prob": 1.367239980086532e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 13730, "start": 143.12, "end": 148.94, "text": " Because what is so compelling about Flitschian's approach here is that it forces us to confront this exact problem head on.", "tokens": [50656, 1436, 437, 307, 370, 20050, 466, 3235, 1208, 339, 952, 311, 3109, 510, 307, 300, 309, 5874, 505, 281, 12422, 341, 1900, 1154, 1378, 322, 13, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12923324501121436, "compression_ratio": 1.5116279069767442, "no_speech_prob": 1.367239980086532e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 13730, "start": 149.04000000000002, "end": 149.34, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50952, 1779, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12923324501121436, "compression_ratio": 1.5116279069767442, "no_speech_prob": 1.367239980086532e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 13730, "start": 149.68, "end": 157.20000000000002, "text": " The first essay actually begins with this diagnostic question that, frankly, I think every single person listening to this should write on a sticky note.", "tokens": [50984, 440, 700, 16238, 767, 7338, 365, 341, 27897, 1168, 300, 11, 11939, 11, 286, 519, 633, 2167, 954, 4764, 281, 341, 820, 2464, 322, 257, 14470, 3637, 13, 51360], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12923324501121436, "compression_ratio": 1.5116279069767442, "no_speech_prob": 1.367239980086532e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 13730, "start": 157.32000000000002, "end": 157.82000000000002, "text": " Let's hear it.", "tokens": [51366, 961, 311, 1568, 309, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12923324501121436, "compression_ratio": 1.5116279069767442, "no_speech_prob": 1.367239980086532e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 15782, "start": 157.82, "end": 159.42, "text": " The question is essentially this.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1168, 307, 4476, 341, 13, 50445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1508493797451842, "compression_ratio": 1.6377952755905512, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269215149742553e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 15782, "start": 160.07999999999998, "end": 173.14, "text": " If two competent observers examine the exact same system and they disagree about the value of a construct, like, say, its capacity or its resilience, is there a specific procedure that could, in principle, settle that disagreement?", "tokens": [50478, 759, 732, 29998, 48090, 17496, 264, 1900, 912, 1185, 293, 436, 14091, 466, 264, 2158, 295, 257, 7690, 11, 411, 11, 584, 11, 1080, 6042, 420, 1080, 19980, 11, 307, 456, 257, 2685, 10747, 300, 727, 11, 294, 8665, 11, 11852, 300, 38947, 30, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1508493797451842, "compression_ratio": 1.6377952755905512, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269215149742553e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 15782, "start": 173.6, "end": 173.95999999999998, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51154, 3153, 13, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1508493797451842, "compression_ratio": 1.6377952755905512, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269215149742553e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 15782, "start": 174.32, "end": 174.64, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51190, 1033, 13, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1508493797451842, "compression_ratio": 1.6377952755905512, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269215149742553e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 15782, "start": 174.72, "end": 176.26, "text": " So if the answer is yes, then what?", "tokens": [51210, 407, 498, 264, 1867, 307, 2086, 11, 550, 437, 30, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1508493797451842, "compression_ratio": 1.6377952755905512, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269215149742553e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 15782, "start": 176.54, "end": 181.62, "text": " If the answer is yes, then the construct has entered the domain of empirical claims.", "tokens": [51301, 759, 264, 1867, 307, 2086, 11, 550, 264, 7690, 575, 9065, 264, 9274, 295, 31886, 9441, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1508493797451842, "compression_ratio": 1.6377952755905512, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269215149742553e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 15782, "start": 182.29999999999998, "end": 183.35999999999999, "text": " It's real science.", "tokens": [51589, 467, 311, 957, 3497, 13, 51642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1508493797451842, "compression_ratio": 1.6377952755905512, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269215149742553e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 18336, "start": 183.36, "end": 187.92000000000002, "text": " You can run the procedure, look at the output, and declare one observer correct.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 1190, 264, 10747, 11, 574, 412, 264, 5598, 11, 293, 19710, 472, 27878, 3006, 13, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14862353302711664, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 18336, "start": 188.34, "end": 189.22000000000003, "text": " But if the answer is no.", "tokens": [50614, 583, 498, 264, 1867, 307, 572, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14862353302711664, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 18336, "start": 189.38000000000002, "end": 189.54000000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50666, 1779, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14862353302711664, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 18336, "start": 189.58, "end": 194.04000000000002, "text": " If the answer is no, then that term is just doing what Flitschian calls rhetorical work.", "tokens": [50676, 759, 264, 1867, 307, 572, 11, 550, 300, 1433, 307, 445, 884, 437, 3235, 1208, 339, 952, 5498, 24182, 284, 804, 589, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14862353302711664, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 18336, "start": 194.28, "end": 195.20000000000002, "text": " Rhetorical work.", "tokens": [50911, 497, 9092, 284, 804, 589, 13, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14862353302711664, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 18336, "start": 195.28, "end": 195.48000000000002, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50961, 865, 13, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14862353302711664, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 18336, "start": 195.76000000000002, "end": 197.3, "text": " It is organizing our intuition.", "tokens": [50985, 467, 307, 17608, 527, 24002, 13, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14862353302711664, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 18336, "start": 197.92000000000002, "end": 199.48000000000002, "text": " It's suggesting analogies.", "tokens": [51093, 467, 311, 18094, 16660, 530, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14862353302711664, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 18336, "start": 199.66000000000003, "end": 203.34, "text": " And it's lending a very authoritative vocabulary to the paper.", "tokens": [51180, 400, 309, 311, 29823, 257, 588, 3793, 14275, 19864, 281, 264, 3035, 13, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14862353302711664, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 18336, "start": 203.78000000000003, "end": 206.78000000000003, "text": " But it hasn't actually done any real empirical work.", "tokens": [51386, 583, 309, 6132, 380, 767, 1096, 604, 957, 31886, 589, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14862353302711664, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 18336, "start": 206.98000000000002, "end": 209.16000000000003, "text": " You know, it's so much like corporate jargon.", "tokens": [51546, 509, 458, 11, 309, 311, 370, 709, 411, 10896, 15181, 10660, 13, 51655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14862353302711664, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012574516859445e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 20916, "start": 209.16, "end": 215.32, "text": " Think about a boardroom, and the CEO stands up and says, we really need to maximize our team's synergy.", "tokens": [50365, 6557, 466, 257, 3150, 2861, 11, 293, 264, 9282, 7382, 493, 293, 1619, 11, 321, 534, 643, 281, 19874, 527, 1469, 311, 50163, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14211005864180917, "compression_ratio": 1.6045016077170418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 20916, "start": 215.62, "end": 216.6, "text": " Oh, perfect example.", "tokens": [50688, 876, 11, 2176, 1365, 13, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14211005864180917, "compression_ratio": 1.6045016077170418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 20916, "start": 216.88, "end": 217.06, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50751, 1779, 13, 50760], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14211005864180917, "compression_ratio": 1.6045016077170418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 20916, "start": 217.32, "end": 220.16, "text": " Everyone nods because synergy sounds like a measurable quantity.", "tokens": [50773, 5198, 15224, 82, 570, 50163, 3263, 411, 257, 43615, 11275, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14211005864180917, "compression_ratio": 1.6045016077170418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 20916, "start": 220.34, "end": 223.57999999999998, "text": " Like, oh, we had low synergy yesterday, but we have high synergy today.", "tokens": [50924, 1743, 11, 1954, 11, 321, 632, 2295, 50163, 5186, 11, 457, 321, 362, 1090, 50163, 965, 13, 51086], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14211005864180917, "compression_ratio": 1.6045016077170418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 20916, "start": 223.72, "end": 225.34, "text": " But nobody actually has a synergy thermometer.", "tokens": [51093, 583, 5079, 767, 575, 257, 50163, 42539, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14211005864180917, "compression_ratio": 1.6045016077170418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 20916, "start": 225.5, "end": 225.82, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51182, 7587, 13, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14211005864180917, "compression_ratio": 1.6045016077170418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 20916, "start": 226.34, "end": 234.48, "text": " If the VP of sales and the VP of marketing disagree on the current exact level of synergy, there is no physical procedure to settle the bet.", "tokens": [51224, 759, 264, 35812, 295, 5763, 293, 264, 35812, 295, 6370, 14091, 322, 264, 2190, 1900, 1496, 295, 50163, 11, 456, 307, 572, 4001, 10747, 281, 11852, 264, 778, 13, 51631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14211005864180917, "compression_ratio": 1.6045016077170418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 20916, "start": 234.54, "end": 235.92, "text": " It's just a grammatical illusion.", "tokens": [51634, 467, 311, 445, 257, 17570, 267, 804, 18854, 13, 51703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14211005864180917, "compression_ratio": 1.6045016077170418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325107940138526e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 23592, "start": 235.92, "end": 239.33999999999997, "text": " And that parallel holds up perfectly in academia, too.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 300, 8952, 9190, 493, 6239, 294, 28937, 11, 886, 13, 50536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12283343360537574, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840938165212257e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 23592, "start": 239.95999999999998, "end": 247.77999999999997, "text": " The word synergy in your boardroom is doing grammatical work as a measurable quantity, but it lacks an operational procedure.", "tokens": [50567, 440, 1349, 50163, 294, 428, 3150, 2861, 307, 884, 17570, 267, 804, 589, 382, 257, 43615, 11275, 11, 457, 309, 31132, 364, 16607, 10747, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12283343360537574, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840938165212257e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 23592, "start": 248.14, "end": 248.27999999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50976, 1779, 13, 50983], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12283343360537574, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840938165212257e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 23592, "start": 248.51999999999998, "end": 254.1, "text": " In science, you see papers that define a quantity with full mathematical formality.", "tokens": [50995, 682, 3497, 11, 291, 536, 10577, 300, 6964, 257, 11275, 365, 1577, 18894, 1254, 1860, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12283343360537574, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840938165212257e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 23592, "start": 254.7, "end": 260.9, "text": " I mean, they can write down an integral, a functional, a complex coupling term, and still be making this exact same move.", "tokens": [51304, 286, 914, 11, 436, 393, 2464, 760, 364, 11573, 11, 257, 11745, 11, 257, 3997, 37447, 1433, 11, 293, 920, 312, 1455, 341, 1900, 912, 1286, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12283343360537574, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840938165212257e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 23592, "start": 260.98, "end": 262.52, "text": " Because the math looks intimidating.", "tokens": [51618, 1436, 264, 5221, 1542, 29714, 13, 51695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12283343360537574, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840938165212257e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 23592, "start": 262.76, "end": 263.15999999999997, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51707, 7587, 13, 51727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12283343360537574, "compression_ratio": 1.5622775800711743, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840938165212257e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 26316, "start": 263.16, "end": 272.18, "text": " But if the definition was never subjected to the question of how we observe a system with more of this versus less of this, it is just academic synergy.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 264, 7123, 390, 1128, 32153, 281, 264, 1168, 295, 577, 321, 11441, 257, 1185, 365, 544, 295, 341, 5717, 1570, 295, 341, 11, 309, 307, 445, 7778, 50163, 13, 50816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16651333434672294, "compression_ratio": 1.5532994923857868, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668280475139573e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 26316, "start": 272.54, "end": 273.40000000000003, "text": " Academic synergy.", "tokens": [50834, 36139, 50163, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16651333434672294, "compression_ratio": 1.5532994923857868, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668280475139573e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 26316, "start": 273.56, "end": 274.78000000000003, "text": " That is such a good way to put it.", "tokens": [50885, 663, 307, 1270, 257, 665, 636, 281, 829, 309, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16651333434672294, "compression_ratio": 1.5532994923857868, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668280475139573e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 26316, "start": 274.90000000000003, "end": 276.86, "text": " Infliction actually uses the slogan.", "tokens": [50952, 682, 3423, 4105, 767, 4960, 264, 33052, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16651333434672294, "compression_ratio": 1.5532994923857868, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668280475139573e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 26316, "start": 277.04, "end": 280.28000000000003, "text": " They write, new terminology is not new predictive content.", "tokens": [51059, 814, 2464, 11, 777, 27575, 307, 406, 777, 35521, 2701, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16651333434672294, "compression_ratio": 1.5532994923857868, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668280475139573e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 26316, "start": 280.56, "end": 280.8, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51235, 1079, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16651333434672294, "compression_ratio": 1.5532994923857868, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668280475139573e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 28080, "start": 280.8, "end": 287.94, "text": " Just renaming existing observable things in more evocative fancy language doesn't actually add to human knowledge.", "tokens": [50365, 1449, 8124, 5184, 6741, 9951, 712, 721, 294, 544, 1073, 905, 1166, 10247, 2856, 1177, 380, 767, 909, 281, 1952, 3601, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11884314064087907, "compression_ratio": 1.57679180887372, "no_speech_prob": 1.455294652147332e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 28080, "start": 288.42, "end": 290.28000000000003, "text": " But, okay, I do want to push back on this a little bit.", "tokens": [50746, 583, 11, 1392, 11, 286, 360, 528, 281, 2944, 646, 322, 341, 257, 707, 857, 13, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11884314064087907, "compression_ratio": 1.57679180887372, "no_speech_prob": 1.455294652147332e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 28080, "start": 290.36, "end": 290.48, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [50843, 4894, 13, 50849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11884314064087907, "compression_ratio": 1.57679180887372, "no_speech_prob": 1.455294652147332e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 28080, "start": 290.64, "end": 290.92, "text": " Go for it.", "tokens": [50857, 1037, 337, 309, 13, 50871], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11884314064087907, "compression_ratio": 1.57679180887372, "no_speech_prob": 1.455294652147332e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 28080, "start": 291.18, "end": 295.04, "text": " Because when I was reading the first essay, I kept thinking about the history of science.", "tokens": [50884, 1436, 562, 286, 390, 3760, 264, 700, 16238, 11, 286, 4305, 1953, 466, 264, 2503, 295, 3497, 13, 51077], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11884314064087907, "compression_ratio": 1.57679180887372, "no_speech_prob": 1.455294652147332e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 28080, "start": 295.18, "end": 299.74, "text": " I mean, didn't atomic theory exist long before we had electron microscopes to actually see atoms?", "tokens": [51084, 286, 914, 11, 994, 380, 22275, 5261, 2514, 938, 949, 321, 632, 6084, 30483, 279, 281, 767, 536, 16871, 30, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11884314064087907, "compression_ratio": 1.57679180887372, "no_speech_prob": 1.455294652147332e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 28080, "start": 299.90000000000003, "end": 300.52, "text": " It did, yeah.", "tokens": [51320, 467, 630, 11, 1338, 13, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11884314064087907, "compression_ratio": 1.57679180887372, "no_speech_prob": 1.455294652147332e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 28080, "start": 300.76, "end": 304.54, "text": " Like, Dalton was talking about atomic weights in, what, the early 1800s?", "tokens": [51363, 1743, 11, 17357, 1756, 390, 1417, 466, 22275, 17443, 294, 11, 437, 11, 264, 2440, 24327, 82, 30, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11884314064087907, "compression_ratio": 1.57679180887372, "no_speech_prob": 1.455294652147332e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 30454, "start": 304.54, "end": 310.22, "text": " So isn't it perfectly okay to invent the word and the concept before we have the technological measurement?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 1943, 380, 309, 6239, 1392, 281, 7962, 264, 1349, 293, 264, 3410, 949, 321, 362, 264, 18439, 13160, 30, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16483459689400412, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493950744459694e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 30454, "start": 310.56, "end": 311.94, "text": " That is a very common defense.", "tokens": [50666, 663, 307, 257, 588, 2689, 7654, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16483459689400412, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493950744459694e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 30454, "start": 312.1, "end": 313.72, "text": " And Fliction actually anticipates it.", "tokens": [50743, 400, 3235, 4105, 767, 10416, 1024, 309, 13, 50824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16483459689400412, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493950744459694e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 30454, "start": 314.1, "end": 321.3, "text": " This isn't a demand for naive verificationism, where we just throw out any theory that can't be immediately photographed right now.", "tokens": [50843, 639, 1943, 380, 257, 4733, 337, 29052, 30206, 1434, 11, 689, 321, 445, 3507, 484, 604, 5261, 300, 393, 380, 312, 4258, 45067, 558, 586, 13, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16483459689400412, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493950744459694e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 30454, "start": 321.44, "end": 321.74, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51210, 1779, 13, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16483459689400412, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493950744459694e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 30454, "start": 321.82000000000005, "end": 323.66, "text": " Because that would stall science completely.", "tokens": [51229, 1436, 300, 576, 19633, 3497, 2584, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16483459689400412, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493950744459694e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 30454, "start": 323.92, "end": 324.32000000000005, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51334, 7587, 13, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16483459689400412, "compression_ratio": 1.5185185185185186, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493950744459694e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 32432, "start": 324.32, "end": 328.04, "text": " The author clarifies an exact timeline index here.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3793, 6093, 11221, 364, 1900, 12933, 8186, 510, 13, 50551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19590578581157483, "compression_ratio": 1.7157894736842105, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893191288915196e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 32432, "start": 328.86, "end": 333.76, "text": " Theoretical constructs are absolutely allowed to precede their measurement procedures.", "tokens": [50592, 440, 26262, 804, 7690, 82, 366, 3122, 4350, 281, 16969, 68, 641, 13160, 13846, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19590578581157483, "compression_ratio": 1.7157894736842105, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893191288915196e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 32432, "start": 334.62, "end": 337.21999999999997, "text": " The failure mode isn't proposing new constructs.", "tokens": [50880, 440, 7763, 4391, 1943, 380, 29939, 777, 7690, 82, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19590578581157483, "compression_ratio": 1.7157894736842105, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893191288915196e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 32432, "start": 337.26, "end": 338.7, "text": " Scientists have to hypothesize.", "tokens": [51012, 32958, 362, 281, 14276, 1125, 13, 51084], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19590578581157483, "compression_ratio": 1.7157894736842105, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893191288915196e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 32432, "start": 338.78, "end": 339.2, "text": " They do.", "tokens": [51088, 814, 360, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19590578581157483, "compression_ratio": 1.7157894736842105, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893191288915196e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 32432, "start": 339.38, "end": 339.96, "text": " They have to.", "tokens": [51118, 814, 362, 281, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19590578581157483, "compression_ratio": 1.7157894736842105, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893191288915196e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 32432, "start": 340.08, "end": 344.15999999999997, "text": " The failure mode is treating the proposal as though it were already a result.", "tokens": [51153, 440, 7763, 4391, 307, 15083, 264, 11494, 382, 1673, 309, 645, 1217, 257, 1874, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19590578581157483, "compression_ratio": 1.7157894736842105, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893191288915196e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 32432, "start": 344.52, "end": 350.5, "text": " A construct doesn't earn its predictive standing until it can actually be recovered from data and tested against alternatives.", "tokens": [51375, 316, 7690, 1177, 380, 6012, 1080, 35521, 4877, 1826, 309, 393, 767, 312, 19542, 490, 1412, 293, 8246, 1970, 20478, 13, 51674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19590578581157483, "compression_ratio": 1.7157894736842105, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893191288915196e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 32432, "start": 351.5, "end": 353.2, "text": " Before that point, it's just a hypothesis.", "tokens": [51724, 4546, 300, 935, 11, 309, 311, 445, 257, 17291, 13, 51809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19590578581157483, "compression_ratio": 1.7157894736842105, "no_speech_prob": 1.2893191288915196e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 35320, "start": 353.2, "end": 357.21999999999997, "text": " So it's fine as a starting point, but you can't build a whole foundation on it yet.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 309, 311, 2489, 382, 257, 2891, 935, 11, 457, 291, 393, 380, 1322, 257, 1379, 7030, 322, 309, 1939, 13, 50566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827227214026073, "compression_ratio": 1.6285714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970275874995556e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 35320, "start": 357.59999999999997, "end": 357.71999999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50585, 1779, 13, 50591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827227214026073, "compression_ratio": 1.6285714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970275874995556e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 35320, "start": 357.9, "end": 359.03999999999996, "text": " It is worth stating.", "tokens": [50600, 467, 307, 3163, 26688, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827227214026073, "compression_ratio": 1.6285714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970275874995556e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 35320, "start": 359.44, "end": 361.44, "text": " It is worth exploring mathematically, sure.", "tokens": [50677, 467, 307, 3163, 12736, 44003, 11, 988, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827227214026073, "compression_ratio": 1.6285714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970275874995556e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 35320, "start": 361.92, "end": 364.42, "text": " But it is not yet a fact about the world.", "tokens": [50801, 583, 309, 307, 406, 1939, 257, 1186, 466, 264, 1002, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827227214026073, "compression_ratio": 1.6285714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970275874995556e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 35320, "start": 364.9, "end": 371.06, "text": " You don't get to claim you've explained a complex system just because you invented a new word for the complexity.", "tokens": [50950, 509, 500, 380, 483, 281, 3932, 291, 600, 8825, 257, 3997, 1185, 445, 570, 291, 14479, 257, 777, 1349, 337, 264, 14024, 13, 51258], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827227214026073, "compression_ratio": 1.6285714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970275874995556e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 35320, "start": 371.48, "end": 371.65999999999997, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51279, 1033, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827227214026073, "compression_ratio": 1.6285714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970275874995556e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 35320, "start": 371.71999999999997, "end": 372.86, "text": " So it has to earn its keep.", "tokens": [51291, 407, 309, 575, 281, 6012, 1080, 1066, 13, 51348], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827227214026073, "compression_ratio": 1.6285714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970275874995556e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 35320, "start": 373.24, "end": 375.74, "text": " It's a hypothesis until it survives testing.", "tokens": [51367, 467, 311, 257, 17291, 1826, 309, 46231, 4997, 13, 51492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827227214026073, "compression_ratio": 1.6285714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970275874995556e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 35320, "start": 376.5, "end": 379.44, "text": " And Fliction doesn't just, you know, complain about this problem.", "tokens": [51530, 400, 3235, 4105, 1177, 380, 445, 11, 291, 458, 11, 11024, 466, 341, 1154, 13, 51677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14827227214026073, "compression_ratio": 1.6285714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970275874995556e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 37944, "start": 379.44, "end": 383.8, "text": " They build this whole philosophical crucible to burn away the nonsense.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 1322, 341, 1379, 25066, 5140, 32128, 281, 5064, 1314, 264, 14925, 13, 50583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17472222873142787, "compression_ratio": 1.5968992248062015, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351701231046237e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 37944, "start": 384.12, "end": 384.28, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50599, 1079, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17472222873142787, "compression_ratio": 1.5968992248062015, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351701231046237e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 37944, "start": 384.44, "end": 385.8, "text": " The identification criteria.", "tokens": [50615, 440, 22065, 11101, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17472222873142787, "compression_ratio": 1.5968992248062015, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351701231046237e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 37944, "start": 386.0, "end": 386.08, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50693, 1779, 13, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17472222873142787, "compression_ratio": 1.5968992248062015, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351701231046237e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 37944, "start": 386.18, "end": 387.48, "text": " It's this four-step filter.", "tokens": [50702, 467, 311, 341, 1451, 12, 16792, 6608, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17472222873142787, "compression_ratio": 1.5968992248062015, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351701231046237e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 37944, "start": 388.0, "end": 389.24, "text": " And it is rigorous.", "tokens": [50793, 400, 309, 307, 29882, 13, 50855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17472222873142787, "compression_ratio": 1.5968992248062015, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351701231046237e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 37944, "start": 389.76, "end": 392.46, "text": " This is the operational core of that first essay.", "tokens": [50881, 639, 307, 264, 16607, 4965, 295, 300, 700, 16238, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17472222873142787, "compression_ratio": 1.5968992248062015, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351701231046237e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 37944, "start": 393.14, "end": 401.18, "text": " Fliction argues that a proposed field or concept only earns that predictive standing if it satisfies four distinct conditions jointly.", "tokens": [51050, 3235, 4105, 38218, 300, 257, 10348, 2519, 420, 3410, 787, 46936, 300, 35521, 4877, 498, 309, 44271, 1451, 10644, 4487, 46557, 13, 51452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17472222873142787, "compression_ratio": 1.5968992248062015, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351701231046237e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 37944, "start": 401.5, "end": 402.52, "text": " Not just one or two.", "tokens": [51468, 1726, 445, 472, 420, 732, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17472222873142787, "compression_ratio": 1.5968992248062015, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351701231046237e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 37944, "start": 402.64, "end": 402.82, "text": " No.", "tokens": [51525, 883, 13, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17472222873142787, "compression_ratio": 1.5968992248062015, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351701231046237e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 37944, "start": 403.15999999999997, "end": 404.18, "text": " Not one, not three.", "tokens": [51551, 1726, 472, 11, 406, 1045, 13, 51602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17472222873142787, "compression_ratio": 1.5968992248062015, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351701231046237e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 37944, "start": 404.3, "end": 405.24, "text": " All four must be met.", "tokens": [51608, 1057, 1451, 1633, 312, 1131, 13, 51655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17472222873142787, "compression_ratio": 1.5968992248062015, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351701231046237e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 40524, "start": 405.24, "end": 407.98, "text": " Okay, let's walk through them because they are incredibly stringent.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1792, 807, 552, 570, 436, 366, 6252, 6798, 317, 13, 50502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1737519044142503, "compression_ratio": 1.651685393258427, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611187693774896e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 40524, "start": 408.14, "end": 410.42, "text": " So step one, it must be reconstructible.", "tokens": [50510, 407, 1823, 472, 11, 309, 1633, 312, 31499, 964, 13, 50624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1737519044142503, "compression_ratio": 1.651685393258427, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611187693774896e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 40524, "start": 410.68, "end": 410.78000000000003, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50637, 1779, 13, 50642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1737519044142503, "compression_ratio": 1.651685393258427, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611187693774896e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 40524, "start": 410.88, "end": 416.24, "text": " Meaning there has to be a precise mechanical procedure to recover this quantity from observational data.", "tokens": [50647, 19948, 456, 575, 281, 312, 257, 13600, 12070, 10747, 281, 8114, 341, 11275, 490, 9951, 1478, 1412, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1737519044142503, "compression_ratio": 1.651685393258427, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611187693774896e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 40524, "start": 416.84000000000003, "end": 423.36, "text": " It has to be stated so clearly that another researcher could run the exact same procedure independently and get the exact same numbers.", "tokens": [50945, 467, 575, 281, 312, 11323, 370, 4448, 300, 1071, 21751, 727, 1190, 264, 1900, 912, 10747, 21761, 293, 483, 264, 1900, 912, 3547, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1737519044142503, "compression_ratio": 1.651685393258427, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611187693774896e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 40524, "start": 423.76, "end": 424.18, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51291, 7587, 13, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1737519044142503, "compression_ratio": 1.651685393258427, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611187693774896e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 40524, "start": 424.56, "end": 425.48, "text": " No vibes allowed.", "tokens": [51331, 883, 27636, 4350, 13, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1737519044142503, "compression_ratio": 1.651685393258427, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611187693774896e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 40524, "start": 426.06, "end": 427.7, "text": " No subjective interpretations.", "tokens": [51406, 883, 25972, 37547, 13, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1737519044142503, "compression_ratio": 1.651685393258427, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611187693774896e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 40524, "start": 428.0, "end": 429.52, "text": " No vibes, just mechanics.", "tokens": [51503, 883, 27636, 11, 445, 12939, 13, 51579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1737519044142503, "compression_ratio": 1.651685393258427, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611187693774896e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 42952, "start": 429.52, "end": 436.26, "text": " But reconstructability alone isn't enough, which leads to step two, it must be comparable.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 31499, 2310, 3312, 1943, 380, 1547, 11, 597, 6689, 281, 1823, 732, 11, 309, 1633, 312, 25323, 13, 50702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1454504740606878, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.579455750216896e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 42952, "start": 436.94, "end": 437.65999999999997, "text": " And this is vital.", "tokens": [50736, 400, 341, 307, 11707, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1454504740606878, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.579455750216896e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 42952, "start": 438.12, "end": 446.26, "text": " Often, an intuitive concept like, well, capacity could be mathematically formalized in a few different perfectly reasonable ways.", "tokens": [50795, 20043, 11, 364, 21769, 3410, 411, 11, 731, 11, 6042, 727, 312, 44003, 9860, 1602, 294, 257, 1326, 819, 6239, 10585, 2098, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1454504740606878, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.579455750216896e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 42952, "start": 446.5, "end": 448.09999999999997, "text": " Depending on who is doing the math.", "tokens": [51214, 22539, 322, 567, 307, 884, 264, 5221, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1454504740606878, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.579455750216896e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 42952, "start": 448.24, "end": 448.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51301, 1779, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1454504740606878, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.579455750216896e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 42952, "start": 448.79999999999995, "end": 457.5, "text": " The criterion demands that these competing formalizations be defined and compared against each other rather than a researcher just picking one by fiat.", "tokens": [51329, 440, 46691, 15107, 300, 613, 15439, 9860, 14455, 312, 7642, 293, 5347, 1970, 1184, 661, 2831, 813, 257, 21751, 445, 8867, 472, 538, 283, 7676, 13, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1454504740606878, "compression_ratio": 1.5724637681159421, "no_speech_prob": 1.579455750216896e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 45750, "start": 457.5, "end": 462.08, "text": " Because if you just pick one, you're back to asserting things based on preference.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 498, 291, 445, 1888, 472, 11, 291, 434, 646, 281, 1256, 27187, 721, 2361, 322, 17502, 13, 50594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12793044156806413, "compression_ratio": 1.6928104575163399, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892517557693608e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 45750, "start": 462.64, "end": 469.32, "text": " You have to prove why your specific mathematical definition is the right one by stacking it up against the alternatives.", "tokens": [50622, 509, 362, 281, 7081, 983, 428, 2685, 18894, 7123, 307, 264, 558, 472, 538, 41376, 309, 493, 1970, 264, 20478, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12793044156806413, "compression_ratio": 1.6928104575163399, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892517557693608e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 45750, "start": 469.68, "end": 470.88, "text": " Which brings us to step three.", "tokens": [50974, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 1823, 1045, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12793044156806413, "compression_ratio": 1.6928104575163399, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892517557693608e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 45750, "start": 471.48, "end": 472.48, "text": " It must be stable.", "tokens": [51064, 467, 1633, 312, 8351, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12793044156806413, "compression_ratio": 1.6928104575163399, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892517557693608e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 45750, "start": 473.24, "end": 478.96, "text": " The coefficients or parameters of this construct have to remain stable across what they call nuisance parameters.", "tokens": [51152, 440, 31994, 420, 9834, 295, 341, 7690, 362, 281, 6222, 8351, 2108, 437, 436, 818, 3822, 46852, 9834, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12793044156806413, "compression_ratio": 1.6928104575163399, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892517557693608e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 45750, "start": 479.16, "end": 480.0, "text": " Okay, let's pause there.", "tokens": [51448, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 10465, 456, 13, 51490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12793044156806413, "compression_ratio": 1.6928104575163399, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892517557693608e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 45750, "start": 480.12, "end": 480.98, "text": " Nuisance parameters.", "tokens": [51496, 426, 8479, 719, 9834, 13, 51539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12793044156806413, "compression_ratio": 1.6928104575163399, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892517557693608e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 45750, "start": 481.18, "end": 481.56, "text": " Like what?", "tokens": [51549, 1743, 437, 30, 51568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12793044156806413, "compression_ratio": 1.6928104575163399, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892517557693608e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 45750, "start": 481.66, "end": 483.44, "text": " Well, things like the coarse graining scale.", "tokens": [51573, 1042, 11, 721, 411, 264, 39312, 1295, 1760, 4373, 13, 51662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12793044156806413, "compression_ratio": 1.6928104575163399, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892517557693608e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 45750, "start": 483.52, "end": 484.86, "text": " Okay, let me try to translate that for a second.", "tokens": [51666, 1033, 11, 718, 385, 853, 281, 13799, 300, 337, 257, 1150, 13, 51733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12793044156806413, "compression_ratio": 1.6928104575163399, "no_speech_prob": 1.4892517557693608e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 48486, "start": 484.86, "end": 487.98, "text": " Coarse graining, that's basically like blurring an image, right?", "tokens": [50365, 3066, 11668, 1295, 1760, 11, 300, 311, 1936, 411, 14257, 2937, 364, 3256, 11, 558, 30, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14487273352486746, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 1.707803169714861e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 48486, "start": 488.08000000000004, "end": 489.14, "text": " Or looking at a map.", "tokens": [50526, 1610, 1237, 412, 257, 4471, 13, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14487273352486746, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 1.707803169714861e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 48486, "start": 489.26, "end": 490.36, "text": " That's a good way to think of it.", "tokens": [50585, 663, 311, 257, 665, 636, 281, 519, 295, 309, 13, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14487273352486746, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 1.707803169714861e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 48486, "start": 490.58000000000004, "end": 494.78000000000003, "text": " Like, if I look at a map of a city, street by street, that's fine grained.", "tokens": [50651, 1743, 11, 498, 286, 574, 412, 257, 4471, 295, 257, 2307, 11, 4838, 538, 4838, 11, 300, 311, 2489, 1295, 2001, 13, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14487273352486746, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 1.707803169714861e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 48486, "start": 495.02000000000004, "end": 500.48, "text": " But if I zoom out until the city is just a single dot on a state map, that's coarse grained.", "tokens": [50873, 583, 498, 286, 8863, 484, 1826, 264, 2307, 307, 445, 257, 2167, 5893, 322, 257, 1785, 4471, 11, 300, 311, 39312, 1295, 2001, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14487273352486746, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 1.707803169714861e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 48486, "start": 500.64, "end": 503.38, "text": " I'm losing the tiny details to see the big picture.", "tokens": [51154, 286, 478, 7027, 264, 5870, 4365, 281, 536, 264, 955, 3036, 13, 51291], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14487273352486746, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 1.707803169714861e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 48486, "start": 503.56, "end": 504.78000000000003, "text": " That is an excellent analogy.", "tokens": [51300, 663, 307, 364, 7103, 21663, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14487273352486746, "compression_ratio": 1.618421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 1.707803169714861e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 50478, "start": 504.78, "end": 511.08, "text": " In physics, or really any data science, you often have to decide what resolution to look at your data.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 10649, 11, 420, 534, 604, 1412, 3497, 11, 291, 2049, 362, 281, 4536, 437, 8669, 281, 574, 412, 428, 1412, 13, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16531162069301414, "compression_ratio": 1.6378600823045268, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639235361447398e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 50478, "start": 511.29999999999995, "end": 511.4, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50691, 1779, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16531162069301414, "compression_ratio": 1.6378600823045268, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639235361447398e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 50478, "start": 511.78, "end": 513.1999999999999, "text": " Are you looking at individual atoms?", "tokens": [50715, 2014, 291, 1237, 412, 2609, 16871, 30, 50786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16531162069301414, "compression_ratio": 1.6378600823045268, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639235361447398e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 50478, "start": 513.52, "end": 515.54, "text": " Or clusters of 100 atoms?", "tokens": [50802, 1610, 23313, 295, 2319, 16871, 30, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16531162069301414, "compression_ratio": 1.6378600823045268, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639235361447398e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 50478, "start": 515.64, "end": 517.02, "text": " Or a whole fluid flow?", "tokens": [50908, 1610, 257, 1379, 9113, 3095, 30, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16531162069301414, "compression_ratio": 1.6378600823045268, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639235361447398e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 50478, "start": 517.3, "end": 523.12, "text": " If your amazing new scientific metric completely changes its meaning or its mathematical sign,", "tokens": [50991, 759, 428, 2243, 777, 8134, 20678, 2584, 2962, 1080, 3620, 420, 1080, 18894, 1465, 11, 51282], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16531162069301414, "compression_ratio": 1.6378600823045268, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639235361447398e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 50478, "start": 523.26, "end": 525.28, "text": " just because you zoomed out a little bit on your data.", "tokens": [51289, 445, 570, 291, 8863, 292, 484, 257, 707, 857, 322, 428, 1412, 13, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16531162069301414, "compression_ratio": 1.6378600823045268, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639235361447398e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 50478, "start": 525.28, "end": 527.68, "text": " Just because you changed your coarse graining scale.", "tokens": [51390, 1449, 570, 291, 3105, 428, 39312, 1295, 1760, 4373, 13, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16531162069301414, "compression_ratio": 1.6378600823045268, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639235361447398e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 52768, "start": 527.68, "end": 528.16, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14120414040305398, "compression_ratio": 1.5594405594405594, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 52768, "start": 528.42, "end": 533.0799999999999, "text": " If it changes just because of that, then it's not a real physical property of the system.", "tokens": [50402, 759, 309, 2962, 445, 570, 295, 300, 11, 550, 309, 311, 406, 257, 957, 4001, 4707, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14120414040305398, "compression_ratio": 1.5594405594405594, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 52768, "start": 533.7399999999999, "end": 535.6999999999999, "text": " It's an artifact of your zoom level.", "tokens": [50668, 467, 311, 364, 34806, 295, 428, 8863, 1496, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14120414040305398, "compression_ratio": 1.5594405594405594, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 52768, "start": 535.9599999999999, "end": 539.0999999999999, "text": " It has to be stable regardless of those nuisance parameters.", "tokens": [50779, 467, 575, 281, 312, 8351, 10060, 295, 729, 3822, 46852, 9834, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14120414040305398, "compression_ratio": 1.5594405594405594, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 52768, "start": 539.2399999999999, "end": 539.9399999999999, "text": " That makes total sense.", "tokens": [50943, 663, 1669, 3217, 2020, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14120414040305398, "compression_ratio": 1.5594405594405594, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 52768, "start": 540.02, "end": 544.16, "text": " I mean, if gravity only worked when I looked at it through a specific magnifying glass,", "tokens": [50982, 286, 914, 11, 498, 12110, 787, 2732, 562, 286, 2956, 412, 309, 807, 257, 2685, 4944, 5489, 4276, 11, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14120414040305398, "compression_ratio": 1.5594405594405594, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 52768, "start": 544.3, "end": 545.8199999999999, "text": " we wouldn't call it a fundamental force.", "tokens": [51196, 321, 2759, 380, 818, 309, 257, 8088, 3464, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14120414040305398, "compression_ratio": 1.5594405594405594, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 52768, "start": 545.9799999999999, "end": 546.4599999999999, "text": " Spot on.", "tokens": [51280, 19102, 322, 13, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14120414040305398, "compression_ratio": 1.5594405594405594, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 52768, "start": 546.68, "end": 548.8399999999999, "text": " And then there's the final step, the ultimate hurdle.", "tokens": [51315, 400, 550, 456, 311, 264, 2572, 1823, 11, 264, 9705, 47423, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14120414040305398, "compression_ratio": 1.5594405594405594, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 52768, "start": 549.18, "end": 550.9, "text": " Step four, it must be predictive.", "tokens": [51440, 5470, 1451, 11, 309, 1633, 312, 35521, 13, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14120414040305398, "compression_ratio": 1.5594405594405594, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 55090, "start": 550.9, "end": 558.0, "text": " The construct must actually improve prediction on held-out data, meaning data it wasn't trained on,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 7690, 1633, 767, 3470, 17630, 322, 5167, 12, 346, 1412, 11, 3620, 1412, 309, 2067, 380, 8895, 322, 11, 50720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15140103376828706, "compression_ratio": 1.6156583629893237, "no_speech_prob": 1.1378206319842543e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 55090, "start": 558.36, "end": 561.84, "text": " relative to the strongest established baseline already available.", "tokens": [50738, 4972, 281, 264, 16595, 7545, 20518, 1217, 2435, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15140103376828706, "compression_ratio": 1.6156583629893237, "no_speech_prob": 1.1378206319842543e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 55090, "start": 562.26, "end": 566.26, "text": " It has to beat the reigning champion, not just fit the data it was calibrated on.", "tokens": [50933, 467, 575, 281, 4224, 264, 319, 9676, 10971, 11, 406, 445, 3318, 264, 1412, 309, 390, 21583, 5468, 322, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15140103376828706, "compression_ratio": 1.6156583629893237, "no_speech_prob": 1.1378206319842543e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 55090, "start": 566.54, "end": 569.24, "text": " And this is where the discipline of this approach really shines.", "tokens": [51147, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 13635, 295, 341, 3109, 534, 28056, 13, 51282], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15140103376828706, "compression_ratio": 1.6156583629893237, "no_speech_prob": 1.1378206319842543e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 55090, "start": 569.86, "end": 576.12, "text": " Affliction makes a huge point of explaining why failing to require all four of these together is so dangerous.", "tokens": [51313, 12840, 75, 4105, 1669, 257, 2603, 935, 295, 13468, 983, 18223, 281, 3651, 439, 1451, 295, 613, 1214, 307, 370, 5795, 13, 51626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15140103376828706, "compression_ratio": 1.6156583629893237, "no_speech_prob": 1.1378206319842543e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 55090, "start": 576.8199999999999, "end": 578.22, "text": " What happens if you skip some?", "tokens": [51661, 708, 2314, 498, 291, 10023, 512, 30, 51731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15140103376828706, "compression_ratio": 1.6156583629893237, "no_speech_prob": 1.1378206319842543e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 57822, "start": 578.22, "end": 581.6600000000001, "text": " Well, the author carefully names the failure modes for each step.", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 264, 3793, 7500, 5288, 264, 7763, 14068, 337, 1184, 1823, 13, 50537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13031856597415983, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074979025503366e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 57822, "start": 582.0600000000001, "end": 586.64, "text": " For example, if you only require reconstructability, you can just take pure background noise,", "tokens": [50557, 1171, 1365, 11, 498, 291, 787, 3651, 31499, 2310, 11, 291, 393, 445, 747, 6075, 3678, 5658, 11, 50786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13031856597415983, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074979025503366e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 57822, "start": 587.12, "end": 588.96, "text": " apply a mathematical smoothing function,", "tokens": [50810, 3079, 257, 18894, 899, 6259, 571, 2445, 11, 50902], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13031856597415983, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074979025503366e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 57822, "start": 589.34, "end": 595.2, "text": " and produce a nice, wavy spatial field that looks like real data but means absolutely nothing.", "tokens": [50921, 293, 5258, 257, 1481, 11, 261, 15498, 23598, 2519, 300, 1542, 411, 957, 1412, 457, 1355, 3122, 1825, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13031856597415983, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074979025503366e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 57822, "start": 595.28, "end": 597.32, "text": " So you've successfully reconstructed nonsense.", "tokens": [51218, 407, 291, 600, 10727, 31499, 292, 14925, 13, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13031856597415983, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074979025503366e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 57822, "start": 597.72, "end": 598.1600000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51340, 7587, 13, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13031856597415983, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074979025503366e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 57822, "start": 598.44, "end": 602.1, "text": " And if you only require stability, well, the number five is perfectly stable.", "tokens": [51376, 400, 498, 291, 787, 3651, 11826, 11, 731, 11, 264, 1230, 1732, 307, 6239, 8351, 13, 51559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13031856597415983, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074979025503366e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 57822, "start": 602.32, "end": 602.58, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [51570, 4894, 13, 51583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13031856597415983, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074979025503366e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 57822, "start": 602.76, "end": 604.88, "text": " It never changes regardless of the zoom level.", "tokens": [51592, 467, 1128, 2962, 10060, 295, 264, 8863, 1496, 13, 51698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13031856597415983, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074979025503366e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 57822, "start": 605.32, "end": 607.5600000000001, "text": " But a constant is utterly uninformative.", "tokens": [51720, 583, 257, 5754, 307, 30251, 517, 37811, 1166, 13, 51832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13031856597415983, "compression_ratio": 1.6394984326018809, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074979025503366e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 60756, "start": 607.56, "end": 607.92, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17595869122129498, "compression_ratio": 1.4775280898876404, "no_speech_prob": 1.868605530724876e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 60756, "start": 608.1199999999999, "end": 611.16, "text": " Knowing everything equals five doesn't help me predict the weather.", "tokens": [50393, 25499, 1203, 6915, 1732, 1177, 380, 854, 385, 6069, 264, 5503, 13, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17595869122129498, "compression_ratio": 1.4775280898876404, "no_speech_prob": 1.868605530724876e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 60756, "start": 611.5, "end": 615.0, "text": " And what if you only require predictive improvement, isolated from the other three?", "tokens": [50562, 400, 437, 498, 291, 787, 3651, 35521, 10444, 11, 14621, 490, 264, 661, 1045, 30, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17595869122129498, "compression_ratio": 1.4775280898876404, "no_speech_prob": 1.868605530724876e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 60756, "start": 615.42, "end": 620.5799999999999, "text": " Then you are inviting the most common sin in modern data science, which is overfitting.", "tokens": [50758, 1396, 291, 366, 18202, 264, 881, 2689, 3343, 294, 4363, 1412, 3497, 11, 597, 307, 670, 69, 2414, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17595869122129498, "compression_ratio": 1.4775280898876404, "no_speech_prob": 1.868605530724876e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 60756, "start": 620.78, "end": 621.8, "text": " Ah, overfitting.", "tokens": [51026, 2438, 11, 670, 69, 2414, 13, 51077], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17595869122129498, "compression_ratio": 1.4775280898876404, "no_speech_prob": 1.868605530724876e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 62180, "start": 621.8, "end": 628.1999999999999, "text": " If you have enough free parameters, you can build a mathematical construct that perfectly predicts the data set it was built on.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 362, 1547, 1737, 9834, 11, 291, 393, 1322, 257, 18894, 7690, 300, 6239, 6069, 82, 264, 1412, 992, 309, 390, 3094, 322, 13, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1288135528564453, "compression_ratio": 1.5825242718446602, "no_speech_prob": 2.465815095512025e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 62180, "start": 628.4399999999999, "end": 633.8399999999999, "text": " But it fails miserably when applied to new, unseen data in the real world.", "tokens": [50697, 583, 309, 18199, 17725, 1188, 562, 6456, 281, 777, 11, 40608, 1412, 294, 264, 957, 1002, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1288135528564453, "compression_ratio": 1.5825242718446602, "no_speech_prob": 2.465815095512025e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 62180, "start": 634.0799999999999, "end": 642.04, "text": " It's like a financial model that perfectly predicts the stock market of 2024 because you built it in 2025 using 2024 data.", "tokens": [50979, 467, 311, 411, 257, 4669, 2316, 300, 6239, 6069, 82, 264, 4127, 2142, 295, 45237, 570, 291, 3094, 309, 294, 39209, 1228, 45237, 1412, 13, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1288135528564453, "compression_ratio": 1.5825242718446602, "no_speech_prob": 2.465815095512025e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 64204, "start": 642.04, "end": 645.52, "text": " But when you turn it on in 2025, it instantly goes bankrupt.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 562, 291, 1261, 309, 322, 294, 39209, 11, 309, 13518, 1709, 21780, 13, 50539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16368849235668517, "compression_ratio": 1.3550295857988166, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211924160237535e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 64204, "start": 645.8399999999999, "end": 649.0, "text": " You basically drew a bullseye around the arrow after you shot it.", "tokens": [50555, 509, 1936, 12804, 257, 4693, 405, 1200, 926, 264, 11610, 934, 291, 3347, 309, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16368849235668517, "compression_ratio": 1.3550295857988166, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211924160237535e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 64204, "start": 649.4399999999999, "end": 649.78, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50735, 48746, 736, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16368849235668517, "compression_ratio": 1.3550295857988166, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211924160237535e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 64204, "start": 649.9, "end": 653.4599999999999, "text": " Which actually brings up something in this first essay that I found remarkably disciplined.", "tokens": [50758, 3013, 767, 5607, 493, 746, 294, 341, 700, 16238, 300, 286, 1352, 37381, 40061, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16368849235668517, "compression_ratio": 1.3550295857988166, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211924160237535e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 65346, "start": 653.46, "end": 663.88, "text": " Before fliction even runs a single line of simulation code, before any data is collected, they publish a pre-registered interpretation scheme.", "tokens": [50365, 4546, 932, 4105, 754, 6676, 257, 2167, 1622, 295, 16575, 3089, 11, 949, 604, 1412, 307, 11087, 11, 436, 11374, 257, 659, 12, 3375, 1964, 292, 14174, 12232, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13094204266866047, "compression_ratio": 1.4770114942528736, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622733784403155e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 65346, "start": 663.9200000000001, "end": 665.12, "text": " Yes, figure one in the paper.", "tokens": [50888, 1079, 11, 2573, 472, 294, 264, 3035, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13094204266866047, "compression_ratio": 1.4770114942528736, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622733784403155e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 65346, "start": 665.38, "end": 669.1800000000001, "text": " They define exactly what success and exactly what failure will look like in advance.", "tokens": [50961, 814, 6964, 2293, 437, 2245, 293, 2293, 437, 7763, 486, 574, 411, 294, 7295, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13094204266866047, "compression_ratio": 1.4770114942528736, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622733784403155e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 66918, "start": 669.18, "end": 674.9599999999999, "text": " This is incredibly rare in exploratory physics, and it's a real testament to the intellectual honesty of the project.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 6252, 5892, 294, 24765, 4745, 10649, 11, 293, 309, 311, 257, 957, 35499, 281, 264, 12576, 26839, 295, 264, 1716, 13, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1169609482755366, "compression_ratio": 1.5763358778625953, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016168647061234e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 66918, "start": 675.4399999999999, "end": 683.0799999999999, "text": " Human beings, even highly trained scientists, have a profound psychological temptation to negotiate with their data after the fact.", "tokens": [50678, 10294, 8958, 11, 754, 5405, 8895, 7708, 11, 362, 257, 14382, 14346, 30423, 281, 21713, 365, 641, 1412, 934, 264, 1186, 13, 51060], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1169609482755366, "compression_ratio": 1.5763358778625953, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016168647061234e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 66918, "start": 683.4399999999999, "end": 684.16, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [51078, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1169609482755366, "compression_ratio": 1.5763358778625953, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016168647061234e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 66918, "start": 684.4, "end": 685.52, "text": " There's tenure on the line.", "tokens": [51126, 821, 311, 32256, 322, 264, 1622, 13, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1169609482755366, "compression_ratio": 1.5763358778625953, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016168647061234e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 66918, "start": 685.62, "end": 686.6999999999999, "text": " There are grants to win.", "tokens": [51187, 821, 366, 16101, 281, 1942, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1169609482755366, "compression_ratio": 1.5763358778625953, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016168647061234e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 66918, "start": 687.18, "end": 691.68, "text": " The pressure to torture the data until it shows a positive correlation must be immense.", "tokens": [51265, 440, 3321, 281, 20711, 264, 1412, 1826, 309, 3110, 257, 3353, 20009, 1633, 312, 22920, 13, 51490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1169609482755366, "compression_ratio": 1.5763358778625953, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016168647061234e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 66918, "start": 691.9, "end": 692.28, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51501, 467, 307, 13, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1169609482755366, "compression_ratio": 1.5763358778625953, "no_speech_prob": 1.5016168647061234e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 69228, "start": 692.28, "end": 701.56, "text": " If the data doesn't quite fit the theory, we tend to invent reasons why the anomaly actually proves the theory right, or we redefine our terms on the fly.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 1412, 1177, 380, 1596, 3318, 264, 5261, 11, 321, 3928, 281, 7962, 4112, 983, 264, 42737, 767, 25019, 264, 5261, 558, 11, 420, 321, 38818, 533, 527, 2115, 322, 264, 3603, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1302685578664144, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109919388079819e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 69228, "start": 701.74, "end": 705.18, "text": " Just tweak the definition of capacity a little bit until the chart goes up.", "tokens": [50838, 1449, 29879, 264, 7123, 295, 6042, 257, 707, 857, 1826, 264, 6927, 1709, 493, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1302685578664144, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109919388079819e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 69228, "start": 705.3199999999999, "end": 705.76, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51017, 7587, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1302685578664144, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109919388079819e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 69228, "start": 706.3399999999999, "end": 711.3, "text": " But by pre-registering the interpretation, Flixiana locks the goalposts in concrete.", "tokens": [51068, 583, 538, 659, 12, 3375, 1964, 278, 264, 14174, 11, 3235, 970, 8497, 20703, 264, 3387, 23744, 82, 294, 9859, 13, 51316], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1302685578664144, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109919388079819e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 69228, "start": 711.88, "end": 714.42, "text": " They explicitly define what a clean failure would be.", "tokens": [51345, 814, 20803, 6964, 437, 257, 2541, 7763, 576, 312, 13, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1302685578664144, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109919388079819e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 69228, "start": 714.8, "end": 715.3199999999999, "text": " What is it?", "tokens": [51491, 708, 307, 309, 30, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1302685578664144, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109919388079819e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 69228, "start": 715.3199999999999, "end": 719.88, "text": " A clean failure is a scenario where the fields are reconstructable, the coefficients are stable,", "tokens": [51517, 316, 2541, 7763, 307, 257, 9005, 689, 264, 7909, 366, 31499, 712, 11, 264, 31994, 366, 8351, 11, 51745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1302685578664144, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109919388079819e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 71988, "start": 719.88, "end": 722.9399999999999, "text": " but there is no predictive gain over the baseline.", "tokens": [50365, 457, 456, 307, 572, 35521, 6052, 670, 264, 20518, 13, 50518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16427845425075954, "compression_ratio": 1.583657587548638, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612929785829843e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 71988, "start": 723.4, "end": 726.38, "text": " If that happens, it means the new construct added nothing.", "tokens": [50541, 759, 300, 2314, 11, 309, 1355, 264, 777, 7690, 3869, 1825, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16427845425075954, "compression_ratio": 1.583657587548638, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612929785829843e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 71988, "start": 726.64, "end": 726.88, "text": " Period.", "tokens": [50703, 34976, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16427845425075954, "compression_ratio": 1.583657587548638, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612929785829843e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 71988, "start": 727.2, "end": 727.74, "text": " No spin.", "tokens": [50731, 883, 6060, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16427845425075954, "compression_ratio": 1.583657587548638, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612929785829843e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 71988, "start": 727.84, "end": 729.14, "text": " No moving the goalposts.", "tokens": [50763, 883, 2684, 264, 3387, 23744, 82, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16427845425075954, "compression_ratio": 1.583657587548638, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612929785829843e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 71988, "start": 729.2, "end": 733.8, "text": " So we have this philosophical crucible, this impenetrable four-step standard.", "tokens": [50831, 407, 321, 362, 341, 25066, 5140, 32128, 11, 341, 704, 268, 302, 424, 638, 1451, 12, 16792, 3832, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16427845425075954, "compression_ratio": 1.583657587548638, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612929785829843e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 71988, "start": 734.28, "end": 737.02, "text": " But, you know, a crucible is useless without something to put inside it.", "tokens": [51085, 583, 11, 291, 458, 11, 257, 5140, 32128, 307, 14115, 1553, 746, 281, 829, 1854, 309, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16427845425075954, "compression_ratio": 1.583657587548638, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612929785829843e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 71988, "start": 737.06, "end": 737.22, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51224, 1779, 13, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16427845425075954, "compression_ratio": 1.583657587548638, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612929785829843e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 71988, "start": 737.28, "end": 738.1, "text": " You need a test case.", "tokens": [51235, 509, 643, 257, 1500, 1389, 13, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16427845425075954, "compression_ratio": 1.583657587548638, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612929785829843e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 71988, "start": 738.28, "end": 742.12, "text": " To prove this standard actually works, Flixia needed to select a test case.", "tokens": [51285, 1407, 7081, 341, 3832, 767, 1985, 11, 3235, 970, 654, 2978, 281, 3048, 257, 1500, 1389, 13, 51477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16427845425075954, "compression_ratio": 1.583657587548638, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612929785829843e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 74212, "start": 742.12, "end": 745.28, "text": " And they picked an intentionally brutally hard one.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 436, 6183, 364, 22062, 48476, 1152, 472, 13, 50523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17409074531411226, "compression_ratio": 1.5667870036101084, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383366459674862e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 74212, "start": 745.84, "end": 750.04, "text": " They chose to test a proposed capacity transport dissipation framework.", "tokens": [50551, 814, 5111, 281, 1500, 257, 10348, 6042, 5495, 29544, 399, 8388, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17409074531411226, "compression_ratio": 1.5667870036101084, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383366459674862e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 74212, "start": 750.46, "end": 751.5600000000001, "text": " Try saying that three times fast.", "tokens": [50782, 6526, 1566, 300, 1045, 1413, 2370, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17409074531411226, "compression_ratio": 1.5667870036101084, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383366459674862e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 74212, "start": 751.66, "end": 752.18, "text": " I know, right?", "tokens": [50842, 286, 458, 11, 558, 30, 50868], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17409074531411226, "compression_ratio": 1.5667870036101084, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383366459674862e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 74212, "start": 753.02, "end": 756.52, "text": " It's inspired by something called RSVP field dynamics.", "tokens": [50910, 467, 311, 7547, 538, 746, 1219, 25855, 53, 47, 2519, 15679, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17409074531411226, "compression_ratio": 1.5667870036101084, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383366459674862e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 74212, "start": 756.92, "end": 763.84, "text": " And the system they chased to test it on is motility-induced phase separation in active Brownian particle systems.", "tokens": [51105, 400, 264, 1185, 436, 33091, 281, 1500, 309, 322, 307, 2184, 1140, 12, 471, 41209, 5574, 14634, 294, 4967, 8030, 952, 12359, 3652, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17409074531411226, "compression_ratio": 1.5667870036101084, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383366459674862e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 74212, "start": 764.16, "end": 764.48, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51467, 1033, 13, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17409074531411226, "compression_ratio": 1.5667870036101084, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383366459674862e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 74212, "start": 764.62, "end": 768.36, "text": " Let's break down the physical system here because it is fascinating in its own right.", "tokens": [51490, 961, 311, 1821, 760, 264, 4001, 1185, 510, 570, 309, 307, 10343, 294, 1080, 1065, 558, 13, 51677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17409074531411226, "compression_ratio": 1.5667870036101084, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383366459674862e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 76836, "start": 768.36, "end": 775.2, "text": " I'm really glad we are because motility-induced phase separation in active Brownian particles is just a wall of jargon.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 478, 534, 5404, 321, 366, 570, 2184, 1140, 12, 471, 41209, 5574, 14634, 294, 4967, 8030, 952, 10007, 307, 445, 257, 2929, 295, 15181, 10660, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481967163085938, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856374373235393e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 76836, "start": 775.82, "end": 779.66, "text": " But the physical concept is actually really intuitive once you visualize it.", "tokens": [50738, 583, 264, 4001, 3410, 307, 767, 534, 21769, 1564, 291, 23273, 309, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481967163085938, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856374373235393e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 76836, "start": 779.78, "end": 780.1800000000001, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [50936, 467, 307, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481967163085938, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856374373235393e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 76836, "start": 780.42, "end": 784.02, "text": " So imagine you're looking down at a flat two-dimensional table.", "tokens": [50968, 407, 3811, 291, 434, 1237, 760, 412, 257, 4962, 732, 12, 18759, 3199, 13, 51148], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481967163085938, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856374373235393e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 76836, "start": 784.74, "end": 788.26, "text": " On this table are thousands of little microscopic disks.", "tokens": [51184, 1282, 341, 3199, 366, 5383, 295, 707, 47897, 41617, 13, 51360], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481967163085938, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856374373235393e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 76836, "start": 788.5600000000001, "end": 788.82, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51375, 1033, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481967163085938, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856374373235393e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 76836, "start": 789.04, "end": 789.82, "text": " Got my table of disks.", "tokens": [51399, 5803, 452, 3199, 295, 41617, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481967163085938, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856374373235393e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 76836, "start": 790.1, "end": 793.86, "text": " Now, in standard Brownian motion, like dust particles floating in water,", "tokens": [51452, 823, 11, 294, 3832, 8030, 952, 5394, 11, 411, 8634, 10007, 12607, 294, 1281, 11, 51640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481967163085938, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856374373235393e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 76836, "start": 793.86, "end": 797.9200000000001, "text": " they just jiggle around randomly because water molecules are bumping into them.", "tokens": [51640, 436, 445, 361, 19694, 926, 16979, 570, 1281, 13093, 366, 9961, 278, 666, 552, 13, 51843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14481967163085938, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856374373235393e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 79792, "start": 797.92, "end": 798.9399999999999, "text": " They are passive.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 366, 14975, 13, 50416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17893322369524542, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507011264665691e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 79792, "start": 799.4599999999999, "end": 801.0999999999999, "text": " But these disks are active.", "tokens": [50442, 583, 613, 41617, 366, 4967, 13, 50524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17893322369524542, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507011264665691e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 79792, "start": 801.26, "end": 803.04, "text": " Active meaning they move on their own?", "tokens": [50532, 26635, 3620, 436, 1286, 322, 641, 1065, 30, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17893322369524542, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507011264665691e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 79792, "start": 803.0999999999999, "end": 803.3399999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50624, 1079, 13, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17893322369524542, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507011264665691e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 79792, "start": 803.8, "end": 805.3399999999999, "text": " They have their own internal propulsion.", "tokens": [50659, 814, 362, 641, 1065, 6920, 49375, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17893322369524542, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507011264665691e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 79792, "start": 805.52, "end": 808.4399999999999, "text": " They're constantly pushing themselves forward at a constant speed.", "tokens": [50745, 814, 434, 6460, 7380, 2969, 2128, 412, 257, 5754, 3073, 13, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17893322369524542, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507011264665691e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 79792, "start": 808.9, "end": 813.4799999999999, "text": " Think of them like tiny microscopic bumper cars where the gas pedal is permanently stuck down.", "tokens": [50914, 6557, 295, 552, 411, 5870, 47897, 23992, 5163, 689, 264, 4211, 19122, 307, 24042, 5541, 760, 13, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17893322369524542, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507011264665691e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 79792, "start": 813.64, "end": 815.3399999999999, "text": " So they're constantly driving forward.", "tokens": [51151, 407, 436, 434, 6460, 4840, 2128, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17893322369524542, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507011264665691e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 79792, "start": 815.86, "end": 817.38, "text": " And they can't overlap, right?", "tokens": [51262, 400, 436, 393, 380, 19959, 11, 558, 30, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17893322369524542, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507011264665691e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 79792, "start": 817.4799999999999, "end": 819.0, "text": " Like they can't drive through each other.", "tokens": [51343, 1743, 436, 393, 380, 3332, 807, 1184, 661, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17893322369524542, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507011264665691e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 79792, "start": 819.18, "end": 819.5, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51428, 12753, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17893322369524542, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507011264665691e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 79792, "start": 819.5, "end": 826.0, "text": " The simulation uses something called a Weeks-Chandler-Anderson, or WCA, repulsive potential.", "tokens": [51444, 440, 16575, 4960, 746, 1219, 257, 12615, 82, 12, 34, 5543, 1918, 12, 5289, 3953, 11, 420, 343, 15515, 11, 1085, 32657, 3995, 13, 51769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17893322369524542, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.3507011264665691e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 82600, "start": 826.0, "end": 828.3, "text": " Okay, I won't ask you to explain the math on that.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 286, 1582, 380, 1029, 291, 281, 2903, 264, 5221, 322, 300, 13, 50480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11081591154399671, "compression_ratio": 1.6016949152542372, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 82600, "start": 828.38, "end": 829.68, "text": " You don't need to worry about the math of it.", "tokens": [50484, 509, 500, 380, 643, 281, 3292, 466, 264, 5221, 295, 309, 13, 50549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11081591154399671, "compression_ratio": 1.6016949152542372, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 82600, "start": 830.08, "end": 836.28, "text": " Just think of it as a very stiff microscopic spring wrapped around each bumper car.", "tokens": [50569, 1449, 519, 295, 309, 382, 257, 588, 15451, 47897, 5587, 14226, 926, 1184, 23992, 1032, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11081591154399671, "compression_ratio": 1.6016949152542372, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 82600, "start": 836.98, "end": 841.28, "text": " If they get too close to each other, the spring violently pushes them apart.", "tokens": [50914, 759, 436, 483, 886, 1998, 281, 1184, 661, 11, 264, 5587, 46728, 21020, 552, 4936, 13, 51129], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11081591154399671, "compression_ratio": 1.6016949152542372, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 82600, "start": 841.74, "end": 848.06, "text": " Okay, so we have thousands of tiny bumper cars all driving forward constantly and bouncing off each other.", "tokens": [51152, 1033, 11, 370, 321, 362, 5383, 295, 5870, 23992, 5163, 439, 4840, 2128, 6460, 293, 27380, 766, 1184, 661, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11081591154399671, "compression_ratio": 1.6016949152542372, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 82600, "start": 848.16, "end": 848.68, "text": " What happens?", "tokens": [51473, 708, 2314, 30, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11081591154399671, "compression_ratio": 1.6016949152542372, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310985986005665e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 84868, "start": 848.68, "end": 855.3599999999999, "text": " At low densities, when there's plenty of open space on the table, they just zoom around, occasionally bouncing off one another.", "tokens": [50365, 1711, 2295, 24505, 1088, 11, 562, 456, 311, 7140, 295, 1269, 1901, 322, 264, 3199, 11, 436, 445, 8863, 926, 11, 16895, 27380, 766, 472, 1071, 13, 50699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11593873412520797, "compression_ratio": 1.5693950177935942, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349412921932594e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 84868, "start": 855.9599999999999, "end": 856.6999999999999, "text": " They act like a gas.", "tokens": [50729, 814, 605, 411, 257, 4211, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11593873412520797, "compression_ratio": 1.5693950177935942, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349412921932594e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 84868, "start": 856.7199999999999, "end": 857.8199999999999, "text": " Just free-flowing.", "tokens": [50767, 1449, 1737, 12, 43955, 13, 50822], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11593873412520797, "compression_ratio": 1.5693950177935942, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349412921932594e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 84868, "start": 858.3199999999999, "end": 863.38, "text": " But if you pack enough of them onto the table and they are driving fast enough, something remarkable happens.", "tokens": [50847, 583, 498, 291, 2844, 1547, 295, 552, 3911, 264, 3199, 293, 436, 366, 4840, 2370, 1547, 11, 746, 12802, 2314, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11593873412520797, "compression_ratio": 1.5693950177935942, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349412921932594e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 84868, "start": 863.92, "end": 869.42, "text": " When two particles collide head-on, they get temporarily stuck, pushing against each other's repulsive springs.", "tokens": [51127, 1133, 732, 10007, 49093, 1378, 12, 266, 11, 436, 483, 23750, 5541, 11, 7380, 1970, 1184, 661, 311, 1085, 32657, 24647, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11593873412520797, "compression_ratio": 1.5693950177935942, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349412921932594e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 84868, "start": 869.66, "end": 871.4, "text": " Right, because their gas pedals are stuck.", "tokens": [51414, 1779, 11, 570, 641, 4211, 35217, 366, 5541, 13, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11593873412520797, "compression_ratio": 1.5693950177935942, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349412921932594e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 84868, "start": 871.52, "end": 871.8599999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51507, 7587, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11593873412520797, "compression_ratio": 1.5693950177935942, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349412921932594e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 87186, "start": 871.86, "end": 879.08, "text": " And because they are packed so densely, before they can slide past one another, a third particle crashes into them, then a fourth.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 570, 436, 366, 13265, 370, 24505, 736, 11, 949, 436, 393, 4137, 1791, 472, 1071, 11, 257, 2636, 12359, 28642, 666, 552, 11, 550, 257, 6409, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11254602862942603, "compression_ratio": 1.611842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437458390262337e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 87186, "start": 879.44, "end": 880.34, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [50744, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11254602862942603, "compression_ratio": 1.611842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437458390262337e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 87186, "start": 880.5, "end": 881.62, "text": " It's a traffic jam.", "tokens": [50797, 467, 311, 257, 6419, 7872, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11254602862942603, "compression_ratio": 1.611842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437458390262337e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 87186, "start": 881.72, "end": 884.34, "text": " A spontaneous, self-reinforcing traffic jam.", "tokens": [50858, 316, 32744, 11, 2698, 12, 265, 259, 2994, 2175, 6419, 7872, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11254602862942603, "compression_ratio": 1.611842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437458390262337e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 87186, "start": 885.12, "end": 891.0, "text": " Even though there are absolutely no attractive forces that don't want to stick together, they actually repel each other.", "tokens": [51028, 2754, 1673, 456, 366, 3122, 572, 12609, 5874, 300, 500, 380, 528, 281, 2897, 1214, 11, 436, 767, 1085, 338, 1184, 661, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11254602862942603, "compression_ratio": 1.611842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437458390262337e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 87186, "start": 891.72, "end": 897.9, "text": " Their constant forward drive causes them to clump together into massive, dense, solid-like clusters.", "tokens": [51358, 6710, 5754, 2128, 3332, 7700, 552, 281, 596, 1420, 1214, 666, 5994, 11, 18011, 11, 5100, 12, 4092, 23313, 13, 51667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11254602862942603, "compression_ratio": 1.611842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437458390262337e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 87186, "start": 898.1, "end": 900.74, "text": " Leaving all these large, empty voids in between them, I assume.", "tokens": [51677, 41253, 439, 613, 2416, 11, 6707, 1650, 3742, 294, 1296, 552, 11, 286, 6552, 13, 51809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11254602862942603, "compression_ratio": 1.611842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437458390262337e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 90074, "start": 900.74, "end": 906.2, "text": " Yes, and this spontaneous clumping is motility-induced phase separation, or MIPS.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 293, 341, 32744, 596, 35313, 307, 2184, 1140, 12, 471, 41209, 5574, 14634, 11, 420, 13696, 6273, 13, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11520540714263916, "compression_ratio": 1.5862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040570122848654e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 90074, "start": 906.74, "end": 912.9, "text": " It's a phase transition from a fluid-like state to a clustered state, driven entirely by their stubborn activity.", "tokens": [50665, 467, 311, 257, 5574, 6034, 490, 257, 9113, 12, 4092, 1785, 281, 257, 596, 38624, 1785, 11, 9555, 7696, 538, 641, 24137, 5191, 13, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11520540714263916, "compression_ratio": 1.5862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040570122848654e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 90074, "start": 913.0, "end": 913.36, "text": " It's amazing.", "tokens": [50978, 467, 311, 2243, 13, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11520540714263916, "compression_ratio": 1.5862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040570122848654e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 90074, "start": 913.46, "end": 917.8, "text": " It's order arising from chaos, just because everyone is trying to move forward at the same time.", "tokens": [51001, 467, 311, 1668, 44900, 490, 14158, 11, 445, 570, 1518, 307, 1382, 281, 1286, 2128, 412, 264, 912, 565, 13, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11520540714263916, "compression_ratio": 1.5862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040570122848654e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 90074, "start": 917.9, "end": 918.26, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51223, 7587, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11520540714263916, "compression_ratio": 1.5862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040570122848654e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 90074, "start": 918.48, "end": 925.54, "text": " So, Fliction is taking this proposed capacity framework and trying to use it to predict when and where these traffic jams are going to happen.", "tokens": [51252, 407, 11, 3235, 4105, 307, 1940, 341, 10348, 6042, 8388, 293, 1382, 281, 764, 309, 281, 6069, 562, 293, 689, 613, 6419, 361, 4070, 366, 516, 281, 1051, 13, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11520540714263916, "compression_ratio": 1.5862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040570122848654e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 90074, "start": 926.2, "end": 927.46, "text": " But here's my question.", "tokens": [51638, 583, 510, 311, 452, 1168, 13, 51701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11520540714263916, "compression_ratio": 1.5862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040570122848654e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 90074, "start": 927.92, "end": 929.2, "text": " Why choose this system?", "tokens": [51724, 1545, 2826, 341, 1185, 30, 51788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11520540714263916, "compression_ratio": 1.5862068965517242, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040570122848654e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 92920, "start": 929.2, "end": 932.24, "text": " MIPS is already super well understood, right?", "tokens": [50365, 13696, 6273, 307, 1217, 1687, 731, 7320, 11, 558, 30, 50517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17147526533707327, "compression_ratio": 1.5278969957081545, "no_speech_prob": 1.513030152555661e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 92920, "start": 932.32, "end": 933.34, "text": " We have kinetic theories.", "tokens": [50521, 492, 362, 27135, 13667, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17147526533707327, "compression_ratio": 1.5278969957081545, "no_speech_prob": 1.513030152555661e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 92920, "start": 933.5200000000001, "end": 936.76, "text": " We have hydrodynamic theories that explain the phase separation pretty well.", "tokens": [50581, 492, 362, 5796, 11452, 5216, 299, 13667, 300, 2903, 264, 5574, 14634, 1238, 731, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17147526533707327, "compression_ratio": 1.5278969957081545, "no_speech_prob": 1.513030152555661e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 92920, "start": 936.88, "end": 937.58, "text": " We do, yes.", "tokens": [50749, 492, 360, 11, 2086, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17147526533707327, "compression_ratio": 1.5278969957081545, "no_speech_prob": 1.513030152555661e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 92920, "start": 937.72, "end": 942.3000000000001, "text": " So, if you invent a fancy new theoretical construct, wouldn't you want to test it on a mystery?", "tokens": [50791, 407, 11, 498, 291, 7962, 257, 10247, 777, 20864, 7690, 11, 2759, 380, 291, 528, 281, 1500, 309, 322, 257, 11422, 30, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17147526533707327, "compression_ratio": 1.5278969957081545, "no_speech_prob": 1.513030152555661e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 92920, "start": 942.94, "end": 944.7, "text": " Somewhere we don't already know all the answers.", "tokens": [51052, 34500, 321, 500, 380, 1217, 458, 439, 264, 6338, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17147526533707327, "compression_ratio": 1.5278969957081545, "no_speech_prob": 1.513030152555661e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 92920, "start": 945.08, "end": 947.94, "text": " Your instinct is exactly what most researchers do.", "tokens": [51159, 2260, 16556, 307, 2293, 437, 881, 10309, 360, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17147526533707327, "compression_ratio": 1.5278969957081545, "no_speech_prob": 1.513030152555661e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 94794, "start": 947.94, "end": 955.74, "text": " They find an unexplained phenomenon, an explanatory vacuum, they apply their new theory, and when it somewhat fits the data, they claim victory.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 915, 364, 11572, 564, 3563, 14029, 11, 364, 9045, 4745, 14224, 11, 436, 3079, 641, 777, 5261, 11, 293, 562, 309, 8344, 9001, 264, 1412, 11, 436, 3932, 9812, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1311328382377165, "compression_ratio": 1.603960396039604, "no_speech_prob": 1.4099988537852326e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 94794, "start": 955.9000000000001, "end": 957.4200000000001, "text": " Because there's nothing to prove them wrong.", "tokens": [50763, 1436, 456, 311, 1825, 281, 7081, 552, 2085, 13, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1311328382377165, "compression_ratio": 1.603960396039604, "no_speech_prob": 1.4099988537852326e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 94794, "start": 957.5, "end": 957.7, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50843, 1779, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1311328382377165, "compression_ratio": 1.603960396039604, "no_speech_prob": 1.4099988537852326e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 94794, "start": 958.08, "end": 961.0400000000001, "text": " But Fliction points out the fatal flaw in that approach.", "tokens": [50872, 583, 3235, 4105, 2793, 484, 264, 24069, 13717, 294, 300, 3109, 13, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1311328382377165, "compression_ratio": 1.603960396039604, "no_speech_prob": 1.4099988537852326e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 94794, "start": 961.72, "end": 966.0400000000001, "text": " If you test a new theory in an explanatory vacuum, it wins by default.", "tokens": [51054, 759, 291, 1500, 257, 777, 5261, 294, 364, 9045, 4745, 14224, 11, 309, 10641, 538, 7576, 13, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1311328382377165, "compression_ratio": 1.603960396039604, "no_speech_prob": 1.4099988537852326e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 96604, "start": 966.04, "end": 973.4, "text": " That seems like a massive career risk on Fliction's part.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 2544, 411, 257, 5994, 3988, 3148, 322, 3235, 4105, 311, 644, 13, 50733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1664047891443426, "compression_ratio": 1.3333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4045040087548588e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 96604, "start": 973.54, "end": 978.7199999999999, "text": " I mean, most researchers wouldn't touch a system with a baseline that strong because you're almost guaranteeing a null result.", "tokens": [50740, 286, 914, 11, 881, 10309, 2759, 380, 2557, 257, 1185, 365, 257, 20518, 300, 2068, 570, 291, 434, 1920, 10815, 278, 257, 18184, 1874, 13, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1664047891443426, "compression_ratio": 1.3333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4045040087548588e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 97872, "start": 978.72, "end": 989.2, "text": " By choosing MIPS, where the conventional baseline theories are already incredibly accurate, they are subjecting this capacity vocabulary to a true, hard test.", "tokens": [50365, 3146, 10875, 13696, 6273, 11, 689, 264, 16011, 20518, 13667, 366, 1217, 6252, 8559, 11, 436, 366, 3983, 278, 341, 6042, 19864, 281, 257, 2074, 11, 1152, 1500, 13, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12552618257927173, "compression_ratio": 1.253968253968254, "no_speech_prob": 1.4210533791358948e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 98920, "start": 989.2, "end": 991.46, "text": " And that is precisely the point of the paper.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 300, 307, 13402, 264, 935, 295, 264, 3035, 13, 50478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09422602695701397, "compression_ratio": 1.7142857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619690649741226e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 98920, "start": 992.1, "end": 997.2, "text": " If the new capacity vocabulary adds nothing here, it is a definitive, informative failure.", "tokens": [50510, 759, 264, 777, 6042, 19864, 10860, 1825, 510, 11, 309, 307, 257, 28152, 11, 27759, 7763, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09422602695701397, "compression_ratio": 1.7142857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619690649741226e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 98920, "start": 997.6800000000001, "end": 999.4200000000001, "text": " We know it wasn't just a lack of data.", "tokens": [50789, 492, 458, 309, 2067, 380, 445, 257, 5011, 295, 1412, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09422602695701397, "compression_ratio": 1.7142857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619690649741226e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 98920, "start": 999.74, "end": 1005.98, "text": " It was that the construct itself didn't offer any new information that the existing density theories didn't already have.", "tokens": [50892, 467, 390, 300, 264, 7690, 2564, 994, 380, 2626, 604, 777, 1589, 300, 264, 6741, 10305, 13667, 994, 380, 1217, 362, 13, 51204], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09422602695701397, "compression_ratio": 1.7142857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619690649741226e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 98920, "start": 1006.26, "end": 1017.3000000000001, "text": " But, conversely, if it does add something here, if it manages to beat the reigning heavyweight champion of active matter physics, then it is a massive, undeniable, genuine discovery.", "tokens": [51218, 583, 11, 2615, 736, 11, 498, 309, 775, 909, 746, 510, 11, 498, 309, 22489, 281, 4224, 264, 319, 9676, 4676, 12329, 10971, 295, 4967, 1871, 10649, 11, 550, 309, 307, 257, 5994, 11, 674, 268, 9364, 11, 16699, 12114, 13, 51770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09422602695701397, "compression_ratio": 1.7142857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619690649741226e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 101730, "start": 1017.3, "end": 1023.52, "text": " And beyond just having strong baselines, there are mechanical reasons this simulation is the perfect testbed.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 4399, 445, 1419, 2068, 987, 9173, 11, 456, 366, 12070, 4112, 341, 16575, 307, 264, 2176, 1500, 2883, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18604461592857283, "compression_ratio": 1.576, "no_speech_prob": 2.4754319687819715e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 101730, "start": 1023.88, "end": 1026.8799999999999, "text": " First, the simulated trajectories are exact.", "tokens": [50694, 2386, 11, 264, 41713, 18257, 2083, 366, 1900, 13, 50844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18604461592857283, "compression_ratio": 1.576, "no_speech_prob": 2.4754319687819715e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 101730, "start": 1027.28, "end": 1028.84, "text": " There is no measurement noise.", "tokens": [50864, 821, 307, 572, 13160, 5658, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18604461592857283, "compression_ratio": 1.576, "no_speech_prob": 2.4754319687819715e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 101730, "start": 1029.08, "end": 1029.3, "text": " None.", "tokens": [50954, 14492, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18604461592857283, "compression_ratio": 1.576, "no_speech_prob": 2.4754319687819715e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 101730, "start": 1029.56, "end": 1029.76, "text": " Ball.", "tokens": [50978, 10744, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18604461592857283, "compression_ratio": 1.576, "no_speech_prob": 2.4754319687819715e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 101730, "start": 1029.82, "end": 1035.94, "text": " The computer knows the precise position and orientation of every single particle at every microsecond.", "tokens": [50991, 440, 3820, 3255, 264, 13600, 2535, 293, 14764, 295, 633, 2167, 12359, 412, 633, 3123, 37841, 18882, 13, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18604461592857283, "compression_ratio": 1.576, "no_speech_prob": 2.4754319687819715e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 101730, "start": 1036.24, "end": 1041.44, "text": " You can't blame a negative result on, like, faulty sensors or a dirty Petri dish.", "tokens": [51312, 509, 393, 380, 10127, 257, 3671, 1874, 322, 11, 411, 11, 2050, 5773, 14840, 420, 257, 9360, 10472, 470, 5025, 13, 51572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18604461592857283, "compression_ratio": 1.576, "no_speech_prob": 2.4754319687819715e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 101730, "start": 1041.5, "end": 1042.24, "text": " No excuses.", "tokens": [51575, 883, 24666, 13, 51612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18604461592857283, "compression_ratio": 1.576, "no_speech_prob": 2.4754319687819715e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 104224, "start": 1042.24, "end": 1049.2, "text": " And second, the phase transition itself, the clumping into traffic jams, is a genuine, objectively measurable event.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 1150, 11, 264, 5574, 6034, 2564, 11, 264, 596, 35313, 666, 6419, 361, 4070, 11, 307, 257, 16699, 11, 46067, 43615, 2280, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11316874532988577, "compression_ratio": 1.5592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 1.335452039750995e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 104224, "start": 1049.52, "end": 1053.2, "text": " You can define when a cluster has formed without ever mentioning the word capacity.", "tokens": [50729, 509, 393, 6964, 562, 257, 13630, 575, 8693, 1553, 1562, 18315, 264, 1349, 6042, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11316874532988577, "compression_ratio": 1.5592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 1.335452039750995e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 104224, "start": 1053.42, "end": 1054.04, "text": " Which is so important.", "tokens": [50924, 3013, 307, 370, 1021, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11316874532988577, "compression_ratio": 1.5592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 1.335452039750995e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 104224, "start": 1054.14, "end": 1059.24, "text": " The target variable doesn't know it's being used to test a new theory, which completely prevents circular reasoning.", "tokens": [50960, 440, 3779, 7006, 1177, 380, 458, 309, 311, 885, 1143, 281, 1500, 257, 777, 5261, 11, 597, 2584, 22367, 16476, 21577, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11316874532988577, "compression_ratio": 1.5592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 1.335452039750995e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 104224, "start": 1059.46, "end": 1059.84, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51226, 7587, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11316874532988577, "compression_ratio": 1.5592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 1.335452039750995e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 104224, "start": 1060.1200000000001, "end": 1061.94, "text": " Okay, so the test subject is chosen.", "tokens": [51259, 1033, 11, 370, 264, 1500, 3983, 307, 8614, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11316874532988577, "compression_ratio": 1.5592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 1.335452039750995e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 104224, "start": 1062.32, "end": 1063.8, "text": " The philosophical standard is set.", "tokens": [51369, 440, 25066, 3832, 307, 992, 13, 51443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11316874532988577, "compression_ratio": 1.5592592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 1.335452039750995e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 106380, "start": 1063.8, "end": 1073.6599999999999, "text": " Now, the actual empirical work begins, and this is where the paper gets really granular, really messy, and honestly really relatable for anyone who has ever tried to write code for a complex system.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 11, 264, 3539, 31886, 589, 7338, 11, 293, 341, 307, 689, 264, 3035, 2170, 534, 39962, 11, 534, 16191, 11, 293, 6095, 534, 42355, 337, 2878, 567, 575, 1562, 3031, 281, 2464, 3089, 337, 257, 3997, 1185, 13, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12820213668200434, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 2.380246390612517e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 106380, "start": 1073.9199999999998, "end": 1075.18, "text": " Oh, the debugging.", "tokens": [50871, 876, 11, 264, 45592, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12820213668200434, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 2.380246390612517e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 106380, "start": 1075.48, "end": 1079.1, "text": " Real science is about catching your own mistakes before they ruin your data.", "tokens": [50949, 8467, 3497, 307, 466, 16124, 428, 1065, 8038, 949, 436, 15514, 428, 1412, 13, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12820213668200434, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 2.380246390612517e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 106380, "start": 1079.7, "end": 1083.1599999999999, "text": " And Flinction documents these near-misses with total transparency.", "tokens": [51160, 400, 3235, 12987, 8512, 613, 2651, 12, 76, 40487, 365, 3217, 17131, 13, 51333], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12820213668200434, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 2.380246390612517e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 106380, "start": 1083.8, "end": 1087.08, "text": " It starts with how they handle the comparability step we talked about earlier.", "tokens": [51365, 467, 3719, 365, 577, 436, 4813, 264, 6311, 2310, 1823, 321, 2825, 466, 3071, 13, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12820213668200434, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 2.380246390612517e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 108708, "start": 1087.08, "end": 1089.9199999999998, "text": " They didn't just pick one definition of capacity.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 994, 380, 445, 1888, 472, 7123, 295, 6042, 13, 50507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15916373211404553, "compression_ratio": 1.6564625850340136, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305315608643566e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 108708, "start": 1090.12, "end": 1094.1799999999998, "text": " They built three competing operationalizations to test side by side.", "tokens": [50517, 814, 3094, 1045, 15439, 16607, 14455, 281, 1500, 1252, 538, 1252, 13, 50720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15916373211404553, "compression_ratio": 1.6564625850340136, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305315608643566e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 108708, "start": 1094.5, "end": 1100.4399999999998, "text": " Let's go through these, because it demystifies what a construct actually looks like when you force it into math.", "tokens": [50736, 961, 311, 352, 807, 613, 11, 570, 309, 1371, 38593, 11221, 437, 257, 7690, 767, 1542, 411, 562, 291, 3464, 309, 666, 5221, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15916373211404553, "compression_ratio": 1.6564625850340136, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305315608643566e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 108708, "start": 1100.6, "end": 1100.78, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51041, 1033, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15916373211404553, "compression_ratio": 1.6564625850340136, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305315608643566e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 108708, "start": 1100.96, "end": 1102.8999999999999, "text": " The first one is the imposed variant.", "tokens": [51059, 440, 700, 472, 307, 264, 26491, 17501, 13, 51156], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15916373211404553, "compression_ratio": 1.6564625850340136, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305315608643566e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 108708, "start": 1103.32, "end": 1108.1399999999999, "text": " This basically just treats capacity as the raw propulsion speed built into the particles.", "tokens": [51177, 639, 1936, 445, 19566, 6042, 382, 264, 8936, 49375, 3073, 3094, 666, 264, 10007, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15916373211404553, "compression_ratio": 1.6564625850340136, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305315608643566e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 108708, "start": 1108.4199999999998, "end": 1108.6399999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51432, 1779, 13, 51443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15916373211404553, "compression_ratio": 1.6564625850340136, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305315608643566e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 108708, "start": 1109.1, "end": 1115.22, "text": " But since all the particles in this specific model move at a constant speed, this is mostly a flat, uniform field.", "tokens": [51466, 583, 1670, 439, 264, 10007, 294, 341, 2685, 2316, 1286, 412, 257, 5754, 3073, 11, 341, 307, 5240, 257, 4962, 11, 9452, 2519, 13, 51772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15916373211404553, "compression_ratio": 1.6564625850340136, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305315608643566e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 111522, "start": 1115.22, "end": 1118.72, "text": " It's essentially a control group to make sure the software pipeline is working.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 4476, 257, 1969, 1594, 281, 652, 988, 264, 4722, 15517, 307, 1364, 13, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11859808849687335, "compression_ratio": 1.7269736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.1970965668392508e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 111522, "start": 1119.18, "end": 1119.54, "text": " Makes sense.", "tokens": [50563, 25245, 2020, 13, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11859808849687335, "compression_ratio": 1.7269736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.1970965668392508e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 111522, "start": 1119.92, "end": 1121.72, "text": " Then there's the signed-realized variant.", "tokens": [50600, 1396, 456, 311, 264, 8175, 12, 9342, 1602, 17501, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11859808849687335, "compression_ratio": 1.7269736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.1970965668392508e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 111522, "start": 1122.3, "end": 1124.98, "text": " This defines capacity as the active work being done.", "tokens": [50719, 639, 23122, 6042, 382, 264, 4967, 589, 885, 1096, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11859808849687335, "compression_ratio": 1.7269736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.1970965668392508e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 111522, "start": 1125.44, "end": 1132.2, "text": " It measures the alignment between the direction the particle wants to go, its internal propulsion direction, and the direction it is actually moving.", "tokens": [50876, 467, 8000, 264, 18515, 1296, 264, 3513, 264, 12359, 2738, 281, 352, 11, 1080, 6920, 49375, 3513, 11, 293, 264, 3513, 309, 307, 767, 2684, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11859808849687335, "compression_ratio": 1.7269736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.1970965668392508e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 111522, "start": 1132.54, "end": 1135.98, "text": " Because if it's trapped in the middle of a traffic jam, it wants to go forward.", "tokens": [51231, 1436, 498, 309, 311, 14994, 294, 264, 2808, 295, 257, 6419, 7872, 11, 309, 2738, 281, 352, 2128, 13, 51403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11859808849687335, "compression_ratio": 1.7269736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.1970965668392508e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 111522, "start": 1136.38, "end": 1142.2, "text": " But the crowd of particles might be physically pushing it backward, so this value can actually go negative.", "tokens": [51423, 583, 264, 6919, 295, 10007, 1062, 312, 9762, 7380, 309, 23897, 11, 370, 341, 2158, 393, 767, 352, 3671, 13, 51714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11859808849687335, "compression_ratio": 1.7269736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.1970965668392508e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 114220, "start": 1142.2, "end": 1149.42, "text": " Okay. And the third is the usable forward variant, which takes that same measurement, but throws away the negative numbers.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 400, 264, 2636, 307, 264, 29975, 2128, 17501, 11, 597, 2516, 300, 912, 13160, 11, 457, 19251, 1314, 264, 3671, 3547, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10565668741861979, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037752281402364e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 114220, "start": 1149.6200000000001, "end": 1152.92, "text": " It only counts realized propulsion in the forward direction.", "tokens": [50736, 467, 787, 14893, 5334, 49375, 294, 264, 2128, 3513, 13, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10565668741861979, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037752281402364e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 114220, "start": 1153.04, "end": 1160.5800000000002, "text": " Right. By running all three, fliction avoids the trap of just handpicking whichever one happens to work best after the fact.", "tokens": [50907, 1779, 13, 3146, 2614, 439, 1045, 11, 932, 4105, 3641, 3742, 264, 11487, 295, 445, 1011, 79, 10401, 24123, 472, 2314, 281, 589, 1151, 934, 264, 1186, 13, 51284], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10565668741861979, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037752281402364e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 114220, "start": 1160.72, "end": 1165.8600000000001, "text": " But before they could even measure these things, the simulation engine itself nearly blew up.", "tokens": [51291, 583, 949, 436, 727, 754, 3481, 613, 721, 11, 264, 16575, 2848, 2564, 6217, 19075, 493, 13, 51548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10565668741861979, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037752281402364e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 114220, "start": 1166.24, "end": 1168.4, "text": " Literally, mathematically blew up.", "tokens": [51567, 23768, 11, 44003, 19075, 493, 13, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10565668741861979, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037752281402364e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 114220, "start": 1168.46, "end": 1169.7, "text": " Yes, the force explosion.", "tokens": [51678, 1079, 11, 264, 3464, 15673, 13, 51740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10565668741861979, "compression_ratio": 1.6223776223776223, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037752281402364e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 116970, "start": 1169.7, "end": 1174.96, "text": " They document this in the paper, and it is a fascinating look under the hood of computational physics.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 4166, 341, 294, 264, 3035, 11, 293, 309, 307, 257, 10343, 574, 833, 264, 13376, 295, 28270, 10649, 13, 50628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0718451976776123, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068105183729807e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 116970, "start": 1175.6000000000001, "end": 1185.04, "text": " They were using a standard mathematical method called Euler-Mariyama to calculate how the particles move based on those microscopic repulsive springs we talked about earlier.", "tokens": [50660, 814, 645, 1228, 257, 3832, 18894, 3170, 1219, 462, 26318, 12, 44, 3504, 88, 2404, 281, 8873, 577, 264, 10007, 1286, 2361, 322, 729, 47897, 1085, 32657, 24647, 321, 2825, 466, 3071, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0718451976776123, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068105183729807e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 116970, "start": 1185.26, "end": 1191.9, "text": " And to understand why this is tricky, you have to realize that computers can't simulate continuous flowing time.", "tokens": [51143, 400, 281, 1223, 983, 341, 307, 12414, 11, 291, 362, 281, 4325, 300, 10807, 393, 380, 27817, 10957, 13974, 565, 13, 51475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0718451976776123, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068105183729807e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 116970, "start": 1192.32, "end": 1197.04, "text": " They have to chop time up into tiny, discrete frames like a movie reel.", "tokens": [51496, 814, 362, 281, 7931, 565, 493, 666, 5870, 11, 27706, 12083, 411, 257, 3169, 34973, 13, 51732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0718451976776123, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.5068105183729807e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 119704, "start": 1197.04, "end": 1205.1599999999999, "text": " The Euler-Mariyama method calculates the forces in frame one, moves the particles a tiny bit based on those forces, and then calculates frame two.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 462, 26318, 12, 44, 3504, 88, 2404, 3170, 4322, 1024, 264, 5874, 294, 3920, 472, 11, 6067, 264, 10007, 257, 5870, 857, 2361, 322, 729, 5874, 11, 293, 550, 4322, 1024, 3920, 732, 13, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060443878173828125, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.54914742058615e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 119704, "start": 1205.7, "end": 1211.62, "text": " And for 38,000 steps, everything looked totally fine, which is an eternity in computational time.", "tokens": [50798, 400, 337, 12843, 11, 1360, 4439, 11, 1203, 2956, 3879, 2489, 11, 597, 307, 364, 27162, 294, 28270, 565, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060443878173828125, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.54914742058615e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 119704, "start": 1212.1399999999999, "end": 1220.1599999999999, "text": " I mean, a lot of people would run a quick 5,000-step validation, see that the particles are moving normally, and just go home for the weekend while the main simulation runs.", "tokens": [51120, 286, 914, 11, 257, 688, 295, 561, 576, 1190, 257, 1702, 1025, 11, 1360, 12, 16792, 24071, 11, 536, 300, 264, 10007, 366, 2684, 5646, 11, 293, 445, 352, 1280, 337, 264, 6711, 1339, 264, 2135, 16575, 6676, 13, 51521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060443878173828125, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.54914742058615e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 122016, "start": 1220.16, "end": 1222.8600000000001, "text": " But fliction let the validation run longer.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 932, 4105, 718, 264, 24071, 1190, 2854, 13, 50500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2854876310929008, "compression_ratio": 1.2993197278911566, "no_speech_prob": 1.536523512590815e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 122016, "start": 1223.78, "end": 1229.96, "text": " And suddenly, at step 38,000-something, the simulation encountered a catastrophic failure.", "tokens": [50546, 400, 5800, 11, 412, 1823, 12843, 11, 1360, 12, 31681, 11, 264, 16575, 20381, 257, 34915, 7763, 13, 50855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2854876310929008, "compression_ratio": 1.2993197278911566, "no_speech_prob": 1.536523512590815e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 122016, "start": 1230.0400000000002, "end": 1230.52, "text": " Bad.", "tokens": [50859, 11523, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2854876310929008, "compression_ratio": 1.2993197278911566, "no_speech_prob": 1.536523512590815e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 122016, "start": 1231.38, "end": 1234.16, "text": " Remember those extremely stiff microscopic springs?", "tokens": [50926, 5459, 729, 4664, 15451, 47897, 24647, 30, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2854876310929008, "compression_ratio": 1.2993197278911566, "no_speech_prob": 1.536523512590815e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 123416, "start": 1234.16, "end": 1245.14, "text": " If the simulation takes a time step that is just slightly too large, a bumper car might essentially teleport slightly inside the physical barrier of another bumper car in a single frame.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 16575, 2516, 257, 565, 1823, 300, 307, 445, 4748, 886, 2416, 11, 257, 23992, 1032, 1062, 4476, 28050, 4748, 1854, 264, 4001, 13357, 295, 1071, 23992, 1032, 294, 257, 2167, 3920, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07941102981567383, "compression_ratio": 1.609442060085837, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830370426658027e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 123416, "start": 1245.4, "end": 1252.42, "text": " Like a video game glitch where your character accidentally steps halfway inside a solid wall, and the game's physics engine completely panics.", "tokens": [50927, 1743, 257, 960, 1216, 23552, 689, 428, 2517, 15715, 4439, 15461, 1854, 257, 5100, 2929, 11, 293, 264, 1216, 311, 10649, 2848, 2584, 2462, 1167, 13, 51278], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07941102981567383, "compression_ratio": 1.609442060085837, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830370426658027e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 123416, "start": 1252.5800000000002, "end": 1254.2, "text": " That is exactly what happened mathematically.", "tokens": [51286, 663, 307, 2293, 437, 2011, 44003, 13, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07941102981567383, "compression_ratio": 1.609442060085837, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830370426658027e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 125420, "start": 1254.2, "end": 1261.3, "text": " The distance between the particles became so small that the equation for the repulsive spring returned an astronomically massive number.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4560, 1296, 264, 10007, 3062, 370, 1359, 300, 264, 5367, 337, 264, 1085, 32657, 5587, 8752, 364, 26302, 984, 5994, 1230, 13, 50720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09513868719844495, "compression_ratio": 1.7210884353741496, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995425911933479e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 125420, "start": 1261.8600000000001, "end": 1265.22, "text": " The force magnitude exploded to 4 times 10 to the 10th power.", "tokens": [50748, 440, 3464, 15668, 27049, 281, 1017, 1413, 1266, 281, 264, 1266, 392, 1347, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09513868719844495, "compression_ratio": 1.7210884353741496, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995425911933479e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 125420, "start": 1265.5800000000002, "end": 1267.74, "text": " Wow. 4 times 10 to the 10th.", "tokens": [50934, 3153, 13, 1017, 1413, 1266, 281, 264, 1266, 392, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09513868719844495, "compression_ratio": 1.7210884353741496, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995425911933479e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 125420, "start": 1267.76, "end": 1268.0, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51043, 1079, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09513868719844495, "compression_ratio": 1.7210884353741496, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995425911933479e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 125420, "start": 1268.46, "end": 1275.66, "text": " A completely non-physical force that would launch the particle out of the solar system, basically shattering the entire simulation.", "tokens": [51078, 316, 2584, 2107, 12, 950, 36280, 3464, 300, 576, 4025, 264, 12359, 484, 295, 264, 7936, 1185, 11, 1936, 402, 14849, 264, 2302, 16575, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09513868719844495, "compression_ratio": 1.7210884353741496, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995425911933479e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 125420, "start": 1275.8400000000001, "end": 1282.4, "text": " And the reason this is detailed in the paper is to show that the safe time step for this specific setup isn't just based on the static rules.", "tokens": [51447, 400, 264, 1778, 341, 307, 9942, 294, 264, 3035, 307, 281, 855, 300, 264, 3273, 565, 1823, 337, 341, 2685, 8657, 1943, 380, 445, 2361, 322, 264, 13437, 4474, 13, 51775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09513868719844495, "compression_ratio": 1.7210884353741496, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995425911933479e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 128240, "start": 1282.4, "end": 1286.1000000000001, "text": " It depends heavily on the propulsion speed and the thermal diffusion.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 5946, 10950, 322, 264, 49375, 3073, 293, 264, 15070, 25242, 13, 50550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11987634138627486, "compression_ratio": 1.5815602836879432, "no_speech_prob": 1.5798396662061731e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 128240, "start": 1286.3000000000002, "end": 1286.8600000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50560, 7587, 13, 50588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11987634138627486, "compression_ratio": 1.5815602836879432, "no_speech_prob": 1.5798396662061731e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 128240, "start": 1287.52, "end": 1293.5800000000002, "text": " Flicksten had to drop the time step down to 10 to the negative 4, an incredibly fine resolution.", "tokens": [50621, 3235, 618, 6266, 632, 281, 3270, 264, 565, 1823, 760, 281, 1266, 281, 264, 3671, 1017, 11, 364, 6252, 2489, 8669, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11987634138627486, "compression_ratio": 1.5815602836879432, "no_speech_prob": 1.5798396662061731e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 128240, "start": 1294.02, "end": 1298.5800000000002, "text": " And they actually built a permanent, hard-coded diagnostic into the engine, right?", "tokens": [50946, 400, 436, 767, 3094, 257, 10996, 11, 1152, 12, 66, 12340, 27897, 666, 264, 2848, 11, 558, 30, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11987634138627486, "compression_ratio": 1.5815602836879432, "no_speech_prob": 1.5798396662061731e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 128240, "start": 1299.14, "end": 1309.2, "text": " Like, if the forces ever exceeded a specific threshold, the simulation would intentionally crash and throw an error message, rather than quietly writing garbage data into the output file.", "tokens": [51202, 1743, 11, 498, 264, 5874, 1562, 38026, 257, 2685, 14678, 11, 264, 16575, 576, 22062, 8252, 293, 3507, 364, 6713, 3636, 11, 2831, 813, 19141, 3579, 14150, 1412, 666, 264, 5598, 3991, 13, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11987634138627486, "compression_ratio": 1.5815602836879432, "no_speech_prob": 1.5798396662061731e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 130920, "start": 1309.2, "end": 1311.3600000000001, "text": " Which is a cardinal rule of scientific computing.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 307, 257, 2920, 2071, 4978, 295, 8134, 15866, 13, 50473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16705860103572812, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944961461020876e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 130920, "start": 1311.68, "end": 1313.22, "text": " Never trust silent failures.", "tokens": [50489, 7344, 3361, 12784, 20774, 13, 50566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16705860103572812, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944961461020876e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 130920, "start": 1313.38, "end": 1316.1200000000001, "text": " You want your code to scream at you if physics is violated.", "tokens": [50574, 509, 528, 428, 3089, 281, 7291, 412, 291, 498, 10649, 307, 33239, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16705860103572812, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944961461020876e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 130920, "start": 1316.18, "end": 1316.42, "text": " Seriously.", "tokens": [50714, 14063, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16705860103572812, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944961461020876e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 130920, "start": 1316.56, "end": 1319.16, "text": " But the most terrifying near-miss wasn't even the force explosion.", "tokens": [50733, 583, 264, 881, 18106, 2651, 12, 76, 891, 2067, 380, 754, 264, 3464, 15673, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16705860103572812, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944961461020876e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 130920, "start": 1319.3, "end": 1320.6200000000001, "text": " It was the F-max artifact.", "tokens": [50870, 467, 390, 264, 479, 12, 41167, 34806, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16705860103572812, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944961461020876e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 130920, "start": 1320.98, "end": 1321.5, "text": " Ah, yes.", "tokens": [50954, 2438, 11, 2086, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16705860103572812, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944961461020876e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 130920, "start": 1322.14, "end": 1323.48, "text": " The F-max artifact.", "tokens": [51012, 440, 479, 12, 41167, 34806, 13, 51079], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16705860103572812, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944961461020876e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 130920, "start": 1324.02, "end": 1326.6000000000001, "text": " This is the elevator analogy from the beginning of the show.", "tokens": [51106, 639, 307, 264, 18782, 21663, 490, 264, 2863, 295, 264, 855, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16705860103572812, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944961461020876e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 130920, "start": 1326.96, "end": 1330.64, "text": " It is a master class in why you must validate your target variables.", "tokens": [51253, 467, 307, 257, 4505, 1508, 294, 983, 291, 1633, 29562, 428, 3779, 9102, 13, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16705860103572812, "compression_ratio": 1.5642023346303502, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944961461020876e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 133064, "start": 1330.64, "end": 1335.74, "text": " So, remember, the goal is to predict when the particles clump up, when they undergo phase separation.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 1604, 11, 264, 3387, 307, 281, 6069, 562, 264, 10007, 596, 1420, 493, 11, 562, 436, 26426, 5574, 14634, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11959159068572216, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924089284141134e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 133064, "start": 1336.24, "end": 1343.2800000000002, "text": " The most obvious standard way to measure this in the literature is to calculate the fraction of particles that are physically touching each other.", "tokens": [50645, 440, 881, 6322, 3832, 636, 281, 3481, 341, 294, 264, 10394, 307, 281, 8873, 264, 14135, 295, 10007, 300, 366, 9762, 11175, 1184, 661, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11959159068572216, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924089284141134e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 133064, "start": 1343.3600000000001, "end": 1346.74, "text": " They call this metric F-max, the particle contact cluster fraction.", "tokens": [51001, 814, 818, 341, 20678, 479, 12, 41167, 11, 264, 12359, 3385, 13630, 14135, 13, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11959159068572216, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924089284141134e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 133064, "start": 1346.8200000000002, "end": 1347.0200000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51174, 1779, 13, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11959159068572216, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924089284141134e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 133064, "start": 1347.24, "end": 1350.7800000000002, "text": " So if F-max is a high number, you have a massive traffic jam.", "tokens": [51195, 407, 498, 479, 12, 41167, 307, 257, 1090, 1230, 11, 291, 362, 257, 5994, 6419, 7872, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11959159068572216, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924089284141134e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 133064, "start": 1350.96, "end": 1352.96, "text": " If it's low, they are flying free.", "tokens": [51381, 759, 309, 311, 2295, 11, 436, 366, 7137, 1737, 13, 51481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11959159068572216, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924089284141134e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 133064, "start": 1353.0600000000002, "end": 1354.1000000000001, "text": " Makes total sense.", "tokens": [51486, 25245, 3217, 2020, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11959159068572216, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924089284141134e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 133064, "start": 1354.3000000000002, "end": 1355.38, "text": " It sounds perfectly logical.", "tokens": [51548, 467, 3263, 6239, 14978, 13, 51602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11959159068572216, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924089284141134e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 135538, "start": 1355.38, "end": 1358.1000000000001, "text": " Until you actually test it at high densities.", "tokens": [50365, 9088, 291, 767, 1500, 309, 412, 1090, 24505, 1088, 13, 50501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15215063931649192, "compression_ratio": 1.5795053003533568, "no_speech_prob": 1.340673448993468e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 135538, "start": 1358.66, "end": 1366.68, "text": " Fliction set up a simulation with a very high packing fraction, meaning the table is incredibly crowded with particles right from the start.", "tokens": [50529, 3235, 4105, 992, 493, 257, 16575, 365, 257, 588, 1090, 20815, 14135, 11, 3620, 264, 3199, 307, 6252, 21634, 365, 10007, 558, 490, 264, 722, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15215063931649192, "compression_ratio": 1.5795053003533568, "no_speech_prob": 1.340673448993468e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 135538, "start": 1366.8000000000002, "end": 1368.22, "text": " Okay, so a very crowded room.", "tokens": [50936, 1033, 11, 370, 257, 588, 21634, 1808, 13, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15215063931649192, "compression_ratio": 1.5795053003533568, "no_speech_prob": 1.340673448993468e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 135538, "start": 1368.5400000000002, "end": 1376.92, "text": " They hit start, and at time equals zero, before a single particle is even moved, the F-max metric read exactly 1.000.", "tokens": [51023, 814, 2045, 722, 11, 293, 412, 565, 6915, 4018, 11, 949, 257, 2167, 12359, 307, 754, 4259, 11, 264, 479, 12, 41167, 20678, 1401, 2293, 502, 13, 1360, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15215063931649192, "compression_ratio": 1.5795053003533568, "no_speech_prob": 1.340673448993468e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 135538, "start": 1377.5, "end": 1381.22, "text": " It declared 100% of the particles are in a giant cluster.", "tokens": [51471, 467, 15489, 2319, 4, 295, 264, 10007, 366, 294, 257, 7410, 13630, 13, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15215063931649192, "compression_ratio": 1.5795053003533568, "no_speech_prob": 1.340673448993468e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 135538, "start": 1381.8200000000002, "end": 1383.2, "text": " Phase separation has occurred.", "tokens": [51687, 24432, 14634, 575, 11068, 13, 51756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15215063931649192, "compression_ratio": 1.5795053003533568, "no_speech_prob": 1.340673448993468e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 135538, "start": 1383.2800000000002, "end": 1384.22, "text": " And why did it do that?", "tokens": [51760, 400, 983, 630, 309, 360, 300, 30, 51807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15215063931649192, "compression_ratio": 1.5795053003533568, "no_speech_prob": 1.340673448993468e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 138422, "start": 1384.22, "end": 1392.98, "text": " Because at that high packing fraction, the physical space between the particles was simply smaller than the fixed contact distance cutoff used by the formula.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 412, 300, 1090, 20815, 14135, 11, 264, 4001, 1901, 1296, 264, 10007, 390, 2935, 4356, 813, 264, 6806, 3385, 4560, 1723, 4506, 1143, 538, 264, 8513, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625525456554485, "compression_ratio": 1.686832740213523, "no_speech_prob": 1.449613866444377e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 138422, "start": 1393.48, "end": 1395.94, "text": " It wasn't measuring a dynamical phase transition.", "tokens": [50828, 467, 2067, 380, 13389, 257, 5999, 804, 5574, 6034, 13, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625525456554485, "compression_ratio": 1.686832740213523, "no_speech_prob": 1.449613866444377e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 138422, "start": 1396.18, "end": 1399.1200000000001, "text": " It wasn't measuring traffic jams caused by activity.", "tokens": [50963, 467, 2067, 380, 13389, 6419, 361, 4070, 7008, 538, 5191, 13, 51110], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625525456554485, "compression_ratio": 1.686832740213523, "no_speech_prob": 1.449613866444377e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 138422, "start": 1399.34, "end": 1404.6200000000001, "text": " It was just measuring the geometric reality that you crammed a lot of circles into a small box.", "tokens": [51121, 467, 390, 445, 13389, 264, 33246, 4103, 300, 291, 941, 19859, 257, 688, 295, 13040, 666, 257, 1359, 2424, 13, 51385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625525456554485, "compression_ratio": 1.686832740213523, "no_speech_prob": 1.449613866444377e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 138422, "start": 1404.74, "end": 1406.58, "text": " Just like putting 50 people in an elevator.", "tokens": [51391, 1449, 411, 3372, 2625, 561, 294, 364, 18782, 13, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625525456554485, "compression_ratio": 1.686832740213523, "no_speech_prob": 1.449613866444377e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 138422, "start": 1406.84, "end": 1410.78, "text": " They are physically touching, but they aren't a socially cohesive group.", "tokens": [51496, 814, 366, 9762, 11175, 11, 457, 436, 3212, 380, 257, 21397, 43025, 1594, 13, 51693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625525456554485, "compression_ratio": 1.686832740213523, "no_speech_prob": 1.449613866444377e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 141078, "start": 1410.78, "end": 1413.52, "text": " The metric was completely blind to the physics.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 20678, 390, 2584, 6865, 281, 264, 10649, 13, 50502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13493912036602312, "compression_ratio": 1.5495867768595042, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206376006868e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 141078, "start": 1413.7, "end": 1415.6, "text": " It was only seeing the geometry.", "tokens": [50511, 467, 390, 787, 2577, 264, 18426, 13, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13493912036602312, "compression_ratio": 1.5495867768595042, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206376006868e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 141078, "start": 1416.3999999999999, "end": 1421.1399999999999, "text": " And it is terrifying to think how a less rigorous researcher could have accidentally published that.", "tokens": [50646, 400, 309, 307, 18106, 281, 519, 577, 257, 1570, 29882, 21751, 727, 362, 15715, 6572, 300, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13493912036602312, "compression_ratio": 1.5495867768595042, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206376006868e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 141078, "start": 1421.5, "end": 1422.54, "text": " They run the simulation.", "tokens": [50901, 814, 1190, 264, 16575, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13493912036602312, "compression_ratio": 1.5495867768595042, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206376006868e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 141078, "start": 1422.8, "end": 1424.94, "text": " They see F-max shoot up to 1.0.", "tokens": [50966, 814, 536, 479, 12, 41167, 3076, 493, 281, 502, 13, 15, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13493912036602312, "compression_ratio": 1.5495867768595042, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206376006868e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 141078, "start": 1425.12, "end": 1427.94, "text": " They correlate it with their shiny new capacity term.", "tokens": [51082, 814, 48742, 309, 365, 641, 16997, 777, 6042, 1433, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13493912036602312, "compression_ratio": 1.5495867768595042, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206376006868e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 141078, "start": 1428.04, "end": 1433.16, "text": " And boom, they write a paper claiming a groundbreaking discovery in active matter.", "tokens": [51228, 400, 9351, 11, 436, 2464, 257, 3035, 19232, 257, 42491, 12114, 294, 4967, 1871, 13, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13493912036602312, "compression_ratio": 1.5495867768595042, "no_speech_prob": 1.555206376006868e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 143316, "start": 1433.16, "end": 1438.22, "text": " This raises such an important question for anyone listening who works with analytics, dashboards, or data science.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 19658, 1270, 364, 1021, 1168, 337, 2878, 4764, 567, 1985, 365, 15370, 11, 8240, 17228, 11, 420, 1412, 3497, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11997975801166735, "compression_ratio": 1.3308823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.415818092105614e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 143316, "start": 1438.7, "end": 1441.7, "text": " Are your metrics measuring the phenomenon you actually care about?", "tokens": [50642, 2014, 428, 16367, 13389, 264, 14029, 291, 767, 1127, 466, 30, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11997975801166735, "compression_ratio": 1.3308823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 1.415818092105614e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 144170, "start": 1441.7, "end": 1445.38, "text": " Or are they just measuring the geometry of the test environment itself?", "tokens": [50365, 1610, 366, 436, 445, 13389, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 1500, 2823, 2564, 30, 50549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1343414887138035, "compression_ratio": 1.607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582746882407243e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 144170, "start": 1445.92, "end": 1453.78, "text": " Fliction only caught this because they ran a validity scan against independent measures, like the bimodality of the density field, and found zero correlation.", "tokens": [50576, 3235, 4105, 787, 5415, 341, 570, 436, 5872, 257, 40943, 11049, 1970, 6695, 8000, 11, 411, 264, 272, 332, 378, 1860, 295, 264, 10305, 2519, 11, 293, 1352, 4018, 20009, 13, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1343414887138035, "compression_ratio": 1.607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582746882407243e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 144170, "start": 1454.16, "end": 1458.8, "text": " So if absolute distance is broken, they must have had to make the metric dynamic somehow.", "tokens": [50988, 407, 498, 8236, 4560, 307, 5463, 11, 436, 1633, 362, 632, 281, 652, 264, 20678, 8546, 6063, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1343414887138035, "compression_ratio": 1.607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582746882407243e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 144170, "start": 1459.42, "end": 1462.68, "text": " Like measuring how crowded a neighborhood is compared to the rest of the city.", "tokens": [51251, 1743, 13389, 577, 21634, 257, 7630, 307, 5347, 281, 264, 1472, 295, 264, 2307, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1343414887138035, "compression_ratio": 1.607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582746882407243e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 144170, "start": 1462.9, "end": 1463.3400000000001, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51425, 48746, 736, 13, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1343414887138035, "compression_ratio": 1.607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582746882407243e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 146334, "start": 1463.34, "end": 1468.9599999999998, "text": " They replaced the absolute particle contact metric with a composite of density domain indicators.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 10772, 264, 8236, 12359, 3385, 20678, 365, 257, 25557, 295, 10305, 9274, 22176, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12542295455932617, "compression_ratio": 1.6715328467153285, "no_speech_prob": 1.675223978633844e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 146334, "start": 1469.4599999999998, "end": 1480.52, "text": " Instead of a fixed, hard-coded distance cutoff, they looked at the coarse-grained density field and defined thresholds relative to that specific snapshot's own mean density.", "tokens": [50671, 7156, 295, 257, 6806, 11, 1152, 12, 66, 12340, 4560, 1723, 4506, 11, 436, 2956, 412, 264, 39312, 12, 20735, 2001, 10305, 2519, 293, 7642, 14678, 82, 4972, 281, 300, 2685, 30163, 311, 1065, 914, 10305, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12542295455932617, "compression_ratio": 1.6715328467153285, "no_speech_prob": 1.675223978633844e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 146334, "start": 1481.04, "end": 1482.76, "text": " So how does that work mechanically?", "tokens": [51250, 407, 577, 775, 300, 589, 4236, 984, 30, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12542295455932617, "compression_ratio": 1.6715328467153285, "no_speech_prob": 1.675223978633844e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 146334, "start": 1483.1399999999999, "end": 1485.74, "text": " I think the paper mentions a connected components procedure.", "tokens": [51355, 286, 519, 264, 3035, 23844, 257, 4582, 6677, 10747, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12542295455932617, "compression_ratio": 1.6715328467153285, "no_speech_prob": 1.675223978633844e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 146334, "start": 1485.8999999999999, "end": 1489.84, "text": " Yeah, so you can think of a connected components procedure like a game of infectious tag.", "tokens": [51493, 865, 11, 370, 291, 393, 519, 295, 257, 4582, 6677, 10747, 411, 257, 1216, 295, 26780, 6162, 13, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12542295455932617, "compression_ratio": 1.6715328467153285, "no_speech_prob": 1.675223978633844e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 148984, "start": 1489.84, "end": 1496.12, "text": " The algorithm scans the grid and looks for a spot where the density is significantly higher than the room's average.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 9284, 35116, 264, 10748, 293, 1542, 337, 257, 4008, 689, 264, 10305, 307, 10591, 2946, 813, 264, 1808, 311, 4274, 13, 50679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1447313008485017, "compression_ratio": 1.7104247104247103, "no_speech_prob": 2.043938802931411e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 148984, "start": 1496.4399999999998, "end": 1498.1399999999999, "text": " If it finds one, it tags it.", "tokens": [50695, 759, 309, 10704, 472, 11, 309, 18632, 309, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1447313008485017, "compression_ratio": 1.7104247104247103, "no_speech_prob": 2.043938802931411e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 148984, "start": 1498.76, "end": 1501.52, "text": " Then it checks the immediate neighbors of that spot.", "tokens": [50811, 1396, 309, 13834, 264, 11629, 12512, 295, 300, 4008, 13, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1447313008485017, "compression_ratio": 1.7104247104247103, "no_speech_prob": 2.043938802931411e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 148984, "start": 1501.84, "end": 1505.32, "text": " If they are also highly dense, they get tagged and join the cluster group.", "tokens": [50965, 759, 436, 366, 611, 5405, 18011, 11, 436, 483, 40239, 293, 3917, 264, 13630, 1594, 13, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1447313008485017, "compression_ratio": 1.7104247104247103, "no_speech_prob": 2.043938802931411e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 148984, "start": 1505.6799999999998, "end": 1511.6, "text": " The tag spreads outwards, cell by cell, until the density drops below the threshold and the cluster stops growing.", "tokens": [51157, 440, 6162, 25728, 484, 2015, 11, 2815, 538, 2815, 11, 1826, 264, 10305, 11438, 2507, 264, 14678, 293, 264, 13630, 10094, 4194, 13, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1447313008485017, "compression_ratio": 1.7104247104247103, "no_speech_prob": 2.043938802931411e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 148984, "start": 1511.8799999999999, "end": 1513.04, "text": " That's incredibly smart.", "tokens": [51467, 663, 311, 6252, 4069, 13, 51525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1447313008485017, "compression_ratio": 1.7104247104247103, "no_speech_prob": 2.043938802931411e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 148984, "start": 1513.76, "end": 1515.4199999999998, "text": " So the whole room is crowded.", "tokens": [51561, 407, 264, 1379, 1808, 307, 21634, 13, 51644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1447313008485017, "compression_ratio": 1.7104247104247103, "no_speech_prob": 2.043938802931411e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 151542, "start": 1515.42, "end": 1521.4, "text": " It only counts as a cluster if a specific area is significantly more crowded than the background average.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 787, 14893, 382, 257, 13630, 498, 257, 2685, 1859, 307, 10591, 544, 21634, 813, 264, 3678, 4274, 13, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881775370815344, "compression_ratio": 1.5775577557755776, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211825497839839e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 151542, "start": 1522.02, "end": 1525.22, "text": " The high-packing fraction alone could no longer trigger a false positive.", "tokens": [50695, 440, 1090, 12, 9539, 278, 14135, 3312, 727, 572, 2854, 7875, 257, 7908, 3353, 13, 50855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881775370815344, "compression_ratio": 1.5775577557755776, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211825497839839e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 151542, "start": 1525.3400000000001, "end": 1525.64, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50861, 7587, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881775370815344, "compression_ratio": 1.5775577557755776, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211825497839839e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 151542, "start": 1525.9, "end": 1532.42, "text": " And they verified this by taking the exact same starting configuration that gave them a 1.00 earlier,", "tokens": [50889, 400, 436, 31197, 341, 538, 1940, 264, 1900, 912, 2891, 11694, 300, 2729, 552, 257, 502, 13, 628, 3071, 11, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881775370815344, "compression_ratio": 1.5775577557755776, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211825497839839e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 151542, "start": 1532.92, "end": 1536.88, "text": " ran it through the new relative metric, and it output exactly 0.000.", "tokens": [51240, 5872, 309, 807, 264, 777, 4972, 20678, 11, 293, 309, 5598, 2293, 1958, 13, 1360, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881775370815344, "compression_ratio": 1.5775577557755776, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211825497839839e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 151542, "start": 1537.3000000000002, "end": 1539.2, "text": " The artifact was completely neutralized.", "tokens": [51459, 440, 34806, 390, 2584, 10598, 1602, 13, 51554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881775370815344, "compression_ratio": 1.5775577557755776, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211825497839839e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 151542, "start": 1539.3000000000002, "end": 1541.8000000000002, "text": " Crisis averted through rigorous methodology.", "tokens": [51559, 42846, 257, 18537, 807, 29882, 24850, 13, 51684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881775370815344, "compression_ratio": 1.5775577557755776, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211825497839839e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 151542, "start": 1542.0800000000002, "end": 1542.3200000000002, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51698, 1033, 13, 51710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881775370815344, "compression_ratio": 1.5775577557755776, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211825497839839e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 151542, "start": 1542.46, "end": 1543.6200000000001, "text": " So the software is stable.", "tokens": [51717, 407, 264, 4722, 307, 8351, 13, 51775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13881775370815344, "compression_ratio": 1.5775577557755776, "no_speech_prob": 1.7211825497839839e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 154362, "start": 1543.62, "end": 1546.1399999999999, "text": " The target variable is actually measuring reality.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3779, 7006, 307, 767, 13389, 4103, 13, 50491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1540268761771066, "compression_ratio": 1.662686567164179, "no_speech_prob": 2.6145869323757065e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 154362, "start": 1546.62, "end": 1553.1399999999999, "text": " We have our three competing capacity definitions, and we have our baseline data, which is just plain old density metrics.", "tokens": [50515, 492, 362, 527, 1045, 15439, 6042, 21988, 11, 293, 321, 362, 527, 20518, 1412, 11, 597, 307, 445, 11121, 1331, 10305, 16367, 13, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1540268761771066, "compression_ratio": 1.662686567164179, "no_speech_prob": 2.6145869323757065e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 154362, "start": 1553.62, "end": 1555.1, "text": " It is finally time for the crucible.", "tokens": [50865, 467, 307, 2721, 565, 337, 264, 5140, 32128, 13, 50939], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1540268761771066, "compression_ratio": 1.662686567164179, "no_speech_prob": 2.6145869323757065e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 154362, "start": 1555.58, "end": 1556.6999999999998, "text": " The regression analysis.", "tokens": [50963, 440, 24590, 5215, 13, 51019], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1540268761771066, "compression_ratio": 1.662686567164179, "no_speech_prob": 2.6145869323757065e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 154362, "start": 1557.26, "end": 1559.3799999999999, "text": " Did the fancy vocabulary predict the future?", "tokens": [51047, 2589, 264, 10247, 19864, 6069, 264, 2027, 30, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1540268761771066, "compression_ratio": 1.662686567164179, "no_speech_prob": 2.6145869323757065e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 154362, "start": 1559.86, "end": 1562.36, "text": " Did capacity tell us something density didn't?", "tokens": [51177, 2589, 6042, 980, 505, 746, 10305, 994, 380, 30, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1540268761771066, "compression_ratio": 1.662686567164179, "no_speech_prob": 2.6145869323757065e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 154362, "start": 1562.76, "end": 1564.4199999999998, "text": " The results are striking in their clarity.", "tokens": [51322, 440, 3542, 366, 18559, 294, 641, 16992, 13, 51405], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1540268761771066, "compression_ratio": 1.662686567164179, "no_speech_prob": 2.6145869323757065e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 154362, "start": 1564.86, "end": 1567.4799999999998, "text": " They used a LassoCV methodology to test this.", "tokens": [51427, 814, 1143, 257, 10663, 539, 34, 53, 24850, 281, 1500, 341, 13, 51558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1540268761771066, "compression_ratio": 1.662686567164179, "no_speech_prob": 2.6145869323757065e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 154362, "start": 1567.54, "end": 1567.78, "text": " Wait.", "tokens": [51561, 3802, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1540268761771066, "compression_ratio": 1.662686567164179, "no_speech_prob": 2.6145869323757065e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 154362, "start": 1567.8799999999999, "end": 1571.1599999999999, "text": " Before we look at the results, for those who don't build machine learning models every day,", "tokens": [51578, 4546, 321, 574, 412, 264, 3542, 11, 337, 729, 567, 500, 380, 1322, 3479, 2539, 5245, 633, 786, 11, 51742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1540268761771066, "compression_ratio": 1.662686567164179, "no_speech_prob": 2.6145869323757065e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 154362, "start": 1571.26, "end": 1572.28, "text": " what is LassoCV?", "tokens": [51747, 437, 307, 10663, 539, 34, 53, 30, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1540268761771066, "compression_ratio": 1.662686567164179, "no_speech_prob": 2.6145869323757065e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 154362, "start": 1572.28, "end": 1573.54, "text": " How does it actually work?", "tokens": [51798, 1012, 775, 309, 767, 589, 30, 51861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1540268761771066, "compression_ratio": 1.662686567164179, "no_speech_prob": 2.6145869323757065e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 157362, "start": 1573.62, "end": 1577.9199999999998, "text": " Machine learning models often have a bad habit of just memorizing the data you feed them.", "tokens": [50365, 22155, 2539, 5245, 2049, 362, 257, 1578, 7164, 295, 445, 10560, 3319, 264, 1412, 291, 3154, 552, 13, 50580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16342036864336798, "compression_ratio": 1.4228571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830561246240384e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 157362, "start": 1578.12, "end": 1582.62, "text": " If you give a model 50 variables, it will try to use all 50 to make a prediction,", "tokens": [50590, 759, 291, 976, 257, 2316, 2625, 9102, 11, 309, 486, 853, 281, 764, 439, 2625, 281, 652, 257, 17630, 11, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16342036864336798, "compression_ratio": 1.4228571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830561246240384e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 157362, "start": 1583.1399999999999, "end": 1585.3799999999999, "text": " even if 49 of them are useless noise.", "tokens": [50841, 754, 498, 16513, 295, 552, 366, 14115, 5658, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16342036864336798, "compression_ratio": 1.4228571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830561246240384e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 157362, "start": 1585.52, "end": 1586.86, "text": " It just wants to use everything.", "tokens": [50960, 467, 445, 2738, 281, 764, 1203, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16342036864336798, "compression_ratio": 1.4228571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830561246240384e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 157362, "start": 1587.04, "end": 1587.2199999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51036, 1779, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16342036864336798, "compression_ratio": 1.4228571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830561246240384e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 158722, "start": 1587.22, "end": 1590.1000000000001, "text": " So Lasso is a type of regularization.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 10663, 539, 307, 257, 2010, 295, 3890, 2144, 13, 50509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1961969765283728, "compression_ratio": 1.5458515283842795, "no_speech_prob": 1.460454587126625e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 158722, "start": 1590.1000000000001, "end": 1596.04, "text": " You can imagine Lasso as a penalty system that punishes the model for using too many variables.", "tokens": [50509, 509, 393, 3811, 10663, 539, 382, 257, 16263, 1185, 300, 9842, 279, 264, 2316, 337, 1228, 886, 867, 9102, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1961969765283728, "compression_ratio": 1.5458515283842795, "no_speech_prob": 1.460454587126625e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 158722, "start": 1596.22, "end": 1601.22, "text": " It essentially tightens the mathematical noose around the variables and forces the weak,", "tokens": [50815, 467, 4476, 4524, 694, 264, 18894, 572, 541, 926, 264, 9102, 293, 5874, 264, 5336, 11, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1961969765283728, "compression_ratio": 1.5458515283842795, "no_speech_prob": 1.460454587126625e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 158722, "start": 1601.64, "end": 1604.1200000000001, "text": " uninformative ones to drop to exactly zero.", "tokens": [51086, 517, 37811, 1166, 2306, 281, 3270, 281, 2293, 4018, 13, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1961969765283728, "compression_ratio": 1.5458515283842795, "no_speech_prob": 1.460454587126625e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 158722, "start": 1604.68, "end": 1606.9, "text": " Only the strongest predictors survive.", "tokens": [51238, 5686, 264, 16595, 6069, 830, 7867, 13, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1961969765283728, "compression_ratio": 1.5458515283842795, "no_speech_prob": 1.460454587126625e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 158722, "start": 1607.1000000000001, "end": 1607.9, "text": " And the CV part.", "tokens": [51359, 400, 264, 22995, 644, 13, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1961969765283728, "compression_ratio": 1.5458515283842795, "no_speech_prob": 1.460454587126625e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 158722, "start": 1608.3, "end": 1610.28, "text": " CV stands for cross-validation.", "tokens": [51419, 22995, 7382, 337, 3278, 12, 3337, 327, 399, 13, 51518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1961969765283728, "compression_ratio": 1.5458515283842795, "no_speech_prob": 1.460454587126625e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 161028, "start": 1610.28, "end": 1614.1, "text": " It's how you test if the model is actually learning or just memorizing.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 577, 291, 1500, 498, 264, 2316, 307, 767, 2539, 420, 445, 10560, 3319, 13, 50556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12694811533732586, "compression_ratio": 1.561904761904762, "no_speech_prob": 1.7410969584477631e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 161028, "start": 1614.58, "end": 1618.84, "text": " You train the model on one chunk of data and test it on a hidden chunk it has never seen.", "tokens": [50580, 509, 3847, 264, 2316, 322, 472, 16635, 295, 1412, 293, 1500, 309, 322, 257, 7633, 16635, 309, 575, 1128, 1612, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12694811533732586, "compression_ratio": 1.561904761904762, "no_speech_prob": 1.7410969584477631e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 161028, "start": 1619.04, "end": 1623.0, "text": " And the paper makes a huge point about doing a chronological train test split here.", "tokens": [50803, 400, 264, 3035, 1669, 257, 2603, 935, 466, 884, 257, 19393, 4383, 3847, 1500, 7472, 510, 13, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12694811533732586, "compression_ratio": 1.561904761904762, "no_speech_prob": 1.7410969584477631e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 161028, "start": 1623.2, "end": 1624.16, "text": " Why is that important?", "tokens": [51011, 1545, 307, 300, 1021, 30, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12694811533732586, "compression_ratio": 1.561904761904762, "no_speech_prob": 1.7410969584477631e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 161028, "start": 1624.32, "end": 1627.26, "text": " Why not just randomize the data like everyone usually does?", "tokens": [51067, 1545, 406, 445, 4974, 1125, 264, 1412, 411, 1518, 2673, 775, 30, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12694811533732586, "compression_ratio": 1.561904761904762, "no_speech_prob": 1.7410969584477631e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 162726, "start": 1627.26, "end": 1632.02, "text": " If you randomly shuffle time series data, you accidentally allow future information to leak", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 16979, 39426, 565, 2638, 1412, 11, 291, 15715, 2089, 2027, 1589, 281, 17143, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13297382477791078, "compression_ratio": 1.7138047138047139, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358907831824e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 162726, "start": 1632.02, "end": 1632.98, "text": " into your training set.", "tokens": [50603, 666, 428, 3097, 992, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13297382477791078, "compression_ratio": 1.7138047138047139, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358907831824e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 162726, "start": 1633.28, "end": 1639.24, "text": " If frame 100 is in your test set, but frame 101 is in your training set, the model can essentially cheat.", "tokens": [50666, 759, 3920, 2319, 307, 294, 428, 1500, 992, 11, 457, 3920, 21055, 307, 294, 428, 3097, 992, 11, 264, 2316, 393, 4476, 17470, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13297382477791078, "compression_ratio": 1.7138047138047139, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358907831824e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 162726, "start": 1639.44, "end": 1640.36, "text": " It already knows what's coming.", "tokens": [50974, 467, 1217, 3255, 437, 311, 1348, 13, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13297382477791078, "compression_ratio": 1.7138047138047139, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358907831824e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 162726, "start": 1640.68, "end": 1641.1, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51036, 7587, 13, 51057], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13297382477791078, "compression_ratio": 1.7138047138047139, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358907831824e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 162726, "start": 1641.36, "end": 1641.52, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51070, 865, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13297382477791078, "compression_ratio": 1.7138047138047139, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358907831824e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 162726, "start": 1641.6, "end": 1646.14, "text": " It's like trying to predict Thursday's weather while already having Friday's weather in your back pocket.", "tokens": [51082, 467, 311, 411, 1382, 281, 6069, 10383, 311, 5503, 1339, 1217, 1419, 6984, 311, 5503, 294, 428, 646, 8963, 13, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13297382477791078, "compression_ratio": 1.7138047138047139, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358907831824e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 162726, "start": 1647.1, "end": 1651.74, "text": " By strictly splitting it chronologically, train on the past, test on the future,", "tokens": [51357, 3146, 20792, 30348, 309, 19393, 17157, 11, 3847, 322, 264, 1791, 11, 1500, 322, 264, 2027, 11, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13297382477791078, "compression_ratio": 1.7138047138047139, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358907831824e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 162726, "start": 1652.36, "end": 1655.02, "text": " Fliction ensured it was a genuine test of prediction.", "tokens": [51620, 3235, 4105, 3489, 3831, 309, 390, 257, 16699, 1500, 295, 17630, 13, 51753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13297382477791078, "compression_ratio": 1.7138047138047139, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358907831824e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 165502, "start": 1655.02, "end": 1657.96, "text": " So, they run this incredibly strict lasso model.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 436, 1190, 341, 6252, 10910, 2439, 539, 2316, 13, 50512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1320883543595024, "compression_ratio": 1.6453900709219857, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362162276115089e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 165502, "start": 1658.9, "end": 1664.58, "text": " The density-only baseline model, the reigning champion, achieved an R-squared of 0.348", "tokens": [50559, 440, 10305, 12, 25202, 20518, 2316, 11, 264, 319, 9676, 10971, 11, 11042, 364, 497, 12, 33292, 1642, 295, 1958, 13, 12249, 23, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1320883543595024, "compression_ratio": 1.6453900709219857, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362162276115089e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 165502, "start": 1664.58, "end": 1667.2, "text": " for predicting the target structure in the near future.", "tokens": [50843, 337, 32884, 264, 3779, 3877, 294, 264, 2651, 2027, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1320883543595024, "compression_ratio": 1.6453900709219857, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362162276115089e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 165502, "start": 1667.34, "end": 1673.44, "text": " Meaning it explained about 34.8% of the variance in when and where the clusters would form,", "tokens": [50981, 19948, 309, 8825, 466, 12790, 13, 23, 4, 295, 264, 21977, 294, 562, 293, 689, 264, 23313, 576, 1254, 11, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1320883543595024, "compression_ratio": 1.6453900709219857, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362162276115089e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 165502, "start": 1674.08, "end": 1677.6399999999999, "text": " which is a very strong baseline for a complex, chaotic system.", "tokens": [51318, 597, 307, 257, 588, 2068, 20518, 337, 257, 3997, 11, 27013, 1185, 13, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1320883543595024, "compression_ratio": 1.6453900709219857, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362162276115089e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 165502, "start": 1677.76, "end": 1680.92, "text": " Then they added the capacity variance, they added the dissipation terms,", "tokens": [51502, 1396, 436, 3869, 264, 6042, 21977, 11, 436, 3869, 264, 29544, 399, 2115, 11, 51660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1320883543595024, "compression_ratio": 1.6453900709219857, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362162276115089e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 165502, "start": 1681.04, "end": 1682.84, "text": " they added cross-field interaction features,", "tokens": [51666, 436, 3869, 3278, 12, 7610, 9285, 4122, 11, 51756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1320883543595024, "compression_ratio": 1.6453900709219857, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362162276115089e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 168284, "start": 1682.84, "end": 1687.72, "text": " they threw the entire new theoretical framework into the lasso model to see how much it would improve.", "tokens": [50365, 436, 11918, 264, 2302, 777, 20864, 8388, 666, 264, 2439, 539, 2316, 281, 536, 577, 709, 309, 576, 3470, 13, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1390802737363835, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.7971980240810703e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 168284, "start": 1687.8999999999999, "end": 1688.34, "text": " And what happened?", "tokens": [50618, 400, 437, 2011, 30, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1390802737363835, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.7971980240810703e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 168284, "start": 1688.6599999999999, "end": 1694.26, "text": " The R-squared with the new capacity vocabulary ranged from 0.348 to 0.349.", "tokens": [50656, 440, 497, 12, 33292, 1642, 365, 264, 777, 6042, 19864, 45570, 490, 1958, 13, 12249, 23, 281, 1958, 13, 12249, 24, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1390802737363835, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.7971980240810703e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 168284, "start": 1694.6599999999999, "end": 1696.1, "text": " Statistically indistinguishable.", "tokens": [50956, 16249, 20458, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1390802737363835, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.7971980240810703e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 168284, "start": 1696.48, "end": 1697.72, "text": " Completely indistinguishable.", "tokens": [51047, 39978, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1390802737363835, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.7971980240810703e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 168284, "start": 1698.1999999999998, "end": 1701.78, "text": " Adding the capacity features did absolutely nothing to improve the prediction", "tokens": [51133, 31204, 264, 6042, 4122, 630, 3122, 1825, 281, 3470, 264, 17630, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1390802737363835, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.7971980240810703e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 168284, "start": 1701.78, "end": 1704.6, "text": " beyond what the simple density baseline already provided.", "tokens": [51312, 4399, 437, 264, 2199, 10305, 20518, 1217, 5649, 13, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1390802737363835, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.7971980240810703e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 170460, "start": 1704.6, "end": 1709.78, "text": " The lasso penalty process almost exclusively retained only the density features,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2439, 539, 16263, 1399, 1920, 20638, 33438, 787, 264, 10305, 4122, 11, 50624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16912476221720377, "compression_ratio": 1.4764150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 2.352566275468093e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 170460, "start": 1710.1599999999999, "end": 1711.98, "text": " dropping the capacity terms to 0.", "tokens": [50643, 13601, 264, 6042, 2115, 281, 1958, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16912476221720377, "compression_ratio": 1.4764150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 2.352566275468093e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 170460, "start": 1712.28, "end": 1716.6999999999998, "text": " It's like bringing a state-of-the-art, million-dollar weather forecasting supercomputer", "tokens": [50749, 467, 311, 411, 5062, 257, 1785, 12, 2670, 12, 3322, 12, 446, 11, 2459, 12, 40485, 5503, 44331, 36708, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16912476221720377, "compression_ratio": 1.4764150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 2.352566275468093e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 170460, "start": 1716.6999999999998, "end": 1718.02, "text": " to a window.", "tokens": [50970, 281, 257, 4910, 13, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16912476221720377, "compression_ratio": 1.4764150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 2.352566275468093e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 170460, "start": 1718.5, "end": 1721.3799999999999, "text": " And it performs exactly as well as a guy just looking out the window and saying,", "tokens": [51060, 400, 309, 26213, 2293, 382, 731, 382, 257, 2146, 445, 1237, 484, 264, 4910, 293, 1566, 11, 51204], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16912476221720377, "compression_ratio": 1.4764150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 2.352566275468093e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 170460, "start": 1721.6999999999998, "end": 1722.4599999999998, "text": " looks like rain.", "tokens": [51220, 1542, 411, 4830, 13, 51258], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16912476221720377, "compression_ratio": 1.4764150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 2.352566275468093e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 172246, "start": 1722.46, "end": 1725.02, "text": " But Flixine didn't stop at a single lasso fit,", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3235, 970, 533, 994, 380, 1590, 412, 257, 2167, 2439, 539, 3318, 11, 50493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1754102394229076, "compression_ratio": 1.6164383561643836, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552645755799067e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 172246, "start": 1725.32, "end": 1728.96, "text": " because a coefficient hitting zero is a weak way to claim a null result.", "tokens": [50508, 570, 257, 17619, 8850, 4018, 307, 257, 5336, 636, 281, 3932, 257, 18184, 1874, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1754102394229076, "compression_ratio": 1.6164383561643836, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552645755799067e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 172246, "start": 1729.44, "end": 1733.68, "text": " They ran grueling permutation tests at the level of entire simulation runs,", "tokens": [50714, 814, 5872, 677, 3483, 278, 4784, 11380, 6921, 412, 264, 1496, 295, 2302, 16575, 6676, 11, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1754102394229076, "compression_ratio": 1.6164383561643836, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552645755799067e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 172246, "start": 1733.8, "end": 1737.48, "text": " not individual frames, to account for time series autocorrelation.", "tokens": [50932, 406, 2609, 12083, 11, 281, 2696, 337, 565, 2638, 45833, 284, 4419, 399, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1754102394229076, "compression_ratio": 1.6164383561643836, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552645755799067e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 172246, "start": 1737.56, "end": 1737.9, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51120, 3153, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1754102394229076, "compression_ratio": 1.6164383561643836, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552645755799067e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 172246, "start": 1738.1200000000001, "end": 1741.92, "text": " And across all these rigorous checks, across coarse graining scales,", "tokens": [51148, 400, 2108, 439, 613, 29882, 13834, 11, 2108, 39312, 1295, 1760, 17408, 11, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1754102394229076, "compression_ratio": 1.6164383561643836, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552645755799067e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 172246, "start": 1742.08, "end": 1744.28, "text": " across different activity levels and replicate counts,", "tokens": [51346, 2108, 819, 5191, 4358, 293, 25356, 14893, 11, 51456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1754102394229076, "compression_ratio": 1.6164383561643836, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552645755799067e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 172246, "start": 1744.64, "end": 1746.54, "text": " the null result held cleanly.", "tokens": [51474, 264, 18184, 1874, 5167, 2541, 356, 13, 51569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1754102394229076, "compression_ratio": 1.6164383561643836, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552645755799067e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 172246, "start": 1746.8, "end": 1748.04, "text": " Capacity added nothing.", "tokens": [51582, 8363, 19008, 3869, 1825, 13, 51644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1754102394229076, "compression_ratio": 1.6164383561643836, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552645755799067e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 172246, "start": 1748.18, "end": 1749.3600000000001, "text": " But there was one anomaly.", "tokens": [51651, 583, 456, 390, 472, 42737, 13, 51710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1754102394229076, "compression_ratio": 1.6164383561643836, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552645755799067e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 174936, "start": 1749.36, "end": 1755.1799999999998, "text": " At a packing fraction of 0.35, the residualized correlation test flagged a mixed result.", "tokens": [50365, 1711, 257, 20815, 14135, 295, 1958, 13, 8794, 11, 264, 27980, 1602, 20009, 1500, 7166, 3004, 257, 7467, 1874, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11896627599542792, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900350255881103e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 174936, "start": 1755.4599999999998, "end": 1757.6599999999999, "text": " Let's define residualized correlation quickly.", "tokens": [50670, 961, 311, 6964, 27980, 1602, 20009, 2661, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11896627599542792, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900350255881103e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 174936, "start": 1758.06, "end": 1761.62, "text": " That's essentially looking at whatever predictive power is left over", "tokens": [50800, 663, 311, 4476, 1237, 412, 2035, 35521, 1347, 307, 1411, 670, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11896627599542792, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900350255881103e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 174936, "start": 1761.62, "end": 1764.58, "text": " after the baseline density model takes its share, right?", "tokens": [50978, 934, 264, 20518, 10305, 2316, 2516, 1080, 2073, 11, 558, 30, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11896627599542792, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900350255881103e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 174936, "start": 1764.76, "end": 1764.9599999999998, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51135, 1079, 13, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11896627599542792, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900350255881103e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 174936, "start": 1765.06, "end": 1768.12, "text": " It isolates what the new variable is bringing to the table uniquely.", "tokens": [51150, 467, 7381, 1024, 437, 264, 777, 7006, 307, 5062, 281, 264, 3199, 31474, 13, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11896627599542792, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900350255881103e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 174936, "start": 1768.28, "end": 1768.4599999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51311, 1779, 13, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11896627599542792, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900350255881103e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 174936, "start": 1768.56, "end": 1772.6599999999999, "text": " And at 0.35, some of their capacity and dissipation features", "tokens": [51325, 400, 412, 1958, 13, 8794, 11, 512, 295, 641, 6042, 293, 29544, 399, 4122, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11896627599542792, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900350255881103e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 174936, "start": 1772.6599999999999, "end": 1775.34, "text": " suddenly seem to show a significant correlation.", "tokens": [51530, 5800, 1643, 281, 855, 257, 4776, 20009, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11896627599542792, "compression_ratio": 1.6200716845878136, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900350255881103e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 177534, "start": 1775.34, "end": 1780.6599999999999, "text": " This is exactly the moment where a less rigorous scientist writes the paper and says,", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 2293, 264, 1623, 689, 257, 1570, 29882, 12662, 13657, 264, 3035, 293, 1619, 11, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15160345419859275, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037862870023957e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 177534, "start": 1781.22, "end": 1785.84, "text": " capacity is highly predictive at exactly 0.35 packing fraction.", "tokens": [50659, 6042, 307, 5405, 35521, 412, 2293, 1958, 13, 8794, 20815, 14135, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15160345419859275, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037862870023957e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 177534, "start": 1786.36, "end": 1787.6799999999998, "text": " We found the magic domain.", "tokens": [50916, 492, 1352, 264, 5585, 9274, 13, 50982], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15160345419859275, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037862870023957e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 177534, "start": 1787.86, "end": 1790.48, "text": " Which is exactly what the psychological temptation would dictate.", "tokens": [50991, 3013, 307, 2293, 437, 264, 14346, 30423, 576, 36071, 13, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15160345419859275, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037862870023957e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 177534, "start": 1790.82, "end": 1794.8799999999999, "text": " It's related to the statistical problem of multiple comparisons, or p-hacking.", "tokens": [51139, 467, 311, 4077, 281, 264, 22820, 1154, 295, 3866, 33157, 11, 420, 280, 12, 71, 14134, 13, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15160345419859275, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037862870023957e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 177534, "start": 1795.6599999999999, "end": 1797.1599999999999, "text": " If you test enough random domains,", "tokens": [51381, 759, 291, 1500, 1547, 4974, 25514, 11, 51456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15160345419859275, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037862870023957e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 177534, "start": 1797.28, "end": 1801.1, "text": " eventually one of them will show a positive result just by pure random chance.", "tokens": [51462, 4728, 472, 295, 552, 486, 855, 257, 3353, 1874, 445, 538, 6075, 4974, 2931, 13, 51653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15160345419859275, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037862870023957e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 177534, "start": 1801.1999999999998, "end": 1802.6999999999998, "text": " So how did Fliction handle it?", "tokens": [51658, 407, 577, 630, 3235, 4105, 4813, 309, 30, 51733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15160345419859275, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037862870023957e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 177534, "start": 1802.9199999999998, "end": 1804.3999999999999, "text": " They investigated it transparently.", "tokens": [51744, 814, 30070, 309, 7132, 6420, 13, 51818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15160345419859275, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.8037862870023957e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 180440, "start": 1804.4, "end": 1810.3200000000002, "text": " They ran the exact same tests at a neighboring packing fraction of 0.2 and at 0.45.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 5872, 264, 1900, 912, 6921, 412, 257, 31521, 20815, 14135, 295, 1958, 13, 17, 293, 412, 1958, 13, 8465, 13, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13548462867736816, "compression_ratio": 1.5280898876404494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108555461746832e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 180440, "start": 1810.9, "end": 1812.68, "text": " The pattern completely vanished.", "tokens": [50690, 440, 5102, 2584, 37518, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13548462867736816, "compression_ratio": 1.5280898876404494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108555461746832e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 180440, "start": 1812.96, "end": 1813.6200000000001, "text": " It didn't replicate.", "tokens": [50793, 467, 994, 380, 25356, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13548462867736816, "compression_ratio": 1.5280898876404494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108555461746832e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 180440, "start": 1814.3200000000002, "end": 1819.24, "text": " So instead of hiding this anomaly or trumpeting it as a domain-specific breakthrough,", "tokens": [50861, 407, 2602, 295, 10596, 341, 42737, 420, 21779, 9880, 309, 382, 257, 9274, 12, 29258, 22397, 11, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13548462867736816, "compression_ratio": 1.5280898876404494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108555461746832e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 180440, "start": 1819.66, "end": 1823.5, "text": " they transparently reported it in the paper as a likely small sample artifact.", "tokens": [51128, 436, 7132, 6420, 7055, 309, 294, 264, 3035, 382, 257, 3700, 1359, 6889, 34806, 13, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13548462867736816, "compression_ratio": 1.5280898876404494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108555461746832e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 180440, "start": 1823.92, "end": 1827.24, "text": " They recorded it, hedged their conclusions appropriately, and moved on.", "tokens": [51341, 814, 8287, 309, 11, 33653, 3004, 641, 22865, 23505, 11, 293, 4259, 322, 13, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13548462867736816, "compression_ratio": 1.5280898876404494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108555461746832e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 180440, "start": 1827.48, "end": 1829.16, "text": " Which begs the ultimate question.", "tokens": [51519, 3013, 4612, 82, 264, 9705, 1168, 13, 51603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13548462867736816, "compression_ratio": 1.5280898876404494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108555461746832e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 182916, "start": 1829.16, "end": 1832.5600000000002, "text": " If you spend months building this massive simulation engine,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 3496, 2493, 2390, 341, 5994, 16575, 2848, 11, 50535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16975042896886025, "compression_ratio": 1.6094276094276094, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080564393423536e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 182916, "start": 1832.66, "end": 1836.0400000000002, "text": " carefully validating everything, surviving Euler-Mariyama explosions,", "tokens": [50540, 7500, 7363, 990, 1203, 11, 24948, 462, 26318, 12, 44, 3504, 88, 2404, 36872, 11, 50709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16975042896886025, "compression_ratio": 1.6094276094276094, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080564393423536e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 182916, "start": 1836.26, "end": 1839.94, "text": " and then your final R-square doesn't improve by even 1%,", "tokens": [50720, 293, 550, 428, 2572, 497, 12, 33292, 543, 1177, 380, 3470, 538, 754, 502, 8923, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16975042896886025, "compression_ratio": 1.6094276094276094, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080564393423536e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 182916, "start": 1839.94, "end": 1841.76, "text": " I mean, did the author just waste their time?", "tokens": [50904, 286, 914, 11, 630, 264, 3793, 445, 5964, 641, 565, 30, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16975042896886025, "compression_ratio": 1.6094276094276094, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080564393423536e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 182916, "start": 1842.26, "end": 1845.02, "text": " Isn't a null result a massive failure for the project?", "tokens": [51020, 6998, 380, 257, 18184, 1874, 257, 5994, 7763, 337, 264, 1716, 30, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16975042896886025, "compression_ratio": 1.6094276094276094, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080564393423536e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 182916, "start": 1845.3600000000001, "end": 1848.2, "text": " I cannot stress enough how firmly we must reject that notion.", "tokens": [51175, 286, 2644, 4244, 1547, 577, 20031, 321, 1633, 8248, 300, 10710, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16975042896886025, "compression_ratio": 1.6094276094276094, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080564393423536e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 182916, "start": 1848.5, "end": 1851.64, "text": " This is the culmination of the pre-registered chart we discussed in the very beginning.", "tokens": [51332, 639, 307, 264, 28583, 399, 295, 264, 659, 12, 3375, 1964, 292, 6927, 321, 7152, 294, 264, 588, 2863, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16975042896886025, "compression_ratio": 1.6094276094276094, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080564393423536e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 182916, "start": 1851.94, "end": 1853.0800000000002, "text": " This is a clean failure.", "tokens": [51504, 639, 307, 257, 2541, 7763, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16975042896886025, "compression_ratio": 1.6094276094276094, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080564393423536e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 182916, "start": 1853.18, "end": 1853.8200000000002, "text": " Clean failure.", "tokens": [51566, 18463, 7763, 13, 51598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16975042896886025, "compression_ratio": 1.6094276094276094, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080564393423536e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 185382, "start": 1853.82, "end": 1855.3799999999999, "text": " It is a boundary line.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 12866, 1622, 13, 50443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16551552196540456, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.818209211662536e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 185382, "start": 1855.72, "end": 1858.4199999999998, "text": " It stops the bleeding of resources into a dead end.", "tokens": [50460, 467, 10094, 264, 19312, 295, 3593, 666, 257, 3116, 917, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16551552196540456, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.818209211662536e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 185382, "start": 1859.1799999999998, "end": 1863.12, "text": " What this null result proves is that the capacity constructs,", "tokens": [50633, 708, 341, 18184, 1874, 25019, 307, 300, 264, 6042, 7690, 82, 11, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16551552196540456, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.818209211662536e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 185382, "start": 1863.28, "end": 1865.6799999999998, "text": " however elegantly they are mathematically defined,", "tokens": [50838, 4461, 14459, 3627, 436, 366, 44003, 7642, 11, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16551552196540456, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.818209211662536e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 185382, "start": 1866.1, "end": 1870.28, "text": " are merely downstream expressions of density-driven clustering.", "tokens": [50979, 366, 17003, 30621, 15277, 295, 10305, 12, 25456, 596, 48673, 13, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16551552196540456, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.818209211662536e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 185382, "start": 1870.8, "end": 1875.54, "text": " They are not independent sources of predictive information in this physical regime.", "tokens": [51214, 814, 366, 406, 6695, 7139, 295, 35521, 1589, 294, 341, 4001, 13120, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16551552196540456, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.818209211662536e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 185382, "start": 1875.76, "end": 1877.78, "text": " It narrows the space of viable theories.", "tokens": [51462, 467, 6397, 1509, 264, 1901, 295, 22024, 13667, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16551552196540456, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.818209211662536e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 185382, "start": 1878.34, "end": 1882.08, "text": " It saves future researchers from spending years going down a blind alley.", "tokens": [51591, 467, 19155, 2027, 10309, 490, 6434, 924, 516, 760, 257, 6865, 26660, 13, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16551552196540456, "compression_ratio": 1.6483516483516483, "no_speech_prob": 1.818209211662536e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 188208, "start": 1882.08, "end": 1884.46, "text": " It proves the philosophical crucible works.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 25019, 264, 25066, 5140, 32128, 1985, 13, 50484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11607503547942896, "compression_ratio": 1.7554179566563468, "no_speech_prob": 1.846562399515639e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 188208, "start": 1885.24, "end": 1888.98, "text": " When a field-like construct is forced to run the gauntlet of reconstructability,", "tokens": [50523, 1133, 257, 2519, 12, 4092, 7690, 307, 7579, 281, 1190, 264, 5959, 2760, 2631, 295, 31499, 2310, 11, 50710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11607503547942896, "compression_ratio": 1.7554179566563468, "no_speech_prob": 1.846562399515639e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 188208, "start": 1889.4199999999998, "end": 1892.6799999999998, "text": " comparability, stability, and prediction, the truth comes out.", "tokens": [50732, 6311, 2310, 11, 11826, 11, 293, 17630, 11, 264, 3494, 1487, 484, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11607503547942896, "compression_ratio": 1.7554179566563468, "no_speech_prob": 1.846562399515639e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 188208, "start": 1893.08, "end": 1894.3999999999999, "text": " Okay, but the story isn't over.", "tokens": [50915, 1033, 11, 457, 264, 1657, 1943, 380, 670, 13, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11607503547942896, "compression_ratio": 1.7554179566563468, "no_speech_prob": 1.846562399515639e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 188208, "start": 1894.6799999999998, "end": 1897.4399999999998, "text": " Because everything we just talked about was purely observational.", "tokens": [50995, 1436, 1203, 321, 445, 2825, 466, 390, 17491, 9951, 1478, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11607503547942896, "compression_ratio": 1.7554179566563468, "no_speech_prob": 1.846562399515639e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 188208, "start": 1897.58, "end": 1901.22, "text": " We were just passively watching the particles bump into each other and trying to predict it.", "tokens": [51140, 492, 645, 445, 1320, 3413, 1976, 264, 10007, 9961, 666, 1184, 661, 293, 1382, 281, 6069, 309, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11607503547942896, "compression_ratio": 1.7554179566563468, "no_speech_prob": 1.846562399515639e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 188208, "start": 1901.4399999999998, "end": 1904.5, "text": " But correlation, even predictive correlation, isn't causation.", "tokens": [51333, 583, 20009, 11, 754, 35521, 20009, 11, 1943, 380, 3302, 399, 13, 51486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11607503547942896, "compression_ratio": 1.7554179566563468, "no_speech_prob": 1.846562399515639e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 188208, "start": 1905.1, "end": 1906.3, "text": " What if we don't just watch?", "tokens": [51516, 708, 498, 321, 500, 380, 445, 1159, 30, 51576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11607503547942896, "compression_ratio": 1.7554179566563468, "no_speech_prob": 1.846562399515639e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 188208, "start": 1906.4399999999998, "end": 1907.8999999999999, "text": " What if we actually poke the system?", "tokens": [51583, 708, 498, 321, 767, 19712, 264, 1185, 30, 51656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11607503547942896, "compression_ratio": 1.7554179566563468, "no_speech_prob": 1.846562399515639e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 188208, "start": 1908.1599999999999, "end": 1910.6, "text": " Now we are entering the second half of the empirical paper,", "tokens": [51669, 823, 321, 366, 11104, 264, 1150, 1922, 295, 264, 31886, 3035, 11, 51791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11607503547942896, "compression_ratio": 1.7554179566563468, "no_speech_prob": 1.846562399515639e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 191060, "start": 1910.6, "end": 1912.12, "text": " the intervention protocol.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 13176, 10336, 13, 50441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357209705171132, "compression_ratio": 1.7228915662650603, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378118921160032e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 191060, "start": 1913.12, "end": 1916.8799999999999, "text": " Affliction shifts from asking if capacity can act as an early warning variable", "tokens": [50491, 12840, 75, 4105, 19201, 490, 3365, 498, 6042, 393, 605, 382, 364, 2440, 9164, 7006, 50679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357209705171132, "compression_ratio": 1.7228915662650603, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378118921160032e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 191060, "start": 1916.8799999999999, "end": 1918.8999999999999, "text": " to asking if it acts as a driver.", "tokens": [50679, 281, 3365, 498, 309, 10672, 382, 257, 6787, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357209705171132, "compression_ratio": 1.7228915662650603, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378118921160032e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 191060, "start": 1919.3999999999999, "end": 1922.58, "text": " To do that, you have to move from observation to causation.", "tokens": [50805, 1407, 360, 300, 11, 291, 362, 281, 1286, 490, 14816, 281, 3302, 399, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357209705171132, "compression_ratio": 1.7228915662650603, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378118921160032e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 191060, "start": 1922.9599999999998, "end": 1926.9599999999998, "text": " And causation is notoriously difficult to prove in complex systems", "tokens": [50983, 400, 3302, 399, 307, 46772, 8994, 2252, 281, 7081, 294, 3997, 3652, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357209705171132, "compression_ratio": 1.7228915662650603, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378118921160032e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 191060, "start": 1926.9599999999998, "end": 1928.5, "text": " because everything is connected.", "tokens": [51183, 570, 1203, 307, 4582, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357209705171132, "compression_ratio": 1.7228915662650603, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378118921160032e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 191060, "start": 1928.9199999999998, "end": 1930.58, "text": " If you change one thing, you change everything.", "tokens": [51281, 759, 291, 1319, 472, 551, 11, 291, 1319, 1203, 13, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357209705171132, "compression_ratio": 1.7228915662650603, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378118921160032e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 191060, "start": 1930.8999999999999, "end": 1932.86, "text": " And it's hard to isolate what caused what.", "tokens": [51380, 400, 309, 311, 1152, 281, 25660, 437, 7008, 437, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357209705171132, "compression_ratio": 1.7228915662650603, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378118921160032e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 191060, "start": 1933.56, "end": 1935.2199999999998, "text": " The butterfly effect ruins everything.", "tokens": [51513, 440, 22140, 1802, 24747, 1203, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357209705171132, "compression_ratio": 1.7228915662650603, "no_speech_prob": 1.4378118921160032e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 193522, "start": 1935.22, "end": 1939.2, "text": " To solve this, they use something called a counterfactual intervention framework.", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 5039, 341, 11, 436, 764, 746, 1219, 257, 5682, 44919, 901, 13176, 8388, 13, 50564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17803021385556175, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158182005258313e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 193522, "start": 1940.02, "end": 1943.28, "text": " Specifically, the common random numbers paired simulation.", "tokens": [50605, 26058, 11, 264, 2689, 4974, 3547, 25699, 16575, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17803021385556175, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158182005258313e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 193522, "start": 1943.74, "end": 1947.2, "text": " This is one of the most powerful tools in stochastic simulation.", "tokens": [50791, 639, 307, 472, 295, 264, 881, 4005, 3873, 294, 342, 8997, 2750, 16575, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17803021385556175, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158182005258313e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 193522, "start": 1947.34, "end": 1948.16, "text": " How does it work?", "tokens": [50971, 1012, 775, 309, 589, 30, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17803021385556175, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158182005258313e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 193522, "start": 1948.58, "end": 1952.6200000000001, "text": " Imagine you have a simulation running, and at a specific moment, you pause it.", "tokens": [51033, 11739, 291, 362, 257, 16575, 2614, 11, 293, 412, 257, 2685, 1623, 11, 291, 10465, 309, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17803021385556175, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158182005258313e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 193522, "start": 1953.18, "end": 1955.64, "text": " You take the entire state of that universe,", "tokens": [51263, 509, 747, 264, 2302, 1785, 295, 300, 6445, 11, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17803021385556175, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158182005258313e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 193522, "start": 1956.08, "end": 1960.0, "text": " the exact position and velocity of every single microscopic bumper car,", "tokens": [51408, 264, 1900, 2535, 293, 9269, 295, 633, 2167, 47897, 23992, 1032, 11, 51604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17803021385556175, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158182005258313e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 193522, "start": 1960.32, "end": 1961.6000000000001, "text": " and you clone it perfectly.", "tokens": [51620, 293, 291, 26506, 309, 6239, 13, 51684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17803021385556175, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158182005258313e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 196160, "start": 1961.6, "end": 1964.8, "text": " You now have two identical parallel universes.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 586, 362, 732, 14800, 8952, 50168, 13, 50525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18393469948805016, "compression_ratio": 1.760797342192691, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204291798636698e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 196160, "start": 1965.2199999999998, "end": 1966.34, "text": " Universe A and Universe B.", "tokens": [50546, 18307, 316, 293, 18307, 363, 13, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18393469948805016, "compression_ratio": 1.760797342192691, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204291798636698e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 196160, "start": 1966.4199999999998, "end": 1970.5, "text": " In Universe A, the control branch, you just press play and let it keep running exactly as it was.", "tokens": [50606, 682, 18307, 316, 11, 264, 1969, 9819, 11, 291, 445, 1886, 862, 293, 718, 309, 1066, 2614, 2293, 382, 309, 390, 13, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18393469948805016, "compression_ratio": 1.760797342192691, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204291798636698e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 196160, "start": 1971.08, "end": 1972.5, "text": " In Universe B, the treatment branch,", "tokens": [50839, 682, 18307, 363, 11, 264, 5032, 9819, 11, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18393469948805016, "compression_ratio": 1.760797342192691, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204291798636698e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 196160, "start": 1972.8799999999999, "end": 1976.2199999999998, "text": " you reach in like a god and apply a localized activity pulse.", "tokens": [50929, 291, 2524, 294, 411, 257, 3044, 293, 3079, 257, 44574, 5191, 17709, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18393469948805016, "compression_ratio": 1.760797342192691, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204291798636698e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 196160, "start": 1976.6799999999998, "end": 1978.4399999999998, "text": " You pick a physical spot on the table,", "tokens": [51119, 509, 1888, 257, 4001, 4008, 322, 264, 3199, 11, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18393469948805016, "compression_ratio": 1.760797342192691, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204291798636698e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 196160, "start": 1978.7199999999998, "end": 1980.1399999999999, "text": " and for a short window of time,", "tokens": [51221, 293, 337, 257, 2099, 4910, 295, 565, 11, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18393469948805016, "compression_ratio": 1.760797342192691, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204291798636698e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 196160, "start": 1980.32, "end": 1983.76, "text": " you crank up the propulsion speed of the particles in that specific radius.", "tokens": [51301, 291, 21263, 493, 264, 49375, 3073, 295, 264, 10007, 294, 300, 2685, 15845, 13, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18393469948805016, "compression_ratio": 1.760797342192691, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204291798636698e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 196160, "start": 1984.1799999999998, "end": 1988.86, "text": " Then crucially, you resume both universes using identical random number seeds.", "tokens": [51494, 1396, 5140, 1909, 11, 291, 15358, 1293, 50168, 1228, 14800, 4974, 1230, 9203, 13, 51728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18393469948805016, "compression_ratio": 1.760797342192691, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204291798636698e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 196160, "start": 1989.28, "end": 1991.32, "text": " Wait, why identical random seeds?", "tokens": [51749, 3802, 11, 983, 14800, 4974, 9203, 30, 51851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18393469948805016, "compression_ratio": 1.760797342192691, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204291798636698e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 199132, "start": 1991.8, "end": 1994.22, "text": " Don't random numbers dictate the thermal noise,", "tokens": [50389, 1468, 380, 4974, 3547, 36071, 264, 15070, 5658, 11, 50510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19535400828377145, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080450552195425e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 199132, "start": 1994.36, "end": 1997.04, "text": " the subtle little random bumps the particles experience?", "tokens": [50517, 264, 13743, 707, 4974, 27719, 264, 10007, 1752, 30, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19535400828377145, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080450552195425e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 199132, "start": 1997.4399999999998, "end": 2000.26, "text": " If you keep them the same, aren't you eliminating the chaos?", "tokens": [50671, 759, 291, 1066, 552, 264, 912, 11, 3212, 380, 291, 31203, 264, 14158, 30, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19535400828377145, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080450552195425e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 199132, "start": 2000.52, "end": 2002.74, "text": " No, you are isolating the causation.", "tokens": [50825, 883, 11, 291, 366, 48912, 264, 3302, 399, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19535400828377145, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080450552195425e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 199132, "start": 2003.28, "end": 2004.8999999999999, "text": " If the random seeds were different,", "tokens": [50963, 759, 264, 4974, 9203, 645, 819, 11, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19535400828377145, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080450552195425e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 199132, "start": 2005.02, "end": 2008.8999999999999, "text": " the two universes would slowly drift apart just from background thermal noise.", "tokens": [51050, 264, 732, 50168, 576, 5692, 19699, 4936, 445, 490, 3678, 15070, 5658, 13, 51244], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19535400828377145, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080450552195425e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 199132, "start": 2009.56, "end": 2010.9199999999998, "text": " Within a few thousand frames,", "tokens": [51277, 15996, 257, 1326, 4714, 12083, 11, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19535400828377145, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080450552195425e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 199132, "start": 2011.2, "end": 2012.98, "text": " the butterfly effect would take over,", "tokens": [51359, 264, 22140, 1802, 576, 747, 670, 11, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19535400828377145, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080450552195425e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 199132, "start": 2013.32, "end": 2015.6799999999998, "text": " and the two universes would look completely different.", "tokens": [51465, 293, 264, 732, 50168, 576, 574, 2584, 819, 13, 51583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19535400828377145, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080450552195425e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 199132, "start": 2016.1399999999999, "end": 2019.98, "text": " You wouldn't know if a difference was due to your poke or just random chance.", "tokens": [51606, 509, 2759, 380, 458, 498, 257, 2649, 390, 3462, 281, 428, 19712, 420, 445, 4974, 2931, 13, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19535400828377145, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080450552195425e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 201998, "start": 2019.98, "end": 2024.44, "text": " By forcing the random number generators to be a bit identical,", "tokens": [50365, 3146, 19030, 264, 4974, 1230, 38662, 281, 312, 257, 857, 14800, 11, 50588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2072544787303511, "compression_ratio": 1.6069868995633187, "no_speech_prob": 2.2363953137288783e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 201998, "start": 2025.02, "end": 2027.52, "text": " you guarantee that if you apply zero perturbation,", "tokens": [50617, 291, 10815, 300, 498, 291, 3079, 4018, 40468, 399, 11, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2072544787303511, "compression_ratio": 1.6069868995633187, "no_speech_prob": 2.2363953137288783e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 201998, "start": 2027.94, "end": 2031.52, "text": " Universe A and Universe B remain perfectly synchronized forever.", "tokens": [50763, 18307, 316, 293, 18307, 363, 6222, 6239, 19331, 1602, 5680, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2072544787303511, "compression_ratio": 1.6069868995633187, "no_speech_prob": 2.2363953137288783e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 201998, "start": 2031.96, "end": 2034.8, "text": " Therefore, if you do apply a perturbation to Universe B,", "tokens": [50964, 7504, 11, 498, 291, 360, 3079, 257, 40468, 399, 281, 18307, 363, 11, 51106], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2072544787303511, "compression_ratio": 1.6069868995633187, "no_speech_prob": 2.2363953137288783e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 201998, "start": 2035.1, "end": 2040.14, "text": " any divergence between the two universes is strictly 100% caused by your intervention.", "tokens": [51121, 604, 47387, 1296, 264, 732, 50168, 307, 20792, 2319, 4, 7008, 538, 428, 13176, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2072544787303511, "compression_ratio": 1.6069868995633187, "no_speech_prob": 2.2363953137288783e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 201998, "start": 2040.72, "end": 2042.66, "text": " It strips away the background noise entirely.", "tokens": [51402, 467, 19842, 1314, 264, 3678, 5658, 7696, 13, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2072544787303511, "compression_ratio": 1.6069868995633187, "no_speech_prob": 2.2363953137288783e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 204266, "start": 2042.66, "end": 2045.74, "text": " It is the ultimate clean laboratory experiment.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 9705, 2541, 16523, 5120, 13, 50519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874976269034452, "compression_ratio": 1.6182572614107884, "no_speech_prob": 1.6479991199816468e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 204266, "start": 2046.48, "end": 2049.48, "text": " They use variations of this in quantitative finance and weather modeling", "tokens": [50556, 814, 764, 17840, 295, 341, 294, 27778, 10719, 293, 5503, 15983, 50706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874976269034452, "compression_ratio": 1.6182572614107884, "no_speech_prob": 1.6479991199816468e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 204266, "start": 2049.48, "end": 2053.76, "text": " to isolate the effect of a single variable in chaotic environments.", "tokens": [50706, 281, 25660, 264, 1802, 295, 257, 2167, 7006, 294, 27013, 12388, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874976269034452, "compression_ratio": 1.6182572614107884, "no_speech_prob": 1.6479991199816468e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 204266, "start": 2054.14, "end": 2056.36, "text": " So they build this dual universe machine,", "tokens": [50939, 407, 436, 1322, 341, 11848, 6445, 3479, 11, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874976269034452, "compression_ratio": 1.6182572614107884, "no_speech_prob": 1.6479991199816468e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 204266, "start": 2056.58, "end": 2060.88, "text": " they get ready to test if different capacity regions react differently to being poked,", "tokens": [51061, 436, 483, 1919, 281, 1500, 498, 819, 6042, 10682, 4515, 7614, 281, 885, 280, 9511, 11, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874976269034452, "compression_ratio": 1.6182572614107884, "no_speech_prob": 1.6479991199816468e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 204266, "start": 2061.3, "end": 2063.48, "text": " and, well, they find another massive bug.", "tokens": [51297, 293, 11, 731, 11, 436, 915, 1071, 5994, 7426, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874976269034452, "compression_ratio": 1.6182572614107884, "no_speech_prob": 1.6479991199816468e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 204266, "start": 2063.64, "end": 2065.0, "text": " The intervention timing error.", "tokens": [51414, 440, 13176, 10822, 6713, 13, 51482], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874976269034452, "compression_ratio": 1.6182572614107884, "no_speech_prob": 1.6479991199816468e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 206500, "start": 2065.0, "end": 2069.2, "text": " This one is a chilling reminder of how easily software can lie to you.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 472, 307, 257, 31047, 13548, 295, 577, 3612, 4722, 393, 4544, 281, 291, 13, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20185805569175913, "compression_ratio": 1.6870503597122302, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832767376825155e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 206500, "start": 2069.52, "end": 2072.62, "text": " So they set up the perturbation to happen for a short window,", "tokens": [50591, 407, 436, 992, 493, 264, 40468, 399, 281, 1051, 337, 257, 2099, 4910, 11, 50746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20185805569175913, "compression_ratio": 1.6870503597122302, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832767376825155e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 206500, "start": 2072.82, "end": 2074.36, "text": " say, two time units.", "tokens": [50756, 584, 11, 732, 565, 6815, 13, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20185805569175913, "compression_ratio": 1.6870503597122302, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832767376825155e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 206500, "start": 2074.72, "end": 2076.34, "text": " But when they looked at the output,", "tokens": [50851, 583, 562, 436, 2956, 412, 264, 5598, 11, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20185805569175913, "compression_ratio": 1.6870503597122302, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832767376825155e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 206500, "start": 2076.82, "end": 2079.32, "text": " the intervention literally never happened.", "tokens": [50956, 264, 13176, 3736, 1128, 2011, 13, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20185805569175913, "compression_ratio": 1.6870503597122302, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832767376825155e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 206500, "start": 2079.44, "end": 2080.46, "text": " The pulse never fired.", "tokens": [51087, 440, 17709, 1128, 11777, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20185805569175913, "compression_ratio": 1.6870503597122302, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832767376825155e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 206500, "start": 2080.46, "end": 2080.74, "text": " And on.", "tokens": [51138, 400, 322, 13, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20185805569175913, "compression_ratio": 1.6870503597122302, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832767376825155e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 206500, "start": 2081.04, "end": 2083.74, "text": " Because the code was evaluating the perturbation window", "tokens": [51167, 1436, 264, 3089, 390, 27479, 264, 40468, 399, 4910, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20185805569175913, "compression_ratio": 1.6870503597122302, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832767376825155e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 206500, "start": 2083.74, "end": 2087.1, "text": " against the simulation state's absolute internal clock", "tokens": [51302, 1970, 264, 16575, 1785, 311, 8236, 6920, 7830, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20185805569175913, "compression_ratio": 1.6870503597122302, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832767376825155e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 206500, "start": 2087.1, "end": 2090.86, "text": " instead of the elapsed time since the counterfactual experiment began.", "tokens": [51470, 2602, 295, 264, 806, 2382, 292, 565, 1670, 264, 5682, 44919, 901, 5120, 4283, 13, 51658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20185805569175913, "compression_ratio": 1.6870503597122302, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832767376825155e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 206500, "start": 2091.14, "end": 2092.14, "text": " To put that in context,", "tokens": [51672, 1407, 829, 300, 294, 4319, 11, 51722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20185805569175913, "compression_ratio": 1.6870503597122302, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832767376825155e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 209214, "start": 2092.14, "end": 2093.66, "text": " before you run these experiments,", "tokens": [50365, 949, 291, 1190, 613, 12050, 11, 50441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612659934517387, "compression_ratio": 1.7491961414790997, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 209214, "start": 2093.92, "end": 2096.7, "text": " you have to let the simulation burn in or equilibrate.", "tokens": [50454, 291, 362, 281, 718, 264, 16575, 5064, 294, 420, 14204, 4404, 13, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612659934517387, "compression_ratio": 1.7491961414790997, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 209214, "start": 2096.8599999999997, "end": 2096.96, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50601, 865, 13, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612659934517387, "compression_ratio": 1.7491961414790997, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 209214, "start": 2097.02, "end": 2099.08, "text": " You let the bumper cars drive around for a long time", "tokens": [50609, 509, 718, 264, 23992, 5163, 3332, 926, 337, 257, 938, 565, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612659934517387, "compression_ratio": 1.7491961414790997, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 209214, "start": 2099.08, "end": 2100.8399999999997, "text": " so they reach a natural chaotic state.", "tokens": [50712, 370, 436, 2524, 257, 3303, 27013, 1785, 13, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612659934517387, "compression_ratio": 1.7491961414790997, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 209214, "start": 2100.96, "end": 2101.12, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50806, 865, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612659934517387, "compression_ratio": 1.7491961414790997, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 209214, "start": 2101.24, "end": 2104.7, "text": " So the internal absolute clock might be at time equals 100,000.", "tokens": [50820, 407, 264, 6920, 8236, 7830, 1062, 312, 412, 565, 6915, 2319, 11, 1360, 13, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612659934517387, "compression_ratio": 1.7491961414790997, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 209214, "start": 2105.1, "end": 2108.56, "text": " But the paired experiment is just starting at relative time equals zero.", "tokens": [51013, 583, 264, 25699, 5120, 307, 445, 2891, 412, 4972, 565, 6915, 4018, 13, 51186], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612659934517387, "compression_ratio": 1.7491961414790997, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 209214, "start": 2108.96, "end": 2109.8199999999997, "text": " The code was saying,", "tokens": [51206, 440, 3089, 390, 1566, 11, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612659934517387, "compression_ratio": 1.7491961414790997, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 209214, "start": 2110.2599999999998, "end": 2112.98, "text": " activate the pulse between time zero and time two.", "tokens": [51271, 13615, 264, 17709, 1296, 565, 4018, 293, 565, 732, 13, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612659934517387, "compression_ratio": 1.7491961414790997, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 209214, "start": 2113.54, "end": 2117.04, "text": " But the universe's absolute clock was already at 100,000.", "tokens": [51435, 583, 264, 6445, 311, 8236, 7830, 390, 1217, 412, 2319, 11, 1360, 13, 51610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612659934517387, "compression_ratio": 1.7491961414790997, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 209214, "start": 2117.52, "end": 2119.2999999999997, "text": " It missed the window by millennia.", "tokens": [51634, 467, 6721, 264, 4910, 538, 21362, 654, 13, 51723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612659934517387, "compression_ratio": 1.7491961414790997, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 209214, "start": 2119.2999999999997, "end": 2121.8199999999997, "text": " It's like setting a kitchen timer to bake a cake.", "tokens": [51723, 467, 311, 411, 3287, 257, 6525, 19247, 281, 16562, 257, 5908, 13, 51849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612659934517387, "compression_ratio": 1.7491961414790997, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 212214, "start": 2122.14, "end": 2126.02, "text": " But the timer is somehow wired to the year the oven was manufactured in a factory", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 19247, 307, 6063, 27415, 281, 264, 1064, 264, 9090, 390, 25738, 294, 257, 9265, 50559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15693950653076172, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555065695048055e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 212214, "start": 2126.02, "end": 2127.94, "text": " instead of the moment you put the cake in.", "tokens": [50559, 2602, 295, 264, 1623, 291, 829, 264, 5908, 294, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15693950653076172, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555065695048055e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 212214, "start": 2128.46, "end": 2130.6, "text": " Bake for 30 minutes starting in 2014?", "tokens": [50681, 42597, 337, 2217, 2077, 2891, 294, 8227, 30, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15693950653076172, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555065695048055e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 212214, "start": 2131.1, "end": 2133.9, "text": " Well, it's 2026, so the oven never turns on.", "tokens": [50813, 1042, 11, 309, 311, 945, 10880, 11, 370, 264, 9090, 1128, 4523, 322, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15693950653076172, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555065695048055e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 212214, "start": 2134.12, "end": 2137.06, "text": " That analogy perfectly captures the absurdity of the bug.", "tokens": [50964, 663, 21663, 6239, 27986, 264, 19774, 507, 295, 264, 7426, 13, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15693950653076172, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555065695048055e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 212214, "start": 2137.24, "end": 2138.3799999999997, "text": " And how did they catch this?", "tokens": [51120, 400, 577, 630, 436, 3745, 341, 30, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15693950653076172, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555065695048055e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 212214, "start": 2138.64, "end": 2141.08, "text": " Because all of their automated validation tests", "tokens": [51190, 1436, 439, 295, 641, 18473, 24071, 6921, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15693950653076172, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555065695048055e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 212214, "start": 2141.08, "end": 2145.52, "text": " used freshly initialized states where the absolute internal clock was zero.", "tokens": [51312, 1143, 34412, 5883, 1602, 4368, 689, 264, 8236, 6920, 7830, 390, 4018, 13, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15693950653076172, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555065695048055e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 212214, "start": 2146.02, "end": 2148.9, "text": " So the bug was completely invisible during automated testing.", "tokens": [51559, 407, 264, 7426, 390, 2584, 14603, 1830, 18473, 4997, 13, 51703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15693950653076172, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555065695048055e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 214890, "start": 2148.9, "end": 2150.1, "text": " So how did they find it?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 577, 630, 436, 915, 309, 30, 50425], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541042804718018, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967498149029648e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 214890, "start": 2150.32, "end": 2153.32, "text": " They only caught it because they manually looked at the particle positions", "tokens": [50436, 814, 787, 5415, 309, 570, 436, 16945, 2956, 412, 264, 12359, 8432, 50586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541042804718018, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967498149029648e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 214890, "start": 2153.32, "end": 2155.84, "text": " of treatment and control branches after a real run", "tokens": [50586, 295, 5032, 293, 1969, 14770, 934, 257, 957, 1190, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541042804718018, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967498149029648e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 214890, "start": 2155.84, "end": 2157.76, "text": " and noticed they were a bit identical.", "tokens": [50712, 293, 5694, 436, 645, 257, 857, 14800, 13, 50808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541042804718018, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967498149029648e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 214890, "start": 2157.9, "end": 2160.6, "text": " If they were a bit identical, the intervention had zero effect.", "tokens": [50815, 759, 436, 645, 257, 857, 14800, 11, 264, 13176, 632, 4018, 1802, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541042804718018, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967498149029648e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 214890, "start": 2160.78, "end": 2161.5, "text": " It never fired.", "tokens": [50959, 467, 1128, 11777, 13, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541042804718018, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967498149029648e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 214890, "start": 2161.64, "end": 2165.48, "text": " This is a profound lesson for anyone doing computational causal inference.", "tokens": [51002, 639, 307, 257, 14382, 6898, 337, 2878, 884, 28270, 38755, 38253, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541042804718018, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967498149029648e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 214890, "start": 2166.42, "end": 2169.88, "text": " An inactive intervention, a bug where your code does nothing,", "tokens": [51241, 1107, 294, 12596, 13176, 11, 257, 7426, 689, 428, 3089, 775, 1825, 11, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541042804718018, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967498149029648e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 214890, "start": 2170.28, "end": 2174.02, "text": " and a genuinely null causal effect look exactly the same on a spreadsheet.", "tokens": [51434, 293, 257, 17839, 18184, 38755, 1802, 574, 2293, 264, 912, 322, 257, 27733, 13, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13541042804718018, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967498149029648e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 217402, "start": 2174.02, "end": 2176.98, "text": " Both return a divergence of zero.", "tokens": [50365, 6767, 2736, 257, 47387, 295, 4018, 13, 50513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18192066656094846, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920880065689591e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 217402, "start": 2177.44, "end": 2178.4, "text": " That is terrifying.", "tokens": [50536, 663, 307, 18106, 13, 50584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18192066656094846, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920880065689591e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 217402, "start": 2179.28, "end": 2183.98, "text": " It means you could write a paper claiming variable X has no causal effect on variable Y", "tokens": [50628, 467, 1355, 291, 727, 2464, 257, 3035, 19232, 7006, 1783, 575, 572, 38755, 1802, 322, 7006, 398, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18192066656094846, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920880065689591e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 217402, "start": 2183.98, "end": 2186.96, "text": " and be completely wrong just because your code was broken.", "tokens": [50863, 293, 312, 2584, 2085, 445, 570, 428, 3089, 390, 5463, 13, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18192066656094846, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920880065689591e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 217402, "start": 2187.16, "end": 2191.54, "text": " The only way to prove your null result is real is to run a positive control check.", "tokens": [51022, 440, 787, 636, 281, 7081, 428, 18184, 1874, 307, 957, 307, 281, 1190, 257, 3353, 1969, 1520, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18192066656094846, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920880065689591e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 217402, "start": 2191.7, "end": 2191.86, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51249, 865, 13, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18192066656094846, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920880065689591e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 217402, "start": 2191.94, "end": 2195.38, "text": " You have to prove that your poke is mechanically capable of doing something.", "tokens": [51261, 509, 362, 281, 7081, 300, 428, 19712, 307, 4236, 984, 8189, 295, 884, 746, 13, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18192066656094846, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920880065689591e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 217402, "start": 2195.66, "end": 2197.74, "text": " You have to prove the oven can actually turn on.", "tokens": [51447, 509, 362, 281, 7081, 264, 9090, 393, 767, 1261, 322, 13, 51551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18192066656094846, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920880065689591e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 217402, "start": 2197.86, "end": 2198.16, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51557, 1779, 13, 51572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18192066656094846, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920880065689591e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 219816, "start": 2198.16, "end": 2202.66, "text": " So Flician fixed the relative clock bug, ran a massive perturbation,", "tokens": [50365, 407, 479, 1050, 952, 6806, 264, 4972, 7830, 7426, 11, 5872, 257, 5994, 40468, 399, 11, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15392153351395219, "compression_ratio": 1.6376811594202898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 219816, "start": 2203.02, "end": 2206.12, "text": " and confirmed that yes, blasting a region with high speed", "tokens": [50608, 293, 11341, 300, 2086, 11, 47134, 257, 4458, 365, 1090, 3073, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15392153351395219, "compression_ratio": 1.6376811594202898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 219816, "start": 2206.12, "end": 2209.2599999999998, "text": " causes the particles to rapidly evacuate that area", "tokens": [50763, 7700, 264, 10007, 281, 12910, 48570, 300, 1859, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15392153351395219, "compression_ratio": 1.6376811594202898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 219816, "start": 2209.2599999999998, "end": 2214.06, "text": " and leaves a permanent measurable scar on the global density of the system.", "tokens": [50920, 293, 5510, 257, 10996, 43615, 10569, 322, 264, 4338, 10305, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15392153351395219, "compression_ratio": 1.6376811594202898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 219816, "start": 2214.66, "end": 2216.96, "text": " The intervention framework was finally validated.", "tokens": [51190, 440, 13176, 8388, 390, 2721, 40693, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15392153351395219, "compression_ratio": 1.6376811594202898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 219816, "start": 2217.2599999999998, "end": 2219.14, "text": " The dual universe machine is fueled up.", "tokens": [51320, 440, 11848, 6445, 3479, 307, 45446, 493, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15392153351395219, "compression_ratio": 1.6376811594202898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 219816, "start": 2219.42, "end": 2220.2999999999997, "text": " The clock is fixed.", "tokens": [51428, 440, 7830, 307, 6806, 13, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15392153351395219, "compression_ratio": 1.6376811594202898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 219816, "start": 2220.48, "end": 2221.7, "text": " The positive control works.", "tokens": [51481, 440, 3353, 1969, 1985, 13, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15392153351395219, "compression_ratio": 1.6376811594202898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 219816, "start": 2222.18, "end": 2225.94, "text": " It is time for the final showdown, the matched region pilot.", "tokens": [51566, 467, 307, 565, 337, 264, 2572, 855, 5093, 11, 264, 21447, 4458, 9691, 13, 51754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15392153351395219, "compression_ratio": 1.6376811594202898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 222594, "start": 2225.94, "end": 2229.08, "text": " The premise here is classic experimental design.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 22045, 510, 307, 7230, 17069, 1715, 13, 50522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259912568379224, "compression_ratio": 1.713355048859935, "no_speech_prob": 1.394086994281618e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 222594, "start": 2229.84, "end": 2233.78, "text": " If we find two regions in the simulation that had the exact same starting density", "tokens": [50560, 759, 321, 915, 732, 10682, 294, 264, 16575, 300, 632, 264, 1900, 912, 2891, 10305, 50757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259912568379224, "compression_ratio": 1.713355048859935, "no_speech_prob": 1.394086994281618e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 222594, "start": 2233.78, "end": 2235.7400000000002, "text": " but very different capacity readings,", "tokens": [50757, 457, 588, 819, 6042, 27319, 11, 50855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259912568379224, "compression_ratio": 1.713355048859935, "no_speech_prob": 1.394086994281618e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 222594, "start": 2236.02, "end": 2238.6, "text": " and we hit them both with the exact same intervention pulse,", "tokens": [50869, 293, 321, 2045, 552, 1293, 365, 264, 1900, 912, 13176, 17709, 11, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259912568379224, "compression_ratio": 1.713355048859935, "no_speech_prob": 1.394086994281618e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 222594, "start": 2238.88, "end": 2239.98, "text": " do they react differently?", "tokens": [51012, 360, 436, 4515, 7614, 30, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259912568379224, "compression_ratio": 1.713355048859935, "no_speech_prob": 1.394086994281618e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 222594, "start": 2240.12, "end": 2243.88, "text": " Does the preexisting capacity predict the magnitude of the response to the poke?", "tokens": [51074, 4402, 264, 659, 36447, 6042, 6069, 264, 15668, 295, 264, 4134, 281, 264, 19712, 30, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259912568379224, "compression_ratio": 1.713355048859935, "no_speech_prob": 1.394086994281618e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 222594, "start": 2244.18, "end": 2247.68, "text": " If it does, then capacity isn't just a downstream observational metric.", "tokens": [51277, 759, 309, 775, 11, 550, 6042, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 30621, 9951, 1478, 20678, 13, 51452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259912568379224, "compression_ratio": 1.713355048859935, "no_speech_prob": 1.394086994281618e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 222594, "start": 2247.86, "end": 2250.66, "text": " It is a real causal driver of the system.", "tokens": [51461, 467, 307, 257, 957, 38755, 6787, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259912568379224, "compression_ratio": 1.713355048859935, "no_speech_prob": 1.394086994281618e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 222594, "start": 2251.02, "end": 2252.66, "text": " So they found four pairs of regions,", "tokens": [51619, 407, 436, 1352, 1451, 15494, 295, 10682, 11, 51701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259912568379224, "compression_ratio": 1.713355048859935, "no_speech_prob": 1.394086994281618e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 222594, "start": 2253.34, "end": 2255.16, "text": " matched them up carefully on density,", "tokens": [51735, 21447, 552, 493, 7500, 322, 10305, 11, 51826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17259912568379224, "compression_ratio": 1.713355048859935, "no_speech_prob": 1.394086994281618e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 225516, "start": 2255.16, "end": 2257.7999999999997, "text": " ran the interventions in the parallel universes,", "tokens": [50365, 5872, 264, 20924, 294, 264, 8952, 50168, 11, 50497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 225516, "start": 2258.12, "end": 2259.44, "text": " and measured the response.", "tokens": [50513, 293, 12690, 264, 4134, 13, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 225516, "start": 2259.62, "end": 2260.3599999999997, "text": " What were the results?", "tokens": [50588, 708, 645, 264, 3542, 30, 50625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 225516, "start": 2260.7, "end": 2262.5, "text": " It was explicitly inconclusive.", "tokens": [50642, 467, 390, 20803, 20972, 66, 7233, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 225516, "start": 2263.2999999999997, "end": 2264.2799999999997, "text": " Out of the four pairs,", "tokens": [50772, 5925, 295, 264, 1451, 15494, 11, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 225516, "start": 2264.72, "end": 2268.0, "text": " two pairs showed a stronger response in the high-capacity region.", "tokens": [50843, 732, 15494, 4712, 257, 7249, 4134, 294, 264, 1090, 12, 9485, 19008, 4458, 13, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 225516, "start": 2268.3399999999997, "end": 2271.68, "text": " The other two pairs showed a stronger response in the low-capacity region.", "tokens": [51024, 440, 661, 732, 15494, 4712, 257, 7249, 4134, 294, 264, 2295, 12, 9485, 19008, 4458, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 225516, "start": 2271.98, "end": 2273.2, "text": " It was a perfect coin toss.", "tokens": [51206, 467, 390, 257, 2176, 11464, 14432, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 225516, "start": 2273.3399999999997, "end": 2273.62, "text": " Wait.", "tokens": [51274, 3802, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 225516, "start": 2274.2999999999997, "end": 2275.52, "text": " We went through all of this,", "tokens": [51322, 492, 1437, 807, 439, 295, 341, 11, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 225516, "start": 2275.56, "end": 2276.46, "text": " the Euler explosions,", "tokens": [51385, 264, 462, 26318, 36872, 11, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 225516, "start": 2276.7, "end": 2277.66, "text": " the geometry artifacts,", "tokens": [51442, 264, 18426, 24617, 11, 51490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 225516, "start": 2277.96, "end": 2278.66, "text": " the time bugs,", "tokens": [51505, 264, 565, 15120, 11, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 225516, "start": 2278.7599999999998, "end": 2279.7799999999997, "text": " the parallel universes,", "tokens": [51545, 264, 8952, 50168, 11, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 225516, "start": 2279.98, "end": 2281.7999999999997, "text": " and the final answer is a coin toss.", "tokens": [51606, 293, 264, 2572, 1867, 307, 257, 11464, 14432, 13, 51697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19231187325936777, "compression_ratio": 1.9236947791164658, "no_speech_prob": 1.2743008688184676e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 228180, "start": 2281.8, "end": 2284.2200000000003, "text": " Why even publish this part if it settles nothing?", "tokens": [50365, 1545, 754, 11374, 341, 644, 498, 309, 5584, 904, 1825, 30, 50486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.183643943385074, "compression_ratio": 1.5483870967741935, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938696117460347e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 228180, "start": 2284.6400000000003, "end": 2286.1200000000003, "text": " Because of intellectual restraint.", "tokens": [50507, 1436, 295, 12576, 49281, 13, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.183643943385074, "compression_ratio": 1.5483870967741935, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938696117460347e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 228180, "start": 2287.1600000000003, "end": 2290.7400000000002, "text": " Four pairs from a single random seed is a tiny sample size.", "tokens": [50633, 7451, 15494, 490, 257, 2167, 4974, 8871, 307, 257, 5870, 6889, 2744, 13, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.183643943385074, "compression_ratio": 1.5483870967741935, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938696117460347e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 228180, "start": 2291.1600000000003, "end": 2292.04, "text": " It's a pilot study,", "tokens": [50833, 467, 311, 257, 9691, 2979, 11, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.183643943385074, "compression_ratio": 1.5483870967741935, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938696117460347e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 228180, "start": 2292.36, "end": 2293.6400000000003, "text": " an exploratory probe.", "tokens": [50893, 364, 24765, 4745, 22715, 13, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.183643943385074, "compression_ratio": 1.5483870967741935, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938696117460347e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 228180, "start": 2294.1800000000003, "end": 2298.5600000000004, "text": " Fliction explicitly writes that the absence of a consistent slope across these four pairs", "tokens": [50984, 3235, 4105, 20803, 13657, 300, 264, 17145, 295, 257, 8398, 13525, 2108, 613, 1451, 15494, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.183643943385074, "compression_ratio": 1.5483870967741935, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938696117460347e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 228180, "start": 2298.5600000000004, "end": 2299.88, "text": " is the honest finding.", "tokens": [51203, 307, 264, 3245, 5006, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.183643943385074, "compression_ratio": 1.5483870967741935, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938696117460347e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 228180, "start": 2300.26, "end": 2304.0600000000004, "text": " They aren't going to extrapolate four data points into a grand theory of everything.", "tokens": [51288, 814, 3212, 380, 516, 281, 48224, 473, 1451, 1412, 2793, 666, 257, 2697, 5261, 295, 1203, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.183643943385074, "compression_ratio": 1.5483870967741935, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938696117460347e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 230406, "start": 2304.06, "end": 2306.08, "text": " If they had over-claimed here,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 436, 632, 670, 12, 66, 22642, 510, 11, 50466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19378110903118728, "compression_ratio": 1.6528301886792454, "no_speech_prob": 1.927919629496344e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 230406, "start": 2306.64, "end": 2310.9, "text": " if they had tortured those four data points until they confessed to a causal link,", "tokens": [50494, 498, 436, 632, 36166, 729, 1451, 1412, 2793, 1826, 436, 41428, 281, 257, 38755, 2113, 11, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19378110903118728, "compression_ratio": 1.6528301886792454, "no_speech_prob": 1.927919629496344e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 230406, "start": 2311.32, "end": 2318.16, "text": " it would have ruined the integrity of the entire four-step identification criterion they built in the first essay.", "tokens": [50728, 309, 576, 362, 17013, 264, 16000, 295, 264, 2302, 1451, 12, 16792, 22065, 46691, 436, 3094, 294, 264, 700, 16238, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19378110903118728, "compression_ratio": 1.6528301886792454, "no_speech_prob": 1.927919629496344e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 230406, "start": 2318.2799999999997, "end": 2319.12, "text": " That makes a lot of sense.", "tokens": [51076, 663, 1669, 257, 688, 295, 2020, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19378110903118728, "compression_ratio": 1.6528301886792454, "no_speech_prob": 1.927919629496344e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 230406, "start": 2319.32, "end": 2319.7, "text": " Instead,", "tokens": [51128, 7156, 11, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19378110903118728, "compression_ratio": 1.6528301886792454, "no_speech_prob": 1.927919629496344e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 230406, "start": 2320.02, "end": 2322.0, "text": " they published the pilot as an open question,", "tokens": [51163, 436, 6572, 264, 9691, 382, 364, 1269, 1168, 11, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19378110903118728, "compression_ratio": 1.6528301886792454, "no_speech_prob": 1.927919629496344e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 230406, "start": 2322.4, "end": 2324.82, "text": " and they provided a completely mapped roadmap", "tokens": [51282, 293, 436, 5649, 257, 2584, 33318, 35738, 51403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19378110903118728, "compression_ratio": 1.6528301886792454, "no_speech_prob": 1.927919629496344e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 230406, "start": 2324.82, "end": 2326.2999999999997, "text": " for how a future,", "tokens": [51403, 337, 577, 257, 2027, 11, 51477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19378110903118728, "compression_ratio": 1.6528301886792454, "no_speech_prob": 1.927919629496344e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 230406, "start": 2326.82, "end": 2329.68, "text": " properly powered study with hundreds of pairs", "tokens": [51503, 6108, 17786, 2979, 365, 6779, 295, 15494, 51646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19378110903118728, "compression_ratio": 1.6528301886792454, "no_speech_prob": 1.927919629496344e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 230406, "start": 2329.68, "end": 2330.94, "text": " must be designed.", "tokens": [51646, 1633, 312, 4761, 13, 51709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19378110903118728, "compression_ratio": 1.6528301886792454, "no_speech_prob": 1.927919629496344e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 233094, "start": 2330.94, "end": 2332.36, "text": " More importantly,", "tokens": [50365, 5048, 8906, 11, 50436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16453669287941672, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759258469530637e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 233094, "start": 2332.56, "end": 2336.06, "text": " they found a massive trap waiting for whoever does that future study.", "tokens": [50446, 436, 1352, 257, 5994, 11487, 3806, 337, 11387, 775, 300, 2027, 2979, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16453669287941672, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759258469530637e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 233094, "start": 2336.48, "end": 2337.96, "text": " The anti-correlation problem.", "tokens": [50642, 440, 6061, 12, 19558, 4419, 399, 1154, 13, 50716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16453669287941672, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759258469530637e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 233094, "start": 2338.14, "end": 2338.36, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50725, 1079, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16453669287941672, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759258469530637e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 233094, "start": 2339.14, "end": 2339.76, "text": " In the pilot,", "tokens": [50775, 682, 264, 9691, 11, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16453669287941672, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759258469530637e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 233094, "start": 2339.98, "end": 2342.42, "text": " they discovered that local density and local capacity", "tokens": [50817, 436, 6941, 300, 2654, 10305, 293, 2654, 6042, 50939], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16453669287941672, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759258469530637e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 233094, "start": 2342.42, "end": 2344.44, "text": " were consistently anti-correlated.", "tokens": [50939, 645, 14961, 6061, 12, 19558, 12004, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16453669287941672, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759258469530637e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 233094, "start": 2344.88, "end": 2347.36, "text": " Places with high density naturally had low capacity,", "tokens": [51062, 2149, 2116, 365, 1090, 10305, 8195, 632, 2295, 6042, 11, 51186], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16453669287941672, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759258469530637e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 233094, "start": 2347.78, "end": 2348.38, "text": " and vice versa.", "tokens": [51207, 293, 11964, 25650, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16453669287941672, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759258469530637e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 233094, "start": 2348.66, "end": 2349.68, "text": " Why does that break the study?", "tokens": [51251, 1545, 775, 300, 1821, 264, 2979, 30, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16453669287941672, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759258469530637e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 233094, "start": 2349.94, "end": 2352.4, "text": " Because the whole point of a matched region study,", "tokens": [51315, 1436, 264, 1379, 935, 295, 257, 21447, 4458, 2979, 11, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16453669287941672, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759258469530637e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 233094, "start": 2352.56, "end": 2354.3, "text": " like a propensity score matching in medicine,", "tokens": [51446, 411, 257, 2365, 6859, 6175, 14324, 294, 7195, 11, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16453669287941672, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759258469530637e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 233094, "start": 2354.58, "end": 2357.44, "text": " is to compare two subjects that are identical in every way", "tokens": [51547, 307, 281, 6794, 732, 13066, 300, 366, 14800, 294, 633, 636, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16453669287941672, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759258469530637e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 233094, "start": 2357.44, "end": 2358.64, "text": " except for the treatment variable.", "tokens": [51690, 3993, 337, 264, 5032, 7006, 13, 51750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16453669287941672, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759258469530637e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 235864, "start": 2358.64, "end": 2362.3799999999997, "text": " You want to compare two regions with the same density but different capacities.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 528, 281, 6794, 732, 10682, 365, 264, 912, 10305, 457, 819, 39396, 13, 50552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19913724490574428, "compression_ratio": 1.6068702290076335, "no_speech_prob": 1.898040101824816e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 235864, "start": 2363.0, "end": 2364.92, "text": " If they are naturally anti-correlated,", "tokens": [50583, 759, 436, 366, 8195, 6061, 12, 19558, 12004, 11, 50679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19913724490574428, "compression_ratio": 1.6068702290076335, "no_speech_prob": 1.898040101824816e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 235864, "start": 2365.3199999999997, "end": 2367.0, "text": " finding a match is incredibly hard.", "tokens": [50699, 5006, 257, 2995, 307, 6252, 1152, 13, 50783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19913724490574428, "compression_ratio": 1.6068702290076335, "no_speech_prob": 1.898040101824816e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 235864, "start": 2367.3399999999997, "end": 2367.58, "text": " Ugh.", "tokens": [50800, 16506, 13, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19913724490574428, "compression_ratio": 1.6068702290076335, "no_speech_prob": 1.898040101824816e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 235864, "start": 2368.3799999999997, "end": 2372.4, "text": " It's like trying to study the effect of a new diet by finding identical twins,", "tokens": [50852, 467, 311, 411, 1382, 281, 2979, 264, 1802, 295, 257, 777, 6339, 538, 5006, 14800, 22555, 11, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19913724490574428, "compression_ratio": 1.6068702290076335, "no_speech_prob": 1.898040101824816e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 235864, "start": 2372.66, "end": 2374.06, "text": " but discovering that naturally,", "tokens": [51066, 457, 24773, 300, 8195, 11, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19913724490574428, "compression_ratio": 1.6068702290076335, "no_speech_prob": 1.898040101824816e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 235864, "start": 2374.2799999999997, "end": 2375.7, "text": " if one twin eats the diet,", "tokens": [51147, 498, 472, 18397, 18109, 264, 6339, 11, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19913724490574428, "compression_ratio": 1.6068702290076335, "no_speech_prob": 1.898040101824816e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 235864, "start": 2376.02, "end": 2377.56, "text": " the other twin physically cannot.", "tokens": [51234, 264, 661, 18397, 9762, 2644, 13, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19913724490574428, "compression_ratio": 1.6068702290076335, "no_speech_prob": 1.898040101824816e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 235864, "start": 2378.08, "end": 2380.1, "text": " You are forced to look at extreme,", "tokens": [51337, 509, 366, 7579, 281, 574, 412, 8084, 11, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19913724490574428, "compression_ratio": 1.6068702290076335, "no_speech_prob": 1.898040101824816e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 235864, "start": 2380.46, "end": 2383.12, "text": " weird outliers of the system to find a match.", "tokens": [51456, 3657, 484, 23646, 295, 264, 1185, 281, 915, 257, 2995, 13, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19913724490574428, "compression_ratio": 1.6068702290076335, "no_speech_prob": 1.898040101824816e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 235864, "start": 2383.3199999999997, "end": 2383.8599999999997, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51599, 7587, 13, 51626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19913724490574428, "compression_ratio": 1.6068702290076335, "no_speech_prob": 1.898040101824816e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 238386, "start": 2383.86, "end": 2387.02, "text": " If you just naively run an automated matching algorithm,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 445, 1667, 3413, 1190, 364, 18473, 14324, 9284, 11, 50523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433158311687532, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351623168489818e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 238386, "start": 2387.46, "end": 2389.28, "text": " it's going to scour the simulation,", "tokens": [50545, 309, 311, 516, 281, 795, 396, 264, 16575, 11, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433158311687532, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351623168489818e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 238386, "start": 2390.0, "end": 2393.1400000000003, "text": " find two complete freak anomalies that happen to match,", "tokens": [50672, 915, 732, 3566, 21853, 24769, 48872, 300, 1051, 281, 2995, 11, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433158311687532, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351623168489818e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 238386, "start": 2393.48, "end": 2395.32, "text": " and pretend it's a normal comparison.", "tokens": [50846, 293, 11865, 309, 311, 257, 2710, 9660, 13, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433158311687532, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351623168489818e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 238386, "start": 2395.48, "end": 2397.3, "text": " You aren't comparing the normal physics anymore.", "tokens": [50946, 509, 3212, 380, 15763, 264, 2710, 10649, 3602, 13, 51037], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433158311687532, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351623168489818e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 238386, "start": 2397.42, "end": 2398.44, "text": " You're comparing the edge cases.", "tokens": [51043, 509, 434, 15763, 264, 4691, 3331, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433158311687532, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351623168489818e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 238386, "start": 2398.54, "end": 2400.7000000000003, "text": " You are extrapolating rather than interpolating.", "tokens": [51099, 509, 366, 48224, 990, 2831, 813, 44902, 990, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433158311687532, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351623168489818e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 238386, "start": 2401.02, "end": 2403.86, "text": " If you only find twins by looking at circus performers,", "tokens": [51223, 759, 291, 787, 915, 22555, 538, 1237, 412, 32155, 30768, 11, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433158311687532, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351623168489818e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 238386, "start": 2404.06, "end": 2406.06, "text": " your study doesn't apply to the general public.", "tokens": [51375, 428, 2979, 1177, 380, 3079, 281, 264, 2674, 1908, 13, 51475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433158311687532, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351623168489818e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 238386, "start": 2406.2000000000003, "end": 2407.54, "text": " By publishing this pilot,", "tokens": [51482, 3146, 17832, 341, 9691, 11, 51549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433158311687532, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351623168489818e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 238386, "start": 2407.7400000000002, "end": 2409.48, "text": " Flixian warns the future researcher", "tokens": [51559, 3235, 970, 952, 12286, 82, 264, 2027, 21751, 51646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1433158311687532, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351623168489818e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 240948, "start": 2409.48, "end": 2412.22, "text": " that they must use common support diagnostics.", "tokens": [50365, 300, 436, 1633, 764, 2689, 1406, 43215, 1167, 13, 50502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1697676522391183, "compression_ratio": 1.6823104693140793, "no_speech_prob": 1.83979459271455e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 240948, "start": 2412.86, "end": 2416.22, "text": " They must ensure they are comparing apples to apples in the normal domain,", "tokens": [50534, 814, 1633, 5586, 436, 366, 15763, 16814, 281, 16814, 294, 264, 2710, 9274, 11, 50702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1697676522391183, "compression_ratio": 1.6823104693140793, "no_speech_prob": 1.83979459271455e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 240948, "start": 2416.68, "end": 2418.18, "text": " not the anomalous fringes.", "tokens": [50725, 406, 264, 24769, 11553, 431, 278, 279, 13, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1697676522391183, "compression_ratio": 1.6823104693140793, "no_speech_prob": 1.83979459271455e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 240948, "start": 2418.46, "end": 2420.22, "text": " They left a map of the minefield.", "tokens": [50814, 814, 1411, 257, 4471, 295, 264, 3892, 7610, 13, 50902], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1697676522391183, "compression_ratio": 1.6823104693140793, "no_speech_prob": 1.83979459271455e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 240948, "start": 2420.64, "end": 2422.78, "text": " It is science functioning exactly as it should.", "tokens": [50923, 467, 307, 3497, 18483, 2293, 382, 309, 820, 13, 51030], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1697676522391183, "compression_ratio": 1.6823104693140793, "no_speech_prob": 1.83979459271455e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 240948, "start": 2423.22, "end": 2426.72, "text": " It's not the Hollywood ending where the scientist screams Eureka in the lab.", "tokens": [51052, 467, 311, 406, 264, 11628, 8121, 689, 264, 12662, 22832, 462, 540, 2330, 294, 264, 2715, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1697676522391183, "compression_ratio": 1.6823104693140793, "no_speech_prob": 1.83979459271455e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 240948, "start": 2426.98, "end": 2430.1, "text": " It's a quiet, meticulous, incredibly useful.", "tokens": [51240, 467, 311, 257, 5677, 11, 41566, 6893, 11, 6252, 4420, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1697676522391183, "compression_ratio": 1.6823104693140793, "no_speech_prob": 1.83979459271455e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 240948, "start": 2430.96, "end": 2431.66, "text": " We don't know yet,", "tokens": [51439, 492, 500, 380, 458, 1939, 11, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1697676522391183, "compression_ratio": 1.6823104693140793, "no_speech_prob": 1.83979459271455e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 240948, "start": 2431.88, "end": 2434.58, "text": " but here's exactly how you find out without fooling yourself.", "tokens": [51485, 457, 510, 311, 2293, 577, 291, 915, 484, 1553, 7979, 278, 1803, 13, 51620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1697676522391183, "compression_ratio": 1.6823104693140793, "no_speech_prob": 1.83979459271455e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 240948, "start": 2434.92, "end": 2436.1, "text": " Let's pull all of this together.", "tokens": [51637, 961, 311, 2235, 439, 295, 341, 1214, 13, 51696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1697676522391183, "compression_ratio": 1.6823104693140793, "no_speech_prob": 1.83979459271455e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 243610, "start": 2436.1, "end": 2440.8399999999997, "text": " We started with a philosophical warning about rhetorical vocabulary in science and business.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1409, 365, 257, 25066, 9164, 466, 24182, 284, 804, 19864, 294, 3497, 293, 1606, 13, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1631989860534668, "compression_ratio": 1.6557377049180328, "no_speech_prob": 2.1672791599564034e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 243610, "start": 2441.2799999999997, "end": 2445.36, "text": " We don't want terms that do grammatical work, but no empirical work.", "tokens": [50624, 492, 500, 380, 528, 2115, 300, 360, 17570, 267, 804, 589, 11, 457, 572, 31886, 589, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1631989860534668, "compression_ratio": 1.6557377049180328, "no_speech_prob": 2.1672791599564034e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 243610, "start": 2446.02, "end": 2448.48, "text": " We saw the construction of a four-step crucible.", "tokens": [50861, 492, 1866, 264, 6435, 295, 257, 1451, 12, 16792, 5140, 32128, 13, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1631989860534668, "compression_ratio": 1.6557377049180328, "no_speech_prob": 2.1672791599564034e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 243610, "start": 2449.14, "end": 2451.8199999999997, "text": " Reconstructible, comparable, stable, predictive.", "tokens": [51017, 1300, 25279, 1757, 964, 11, 25323, 11, 8351, 11, 35521, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1631989860534668, "compression_ratio": 1.6557377049180328, "no_speech_prob": 2.1672791599564034e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 243610, "start": 2452.3399999999997, "end": 2456.18, "text": " We saw how a proposed capacity framework was dropped into that crucible", "tokens": [51177, 492, 1866, 577, 257, 10348, 6042, 8388, 390, 8119, 666, 300, 5140, 32128, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1631989860534668, "compression_ratio": 1.6557377049180328, "no_speech_prob": 2.1672791599564034e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 243610, "start": 2456.18, "end": 2458.58, "text": " using the hardest possible test case.", "tokens": [51369, 1228, 264, 13158, 1944, 1500, 1389, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1631989860534668, "compression_ratio": 1.6557377049180328, "no_speech_prob": 2.1672791599564034e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 243610, "start": 2459.12, "end": 2461.14, "text": " Motility-induced phase separation.", "tokens": [51516, 8956, 1140, 12, 471, 41209, 5574, 14634, 13, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1631989860534668, "compression_ratio": 1.6557377049180328, "no_speech_prob": 2.1672791599564034e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 246114, "start": 2461.14, "end": 2466.04, "text": " We watched the author catch their own artifacts, dodge Euler-Muroyama explosions,", "tokens": [50365, 492, 6337, 264, 3793, 3745, 641, 1065, 24617, 11, 27238, 462, 26318, 12, 44, 374, 939, 2404, 36872, 11, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14050424540484394, "compression_ratio": 1.5286195286195285, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363644380484876e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 246114, "start": 2466.48, "end": 2468.92, "text": " and fix absolute time intervention bugs.", "tokens": [50632, 293, 3191, 8236, 565, 13176, 15120, 13, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14050424540484394, "compression_ratio": 1.5286195286195285, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363644380484876e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 246114, "start": 2469.44, "end": 2474.0, "text": " And ultimately, we arrived at a perfectly bounded, highly informative negative result.", "tokens": [50780, 400, 6284, 11, 321, 6678, 412, 257, 6239, 37498, 11, 5405, 27759, 3671, 1874, 13, 51008], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14050424540484394, "compression_ratio": 1.5286195286195285, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363644380484876e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 246114, "start": 2474.42, "end": 2477.16, "text": " The capacity constructs did not beat the density baseline.", "tokens": [51029, 440, 6042, 7690, 82, 630, 406, 4224, 264, 10305, 20518, 13, 51166], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14050424540484394, "compression_ratio": 1.5286195286195285, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363644380484876e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 246114, "start": 2477.56, "end": 2480.74, "text": " It was a clean failure that narrowed the space of viable theories.", "tokens": [51186, 467, 390, 257, 2541, 7763, 300, 9432, 292, 264, 1901, 295, 22024, 13667, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14050424540484394, "compression_ratio": 1.5286195286195285, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363644380484876e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 246114, "start": 2480.94, "end": 2483.8799999999997, "text": " So how do you, the listener, apply this tomorrow morning?", "tokens": [51355, 407, 577, 360, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 3079, 341, 4153, 2446, 30, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14050424540484394, "compression_ratio": 1.5286195286195285, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363644380484876e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 246114, "start": 2484.24, "end": 2486.92, "text": " When you are reading a bold claim, a new business framework,", "tokens": [51520, 1133, 291, 366, 3760, 257, 11928, 3932, 11, 257, 777, 1606, 8388, 11, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14050424540484394, "compression_ratio": 1.5286195286195285, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363644380484876e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 248692, "start": 2486.92, "end": 2490.04, "text": " or a flashy headline, channel Flixian, look at the buzzwords.", "tokens": [50365, 420, 257, 47873, 28380, 11, 2269, 3235, 970, 952, 11, 574, 412, 264, 13036, 13832, 13, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13914360434322035, "compression_ratio": 1.6046511627906976, "no_speech_prob": 3.0686531874574152e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 248692, "start": 2490.28, "end": 2493.64, "text": " Ask yourself, how exactly did they physically measure this new word?", "tokens": [50533, 12320, 1803, 11, 577, 2293, 630, 436, 9762, 3481, 341, 777, 1349, 30, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13914360434322035, "compression_ratio": 1.6046511627906976, "no_speech_prob": 3.0686531874574152e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 248692, "start": 2494.02, "end": 2497.6800000000003, "text": " And does it predict the future any better than the boring, simple data we already had?", "tokens": [50720, 400, 775, 309, 6069, 264, 2027, 604, 1101, 813, 264, 9989, 11, 2199, 1412, 321, 1217, 632, 30, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13914360434322035, "compression_ratio": 1.6046511627906976, "no_speech_prob": 3.0686531874574152e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 248692, "start": 2497.96, "end": 2499.98, "text": " Demand that their vocabulary earns its keep.", "tokens": [50917, 4686, 474, 300, 641, 19864, 46936, 1080, 1066, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13914360434322035, "compression_ratio": 1.6046511627906976, "no_speech_prob": 3.0686531874574152e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 248692, "start": 2500.2400000000002, "end": 2502.5, "text": " We must be vigilant against the illusion of measurement.", "tokens": [51031, 492, 1633, 312, 45737, 1970, 264, 18854, 295, 13160, 13, 51144], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13914360434322035, "compression_ratio": 1.6046511627906976, "no_speech_prob": 3.0686531874574152e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 248692, "start": 2502.88, "end": 2504.98, "text": " And I want to leave you with a final thought to mull over,", "tokens": [51163, 400, 286, 528, 281, 1856, 291, 365, 257, 2572, 1194, 281, 275, 858, 670, 11, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13914360434322035, "compression_ratio": 1.6046511627906976, "no_speech_prob": 3.0686531874574152e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 248692, "start": 2505.14, "end": 2507.2400000000002, "text": " something that takes this exact framework", "tokens": [51276, 746, 300, 2516, 341, 1900, 8388, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13914360434322035, "compression_ratio": 1.6046511627906976, "no_speech_prob": 3.0686531874574152e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 248692, "start": 2507.2400000000002, "end": 2510.34, "text": " and points it at the technology dictating our lives right now.", "tokens": [51381, 293, 2793, 309, 412, 264, 2899, 12569, 990, 527, 2909, 558, 586, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13914360434322035, "compression_ratio": 1.6046511627906976, "no_speech_prob": 3.0686531874574152e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 251034, "start": 2510.34, "end": 2516.58, "text": " We just watched highly complex formal physics concepts fail this rigorous four-step test.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 445, 6337, 5405, 3997, 9860, 10649, 10392, 3061, 341, 29882, 1451, 12, 16792, 1500, 13, 50677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.118957577580991, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419586823344546e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 251034, "start": 2517.1200000000003, "end": 2519.6400000000003, "text": " What happens if we apply Flixian's exact crucible", "tokens": [50704, 708, 2314, 498, 321, 3079, 3235, 970, 952, 311, 1900, 5140, 32128, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.118957577580991, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419586823344546e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 251034, "start": 2519.6400000000003, "end": 2523.8, "text": " to the algorithmic constructs that social media platforms use every single day?", "tokens": [50830, 281, 264, 9284, 299, 7690, 82, 300, 2093, 3021, 9473, 764, 633, 2167, 786, 30, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.118957577580991, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419586823344546e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 251034, "start": 2523.88, "end": 2526.1400000000003, "text": " That is a very pertinent application of this framework.", "tokens": [51042, 663, 307, 257, 588, 13269, 11058, 3861, 295, 341, 8388, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.118957577580991, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419586823344546e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 251034, "start": 2526.42, "end": 2530.52, "text": " Think about the concepts of engagement, or relevance, or toxicity.", "tokens": [51169, 6557, 466, 264, 10392, 295, 8742, 11, 420, 32684, 11, 420, 45866, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.118957577580991, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419586823344546e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 251034, "start": 2531.06, "end": 2533.46, "text": " Platforms claim they are optimizing for these things.", "tokens": [51401, 28707, 82, 3932, 436, 366, 40425, 337, 613, 721, 13, 51521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.118957577580991, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419586823344546e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 251034, "start": 2533.98, "end": 2536.7200000000003, "text": " But if we subjected engagement to the four-step test,", "tokens": [51547, 583, 498, 321, 32153, 8742, 281, 264, 1451, 12, 16792, 1500, 11, 51684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.118957577580991, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419586823344546e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 251034, "start": 2536.7200000000003, "end": 2540.2400000000002, "text": " is it reconstructable without subjective human vibes?", "tokens": [51684, 307, 309, 31499, 712, 1553, 25972, 1952, 27636, 30, 51860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.118957577580991, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.7419586823344546e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 254034, "start": 2540.86, "end": 2542.34, "text": " Is it comparable against alternatives?", "tokens": [50391, 1119, 309, 25323, 1970, 20478, 30, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1979741967242697, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582742545598553e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 254034, "start": 2542.84, "end": 2546.02, "text": " Is it stable across different zooming scales of user data?", "tokens": [50490, 1119, 309, 8351, 2108, 819, 48226, 17408, 295, 4195, 1412, 30, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1979741967242697, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582742545598553e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 254034, "start": 2546.54, "end": 2549.6600000000003, "text": " And is it actually predictive of a better user experience?", "tokens": [50675, 400, 307, 309, 767, 35521, 295, 257, 1101, 4195, 1752, 30, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1979741967242697, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582742545598553e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 254034, "start": 2549.8, "end": 2550.48, "text": " Would it survive?", "tokens": [50838, 6068, 309, 7867, 30, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1979741967242697, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582742545598553e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 254034, "start": 2550.88, "end": 2552.88, "text": " Or are those terms just rhetorical vocabulary?", "tokens": [50892, 1610, 366, 729, 2115, 445, 24182, 284, 804, 19864, 30, 50992], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1979741967242697, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582742545598553e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 254034, "start": 2553.34, "end": 2556.6200000000003, "text": " Are they just complex smoke screens for baseline primitive metrics", "tokens": [51015, 2014, 436, 445, 3997, 8439, 11171, 337, 20518, 28540, 16367, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1979741967242697, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582742545598553e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 254034, "start": 2556.6200000000003, "end": 2558.84, "text": " like time spent scrolling or number of clicks?", "tokens": [51179, 411, 565, 4418, 29053, 420, 1230, 295, 18521, 30, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1979741967242697, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582742545598553e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 254034, "start": 2559.32, "end": 2562.02, "text": " If two engineers disagree on a post's relevance,", "tokens": [51314, 759, 732, 11955, 14091, 322, 257, 2183, 311, 32684, 11, 51449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1979741967242697, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582742545598553e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 254034, "start": 2562.32, "end": 2563.98, "text": " is there a procedure to settle it?", "tokens": [51464, 307, 456, 257, 10747, 281, 11852, 309, 30, 51547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1979741967242697, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582742545598553e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 254034, "start": 2563.98, "end": 2568.38, "text": " Or is it just an illusion of measurement masking an automated feedback loop?", "tokens": [51547, 1610, 307, 309, 445, 364, 18854, 295, 13160, 31226, 364, 18473, 5824, 6367, 30, 51767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1979741967242697, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582742545598553e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 256838, "start": 2568.38, "end": 2572.34, "text": " The next time a platform claims their algorithm knows exactly what you want to see,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 958, 565, 257, 3663, 9441, 641, 9284, 3255, 2293, 437, 291, 528, 281, 536, 11, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14744916455499057, "compression_ratio": 1.5381165919282511, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944892072081837e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 256838, "start": 2572.54, "end": 2574.84, "text": " think about that broken elevator metric.", "tokens": [50573, 519, 466, 300, 5463, 18782, 20678, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14744916455499057, "compression_ratio": 1.5381165919282511, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944892072081837e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 256838, "start": 2575.1, "end": 2577.04, "text": " Think about the murky waters of language.", "tokens": [50701, 6557, 466, 264, 5257, 4133, 12975, 295, 2856, 13, 50798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14744916455499057, "compression_ratio": 1.5381165919282511, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944892072081837e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 256838, "start": 2577.4, "end": 2579.04, "text": " Are they showing you a real phenomenon?", "tokens": [50816, 2014, 436, 4099, 291, 257, 957, 14029, 30, 50898], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14744916455499057, "compression_ratio": 1.5381165919282511, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944892072081837e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 256838, "start": 2579.36, "end": 2582.32, "text": " Or are they just pointing at the geometry of the box they trapped you in?", "tokens": [50914, 1610, 366, 436, 445, 12166, 412, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 2424, 436, 14994, 291, 294, 30, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14744916455499057, "compression_ratio": 1.5381165919282511, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944892072081837e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 256838, "start": 2582.6400000000003, "end": 2583.6600000000003, "text": " Something to maul over.", "tokens": [51078, 6595, 281, 463, 425, 670, 13, 51129], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14744916455499057, "compression_ratio": 1.5381165919282511, "no_speech_prob": 2.4944892072081